    "https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/all_jobs.atom": {
      "title": "Rutgers University-New Brunswick: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:jobs.rutgers.edu,2005:/postings/all_jobs Rutgers University-New Brunswick: All Jobs 2026-02-04T13:01:28-05:00 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/268562 2026-02-04T13:01:27-05:00 2026-02-04T13:01:28-05:00 Open Rank Medical Director <div>The Medical Director serves as a senior clinical and organizational leader within the Health Center and is directly responsible for all clinical operations, quality of care, and patient safety initiatives. In this role, the Medical Director provides strategic oversight of medical services, ensuring the delivery of high-quality, evidence-based, and patient-centered care across all programs.</div><div>Working collaboratively with the Executive Director and the broader leadership team, the Medical Director helps advance the mission of the Health Center by aligning clinical operations with organizational goals, regulatory requirements, and community needs. This partnership includes shared responsibility for strategic planning, program development, performance improvement, and resource optimization.</div><div>The Medical Director leads and supports clinical staff, fosters a culture of professionalism and accountability, and promotes continuous quality improvement through data-driven decision making, provider education, and adherence to best practices. Key responsibilities also include oversight of clinical policies and procedures, compliance with federal, state, and accreditation standards, and integration of care models that improve access, outcomes, and patient experience.</div><div>As a visible leader within the organization, the Medical Director champions health equity, supports interdisciplinary collaboration, and serves as a clinical ambassador to internal stakeholders and external partners. Through effective leadership and partnership with executive management, the Medical Director plays a critical role in ensuring that clinical excellence remains central to fulfilling the Health Center’s mission and commitment to the community.</div> RWJ - EBCHC Medical RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7967 26FA0097 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280377 2026-09-03T10:43:07-04:00 2026-09-03T10:43:07-04:00 Manager Data Administration <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Manager of Data Administration for the Institute for Health Survey / Data Core.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Manager of Data Administration is to manage existing large health insurance claims databases, help develop more efficient use and processes of Core data, and assist with project-specific data management and analysis as needed. The Data Manager will be proficient with using SAS and other software packages and be able to write and review programming code that manages, cleans, and analyzes large, complex healthcare datasets.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Manages the integration, cleaning, and quality checks of new and updated data, ensuring compliance with data standards and thorough documentation.</li><li>Incorporates new data and updates to existing data into the Core to make data ready for storage and research, including decryption, extraction, management, cleaning, conduct of quality checks, and creation or updating of documentation</li><li>Supervisory support of analytical staff; supervises users of the Core, ensuring adherence to established Core data management and utilization policies.</li><li>Works with leadership team to provide updates to and expand the Core’s service offerings</li><li>Establishes data governance policies and promotes best practices to maintain data integrity, security, and compliance. Develops new approaches to improve the efficiency of the management and analysis of Core data.</li><li>Creates data cuts and assists with data preparation for faculty, staff, and student users using Core data</li><li>Develops guidance on best practices for use of Core data and computing resources</li><li>Designs and leads training and research support for faculty, staff, and students using Core data and resources</li><li>Keeps abreast of all pertinent federal, state and Rutgers regulations, laws and policies as they presently exist and as they change or are modified.</li></ul> Institute for Health, Health C RBHS Chancellor-L2 Institute for Health, Health C-L3 8086 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1715 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279238 2026-07-31T11:17:29-04:00 2026-07-31T11:17:29-04:00 Post Doctoral Associate <div>Rutgers is seeking a Post Doctoral Associate for the Institute for Nicotine and Tobacco Studies (INTS), located in New Brunswick, NJ. Under the direction of the P.I., supports and conducts highly specialized and technical research on cannabis and tobacco marketing and influence at the Rutgers Institute of Nicotine and Tobacco Studies (INTS). The Postdoctoral Associate will work closely with the Principal Investigator and research team on federally funded and related studies examining cannabis and tobacco product marketing, consumer perceptions, and health behavior.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Lead and support research projects examining the marketing of cannabis and tobacco products across digital, social media, retail,&nbsp;product packaging, and other communication channels.</li><li>Contribute to the design and implementation of observational studies, content analyses, surveys, randomized experiments,&nbsp;qualitative studies, and mixed-methods research.</li><li>Develop research protocols, coding instruments, codebooks, survey questionnaires, experimental stimuli, interview guides, and&nbsp;data-collection procedures.</li><li>Coordinate the collection and management of data from brand websites, social media platforms, direct-to-consumer&nbsp;communications, online retailers, product packages, surveys, interviews, and other relevant sources.</li></ul> Nicotine & Tobacco Institute RBHS Chancellor-L2 Nicotine & Tobacco Institute-L3 8529 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1578 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/272672 2026-04-08T15:38:01-04:00 2026-04-08T15:38:01-04:00 Assistant Teaching Professor (NTT) <div>The Graduate School of Applied and Professional Psychology (GSAPP) at Rutgers University-New Brunswick invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure track Assistant Teaching Professor faculty position in the Clinical Psychology Department. This faculty member will oversee the practicum and externship placements network for our Clinical Psychology Psy.D. students and support students in their application to these placements and externships in clinical settings. They will also liaise with site supervisors and collaborate with the Program Director in the Clinical Psychology Psy.D. program regarding field-based experiences and opportunities. Teaching responsibilities include supervision courses and other courses depending on the candidate’s expertise and departmental needs and opportunities for direct training and supervision. Competitive candidates will demonstrate related graduate-level teaching and professional practice experience, excellence in teaching, and specialized knowledge in clinical psychology. In addition, they should be knowledgeable about certification and licensure requirements. Applicants will also show the capacity to contribute to the mission and goals of GSAPP and the professional community.</div><div>For more information about GSAPP’s Clinical Psychology Psy.D. program, please see link:</div><div><a href=\"https://gsapp.rutgers.edu/academic-programs/clinical-department\"><strong>https://gsapp.rutgers.edu/academic-programs/clinical-department</strong></a></div> Clinical Psychology New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Graduate School of Applied & P-L3 6827 26FA0340 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279590 2026-08-14T11:13:28-04:00 2026-08-14T11:13:29-04:00 Graduate Assistant (3) Positions <div>Rutgers School of Health Professions (SHP) is seeking a Graduate Assistant to work in the Department of Health Informatics.<br><br>This Graduate Assistant position is designed to support the teacher with various aspects of online teaching, including grading, working individually with students to improve their performance, and answering questions about the course content.<br><br></div><div>Essential duties and responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Facilitating online lessons, tutorials or discussions in concert with the Instructor.</li><li>Grade assignments, exams, quizzes, and projects.</li><li>Maintain and update student grades as an Excel Sheet to be submitted to the Instructor.</li><li>Assist the Instructor in preparing and sharing reading materials, supplementary notes.</li></ul> SHP - Health Informatics RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Health Professions-L3 7582 Piscataway NJ 26ST1616 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279834 2026-08-21T14:05:27-04:00 2026-08-21T14:05:27-04:00 Coadjutant Researcher RCSB PDB <div>RCSB Protein Data Bank is seeking a highly motivated database programmer with experience in database administration and domain experience in computer science or relevant certification. This position will involve collaboration with wwPDB scientists and software developers in a collaborative team environment. The candidate should be comfortable working in a dynamic environment, and able to demonstrate an ability to think creatively, generate new ideas, and implement solutions. The candidate should be interested in structural biological data and enjoy engaging with other programmers and scientists in a collaborative team environment.&nbsp;<br><br>Responsibilities:<br>Perform weekly update processes for updating PDB archives</div><div>Monitor update performance and implement changes for improvements</div><div>Extend and maintain data exchange with wwPDB partners</div><div>Improve and maintain weekly update related software/scripts</div><div>Extend and maintain new content types in the PDB archives</div><div>Build and support database systems of high availability and quality</div><div>Design new relational database schema, integrate complex bioinformatics data, and improve existing schemas through normalization</div><div>Improve existing backup processes for both relational and non-relational DBMS</div><div>Provide users with data in appropriate formats and in a timely manner for data analysis and statistical reports</div><div>Indexing and query performance tuning</div><div>Monitor database performance, implement changes, apply new patches and update versions when required</div><div>Use high-speed transaction recovery techniques for database backups</div> Quantitative Biomedicine Inst New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 6749 26FA0731 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277719 2026-06-24T18:14:00-04:00 2026-06-24T18:14:00-04:00 Pediatric Endocrinology RBHS Instructor/Assistant Professor <div>The Department of Pediatrics at Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School seeks a dynamic career-oriented physician to join the Division of Endocrinology at the Clinical Instructor or Assistant Professor level. Candidates who have successfully completed a fellowship and are board certified/board eligible in Pediatric Endocrinology will be considered. The physician will be responsible for both inpatient and outpatient clinical care as well as teaching in the undergraduate, graduate and continuing medical education programs at the institution. The physician would also be expected to engage in scholarly and outreach activities. The physician would join four full time faculty members in the division who provide 24/7 coverage for the inpatient consultation service, as well as provide consultation services in the ambulatory practice.</div><div>The Department of Pediatrics is composed of 124 full-time and more than 200 volunteer faculty members, organized into 18 divisions covering all of the pediatric subspecialties in conjunction with four key surgical services. The department is undergoing a renaissance following the integration of the medical school with Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, and the recent merger of two major health systems to form RWJ Barnabas. The department has already recruited 43 new faculty members with plans for hiring additional faculty, allowing us to expand our research and clinical programs and provide improved care to our patients. Our educational mission focuses on the development of the next generation of multi-talented physicians who will become leaders in education, research and patient care. Our ACGME-accredited training programs continue to thrive and expand. We have an outstanding pediatric residency and a fellowship training program in Pediatric Endocrinology.</div><div>The inpatient clinical services are provided at the Bristol-Myers Squibb Children’s Hospital of the Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital in New Brunswick, NJ a five-time Magnet recipient recognized as “One of America’s Best Children’s Hospitals” by <em>U.S. News and World Report </em>for the sixth time. This is a 105-bed acute care hospital located on the only pediatric academic health campus in New Jersey. Adjacent to the Children’s hospital is the PSE&amp;G Children’s Specialized Hospital which is one of the country’s largest inpatient acute rehabilitation hospitals for children. Across the street is the Rutgers Cancer Institute of New Jersey – the only NCI designated center in the state of New Jersey as well as the Ronald MacDonald House. The outpatient services are located in the Rutgers Child Health Institute of NJ, a state-of-the-art 5-story facility that includes a Pediatric CRC and Pediatric subspecialty offices. Our New Brunswick–based clinical programs have achieved Accredited Status for Ambulatory Health Care by the Joint Commission, one of only a small number of academic ambulatory practices to receive this status.</div><div>The Robert Wood Johnson School of Medicine is consistently ranked as one of the highly NIH-funded academic universities and Rutgers is a member of the Association of American Universities comprising the top comprehensive research universities in North America. As the State’s premier institution, there are many opportunities to collaborate across campuses with all the health professional schools and biomedical science school at the Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences.</div><div>The New Brunswick/Piscataway campus is situated in central New Jersey with easy access to New York City and Philadelphia. The region is home to world class universities, numerous pharmaceutical and biotech research facilities and corporate headquarters. Central New Jersey offers vibrant and diverse cultural activities, outstanding public and private schools and opportunities to live in urban, suburban or small town settings within a short distance of the Rutgers campus.</div><div>This is an excellent opportunity for dynamic career-oriented physicians. The position offers a generous salary and benefits package and academic rank commensurate with experience.</div><div><br>Interested candidates should apply to this posting and email a cover letter and your CV to:</div><div>Ahmed Khattab</div><div>Division of Pediatric Endocrinology</div><div>Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School</div><div>89 French Street</div><div>New Brunswick, NJ 08901</div><div>Email: <a href=\"mailto:ak1684@rwjms.rutgers.edu\"><strong>ak1684@rwjms.rutgers.edu</strong></a></div> RWJ - Pediatrics Endocrinology RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7805 25FA0450 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274586 2026-05-07T18:25:24-04:00 2026-05-07T18:25:25-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate <div>A Post-Doctoral Associate position is now open in the McGinty lab in the Center for Molecular and Behavioral Neuroscience (CMBN) at Rutgers University. Our lab studies how the brain organizes value-based decision-making and other motivated behaviors. We are seeking a talented and motivated postdoctoral scientist to conduct NIH-funded research on the neural computations that underlie decision-making, with a focus on the prefrontal cortex and limbic system. In addition to scientific training, our lab offers supportive mentorship and intensive career development. Primary techniques include nonhuman primate behavior, high-channel-count neural recordings, intracranial microstimulation, and state-of-the-art machine-learning analyses and modeling. Primate experience is not necessary, but familiarity with neural recording, data analysis, or modeling is strongly recommended. For more information on our work, see McGinty &amp; Lupkin 2023 (Nature Neuroscience) and Lupkin &amp; McGinty 2023 (eLife). Anticipated Start Date: January 1, 2027.</div> CMBN Newark Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences Newa-L3 6804 26FA0470 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266195 2025-12-31T09:35:08-05:00 2025-12-31T09:35:08-05:00 Dean of the Honors Living-Learning Community (HLLC) at Rutgers University–Newark (Faculty) <div>********INTERNAL POSTING to RUTGERS UNIVERSITY ONLY********<br><br>The Honors Living-Learning Community (HLLC; <a href=\"https://hllc.newark.rutgers.edu/\"><strong>https://hllc.newark.rutgers.edu/</strong></a>) at Rutgers University–Newark is searching for a new Dean. Founded in 2015, the HLLC is a transformational college access program that reimagines traditional notions of merit and excellence. It fosters interdisciplinary learning communities that tackle pressing social issues and empower students from historically marginalized backgrounds.<br><br></div><div><strong>About the HLLC Dean</strong></div><div>The next HLLC Dean will lead a nationally recognized initiative that is revolutionizing honors education, cultivating talent, and engaging communities. The next Dean will be a visionary leader committed to innovation and transformative education. The Dean is the chief academic and administrative officer for the HLLC. The Dean provides leadership, direction, and overview for all HLLC programs, services, and initiatives. The Dean works with all stakeholders across the campus including university faculty, administrators, and staff to create an exceptional community of students who share a passion for learning. The Dean of the HLLC reports directly to the Vice Provost.</div> Newark Chancellor Newark Chancellor-L2 Newark Chancellor-L3 6602 25FA1200 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280083 2026-08-27T12:22:08-04:00 2026-08-27T12:22:09-04:00 Mental Health Specialist IV - per diem <div>Rutgers, The State University is seeking a per diem Mental Health Specialist IV in the Acute Psychological Services within Rutgers University Behavioral Healthcare.<br><br>The Mental Health Specialist IV participates as a member of the unit team providing care to assigned patients under the direct supervision of the Registered Nurse.<br><br>Among the key duties of the position are the following:</div><ul><li>Demonstrates the ability to provide patient support and identify, monitor, and communicate changes in patient behavior, affect, functioning, and risk.</li><li>Provides patient support consistent with the individualized established treatment plan.</li><li>Assists multidisciplinary team members in working with patients with cognitive, intellectual, or developmental disabilities.</li><li>Demonstrates ability to keep patients engaged and motivated in their treatment.</li><li>Assists patient in reviewing daily goals and tracking progress.</li><li>Observes patient behaviors, mood, affect, and interactions; promptly reports concerns to the unit staff nurse and/or supervisor.</li></ul> UBHC - Acute Psychological Ser RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7987 Piscataway NJ 26ST1598 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278378 2026-07-08T02:30:43-04:00 2026-07-08T02:30:45-04:00 Mental Health Specialist II- Per diem- NJ Hopeline <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Mental Health Specialist II (Per diem) for the NJ Hopeline within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>Performs functions in support of the Unit’s mission providing streamlined, prompt, and “customer friendly” services to clients of the 988 Lifeline Services. Receives telephone, chat and/or text requests for service, undertakes assessment of the service need of the client and responds by offering support and appropriate referrals or disposition. Demonstrates competency in recognizing the unique needs of clients and applying relevant assessment and support skills with regard to a wide range of issues.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Interacts with client in a therapeutic manner.</li><li>Participates in ensuring that all service requests are handled in an effective and “client friendly” manner.&nbsp;</li><li>Assesses service requests/referrals and responds in accordance with prescribed procedures.&nbsp;</li><li>Assumes overall responsibilities for completion of all request and documentation for disposition.&nbsp;</li><li>Documents assessments, interventions, and interactions with clients in a timely manner and in accordance with established policies.&nbsp;</li></ul> UBHC - NJ Hopeline RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8707 Remote NJ 26ST1486 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267358 2026-01-15T11:14:29-05:00 2026-01-15T11:14:30-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor of Medicine-Multiple Positions (IM Hepatology)) <div>The Department of Medicine, Division of Liver Disease and Transplant Hepatology at Rutgers New Jersey Medical School (NJMS) seeks qualified candidate(s) at the Assistant or Associate Professor level for full-time academic position(s) in liver disease and transplant hepatology. Successful candidate(s) will be board eligible/certified in Internal Medicine and will have completed at least one year of advanced training in liver disease and transplant hepatology. These position(s) will support general and advanced inpatient and outpatient hepatology consultation services at University Hospital. In addition, the candidate(s) will support the training of hepatology fellows and medical residents and will also support the educational needs of New Jersey Medical School in liver disease and transplant hepatology. Candidate(s) will actively support the research mission of the division. The candidate(s) must possess superior clinical, teaching, and interpersonal skills.<br><br></div> NJMS - Medicine Gastroenterolo RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7439 23FA1086 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280242 2026-08-31T15:05:56-04:00 2026-08-31T15:05:57-04:00 Student Assistant <div>Rutgers Institute for Nicotine and Tobacco Studies (INTS) located in New Brunswick, NJ is seeking a highly motivated part-time Student Assistant to work with Dr. Jessie Jensen. This position will assist with coding of local flavored cigar policies.<br><br>Duties include:<br><br></div><ul><li>Conducting content analyses (i.e., coding) of flavored cigar policies.</li><li>Assist with administrative tasks related to content analysis</li></ul> Nicotine & Tobacco Institute RBHS Chancellor-L2 Nicotine & Tobacco Institute-L3 8529 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1699 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278828 2026-07-15T10:38:49-04:00 2026-07-15T10:38:50-04:00 Peer Support Specialist III PD <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Peer Support Specialist III PD for the&nbsp; Care2Caregivers within Rutgers University Behavioral Healthcare.<br><br>Under direction, the Peer Support Specialist III will provide person centered, culturally competent, and “consumer friendly” services to individuals who contact the Call Center. Receives telephone, chat, and text requests for service, undertakes review of the service need of the caller and responds by offering peer support and appropriate referrals and disposition. Assists the Care2Caregiver team.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Provides “customer friendly” services, taking initiative in engaging individuals served in an empathic and concerned manner.</li><li>Provides direct care services consistent with philosophy of UBHC.&nbsp;</li><li>Reviews service requests/referrals for all populations, and responds in accordance with prescribed departmental procedures. &nbsp;</li><li>Documents contacts, interventions, and interactions with callers in a timely manner and in accordance with established policies. &nbsp;</li><li>Maintains knowledge of Center and Unit policies and procedures.&nbsp;</li><li>Demonstrates good work habits.</li><li>Maintains knowledge of UBHC and unit policies and procedures.&nbsp;</li></ul> UBHC - COPSA RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8017 Remote NJ 26ST1526 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/270270 2026-03-05T11:30:08-05:00 2026-03-05T11:30:08-05:00 Postdoctoral Associate <div>Rutgers School of Health Professions (SHP) is seeking a Postdoctoral Associate to work in the Department of Clinical and Preventive Nutrition Sciences, Rawal Nutrition and Health Lab.<br><br>The Department of Clinical and Preventive Nutrition Sciences at Rutgers School of Health Professions is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Associate to join an active research program focused on maternal and cardiometabolic health across the life course.<br><br>Under the direction of the Principal Investigator (PI), the Postdoctoral Associate will contribute to one or more NIH-funded research projects led by the lab. The lab’s work broadly centers on the development, evaluation, and implementation of technology-enabled interventions aimed at both prevention and management of pregnancy-related conditions and complications (including gestational diabetes, hypertensive disorders of pregnancy, and excessive gestational weight gain) and their downstream maternal and neonatal sequelae. Ongoing projects integrate mHealth and digital health tools, clinical trials, implementation science, and global health, with research conducted in both U.S. and international settings, including Nepal.<br><br>The Postdoctoral Associate will assist with scientific and operational aspects of ongoing studies. Responsibilities may include finalizing study protocols; developing manuals of operations and training materials; preparing, submitting, and maintaining IRB documentation; coordinating with domestic and international collaborators; and ensuring high protocol fidelity across study sites.<br><br>The Postdoctoral Associate will participate in regular investigator meetings and contribute to study oversight, data monitoring, and interpretation of findings. The Postdoctoral Associate will lead or co-lead data analyses and play a key role in the dissemination of research findings through peer-reviewed publications and conference presentations. Depending on the associate’s interests and career goals, dedicated mentorship will support the development of an independent line of research, including planning pilot studies and preparing grant applications.<br><br>This position provides strong opportunities for manuscript writing, grant development, study design, and hands-on experience with innovative research methods and digital health technologies. Priority will be given to candidates with expertise in one or more of the following areas: maternal and child health, clinical trials or intervention research, mHealth or digital health, nutritional epidemiology, or implementation science.<br><br></div><div>Essential duties and responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Plan, coordinate, implement, and monitor research projects, including oversight of study timelines, milestones, and follow-up activities.</li><li>Develop and refine study protocols and research materials; conduct statistical analyses; and maintain, manage, and review study databases to ensure data quality and integrity.</li><li>Assist the Principal Investigator (PI) with preparation, submission, and maintenance of Institutional Review Board (IRB) applications, including responsibility for reporting protocol modifications and continuing reviews.</li><li>Contribute to the preparation of scholarly products, including abstracts, peer-reviewed manuscripts, grant applications, progress reports, and other research dissemination materials.</li><li>Maintain flexibility in work hours, as needed, to accommodate participant assessments and meetings with domestic and international research collaborators.</li><li>Perform additional duties related to grant-funded research activities as assigned by the PI.</li></ul> SHP - Clinical & Preventive Nu RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Health Professions-L3 7570 Newark NJ 26ST0430 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280477 2026-09-04T15:42:37-04:00 2026-09-04T15:42:38-04:00 Associate or Full Professor in African American History <div>The Department of History at Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, in New Brunswick invites applications for a full-time senior scholar in African American history. We seek applications from candidates specializing in any thematic area within the field of African American history. We are particularly interested in applicants whose work focuses on the long nineteenth and early twentieth century, and whose scholarship contributes to one or more of our program’s strengths, including gender and sexuality, urban history, and the global Black freedom struggle. We also encourage applications from scholars whose research and teaching interests intersect with the university’s initiatives in public history, law, and the environment. Candidates should have a distinguished record of publication, teaching, and service, and should be suitable for appointment with tenure at the rank of Full Professor or Distinguished Professor, though truly exceptional candidates at the rank of Associate Professor will be considered. Ph.D in History or related field is required.<br><br></div><div>Located in New Jersey, Rutgers’ student body reflects the broad spectrum of backgrounds in the state. We are interested in hiring faculty who can contribute to our many communities through their research, teaching and/or service. The history department at Rutgers offers a top ranked graduate program, with #1 rankings in both African American and Women’s History. The successful candidate will have a 2-2 course load, teach a range of African American history courses at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, and will play a central role in our stellar graduate program. Rutgers also offers exciting centers and departments in Global Racial Justice, Africana Studies, Latino and Caribbean Studies, and Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies, which provide endless opportunities for collaboration.<br><br></div><div>Applicants should upload the following materials: a cover letter, addressed to Professor Leslie Alexander, Search Committee Chair; a CV; the names and e-mail addresses of three referees; and an article-length writing sample directly relevant to the candidate’s expertise in African American history. The cover letter should include discussion of the candidate’s research, teaching, and service, and should explain the candidate’s training in and commitments to African American history. The deadline for submission is Tuesday, May 4, 2027.</div> History New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 8124 25FA0818 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279440 2026-08-10T10:02:47-04:00 2026-08-10T10:02:48-04:00 Mental Health Clinician II UCHC ADTC <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care (UCHC) is seeking a Mental Health Clinician II for Northern State Prison, located in Newark, New Jersey. The Mental Health Clinician II completes specialized psychological testing and assessment of clinical needs of adult inmates sentenced to the Department of Corrections.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Completes specialized psychological testing and assessment of clinical needs of adults sentenced to the Department of Corrections.</li><li>Arrives at diagnoses with precision and accuracy by the end of psychological testing and the evaluation session. Develops treatment plans.</li><li>Makes clinically based decisions regarding appropriateness for treatment, as well as preferred treatment modality. Skilled in in providing group, individual and family therapies</li><li>Assesses and makes referrals for higher levels of care, as appropriate.</li><li>Recognizes the unique needs and behaviors of adult inmate/patients, seniors and their families.</li></ul> UCHC Adult Diagnosis & Treatme RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7651 Avenel NJ 26ST0315 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/276610 2026-06-05T14:43:38-04:00 2026-06-05T14:43:38-04:00 Lecturers, Digital Media <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the School of Arts &amp; Sciences, Digital Studies Department, seeks new lecturers to teach courses for their Digital Media Masters program during the 2026/2027 academic year. Most courses are held during the evening. Courses cover various topics related to the analysis and production of digital media. Instructors will design and present course material during the assigned course times, hold office hours, administer exams, assign grades, and coordinate any other requirements related to course instruction.</div> Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 8076 26FA0577 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274050 2026-04-30T11:50:53-04:00 2026-04-30T11:50:54-04:00 Laboratory Technicians, Chemistry <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the Faculty of Arts &amp; Sciences, Chemistry Department, is seeking part-time Coadjutants in the field of Chemistry to aid in the preparation of laboratory or lecture courses in Introductory, General, or Organic Chemistry as well as Biochemistry and Forensic Chemistry disciplines for courses in Fall 2026, Winter 2027, Spring 2027, and/or Summer 2027.<br>Job duties include, but are not limited to: preparation of reagents for chemistry laboratory courses; washing glassware; maintain cleanliness of laboratory space; assist with the preparation of laboratory exercises; assist the primary course instructor with lecture/laboratory preparation and execution; and assist with data processing or chemical inventory.<br><br></div> Chemistry Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 6759 26FA0411 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266001 2025-12-31T09:12:01-05:00 2025-12-31T09:12:01-05:00 Associate Professor - .20 FTE Prosthodontist <div>The Department of Restorative Dentistry is searching for a .20 FTE, PART-TIME prosthodontist faculty member. The primary functions of this position include: Pre-doctoral education in fixed, removable, implant prosthodontics, occlusion, biomaterials, and operative dentistry. Participation in pre-clinical and post-graduate teaching; possible participation in the Departmental Master of Dental Science degree program; scholarly activity; research; service; teaching preclinical courses; possibly serving as course director for at least one pre-clinical or post-graduate course; serving as an advisor for students; lecturing in departmental courses as directed; participation on committees as assigned; other assignments as directed by the Chair.</div><div>Position will remain open until filled. Salary and rank will be commensurate with experience.</div><div>Rutgers School of Dental Medicine is a component of Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey and is located on the Newark Campus of Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences Division, along with the Rutgers Medical School, the Graduate School of Biomedical Sciences, the School of Health Related Professions, and the School of Nursing. Rutgers School of Dental Medicine is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer. The final candidate will be required to successfully pass a criminal background check prior to employment.</div> RSDM - Restorative Dentistry RBHS Chancellor-L2 Rutgers School of Dental Medic-L3 7550 23FA0341 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279721 2026-08-19T14:44:24-04:00 2026-08-19T14:44:25-04:00 Physician Specialist Psychiatrist PT UCHC GSYCF <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care (UCHC) is seeking a part time Physician Specialist (Psychiatrist) for Garden State Youth Correctional Facility, located in Yardville, NJ. The Physician Specialist provides direct clinical care to state prisoners, functions collaboratively with multidisciplinary teams and maintains effective communication with staff and administration.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Provides assessments, direct clinical care and treatment planning to inmates.</li><li>Conducts comprehensive psychiatrist assessments demonstrating a review of the electronic record, psychotropic medications, history of mental illness, prior psychiatric hospitalization, suicidal, unusual, or bizarre behavior) for new admissions to UCHC’s Special Needs roster according to established timeframes.</li><li>Is knowledgeable about and follows DOC and UCHC policies and procedures, including, but not limited to, emergency and non-emergency forced medication, management of potentially suicidal inmates, psychiatry services, and therapeutic restraint.</li><li>Orders, initiates and interprets laboratory tests according to required time frames or as medically necessary including metabolic monitoring, mood stabilizer blood levels, thyroid function, AIMS testing, and other appropriate biochemical monitoring.</li><li>Prescribes and renews medications that are deemed medically necessary within required time frames.</li></ul> UCHC Garden State Youth Medica RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7653 Yardville NJ 26ST1629 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280024 2026-08-26T12:20:35-04:00 2026-08-26T12:20:36-04:00 Assistant Nurse Manager <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking an Assistant Nurse Manager for the Acute Psychiatric Services (APS) Department within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Assistant Nurse Manager is to be responsible for supervising the provision and management of patient care services for an assigned shift or unit on a consistent basis. The ANM serves as a resource for nursing care across the system on an as needed basis and works with other healthcare professionals to optimize patient outcomes. The ANM promotes quality patient care, patient safety and customer satisfaction. The ANM serves as the resource person for staff in explaining and executing policy and procedure. The ANM functions as a member of the interdisciplinary team; participates in quality improvement activities, educational activities and supports research endeavors. The role is consistent with the scope and standards outlined by the American Psychiatric Nurses Association for Psychiatric-Mental Health Nursing.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Assures the delivery of quality patient care through direct supervision of clinical staff.</li><li>Supervises all high risk situations to assure standards of practice are met on a consistent basis.</li><li>Facilitates effective communication inter and intra departmentally to coordinate efforts, resolve operations problems and improve quality of patient care.</li><li>Assists in interpreting and translating the theoretical concepts of nursing into the delivery of nursing services for all age groups.</li><li>Plans and implements safe staffing based upon patient acuity and defined staff plan.</li><li>Promotes cost effective utilization of resources, develops yearly budget and controls daily expenses of the units.</li><li>Demonstrates respect and regard for the dignity of all patients, families, visitors and fellow employees to ensure a professional, responsible and courteous environment.</li></ul> UBHC - Acute Psychological Ser RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7987 Piscataway NJ 26ST1646 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277785 2026-06-25T11:28:47-04:00 2026-06-25T11:28:48-04:00 Staff Nurse PT Eves UCHC EMCFW (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Healthcare is seeking a Part Time UCHC Staff Nurse for Edna Mahan Correctional Facility located in Clinton, NJ. The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus. Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br><br>Among the duties are:</div><ul><li>Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the inmate-patient including adults (18 to 64 years), and geriatrics (65+) within the framework established by the correctional system.</li><li>Utilizes effective communication skills by demonstrating respect, concern and courtesy in all interpersonal relationships.</li><li>Uses current knowledge to promote a safe environment for providing health care to inmate-patients.</li></ul> UCHC-Edna Mahan Corr-Ancillary RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7682 Clinton NJ 26ST0987 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275555 2026-05-20T15:28:35-04:00 2026-05-20T15:28:35-04:00 SEBS EOF Summer Session (Internal/External 5 Writing Instructors) <div>Rutgers School of Environmental and Biological Sciences (SEBS) Educational Opportunity (EOF) is seeking non-credit instructors to provide virtual and in-person instruction to students in the SEBS EOF Summer START-UP at Rutgers University. Dates include July 6th-July 10th (virtual instruction). July 13th-July 31st (in-person instruction). The candidate will teach Introductory to Expository Writing course, which is designed to introduce first year student writers to the elements of academic argument. Students learn to recognize the fundamental structure of academic argumentative writing as they learn to read and summarize academic essays, and then they apply the fundamental structure in academic essays of their own. Students will study and practice the skills necessary to successfully transition to the Fall semester. The course is organized around two major writing assignments. The course guides students’ practice through pre-writing, drafting, and revising, and includes discussions, workshops, and tutorials with the instructor. Be available to students via email, phone and/or by virtual conference during the first week of the program. After the first orientation week all instruction will occur in person on the Livingston Campus, Piscataway, NJ.</div> EOF New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 7148 26FA0344 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266339 2025-12-31T09:51:30-05:00 2025-12-31T09:51:30-05:00 Assistant/Associate/Full Teaching Professor <div>The Department seeks applications for two teaching positions at the level of Assistant Teaching Professor available beginning September 2026, subject to the availability of funding, with the possibility of appointment at a higher level for well-qualified candidates. These are renewable positions. The initial contract is normally one year, with renewal contracts typically for multi-year terms. Each position runs during the academic year, with a possibility of teaching during the summer for additional salary.<br><br></div><div>This position has a teaching load of 4-4 (four undergraduate mathematics courses in each of the fall and spring semesters), with possible teaching reductions for administrative, advising or other departmental duties. Applicants should have received a Ph.D. and show outstanding evidence of teaching at the undergraduate level. Ideally, candidates will have had at least three years teaching experience by the time the position starts.<br><br></div><div>The academic year salary for an assistant resp. associate resp. full teaching professor will not be less than $82,110 resp. $84,950 resp. $95,764, based on the most recent collective bargaining agreement between the faculty union (AAUP-AFT) and Rutgers University.<br><br>Applicants should complete the online form associated with this listing and submit a curriculum vitae. In addition, you should register as a job applicant at mathjobs.org <a href=\"https://nam02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.mathjobs.org%2Fjobs%2Flist%2F27669&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cmb1186%40math.rutgers.edu%7Cf828c38cad5a4ae57b9208de2b8c4af9%7Cb92d2b234d35447093ff69aca6632ffe%7C1%7C0%7C638996078723946866%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=seJt%2BvhO9i339RhneAqSFCDWBxlcCcxwpLSuC0mI95g%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/27669</strong></a> and complete the application, with the requested supporting documents, for position TF26 under the Rutgers University-New Brunswick listing.</div> Mathematics New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 8125 25FA1178 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280158 2026-08-31T08:45:40-04:00 2026-08-31T08:45:41-04:00 Staff Nurse Per Diem UCHC SWSP (multiple vacancies) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Per Diem Staff Nurse for the Southwoods State Prison located in Bridgeton, NJ.The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus for inmates in the New Jersey Department of Corrections.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br>* Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the resident-patient including adolescents (13-17 years), adults (18 to 64 years) and their family within the framework established by the correctional system.<br>* Performs assessments of resident-patient in a variety of settings such as initial intake area, health care unit for sick call, emergency situations in housing, chronic care clinics and infirmary.<br>* Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br>* Identifies inmate-centered goals and nursing objectives and implements prescribed interventions and solutions for the identified problems.<br>* Plans nursing care by identification of resident-patient needs based on assessments. Makes appropriate, timely referrals and initiates appropriate nursing care based on institutional policies and procedures.<br>* As team leader or charge nurse, delegates duties to other health care team members based on their skill, knowledge and experience and guides the provision of care by others.</div> UCHC South Woods Prison Nursin RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7699 Bridgeton NJ 26ST0541 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278579 2026-07-10T11:05:55-04:00 2026-07-10T11:05:56-04:00 Staff Nurse Per Diem UCHC BSP (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Per Diem Staff Nurse for the Bayside State Prison located in Leesburg, NJ<br><br>The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus for inmates in the New Jersey Department of Corrections.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br>* Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the resident-patient including adolescents (13-17 years), adults (18 to 64 years) and their family within the framework established by the correctional system.<br>* Performs assessments of resident-patient in a variety of settings such as initial intake area, health care unit for sick call, emergency situations in housing, chronic care clinics and infirmary.<br>* Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br>* Identifies inmate-centered goals and nursing objectives and implements prescribed interventions and solutions for the identified problems.<br>* Plans nursing care by identification of resident-patient needs based on assessments. Makes appropriate, timely referrals and initiates appropriate nursing care based on institutional policies and procedures.<br>* As team leader or charge nurse, delegates duties to other health care team members based on their skill, knowledge and experience and guides the provision of care by others</div> UCHC Bayside State Prison Nurs RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7698 Leesburg NJ 26ST0659 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/265897 2025-12-31T08:57:28-05:00 2025-12-31T08:57:29-05:00 Clinical Assistant/ Clinical Associate Professor/ Clinical Professor <div>The Department of Endodontics is searching for a part time faculty at the Clinical Assistant Professor, Clinical Associate Professor or Clinical Professor level. The position would involve clinical teaching of DMD candidates as well as participation in the DMD and Post-doctoral didactic curricula offered by the department. Faculty who have achieved ABE Diplomate status are also eligible to be a clinical attending in the post-graduate clinic. Eligible candidates must have a certificate of completion from a CODA accredited Advanced Education Program in Endodontic. Faculty will be expected to participate in scholarly activities and will have the opportunity to participate in the intramural faculty practice. The position will remain open until filled. Salary and rank will be commensurate with experience and training.<br><br></div> RSDM - Endodontics RBHS Chancellor-L2 Rutgers School of Dental Medic-L3 7545 24FA0045 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279658 2026-08-17T16:07:30-04:00 2026-08-17T16:07:31-04:00 Classroom Assistant II <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Classroom Assistant for the Douglass Developmental Disabilities Center.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Assists the certified special education teacher in providing educational and behavioral programming for students with developmental disabilities at the Douglass Developmental Disabilities Center – School Program.</li><li>Supports classrooms of students with severe behavior challenges; a greater percentage of work time will be spent implementing crisis management techniques including defensive techniques in response to punches, kicks, etc. and will require the use physical restraint.</li><li>Assists in providing educational and/or behavioral programs for pre-kindergarten through 12th grade students, some or all who may have special needs or assists in providing educational and/or behavioral programs for adults with special needs.</li></ul> Douglass Developmnt Disab Cntr New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Graduate School of Applied & P-L3 6829 New Brunswick NJ 26ST0747 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279969 2026-08-25T15:00:17-04:00 2026-08-25T15:00:17-04:00 Research Assistant Professor of Surgery <div>Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School (RWJMS) in New Brunswick, NJ is seeking a full-time Research Assistant Professor of Surgery. The Research Assistant Professor will conduct research activities that support the strategic priorities of the Department of Surgery, contribute to the growth of departmental research programs, collaborate effectively within multidisciplinary teams, and maintain strong communication with faculty, staff, trainees, and administrative leadership. The successful candidate is expected to possess the expertise, technical skills, and scholarly experience necessary to make immediate contributions to their assigned research program with minimal additional training.<br><br></div><div>Candidates should demonstrate a strong record of research productivity and a commitment to advancing the academic mission of the Department of Surgery through innovative and collaborative research.</div><div><br>Appointment to the Research Track is contingent upon the availability of funding from grants, contracts, and other approved sources. Continued appointment is dependent upon sustained funding and satisfactory performance in research-related activities.</div> RWJ - Surgery Vascular RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7844 26FA0687 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277766 2026-06-25T11:10:11-04:00 2026-06-25T11:10:12-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse PT Nights UCHC NSP <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Part Time Licensed Practical Nurse for Northern State Prison located in Newark, NJ<br><br>The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br>* Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs.<br>* Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.<br>* Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.<br>* Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.<br>* Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.<br>* Documents all aspects of patient care.</div> UCHC Northern State Prison Phy_DUP RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7679 Newark NJ 26ST0681 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275343 2026-05-19T08:27:39-04:00 2026-05-19T08:27:40-04:00 Genomic Instability and Cancer Genetics – Tenure Track (Assistant/Associate) <div>The <a href=\"https://cinj.org/research/genomic-instability-and-cancer-genetics-research-program\"><strong>Genomic Instability and Cancer Genetics (GICG) Research Program</strong></a> at Rutgers Cancer Institute seeks outstanding investigators focused on the mechanisms of genomic instability, cancer genome evolution, and their translation into clinical applications. We invite applications for faculty positions at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. Appointments may be tenure track or tenured, depending on qualifications and experience.<br><br>The GICG program investigates how genomic instability arises, how defects in genome maintenance pathways drive tumor initiation and progression, how perturbations in these pathways influence tumor response to treatment. A key effort is on leveraging mechanism-based genomic and molecular markers to identify therapeutic vulnerabilities. Research areas span DNA repair and replication fidelity, chromosome segregation, cancer genome evolution, and gene expression and tissue homeostasis programs that shape tumor development and therapeutic response. Program investigators integrate mechanistic, computational, and translational approaches to define how genome instability drives cancer and to exploit these vulnerabilities for therapeutic intervention.<br><br>We seek candidates pursuing basic, translational, or preclinical research in cancer genetics and genomics using cutting edge approaches. Areas of particular interest include, but are not limited to, mechanisms of genomic instability and DNA repair dysfunction, therapeutic vulnerabilities associated with altered cancer genomes, molecular and cellular mechanisms of radiation and genotoxic response, co-adaptation between the tumor microenvironment and evolving cancer cells, and the genetics of cancer predisposition syndromes.<br><br>Successful candidates will establish or contribute to an innovative, independent, and collaborative research program addressing fundamental questions in cancer biology and genomic instability. Interdisciplinary and translational research approaches are strongly encouraged. Faculty will also have opportunities to participate in teaching activities for medical students and residents, including lectures and mentorship within their areas of expertise. Applicants should hold a PhD, MD, or MD/PhD in a relevant discipline and have completed postdoctoral or equivalent research training. Candidates should demonstrate a strong publication record in cancer genetics, genomics, or related fields and show clear potential to secure independent peer-reviewed funding. Competitive start-up packages, laboratory space, and institutional support are available for outstanding candidates.<br><br>Rutgers Cancer Institute is an NCI-designated, comprehensive and consortium cancer center that includes faculty members from across Rutgers University (including Rutgers Robert Wood Medical School, Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences) and Princeton University. We are a leader in basic, clinical, prevention, and public health science, offering world-class quality cancer care providing the most advanced medicines and treatment options for patients in our health system network across the state. Visit our website at www.cinj.org.</div> Cancer Institute of New Jersey RBHS Chancellor-L2 Cancer Institute of New Jersey-L3 7893 26FA0229 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266267 2025-12-31T09:42:24-05:00 2025-12-31T09:42:24-05:00 Postdoctoral Associate in Structural Biology and Biophysics <div>The Deaconescu Lab at Rutgers University has one opening for a postdoctoral researcher. The laboratory's interests lie primarily in microbial stress responses, with particular emphasis on responses to DNA damage, the mechanochemistry of DNA-based motors. We utilize a combination of biochemical, biophysical and structural techniques. (e.g. X-ray crystallography, small-angle X-ray scattering, transmission electron microscopy). For examples of work, please see Brugger et al. <em>JBC </em>(2023, 2024), Brugger et al. <em>Nature Communications </em>(2020), Dorich et al, <em>Genes Development </em>(2019), Vemu et al. <em>Science </em>(2018), Le TT et al. <em>Cell</em> (2018) etc. More information about the lab can be obtained at <a href=\"https://deaconesculab.com/\">https://deaconesculab.com</a></div> Quantitative Biomedicine Inst New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 6749 25FA0742 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280143 2026-08-31T00:00:58-04:00 2026-08-31T00:00:59-04:00 Edit/Media Assistant <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking an Edit/Media Assistant for Athletjcs.</div><div><br></div><div>Among the key duties of the position are the following:</div><ul><li>Manages student broadcast crew, providing professional training from basic to advanced TV production practices.</li><li>Assists in A/V engineering control room systems as well as manages camera systems for streaming and in-venue productions.</li><li>Works with partners at the Big Ten Network on logistics and scheduling for streaming events, press conferences, and other media requests as needed.</li></ul> Athl - R Vision Intercollegiate Athletics-L2 Athl - R Vision-L3 9119 Piscataway NJ 26ST1639 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278552 2026-07-10T09:05:52-04:00 2026-07-10T09:05:52-04:00 Client Coach (Temporary/Casual) Part time <div>Rutgers University–Camden is seeking Client Coaches for the School of Business Small Business Development Center (RSBDC) to support the growth and success of small businesses throughout the region. This role focuses on providing high-quality advising, training, and outreach services while contributing to the Center’s broader mission, partnerships, and performance goals.<br><br>Job Duties include:</div><ul><li>Utilizing critical thinking and analytical expertise to create customized strategies tailored to each small business client’s specific needs through individualized one-on-one counseling</li><li>Developing and delivering group training sessions and webinars to disseminate knowledge and resources, depending on area(s) of specialty</li><li>Collaborating closely with other NJSBDC counselors to provide comprehensive client support</li><li>Staying informed on emerging trends, regulatory changes, and industry best practices relevant to the assigned specialty area</li><li>Delivering on assigned metrics for federal and state requirements</li><li>Engaging in activities that facilitate cross-functional coordination, stakeholder communication, and the ongoing alignment of programmatic efforts with strategic objectives</li><li>Maintaining and creating new productive working relationships with key statewide small business stakeholders</li><li>Tracking and reporting on outreach and consulting activities, ensuring compliance with organizational guidelines</li><li>Building and maintaining strong client relationships, fostering collaboration and trust throughout the consulting process</li></ul><div><br>*This is a grant funded position contingent upon the availability of continued funding.</div> Small Business Devt Ctr - Cmd Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 School of Business Camden-L3 6666 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267880 2026-01-23T11:56:21-05:00 2026-01-23T11:56:22-05:00 Part Time Course Support (Project Mentor) - Summer 2026 <div>The Professional Science Master’s Program (PSM) invites applications for part time Course Assistants (Project Mentors) for the Summer 2026 term. We seek qualified instructors who can contribute to the university’s educational mission and bridge the gap between the classroom and the industry.<br><br>Course Support (Project Mentor) Responsibilities:</div><ul><li>Assisting faculty with evaluating student progress and performance. Provide constructive feedback on their work, presentations, or prototypes. Help assess the achievement of learning objectives and provide suggestions for improvement.</li><li>Monitors the progress of student projects, ensuring they stay on track and meet established timelines.</li><li>Provides guidance and support to students, collaborates with instructors to ensure students complete their projects successfully.</li><li>Foster effective communication and collaboration among students and between students and instructors. Facilitate group discussions, encourage knowledge sharing, and help resolve conflicts or issues that may arise during the project.</li><li>Assist in coordinating resources needed for student projects, such as equipment, software, or materials. Collaborate with instructors to ensure students have complete their projects successfully.</li><li>Stay informed about the course content, objectives, and expectations to effectively support students.</li></ul> Professional Science Masters New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Professional Science Masters-L3 6665 26FA0060 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280294 2026-09-01T14:46:04-04:00 2026-09-01T14:46:04-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Post-Doctoral Associate in the Department of Obstetrics, Gynecology &amp; Reproductive Health within the New Jersey Medical School (NJMS).<br><br>To evaluate the genomic stability of oocytes and somatic cells exposed to CK2II in combination with cyclophosphamide. This study will perform a comprehensive assessment of DNA damage, including mutation rates, DNA methylation patterns, and histone modifications, to determine the safety of CK2II as a potential fertility preservation agent. De novo mutations will be analyzed in both oocytes and somatic cells, while genome-wide DNA methylation and histone modification profiles will be examined to assess epigenetic integrity.&nbsp;</div><div><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Maintain and manage mouse colonies, including breeding, tissue collection, and record-keeping.</li><li>Perform whole-genome sequencing (WGS) and validation analyses.</li><li>Conduct genome-wide DNA methylation profiling.</li><li>Isolate RNA from oocytes and somatic cells.</li><li>Conduct tissue sectioning (cryostat and paraffin embedding) and histological staining.</li><li>Perform organ culture experiments, including in vitro ovarian culture.</li></ul> NJMS - Obstetrics & Gynocology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7455 Newark NJ 26ST1707 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278993 2026-07-21T09:04:13-04:00 2026-07-21T09:04:14-04:00 Regional Scheduler UCHC BSP <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care (UCHC) is seeking a Regional Scheduler to work at Bayside State Prison, located in Leesburg, New Jersey. Under the guidance of the Administrator, the Regional Scheduler processes all consultation requests and related documentation for the facility. The position will interface with the Statewide Ombudsperson on concerns elevated to a state level.<br><br>Among the key duties for this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Processes all consultation request forms and related paperwork for the facilities, including but not limited to:<br>&nbsp;<ul><li>Entries of consultation requests into the Inmate Eligibility System.</li></ul></li><li>&nbsp;<ul><li>All scheduling functions for the consultation request including those for on-site clinic appointments and for off-site appointments.</li></ul></li><li>&nbsp;<ul><li>Arranges the appropriate transportation of patients for appointments.</li></ul></li><li>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;</li><li>Reviews and investigates inmate grievances related to healthcare, through medical record review and personal interviews with inmates and staff. Finalizes investigation with a written report to be distributed according to policy and procedure.</li><li>Performs other related duties as assigned</li></ul> UCHC Bayside State Prison Anci RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7684 Leesburg NJ 26ST1548 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/271782 2026-03-26T15:07:47-04:00 2026-03-26T15:07:48-04:00 Psychology Lecturer - Summer 2026 <div>The Department of Psychology at Rutgers University invites qualified applicants to serve as Summer Session Instructors for Psychology course offerings. Instructors will teach one or more full undergraduate courses during the Summer Session, which consists of two sessions scheduled between late May and mid-August. Responsibilities include preparing and submitting course syllabi, delivering high‑quality instruction, assessing student work in a timely manner, holding weekly office hours, responding to student emails, submitting final course grades to the registrar, and adhering to all university policies, grade submission procedures, and deadlines. This position reports to the Department Undergraduate Director.</div><div><br></div> Psychology New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 8128 26FA0283 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279519 2026-08-11T17:24:04-04:00 2026-08-11T17:24:06-04:00 Program Director <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Program Director for the Behavioral Research &amp; Training Institute (BRTI) within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Program Director is to provide administrative direction and oversight to assigned programs with multiple projects, assure program integrity and fiscal viability. Responsible for ongoing program development and compliance with regulatory requirements.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Directs the administrative and clinical organization of the programs.</li><li>Establishes clear, measurable objectives for services.</li><li>Ensures that programs meet or exceed objectives.</li><li>Plans, trains and supervises the work of others engaged in program supervision and/or the provision of training and consultation services.</li><li>Collaborates effectively with internal and external service providers, staff members, referral sources and program funders.</li><li>Maintains knowledge of trends and development in the mental health field; regularly attends and participates in in- service meetings and other designated training events that will enhance clinical skills and maintain best practices.</li><li>Effectively contributes to and supports an environment that respects and enhances the individual, their expressed choices, and preferences, and that enhances the positive self-image of all individuals receiving services in his/her oversight.</li></ul> UBHC - BRTI Institute RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8044 Piscataway NJ 26ST1605 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279763 2026-08-20T09:15:44-04:00 2026-08-20T09:15:45-04:00 Health Care Case Manager (Registered Nurse) Camden South-Cherry Hill, NJ <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Health Care Case Manager for the Camden South office for the Child Health Program within the School of Nursing. The Heath Care Case Manager (HCCM) functions to support the Department of Children and Families (DCF)/Child Protection and Permanency (CP&amp;P) in meeting the health care and protection needs of children in out-of-home placement, in collaboration with other staff of the Child Health Unit in that local office.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Upon entry into out-of-home placement, assists with enrollment of a child in a managed care entity and identification of a medical home (primary care provider), and informs the child, caregiver and DCF/CP&amp;P, as needed.</li><li>Assesses a child’s heath care status and needs by retrieving a complete health history through obtaining and reviewing all medical records and interviewing past providers and caregivers; forwards all information to the medical home and other health providers as needed.</li><li>Schedules an Initial Physical Health Evaluation, in consultation with the caregiver and DCF/CP&amp;P, reviews the preliminary and final reports, and ensures that all recommendations for health care are completed.</li><li>Develops a child health care plan in collaboration with the child’s medical home, as well as involved specialists, caregivers, other community service providers, and when appropriate, DCF/CP&amp;P.</li><li>Links the child and caregiver with appropriate health resources and community services.</li><li>Assures that the child is scheduled for and attends timely EPSDT visits and specialty appointments, reviews all reports, and ensures all necessary reports are forwarded to the medical home.</li></ul> Francois-Xavier Bagnoud Center (FXB) Ce RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Nursing Dean's Offic-L3 7618 Cherry Hill NJ 26ST0362 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277210 2026-06-16T11:43:13-04:00 2026-06-16T11:43:13-04:00 Lecturer Fall 2026 <div>&nbsp; The Department of Biomedical Engineering is seeking lecturers for the New Brunswick/Piscataway Campus for Fall 2026. We invite applicants with expertise in one or more of the following areas: data science in healthcare, Tissue Engineering, Biomedical Systems and Devices, and other topics in the Rutgers Biomedical Engineering undergraduate and graduate curricula. &nbsp;</div><div><br><br></div> Biomedical Engineering New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Engineering-L3 7102 26FA0586 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274106 2026-05-01T08:26:32-04:00 2026-05-01T08:26:33-04:00 Lecturers, Political Science <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the Faculty of Arts &amp; Sciences, Department of Political Science, seeks new lecturers to teach in various topics within the discipline for courses in Fall 2026, Winter 2027, Spring 2027 and/or Summer 2027. The instructor will present course material during the assigned course times, hold office hours, administer exams, assign grades, and coordinate any other requirements related to the course instruction.</div> Political Science Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 6770 26FA0432 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266063 2025-12-31T09:24:09-05:00 2025-12-31T09:24:09-05:00 Open Rank (Multiple Positions) Otolaryngology- Pediatric Otolaryngologist <div>Rutgers New Jersey Medical School, Department of Otolaryngology-Head and Neck Surgery is recruiting a Pediatric Otolaryngologist to join our expanding faculty.<br><br></div><div>Experience in Clinical Outcomes Research is desired. The successful applicant will join a very busy Pediatric and Adult practice, provide care for complex pathology, and join a quickly growing clinical and research enterprise. The Department collaborates with an extensive array of health care providers across the Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences units.<br><br></div><div>Applicants for this position must be able to perform at a high level both clinically and academically. Salary will be commensurate with ability, training, and experience and demonstrated prior performance.<br><br></div> NJMS - Otolaryngology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7505 22FA1131 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280054 2026-08-26T15:53:49-04:00 2026-08-26T15:53:50-04:00 Psychologist (Permit) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Psychologist (permit) for the Behavioral Research and Training Institute (BRIT) Institute within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Psychologist positionisto provide therapeutic interventions for the psychological and social needs of individuals served. Supports the integration of evidence-based practices and provide therapeutic interventions based upon the principles of wellness and recovery.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Provides person centered direct care services to individuals with Best Practices Interventions.</li><li>As required by the program, administers high level,specialized, diagnostic psychological testing, evaluations and/or written comprehensive assessment reports as clinically indicated in a timely fashion.</li><li>Consistently involves the individual served and/or family members in the assessment and development of treatment plans and treatment plan reviews.</li><li>Effectively collaborates as clinically indicatedwith other staff members,referral sources, community resources,service providers, case management organizations,families and support systems.</li><li>Effectively contributes to and supports an environment that enhances the positive self-image of individuals served and preserves their human dignity.</li><li>Formulates assessments, treatment plans, treatment plan reviews, progress notes, and termination/discharge summaries.</li></ul> UBHC - BRTI Institute RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8044 Piscataway NJ 26ST1668 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278236 2026-07-06T09:23:37-04:00 2026-07-06T09:23:38-04:00 Student Assistant (Research) <div>Rutgers School of Public Health (SPH) is seeking a Student Assistant for the Department of Urban Global Public Health, located in Newark, NJ<br><br>The Student Assistant will work under the supervision of the Associate Dean for Community Engagement, Population Health, and Public Health Service. The Student Assistant will assist the Associate Dean with research projects addressing the mechanisms through which historically and contemporary under resourced populations experience health inequities; engaging in theoretically driven research that seeks to disentangle the effects of different social determinants of health on the outcomes of these populations.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Assist with data management, data analysis, and creation of tables and figures.</li><li>Assist with the editing and preparation of manuscripts, publications, reports and presentations.</li><li>Conduct literature reviews and summarize research findings as requested</li></ul> SPH - Urban & Global Public Health RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Public Health-L3 7709 Newark NJ 25ST2529 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266404 2026-01-04T21:32:36-05:00 2026-01-04T21:32:36-05:00 Post Doctoral Associate <div>&nbsp;The Eastern Pacific Cloud, Aerosol, and Precipitation Experiment (EPCAPE) was designed to investigate Aerosol-Cloud Interactions and cloud brightening in California marine stratocumulus. The EPCAPE was conducted in La Jolla, California where the Atmospheric Radiation Measurement (ARM) Mobile Facility #1 (AMF1) was deployed on the Scripps Pier, which juts several hundred feet into the Pacific Ocean. A second site, Mt. Soledad, was located 3-km inland from the Scripps Pier at an elevation of 250-m and housed Scanning Cloud Radars (SACRs) and a subset of the AMF remote sensors, including a Doppler Lidar, alongside a full suite of in-situ aerosol and cloud analysis instrumentation. A central theme of EPCAPE is the characterization of aerosols and cloud droplet distributions in marine clouds of differing background aerosol composition and to relate these distributions to in-cloud turbulence and cloud brightening. The Doppler lidars at the pier and on Mt. Soledad characterized sub cloud TKE profiles with 2-s resolution and provided a first-line assessment of the integrated turbulence in the sub cloud layer and the distribution of vertical velocities adjacent cloud base. These measurements complement detail aerosol and microphysical assays at Mt. Soledad, henceforth providing a laboratory to investigate aerosol-cloud interactions and their relationship with in-cloud turbulence in unprecedented detail.&nbsp;<br><br>&nbsp;A Post-Doctoral Researcher is sought to assist in all phases of EPCAPE-related research conducted as part of a successful, joint proposal between Rutgers University and the Scripps Institute of Oceanography, and may also contribute to a separate project funded by the National Science Foundation that involves process mechanics in marine boundary layer clouds. The successful applicant must possess a Ph.D. in Atmospheric Science with demonstrated expertise in marine boundary layer cloud microphysics, specifically cloud droplet nucleation processes, aerosol measurement and characterization techniques and remote sensing using active sensors. The successful candidate must have a record of publication that demonstrates a process-level understanding of the forces that shape marine cloud microphysics. An intimate knowledge of marine boundary layer thermodynamics, including decoupling, and the scale and nature of mesoscale circulations, is helpful. This Post-Doctoral Researcher is expected to work effectively in a team and have a demonstrated record of public presentations at research conferences commensurate with a highly energetic research enterprise. Experience using MATLAB or Python scripting languages is a requirement.&nbsp;</div> Environmental Science New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 7137 25FA0919 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280190 2026-08-31T10:50:00-04:00 2026-08-31T10:50:01-04:00 Open Rank Non-Tenure Track Faculty Position <div>The Rutgers Institute for Nicotine &amp; Tobacco Studies (INTS), in partnership with the Rutgers School of Nursing, invites applications for one or more Assistant Professor, Research Track (non-tenure track) positions. The Institute is one of the nation’s leading tobacco focused research centers and its faculty have received over $75 million in extramural funding over the past two decades. As one of the nation’s largest, most comprehensive nursing schools, the Rutgers School of Nursing is dedicated to the pursuit of excellence in education, evidence-based research and health care delivery, and promotion of community health and is ranked among the nation’s top 15 Nursing Schools in US News and World Report.<br><br></div><div>This position is designed for early-career investigators and will primarily support ongoing funded research projects within a highly collaborative environment. Faculty will work closely with established investigators to advance the Institute’s research portfolio, contributing to activities such as data analysis, manuscript preparation, and study coordination. Candidates are expected to contribute immediately to funded projects and collaborate effectively with multidisciplinary teams across Rutgers Health.<br><br></div><div>Research-track faculty may also pursue the development of an independent line of research and will have opportunities to contribute to or lead external grant applications, including as Principal Investigator, as appropriate.<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate will hold a <strong>joint appointment</strong> with INTS and the Rutgers School of Nursing. The Institute provides office space, research infrastructure, and access to resources to support scholarly productivity and career development.<br><br></div><div>This <strong>non-tenure track position is contingent upon the availability of funding</strong>. While this position’s primary responsibility is in conducting research (80-90% effort) to grow and sustain extramurally funded research, a small allocation of effort towards teaching at the School of Nursing (10-20%) is possible.</div> Nicotine & Tobacco Institute RBHS Chancellor-L2 Nicotine & Tobacco Institute-L3 8529 26FA0739 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278633 2026-07-10T14:06:37-04:00 2026-07-10T14:06:38-04:00 Mental Health Specialist III - Part Time <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a part-time Mental Health Specialist III for the Adult Partial Hospital within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Mental Health Specialist III is to provide daily direct care services to the program’s consumers as directed by the unit supervisor in accordance with all regulatory requirements and principles of Wellness and Recovery.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Counsels consumers which may include family members with empathy, respect and concern.</li><li>Responds with sensitivity to spiritual, cultural, and socioeconomic issues of consumer.</li><li>Provides services and interventions that promote consumer strengths, develops the independence and sense of autonomy of all consumers.</li><li>Meets with consumers as assigned to provide case management services which support the treatment team recommendations.</li><li>Completes progress notes as per regulatory requirement and supervisory directive.</li><li>Completes all forms, incident reports, and correspondence as per regulatory requirement.</li><li>Participates in and/or leads therapeutic groups and activities and functions as an active member of the team.</li><li>Effectively contributes to and supports an environment that enhances the positive self image of consumer and preserves their human dignity.</li></ul> UBHC - PH Adult Newark RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8056 Newark NJ 26ST1506 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/269366 2026-02-17T14:00:48-05:00 2026-02-17T14:00:48-05:00 Assistant /Associate Professor Movement Disorder <div><strong><em>FUNCTION:</em></strong></div><div>Participate in clinical care of patients with neurological disorders under the administrative structure of the Robert Wood Johnson University Medical Group according to a schedule determined by the Chair. The principal activity will be care of outpatients with movement disorders.</div><div><strong><em>ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES.</em></strong></div><div><br></div><div>The faculty member will:</div><ol><li>Be Board-certified or -eligible in neurology; have completed a fellowship in movement disorders: and be eligible for a New Jersey license.</li><li>Maintain a practice in the full range of adult movement disorders neurology. To maintain a full schedule while building a referral network, the faculty member may be required to see some patients with neurological conditions other than movement disorders.</li><li>Have skills in botulinum treatment for movement disorders and include such patients in the practice.</li><li>Have skills in evaluation and medical management of patients who are candidates for deep brain stimulation and ablative surgery for movement disorders, and in their postoperative management and stimulator programming. Must coordinate care with neurosurgery, psychiatry and other disciplines as needed.</li><li>Perform night call and weekend inpatient coverage at Barnabas-Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital in equal proportion with the other faculty in rotation.</li><li>Participate in the teaching mission of RWJMS to the extent determined in consultation with the Department Chair. This may include teaching and mentoring medical students, neurology residents, movement disorder fellows and rotators from other departments. The teaching will take place in inpatient and outpatient settings and in seminars and occasional formal lectures in the pre-clinical setting. It may also include supervising a weekly resident Continuity Clinic.</li><li>Participate as site principal investigator or sub-investigator in clinical trials sponsored by industry and other sources.</li><li>Perform and publish other research to the extent consistent with the track of the appointment (Professional Practice, Clinical Educator or Clinical Scholar).</li><li>Refer patients as appropriate to clinical trials and other research activity in the department and otherwise participate in the scholarly productivity and culture of the department.</li><li>Participate in community service responsibilities of the department in such areas as providing neurological care for indigent patients and teaching or advising lay community groups in multiple areas relating to movement disorders, including deep brain stimulation, in coordination with the Department of Neurosurgery.</li><li>Participate in the administrative tasks of the department and medical school. This will include membership in standing or ad hoc departmental and institutional committees as determined in consultation with the Chair and according to RWJMS By-Laws; and attending departmental and institutional faculty meetings.</li><li>Maintain knowledge through continuing education and by maintaining Board certification in neurology and any relevant subspecialty certification.</li></ol> RWJ - Neurology RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7784 26FA0124 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280445 2026-09-04T10:36:05-04:00 2026-09-04T10:36:05-04:00 Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Professor Adolescent Medicine <div><br>The Department of Pediatrics at Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School is seeking a candidate for a faculty position in the Adolescent Medicine Section, Division of Population Health, Quality, and Implementation Sciences. Clinical responsibilities include both outpatient clinics and inpatient consultation. The candidate will assume responsibilities as the Director of the Adolescent Medicine Section, with the potential to grow the Adolescent Medicine enterprise in the Department of Pediatrics. Opportunities for growth include the clinical practice, including at an off-site primary care center, the development of a research enterprise, and building upon existing medical student, resident, and fellow education. The Section is responsible for the required Adolescent Medicine rotation for residents and actively participates in medical student teaching. The ideal candidate will have (or be developing) a track record in health services, translational, clinical research, and/or educational research. Candidates must be a graduate of an accredited medical school and a graduate of a fellowship program in Adolescent Medicine. Board certification in Pediatrics with eligibility for or certification in Adolescent Medicine is required.</div><div>The Division of Population Health, Quality, and Implementation Sciences (PopQuIS in Pediatrics) is an innovative national leader in integrating primary care pediatrics with other whole child specialties such as Adolescent Medicine to develop a transdisciplinary community of scholarship regarding health and health care for children in the context of their communities. The Division leverages the common interests across specialties to enhance research and education while supporting world class clinical care.</div><div>The Department of Pediatrics has a full complement of pediatric medical and surgical subspecialists, and outpatient services are provided at the Child Health Institute of New Jersey which also houses our research faculty. The Department of Pediatrics includes physicians and basic scientists who conduct collaborative research with an emphasis on mechanisms of disease, novel therapies, epidemiology and/or outcomes research in the areas of relevance to childhood diseases. The Department provides a collaborative setting for the study of basic mechanisms of disease, educational scholarship, and clinical, translational and health services research to provide new insights to the mechanisms and treatment of childhood diseases. The Robert Wood Johnson School of Medicine is consistently ranked as one of the highly NIH-funded academic universities and Rutgers both brings the excitement and energy of a Big 10 University and is a member of the Association of American Universities comprising the top comprehensive research universities in North America. Adjacent to the Children’s hospital is the PSE&amp;G Children’s Specialized Hospital which is one of the country’s largest inpatient acute rehabilitation hospitals for children. Across the street is the Rutgers Cancer Institute of New Jersey – the only NCI designated center in the state of New Jersey as well as the Ronald MacDonald House. As the state’s premiere institution, located in central Jersey, there are many opportunities to collaborate across campuses with all the health professional schools and biomedical science schools at the Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences.</div><div><br>Interested candidates should email a cover letter and your CV via email to:<br><br></div><div>Lawrence C. Kleinman, MD, PPH, FAAP</div><div>Director, Division of Population Health, Quality, and Implementation Sciences (PopQuIS)</div><div>Vice Chair for Academic Development</div><div>c/o Department of Pediatrics</div><div>Robert Wood Johnson Medical School</div><div>125 Paterson Street</div><div>Clinical Academic Building, Rm 7106</div><div>New Brunswick, NJ 08901</div><div>Email: Larry.Kleinman@Rutgers.edu</div><div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, age, or any other category covered by law in its admission, programs, activities, or employment matters.</div> RWJ - Pediatrics Adolescent Me RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7818 26FA0748 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279363 2026-08-06T12:13:34-04:00 2026-08-06T12:13:35-04:00 Regional Operations Manager UCHC SWSP & BSP <div>Rutgers University Correctional Healthcare (UCHC) is seeking a Regional Operations Manager for its location in Bridgeton, NJ. Under the direction of the Director of Operations and Accreditation, the Regional Operations Manager will implement procedures and workflows to ensure the efficient delivery of logistical and administrative services for UCHC within the DOC facilities; Supervise UCHC staff as assigned. and performs highly skilled administrative tasks to include training, staff oversight and technical assistance.<br><br>Duties will include:</div><ul><li>Supervise the facility operational plan.<ul><li>Proactively identifies and implements operational enhancements to ensure that operational processes are best suited to the facility patient population, as both patient and DOC needs evolve.</li><li>Generates data reports as assigned.</li><li>Procures and distributes supplies related to operational processes.</li><li>Ensures facility operations are adhering to the National Commission on Correctional Healthcare guidelines, when applicable.</li><li>Works collaboratively with the Quality Improvement/Performance Improvement Team to identify areas for improvement and implement interventions for improvement.</li><li>Will be responsible for participating, as appropriate, in the ongoing, systematic and objective performance measurement and assessment of important key functions and processes.</li><li>Local Performance Improvement activities must be reported at least annually to the Quality Improvement Department.</li></ul></li><li>Collaborate effectively with DOC Administration.<ul><li>Works collaboratively with the DOC facility administrative team(s) to ensure that patient care needs are met and serves as UCHC operational leadership by implementing processes and systems to support facility.</li><li>Partners effectively with DOC within respective facility to ensure patient needs are communicated clearly and concisely.</li><li>Works collaboratively with the DOC facility administrative team(s) to identify and address existing or potential barriers to care and represents UCHC favorably in all interactions.</li></ul></li><li>Manage UCHC administrative workflow effectively.<ul><li>Provides leadership and guidance to assigned staff.</li><li>Hires, supervises, trains, manages, and terminates administrative staff under their supervision.</li><li>Communicates to staff, in a timely manner, appropriate information obtained from meetings and conferences to enhance productivity of facility operations.</li><li>Conducts meetings relevant to job responsibilities to ensure that facility needs are met.</li><li>Ensures annual performance evaluations are conducted and completed with all administrative staff.</li></ul></li></ul> UCHC-South Woods Psn-Ancillary RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7685 Bridgeton NJ 26ST0877 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/276082 2026-05-29T09:52:30-04:00 2026-05-29T09:52:31-04:00 MGSA – Department of Arts Online – (Fall 2026) <div>The Division of Rutgers Arts Online, Mason Gross School of the Arts, Rutgers University invites applications for part-time instructional and academic support for undergraduate courses in Art &amp; Design Online, Dance Online, Music Online, Filmmaking Online, Theater Online and Interdisciplinary.</div> Rutgers Arts Online New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Mason Gross School of Arts Dea-L3 8712 26FA0448 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/273435 2026-04-21T14:08:49-04:00 2026-04-21T14:08:49-04:00 Assistant/Associate Professor or Professor <div>The Department of Endodontics is searching for an Endodontist for a faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor. Responsibilities will involve but are not limited to oversight of endodontic patient care in pre-doctoral clinics: lecturing in pre-doctoral endodontic courses; and participation in postgraduate endodontic seminars and mentoring postgraduate research.</div> RSDM - Endodontics RBHS Chancellor-L2 Rutgers School of Dental Medic-L3 7545 26FA0346 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280160 2026-08-31T08:47:19-04:00 2026-08-31T08:47:20-04:00 Staff Nurse FT Eves UCHC SWSP Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Full Time Staff Nurse for the Southwoods State Prison located in Bridgeton, NJ<br><br>The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus for inmates in the New Jersey Department of Corrections.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br>* Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the resident-patient including adolescents (13-17 years), adults (18 to 64 years) and their family within the framework established by the correctional system.<br>* Performs assessments of resident-patient in a variety of settings such as initial intake area, health care unit for sick call, emergency situations in housing, chronic care clinics and infirmary.<br>* Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br>* Identifies inmate-centered goals and nursing objectives and implements prescribed interventions and solutions for the identified problems.<br>* Plans nursing care by identification of resident-patient needs based on assessments. Makes appropriate, timely referrals and initiates appropriate nursing care based on institutional policies and procedures.<br>* As team leader or charge nurse, delegates duties to other health care team members based on their skill, knowledge and experience and guides the provision of care by others.</div> UCHC-South Woods Psn-Ancillary RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7685 Bridgeton NJ 26ST0545 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278581 2026-07-10T11:09:07-04:00 2026-07-10T11:09:08-04:00 Technician I Per Diem UCHC EJSP (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Per Diem UCHC Technician I for the East Jersey State Prison, located in Rahway, NJ. The UCHC Technician I participates as a member of the clinical and administrative medical team at the Prison.<br><br>Among the duties for this position are:<br><br></div><ul><li>Takes vital signs, height and weight and documents in electronic medical records (EMR).</li><li>Assists the physician/associate practitioner with procedures, including preparing the inmate for the examination.</li><li>Obtains specimen collection and handling, including, but not limited to, drawing blood.</li><li>Assists with the cleaning, sterilization and securing of equipment within the Health Service Unit.</li><li>Maintains or assists in maintaining the supply stock in the Health Service Unit by ordering in a timely and appropriate manner. Maintains the supply stock in the examination rooms.• Aggregates the orders of all medications and forwards to the pharmacy provider / local pharmacy.</li></ul> UCHC East Jersey State Prison_DUP_2 RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7691 Rahway NJ 26ST0869 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/268720 2026-02-06T08:33:46-05:00 2026-02-06T08:33:46-05:00 Clinical Assistant Professor/Ambulatory Care/Psych <div><br>The Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy at Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track faculty position. The faculty member will hold a clinical appointment in Inpatient Behavioral Health at Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital Somerset. The pharmacy school is recognized at all levels—local, state, national, and international—as offering one of the most challenging, dynamic, and rewarding programs leading to the Doctor of Pharmacy degree. Alongside supportive faculty and staff, students at the school develop a foundation for learning that lasts well beyond graduation.</div><div><br>The Department of Pharmacy Practice and Administration emphasizes the clinical and regulatory aspects of pharmacy practice. Its mission is to prepare students to deliver pharmaceutical care in various practice settings. Graduates are equipped with the skills needed to adapt to a constantly evolving healthcare environment. Students also gain a solid foundation in scientific principles, ethics, and attitudes necessary for lifelong adaptation to changes in healthcare. This mission supports the overall goals of the Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy in four key areas: teaching, practice, scholarship, and service.</div><div><br>Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital Somerset (RWJUH Somerset) is a 343-bed community hospital in Somerville, NJ, serving as a teaching site for Rutgers University and hosting the Somerset Family Medicine Residency Program. It has earned national recognition for clinical quality and safety, including the Magnet® Award for Nursing Excellence and an “A” Hospital Safety Grade from Leapfrog. In 2025, it was named one of America’s 250 Best Hospitals by Healthgrades, ranking in the top 5% nationally. RWJUH Somerset was also recognized as a “Leader in LGBT Health Care Equality” by the Human Rights Campaign, becoming the first NJ hospital to provide primary care for the LGBTQIA+ community. The hospital remains committed to delivering high-quality care, continuously adopting the latest evidence and technology. This inpatient psychiatry unit (5W) has 27 beds and serves both voluntary and involuntary psychiatric patients. Care includes daily multidisciplinary rounds for every patient and daily therapeutic group sessions. Once stabilized, patients are transferred from 5W to the onsite partial hospitalization program and clinic for ongoing care. Additionally, the outpatient eating disorder unit has 20 beds, with daily psychiatry rounds and group sessions. While the position focuses on inpatient care, there is room for growth to support other psychiatry services.</div><div><br>The Behavioral Health clinical pharmacist faculty member will collaborate with pharmacists, nurses, and medical staff to optimize patient care in our Behavioral Health program across inpatient, emergency department, and ambulatory (outpatient offices/clinics) settings, with a primary focus on inpatient care. The faculty member will organize, develop, and participate in clinical and quality improvement activities. Clinical activities include, but are not limited to the following: practice under collaborative practice agreement to optimize inpatient and outpatient pharmacotherapy, participation in quality initiatives to reduce readmissions, enhance medication access, participation in multidisciplinary rounds, provide interprofessional education, collaboration on policy and procedure development, committee participation, perform research and medication use evaluations, conduct dosing consults, support Medication Assistance Treatment initiatives, provide community outreach support, and precept Advanced Pharmacy Practice Experiential students and Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital Somerset Post-graduate year 1 pharmacy practice residents on their psychiatry rotation.</div><div><br>Applicants must have a Doctor of Pharmacy degree and have completed at least two years of residency training with a PGY-2 in psychiatry/Behavioral Health or equivalent experience. Candidates must be highly motivated, innovative, and team-oriented and possess excellent communication and interpersonal skills to provide patient-centered care with a commitment to teaching, service, and professional advancement. Board certification is preferred. Eligibility for licensure as a pharmacist in the State of New Jersey is required.</div> Pharmacy Practice & Administra RBHS Chancellor-L2 Ernest Mario School of Pharmac-L3 6720 26FA0114 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280380 2026-09-03T10:53:47-04:00 2026-09-03T10:53:48-04:00 Supervising Habilitation Counselor - IFSS Middlesex <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Supervising Habilitation Counselor - IFSS Middlesex for the Community Based Service within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.&nbsp;<br><br>The primary purpose of the Supervising Habilitation Counselor position is to provide administrative and clinical supervision to the identified program staff and direct services and supports to individuals and families served.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Supervises staff as assigned by supervisor.&nbsp;</li><li>Provides case management and community support services to assist individuals and/or families to gain access to needed medical, social, education, mental health, addiction, co-occurring and other services.&nbsp;</li><li>Monitors that all documentation is done within prescribed time frames and in accordance with UBHC policy, and specific program, funding and billing requirements.&nbsp;</li><li>Performs duties relevant to a leadership position and supports goals and objectives of University Behavioral Health Care.&nbsp;</li><li>Meets annual requirements.</li><li>Understands and adheres to Rutgers’ compliance standards as they appear in RBHS’s Corporate Compliance Policy, Code of Conduct and Conflict of Interest Policy.&nbsp;</li></ul> UBHC - Community-Based Service RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8011 Piscataway NJ 26ST1716 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279242 2026-07-31T11:38:56-04:00 2026-07-31T11:38:57-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Postdoctoral Associate for Dr. Anat Kreimer’s laboratory at the Center for Advanced Biotechnology and Medicine (CABM), located on the Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences (RBHS) campus in Piscataway, New Jersey. The expected start date for this Postdoctoral Associate position is September 1, 2026.</div><div><br>The primary purpose of the Postdoctoral Associate is to conduct research on characterizing non-coding regulatory elements in humans and understanding how these elements change across different conditions. The project will involve developing new modeling approaches for coupling functional genomics techniques with computational analyses to understand gene regulation in health and disease. Such models are based on multi-omics high-throughput assays, either performed by the Postdoctoral Associate or by others in the research group, by collaborators in other groups or from publicly available datasets. The project may also involve use and development of software programs for analysis of multi-dimensional epigenetic, transcriptomic, genetic and functional genomics data. The Postdoctoral Associate will be expected to participate in the configuration and maintenance of data bases necessary for conduct of the project. It is expected that research will lead to publications and the Postdoctoral Associate will be expected to prepare manuscripts as well as contribute to the preparation of grant and fellowship applications. The Postdoctoral Associate will also be expected to guide the research project of undergraduate research assistants.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Develops computational frameworks for coupling functional genomics techniques with computational analyses to understand gene regulation in health and disease. Such models incorporate multi-omics high-throughput assays such as RNA-seq, ChIP-seq, ATAC-seq, MPRA, PC-HiC.</li><li>Participates in the configuration and maintenance of laboratory instrumentation and equipment, including computers and servers, necessary for conduct of the project.</li><li>Prepares scientific manuscripts for publication, and contributes to the preparation of research grant and fellowship applications.</li><li>Assists with and guides the research projects of undergraduate research assistants.</li><li>Performs other related duties as assigned.</li></ul> RBHS RBHS Chancellor-L2 CABM-L3 7883 Piscataway NJ 26ST1325 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/272721 2026-04-09T10:52:26-04:00 2026-04-09T10:52:26-04:00 Part Time Teaching – Blackwood NJ - Fall 2026 <div>We are seeking part time/adjunct clinical faculty to teach in our Entry to Baccalaureate nursing program during the upcoming semester. We are seeking clinical instructors qualified to teach in the following nursing specialties:</div><ul><li>PEDS clinical instructors</li><li>MED-SURG clinical instructors</li><li>NCHP/fundamentals lab and clinical instructors</li></ul><div><br>These open positions are located at our Blackwood campus which is a part of Rutgers School of Nursing at Rutgers Health (RBHS).</div> Entry Baccalaureate Nursing Pr RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Nursing Dean's Offic-L3 7611 26FA0338 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279602 2026-08-14T12:30:55-04:00 2026-08-14T12:30:56-04:00 Mental Health Specialist IV - Part Time - Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is seeking a part-time Mental Health Specialist IV in the Child &amp; Adolescent Services – Children’s Transitional Residence of Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the part-time Mental Health Specialist IV is to provide daily care and supervision to children residing in the Children’s Transitional Residence.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Provides direct supervision to children (ages 5-11 years) residing in the Children’s Transitional Residence.</li><li>Supervises daily activities, such as personal care routines, meals and transportation to and from school or medical appointments.</li><li>Implements recreational and therapeutic activities and trips appropriate to the children’s age, abilities, and therapeutic needs.</li><li>Provides behavioral reinforcement, positive role-modeling and feedback to children to encourage more adaptive and pro-social behaviors.</li><li>Monitors children for a 24-hour day program, including overnight visual checks. e. Intervenes effectively to maintain safety and security for children in crisis by using both verbal and physical crisis intervention strategies.</li><li>Documents all unit activities in unit and communication logs.</li><li>Assists in maintaining a clean, secure, and nurturing environment.</li></ul> UBHC - Inpatient/CTR RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8018 Piscataway NJ 26ST1010 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279869 2026-08-24T12:35:00-04:00 2026-08-24T12:35:00-04:00 Laboratory Technician <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Laboratory Technician for the Department of Molecular Biology and Biochemistry. The position works in the lab of Dr. Kevin Monahan in the Nelson Labs on the Busch Campus. The Laboratory Technician will assist a senior graduate student and departing postdoc with completing their research projects by assisting with routine technical work in the laboratory.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Prepares biological samples.</li><li>Assists lab members with sample collection.</li><li>Processes samples following routine protocols and maintains detailed records for each sample.</li><li>Performs mouse husbandry: genotyping, weaning, and animal care.</li></ul> DLS Molecular Biology & Bioche New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 7063 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277749 2026-06-25T10:51:55-04:00 2026-06-25T10:51:56-04:00 Staff Nurse FT Days UCHC NSP <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Full Time Staff Nurse for Northern State Prison located in Newark, NJ<br><br>The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus for inmates in the New Jersey Department of Corrections.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br>* Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the resident-patient including adolescents (13-17 years), adults (18 to 64 years) and their family within the framework established by the correctional system.<br>* Performs assessments of resident-patient in a variety of settings such as initial intake area, health care unit for sick call, emergency situations in housing, chronic care clinics and infirmary.<br>* Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br>* Identifies inmate-centered goals and nursing objectives and implements prescribed interventions and solutions for the identified problems.<br>* Plans nursing care by identification of resident-patient needs based on assessments. Makes appropriate, timely referrals and initiates appropriate nursing care based on institutional policies and procedures.<br>* As team leader or charge nurse, delegates duties to other health care team members based on their skill, knowledge and experience and guides the provision of care by others.</div> UCHC Northern State Prison Phy_DUP RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7679 Newark NJ 26ST0563 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274660 2026-05-08T14:39:58-04:00 2026-05-27T13:21:23-04:00 Tenure-Track Assistant or Associate Professor <div>Tenure-Track Assistant or Associate Professor position available in the Department of Pharmaceutics at Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy, Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey. The successful candidate must possess a Ph.D. in Pharmaceutical Sciences or in a relevant discipline with postdoctoral experience, a strong record of publications and the ability to develop and sustain an independent, extramurally funded research program. Candidates are expected to teach pharmacokinetics and pharmacodynamics and other course in the professional PharmD program of the School of Pharmacy and the MS and PhD Graduate Program in Pharmaceutical Science.<br><br></div> Pharmaceutics RBHS Chancellor-L2 Ernest Mario School of Pharmac-L3 6719 26FA0472 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266217 2025-12-31T09:37:28-05:00 2025-12-31T09:37:28-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor of Medical Education <div>The Department of Neuroscience and Cell Biology at Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School (RWJMS) invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure track faculty position in medical and graduate education. We seek a dedicated educator with a passion for teaching and curricular innovation to join our collaborative academic team.<br><br>The successful candidate will support the school’s educational mission by teaching clinically relevant basic science content in pre-clerkship courses, with a particular focus in neuroscience or gross anatomy and histology. Responsibilities will include coordinating small-group learning activities such as team-based learning (TBL), case-based discussions, and laboratory sessions. The candidate will also contribute to teaching in the Master’s in Biomedical Sciences program.<br><br><strong>Required qualifications</strong> include a doctoral degree (PhD, MD, or equivalent), teaching experience in neuroscience or anatomy at a medical or health-professional school, and evidence of excellence in teaching and course management. Academic rank will be commensurate with experience. Candidates from diverse backgrounds and those with a demonstrated commitment to advancing equity and inclusion in education are strongly encouraged to apply.<br><br>We are particularly interested in candidates who demonstrate expertise in active learning pedagogy and curricular integration, the ability to bridge foundational and clinical content, experience in course leadership and curriculum development, and a strong commitment to inclusive and student-centered teaching.<br><br>Application materials should include: (1) a letter of interest addressed to the Faculty Search Committee; (2) a curriculum vitae; (3) a summary of educational accomplishments; (4) a statement describing your approach to inclusive teaching and integrating diversity in education; and (5) contact information for at least three professional references. <br><br>Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. All offers of employment are contingent upon successful completion of pre-employment background checks.<br><br><strong>About RWJMS</strong><br>RWJMS is entering an exciting phase of growth, with a new integrated curriculum, a transition to a state-of-the-art medical education building in 2026, and a merger with our sister school to form the Rutgers School of Medicine. These developments provide meaningful opportunities for leadership in medical education and collaboration across disciplines.<br><br>Robert Wood Johnson Medical School is located on the New Brunswick/Piscataway campus of Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey. As one of the nation’s leading comprehensive medical schools, Robert Wood Johnson Medical School is dedicated to the pursuit of excellence in education, research, health care delivery, and the promotion of community health. In cooperation with Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital, the medical school’s principal affiliate, they comprise New Jersey’s premier academic medical center. In addition, Robert Wood Johnson Medical School has 34 other hospital affiliates and ambulatory care sites throughout the region. <br><br>The school encompasses 20 basic science and clinical departments, and hosts centers and institutes including The Cardiovascular Institute, the Child Health Institute of New Jersey, the Institute for Neurological Therapeutics, and the Women’s Health Institute. The medical school maintains educational programs at the undergraduate, graduate, and postgraduate levels for more than 1,500 students on its campuses in New Brunswick and Piscataway and provides continuing education courses for healthcare professionals and community education programs. The Rutgers life and biomedical sciences community includes over 200 faculty members in different departments within Robert Wood Johnson Medical School, School of Arts and Sciences, School of Environmental and Biological Sciences, Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy, School of Engineering as well as within institutes including the New Jersey Institute for Food, Nutrition, and Health (IFNH), Human Genetics Institute of New Jersey (HGINJ), Waksman Institute of Microbiology, Institute for Quantitative Biomedicine, Cancer Institute of New Jersey (CINJ), Child Health Institute of New Jersey (CHI), Rutgers Institute for Infectious and Inflammatory Diseases, the Brain Health Institute, and the Rutgers Institute for Translational Medicine and Science leading the NIH-funded New Jersey Alliance for Clinical and Translational Science (NJ ACTS), with Princeton University and the New Jersey Institute of Technology. To learn more about our department, please visit <a href=\"https://rwjms.rutgers.edu/departments/neuroscience-and-cell-biology/about-the-department\"><strong>Department of Neuroscience &amp; Cell Biology</strong></a>.<br><br>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. We are deeply committed to increasing diversity and especially encourage applications from persons with disabilities, women, veterans, and minority scholars.<br><br></div> RWJ - Neuroscience & Cell Biol RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7786 25FA0676 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280090 2026-08-27T13:56:34-04:00 2026-08-27T13:56:35-04:00 Sr Maintenance Mechanic <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Sr Maintenance Mechanic for the Sr Maintenance Mechanic. Works independently in a \"zone\", or as the only Maintenance Mechanic on a particular campus<br>reportingdirectly to a second level supervisor.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>May guide and instruct other staff in the performance of a wide range of mechanical maintenance duties to repair and maintain equipment in good operating condition.</li><li>Such duties may be based on work orders which provide little or no instruction or assistance.</li><li>Responsible for estimation of work and procuring appropriate materials for him/herself or the group.</li><li>May guide and instruct craft trainees.</li><li>May perform any duties of the group.</li><li>Verifies results of work performed by the outside vendors.</li></ul> Facilities Maintenance Newark EVP & Chief Admin Officer Institutional Planning & Optns-L3 8412 Newark NJ 26ST0650 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278401 2026-07-08T12:13:24-04:00 2026-07-08T12:13:25-04:00 Visiting Researcher <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Visiting Researcher within the Urology Oncology Division of the Rutgers Cancer Institute.<br><br>Under the direction of the principal Investigator, the Visiting Researcher will support the Urologic Oncology Department in data management, study recruitment, and IRB submissions and projects. The Visiting Researcher will also assist in developing protocols and managing study participant data and requirements.</div><div><br>Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Perform data analysis and prepare manuscripts. Publish studies in collaboration with the team.</li><li>Regulatory Submission and IRB/SRB Approval: Manage, organize, and prepare regulatory documentation and submissions, primarily for institutional, multi-institutional, or collaborative industry translational projects. Communicate with IRB/SRB and regulatory staff and investigators.</li><li>Streamline submissions of data use and material transfer agreements, optimizing collaboration with industry or other institutions for clinical and translational projects.</li><li>Maintain database. Manage prospective registries for bladder, prostate, and kidney cancer, focusing on nonmuscle invasive bladder cancer. Coordinate with biobank to summarize inventories of specimens for use in translational studies.</li><li>Recruit participants for the study. Assist in identification, consenting, and enrollment of patients.</li><li>Monitor and collect study participant data. Works with study participants to ensure they complete patient questionnaires Case Report Forms.</li><li>Assist in development of protocols for the investigator-initiated studies. Prepare, evaluate and analyze Case Report Forms in print and electronically using RedCap and other data management systems.</li><li>Prepares weekly urologic oncology regulatory status reports; provides updates on patient accrual, as well as ongoing abstracts, publications, and grants. This will aid in maximizing productivity of the Division.</li></ul> CINJ - Urology Oncology RBHS Chancellor-L2 Cancer Institute of New Jersey-L3 7887 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1490 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267367 2026-01-15T11:46:53-05:00 2026-01-15T11:46:54-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor of Medicine/Infectious Diseases <div>Rutgers, New Jersey Medical School is seeking full-time Infectious Diseases physicians and physician scientists to join the Division of Infectious Diseases and/or the Public Health Research Institute (PHRI). This position includes patient care, teaching, research, and scholarship. Research support is available for qualified candidates.<br><br>The successful candidate(s) will be clinically focused physicians and/or physician scientists who are focused on growing a translational research program, as well exceptional patient care, who can work effectively and collaboratively with colleagues and patients, and who have significant interest in academic medicine, teaching fellows, residents and medical students. Faculty rank will be commensurate with experience and qualifications.<br><br><br></div> NJMS - Medicine Infectious Dis RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7442 24FA0484 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280247 2026-08-31T15:23:37-04:00 2026-08-31T15:23:38-04:00 Supervising Mental Health Specialist (Rotating) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Supervising Mental Health Specialist (Rotating) for the Military Services within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.&nbsp;<br><br>Participates as a member of the management and treatment teams. Ensures the provision of high-quality, comprehensive crisis response, triage, and support services. Responsible for staff supervision, training, and development.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Provides and manages crisis response, triage, and support services for incoming calls, chats, and service requests.&nbsp;</li><li>Supervises assigned staff. &nbsp;</li><li>Provides ongoing supervision, coaching, training, and performance feedback.&nbsp;</li><li>Supports staff in managing high-risk or complex situations, ensuring adherence to risk assessment and safety protocols. &nbsp;</li><li>Reviews call queues, chats, and service requests, and ensures the receipt of person-focused service delivery interventions and appropriate case dispositions.&nbsp;</li><li>Maintains appropriate staffing coverage during assigned shifts. &nbsp;</li><li>Tracks, analyzes, and improves key performance metrics to ensure quality outcomes. &nbsp;</li></ul> UBHC - Military Services RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8040 Piscataway NJ 26ST1701 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278831 2026-07-15T10:49:25-04:00 2026-07-15T10:49:26-04:00 Public Health Representative III <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Public Health Representative III in the Department of Pediatrics within the New Jersey Medical School (NJMS).<br><br>The primary purpose of the Public Health Representative III position is to provide HIV testing, screening, counseling, and referrals in the community through outreach on a Mobile Unit. Provides PrEP screening and counseling to high-risk HIV negative individuals targeting the PrEP eligible population. They will also serve as a backup to the lead HIV Pre-Exposure Prophylaxis (PrEP) Counselor. In addition, the Public Health Representative III will provide sexual risk avoidance and basic family planning counseling to adolescents and young adults. Works closely with the lead PrEP counselor and the Program Coordinator to identify soft sites and mobile unit accessible locations.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Provide HIV and Sexually transmitted infections (STI )testing through blood extraction, phlebotomy, and urine collection.</li><li>Ensure that HIV/ Sexually transmitted infections (STIs) and pre-exposure prophylaxis (PrEP) counseling, testing, and referral are provided in accordance with the standards of the Division of HIV and AIDS (DHAS)/NJ Department of Health and Senior Services (NJDHSS).</li><li>Ensure that blood and other specimens collected adhere to the standards of the New Jersey Department of Health and Senior Services or the NJ Department of Health/Courier pick up site, as appropriate.</li><li>Ensure all data is entered into required databases in a timely manner and maintain client records in compliance with standards set by Division of HIV and AIDS Services.</li><li>Assist in the coordination of activities related to HIV services at health fairs, colleges/universities, and other community sponsored event information and testing sites.</li></ul> NJMS - Pediatrics Adolescent M RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7468 Newark NJ 26ST0477 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/270539 2026-03-10T15:05:14-04:00 2026-03-10T15:05:14-04:00 Lecturer (Part Time Teaching) Summer 2026 <div>The Mathematics Department seeks Lecturers (Part Time Teaching) for the New Brunswick/Piscataway Campus for Summer 2026. The positions available are primarily for course lecturers or recitation instructors for Basic Skills (e.g., Elementary Algebra), Mathematics or Liberal Arts, Precalculus, and Calculus I and II. Candidates for Part Time Teaching or Instructor must be able to teach face-to-face, as well as online, and be available to teach between 9 a.m. and 5 p.m., or else between 5 p.m. and 10 p.m.<br><br>Candidates must have a Master’s Degree or Ph.D. and provide evidence of teaching effectiveness. Course load is up to 9 credits hours per semester, for a maximum of 15 credits hours per academic year.<br><br>All teaching will be in person.</div> Mathematics New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 8125 26FA0131 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280480 2026-09-05T00:02:20-04:00 2026-09-05T00:02:21-04:00 Program Coordinator I <div>Rutgers University-Camden is seeking a Program Coordinator I for the CCR&amp;R, reporting to the Sr. Program Director. The Program Coordinator will serve as the Quality Improvement Specialist (QIS) in Cumberland, Gloucester &amp; Salem Counties, and will have primary responsibility for the planning and implementation of the NJ Quality Rating and Improvement System, Grow NJ Kids. There is a focus on recruitment and enrollment into the statewide program. The position provides staff in enrolled early care and education programs with targeted technical assistance and coaching as part of the Grow NJ Kids continuous improvement cycle. With this system, New Jersey is creating universal standards of quality for all child care and education programs (Head Start, Child Care, Preschool, etc.). Grow NJ Kids provides training and incentives to improve child care programs by providing the framework to meet high-quality standards. The QIS provides the first phase of technical assistance to help improve child care program quality and navigate through the GNJK process.<br><br></div><div>This is a grant funded position contingent upon the availability of funds to support it.</div> Southern Regional CCR&R Agency Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Provost Office Camden-L3 8301 Camden NJ 26ST1680 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279450 2026-08-10T10:30:04-04:00 2026-08-10T10:30:05-04:00 Mental Health Clinician II UCHC NSP <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care (UCHC) is seeking a Mental Health Clinician II for Northern State Prison, located in Newark, New Jersey. The Mental Health Clinician II completes specialized psychological testing and assessment of clinical needs of adult inmates sentenced to the Department of Corrections.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Completes specialized psychological testing and assessment of clinical needs of adults sentenced to the Department of Corrections.</li><li>Arrives at diagnoses with precision and accuracy by the end of psychological testing and the evaluation session. Develops treatment plans.</li><li>Makes clinically based decisions regarding appropriateness for treatment, as well as preferred treatment modality. Skilled in in providing group, individual and family therapies</li><li>Assesses and makes referrals for higher levels of care, as appropriate.</li><li>Recognizes the unique needs and behaviors of adult inmate/patients, seniors and their families.</li></ul> UCHC Northern State Prison Med RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7656 Newark NJ 26ST0314 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/276639 2026-06-08T09:30:53-04:00 2026-06-08T09:30:53-04:00 Coadjutant Non-Teaching <div>Freeman Lab is seeking for a summer assistant to aid with laboratory-based engineering and biomedical engineering research activities related to virtual laboratory development, AI-supported engineering learning environments, multimodal analysis activities, and community engagement initiatives. Responsibilities include assisting with experimental setup, operation of laboratory equipment, software utilization and data analysis, support of multimodal physiological response analysis activities, technical documentation, review and piloting of curricular materials, and support of outreach and educational activities designed to expand student engagement in engineering and STEM learning experiences.</div> Biomedical Engineering New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Engineering-L3 7102 26FA0538 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274053 2026-04-30T12:01:27-04:00 2026-04-30T12:01:27-04:00 Lecturers, Computer Science <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the Faculty of Arts &amp; Sciences, Department of Computer Science, seeks new lecturers to teach in various topics within the discipline for courses in Fall 2026, Winter 2027, Spring 2027 and/or Summer 2027 semester(s). The instructor will present course material during the assigned course times, hold office hours, administer exams, assign grades, and coordinate any other requirements related to course instruction.</div> Computer Science Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 6774 26FA0413 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266003 2025-12-31T09:12:06-05:00 2025-12-31T09:12:06-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The Department of