li><li>Maternal health</li><li>Pediatrics</li><li>Adult health</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>General Responsibilities:<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Attend orientation before beginning of semester.</li><li>Provide instruction and supervision in the clinical, simulation, and/or lab settings.</li><li>Follow course syllabi to help students achieve set learning outcomes.</li><li>Communicate with the Clinical or Lab Coordinator on an ongoing basis regarding student progress or any concerns.</li><li>Attend course faculty meetings before the semester start and when requested.</li><li>Evaluate, grade, and provide feedback on required course assignments and tasks (i.e., Care plans, specialty papers, research projects, med math, etc.)</li><li>Complete evaluation for each student by the due date.</li></ul><div><br><strong>** This opportunity is for weekdays only.</strong></div> Entry Baccalaureate Nursing Pr RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Nursing Dean's Offic-L3 7611 26FA0330 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/270736 2026-03-12T16:20:56-04:00 2026-03-12T16:20:57-04:00 Co Adj Non-Teaching <div>The Center for Psychological Services at the Graduate School of Applied and Professional Psychology (GSAPP) announces an opening for a Clinical Supervisor to lead the Tourette Syndrome Clinic (TS Clinic). The Clinical Supervisor will be involved in direct oversight of programming and provide supervision and training to doctoral students in assessment and/or treatment. The TS Clinic Supervisor will also work with/serve as a liaison to the New Jersey Center for Tourette Syndrome and Associated Disorders (NJCTS) and other community partners as needed. The TS Clinic Supervisor will provide 1 hour of individual and 1 hour of group supervision, each weekly on Thursdays for doctoral-level students placed in the specialty clinic. In addition to supervision, it is expected the Supervisor will provide weekly didactic training related to the treatment of Tourette Syndrome and related disorders. They will create the schedule of didactics and arrange for guest speakers, if desired or appropriate. This position will report to the Director of the Center for Psychological Services at GSAPP and will have a standing biweekly or monthly meeting with the Director of CPS, as needed.</div> Psychological Services Center New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Graduate School of Applied & P-L3 6823 26FA0236 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279457 2026-08-10T11:02:20-04:00 2026-08-10T11:02:21-04:00 Laundry Attendant/Sewing Worker <div>Rutgers, The State University is seeking a Laundry Attendant/Sewing Worker for the Laundry Department within Dining Services. Under the guidance and supervision of a Laundry Group Leader or other senior dining service worker, performs laundry procedures. Also operates sewing machine and handles sewing work.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Receives soiled laundry, counts and verifies against receipt for accuracy. Informs Laundry Group Leader of discrepancies.</li><li>Sorts laundry, loads washing machines, adds detergent and/or other laundry products. Washes, dries, folds or hangs items. Sorts according to operating units.</li><li>Maintains facilities and equipment in a clean and sanitary condition.</li><li>Operates sewing machine and attachments to repair uniforms, draperies, curtains, etc.</li><li>Mends, fits, tailors, and irons uniforms, linens, draperies, curtains, etc. Reports questionable conditions to supervisor. Performs related duties as required.</li></ul> Facilities Dining Hall New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Student Affairs - New Brunswic-L3 6678 Piscataway NJ 26ST1501 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279747 2026-08-20T08:53:19-04:00 2026-08-20T08:53:20-04:00 Staff Nurse PT Eves UCHC GSYCF (multiple vacancies) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Part Time UCHC Staff Nurse for the Garden State Youth Correctional Facility, located in Yardville, NJ<br><br>The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus. Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment. Frequently functions guided by nursing protocols. Functions as a team leader as assigned. Demonstrates competency in assessment and identification of the physical health of adults (18 to 64 years), and geriatrics (65+) all population groups and their personal strengths. Identifies inmate-centered goals and nursing objectives and implements prescribed interventions and solutions for the identified problems.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the inmate-patient including adults (18 to 64 years), and geriatrics (65+) and their family within the framework established by the correctional system.</li><li>Utilizes effective communication skills by demonstrating respect, concern and courtesy in all interpersonal relationships.</li><li>Uses current knowledge to promote a safe environment for providing health care to inmate-patients.</li></ul><div>.</div> UCHC Garden State Youth Physic RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7676 Yardville NJ 26ST1279 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/276677 2026-06-08T15:39:56-04:00 2026-06-08T15:39:57-04:00 Co Adj – Non Teaching, Supervisor <div>The Center for Psychological Services at the Graduate School of Applied and Professional Psychology (GSAPP) announces an opening for Clinical Supervisors to lead the Tourette Syndrome Clinic (TS Clinic). The Clinical Supervisor will be involved in direct oversight of programming and provide supervision and training to doctoral students in assessment and/or treatment. The TS Clinic Supervisor will also work with/serve as a liaison to the New Jersey Center for Tourette Syndrome and Associated Disorders (NJCTS) and other community partners as needed. The TS Clinic Supervisor will provide 1 hour of individual and 1 hour of group supervision, each weekly on Thursdays for doctoral-level students placed in the specialty clinic. In addition to supervision, it is expected the Supervisor will provide weekly didactic training related to the treatment of Tourette Syndrome and related disorders. They will create the schedule of didactics and arrange for guest speakers, if desired or appropriate. This position will report to the Director of the Center for Psychological Services at GSAPP and will have a standing biweekly or monthly meeting with the Director of CPS, as needed.</div> Psychological Services Center New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Graduate School of Applied & P-L3 6823 26FA0583 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274060 2026-04-30T12:30:35-04:00 2026-04-30T12:30:35-04:00 Lecturers, Digital Studies <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the Faculty of Arts &amp; Sciences, Digital Studies Department, seeks new lecturers to teach various topics within the discipline for courses for Fall 2026, Winter 2027, Spring 2027 and/or Summer 2027. The instructor will present course material during the assigned course times, hold office hours, administer exams, assign grades and coordinate any other requirements related to course instruction.</div> Digital Studies Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 9010 26FA0416 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266005 2025-12-31T09:12:11-05:00 2025-12-31T09:12:12-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor - Full-time Prosthodontist <div>The Department of Restorative Dentistry is searching for multiple full-time, non-tenure track, faculty positions at the rank of Assistant/Associate Professor, 100% FTE. The faculty person will be responsible for didactic and clinical teaching at both the postgraduate and undergraduate level. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: predoctoral education of fixed, removable, implant prosthodontics, dental anatomy, occlusion, biomaterials, and operative dentistry. Participation in predoctoral and post-doctoral teaching, as well as participation in the Departmental Master of Dental Science degree program; scholarly activity, research, and service is expected. The selected candidate will teach and/or direct preclinical courses, serve as an advisor for students, lecture in departmental courses as directed, participate on committees as assigned, and other assignments as directed by the Chair.<br><br></div><div>Position will remain open until filled. Salary and rank will be commensurate with experience.</div><div><br>Rutgers School of Dental Medicine is a component of Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey and is located on the Newark Campus of Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences Division, along with the Rutgers Medical School, the Graduate School of Biomedical Sciences, the School of Health Related Professions, and the School of Nursing. Rutgers School of Dental Medicine is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer. The final candidate will be required to successfully pass a background check prior to employment.</div> RSDM - Restorative Dentistry RBHS Chancellor-L2 Rutgers School of Dental Medic-L3 7550 24FA0223 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279738 2026-08-20T08:43:52-04:00 2026-08-20T08:43:53-04:00 Technician I PT Nights UCHC GSYCF <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Part Time Technician I for Garden State Youth Correctional Facility located in Yardville, NJ. The Technician I participates as a member of the clinical and administrative medical team at the Prison.<br><br>Among the duties for the position are:<br><br></div><ul><li>Takes vital signs, height and weight and documents in electronic medical records (EMR).</li><li>Assists the physician/associate practitioner with procedures, including preparing the inmate for the examination.</li><li>Obtains specimen collection and handling, including, but not limited to, drawing blood.</li><li>Assists with the cleaning, sterilization and securing of equipment within the Health Service Unit.</li><li>Maintains or assists in maintaining the supply stock in the Health Service Unit by ordering in a timely and appropriate manner.</li><li>Maintains the supply stock in the examination rooms.</li><li>Aggregates the orders of all medications and forwards to the pharmacy provider / local pharmacy.</li></ul> UCHC Garden State Youth Nursin RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7690 Yardville NJ 26ST0189 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/269405 2026-02-18T11:09:06-05:00 2026-02-18T11:09:07-05:00 Assistant Professor <div>SUMMARY: (Basic purpose of the job)<br>The Institute for Infectious and Inflammatory Diseases (i3), Rutgers New Jersey Medical School and the Center for Immunity and Inflammation (CII) invites applications for a full-time appointment at the Assistant Professor level. We are currently recruiting candidates with expertise in infectious disease and inflammation. The position will be supported by a competitive start up package with exceptional candidates being considered for further support as Chancellor Scholars.<br><br></div> NJMS - Immunity & Infection Ce RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7451 21FA0797 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280453 2026-09-04T11:45:05-04:00 2026-09-04T11:45:06-04:00 Nurse Anesthetist <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Nurse Anesthetist for the department of Anesthesiology at the Robert Wood Johnson Medical School.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Nurse Anesthetist (Certified Registered) position is to administer anesthesia – related care in four general categories. (1) pre-anesthetic preparation and evaluation (2) anesthesia induction, maintenance and emergence, (3) post anesthesia care and (4) peri anesthetic and clinical support functions.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Performing and documenting a pre-anesthetic assessment and evaluation of the patient, including requesting consultations and diagnostic studies, selecting, obtaining ordering or administering pre-anesthetic medications and fluids; and obtaining informed consent for anesthesia.</li><li>Develops and implements an anesthetic plan.</li><li>Selecting and initiating the planned anesthetic technique which may include: general regional and local anesthesia and intravenous sedation/monitored anesthesia care (MAC).</li><li>Selecting, obtaining or administering the anesthetics, adjuvant drugs, accessory drugs, and fluids necessary to manage the anesthetic, to maintain the patient’s physiologic homeostasis, and to correct abnormal responses to the anesthesia or surgery.</li><li>Selecting, applying, or inserting appropriate non-invasive and invasive monitoring modalities for collecting and interpreting patient physiological data.</li><li>Managing a patient’s airway and pulmonary status using endotracheal intubation, mechanical ventilation, pharmacological support, respiratory therapy or extubation.</li></ul> RWJ - Anesthesiology RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7729 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1482 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279385 2026-08-07T00:00:52-04:00 2026-08-07T00:00:54-04:00 Accounting Assistant II <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking an Accounting Assistant II for the Athletics Business Office.</div><div><br></div><div>Among the key duties of the position are the following:</div><ul><li>Assists in general accounting and Procurement (P2P) functions including the vendor management, processing of purchase orders, invoices, facilitating credit card payments, and the like.</li><li>Assists with the management of Game Contracts/Non-Conference Guarantees.</li><li>Works with all necessary support groups to see the full process of contracts through to the end.</li><li>Tracks and reconciles all payments made.</li></ul> Athl - Business Office Intercollegiate Athletics-L2 Athl - Business Office-L3 6845 Piscataway NJ 26ST1571 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/276120 2026-05-29T11:53:41-04:00 2026-05-29T11:53:41-04:00 NTT Assistant Teaching Professor: Biology <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the School of Art &amp; Sciences, Biology Department, invites applications for a non-tenure track Assistant Teaching Professor faculty position in biology. We seek an outstanding individual with innovative and integrative teaching approaches to lead the Anatomy and Physiology education to both biology majors (Advanced A&amp;P+Lab) and non-major, including Health Science majors (Basic A&amp;P+Lab).<br>While this position focuses on A&amp;P, it is expected that the candidate will be proficient in teaching other disciplines in biology complimentary to existing members of the department and in new areas of focus, including, but not limited to molecular biology, genetics/genomics, ecology/evolution, virology, and student-led research in biology within the context of teaching labs.<br>We encourage those to apply who are dedicated to undergraduate education using approaches that capture the current body of students, while maintaining the expected high level of education provided by Rutgers University.<br>The successful candidate is expected to lead the A&amp;P mission of biology, and contribute to the general needs of the academic program. The candidate will be a contributing member of the department by serving on relevant departmental, campus, and university committees.<br>The candidate should also have great interest and preferably experience in guiding capstone MS students in both the Biology Department and more campus-wide interdisciplinary research through the Center for Computational and Integrative Biology (CCIB).<br><br>The teaching load for teaching professors is 4-4, and salaries and benefits are competitive.<br><br>The successful applicant is expected to contribute to the development and implementation of innovative curriculum taking courses in new directions and is expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses.<br>Please find further information on the Biology Department https://biology.camden.rutgers.edu/ and CCIB https://ccib.camden.rutgers.edu/. First consideration will be given to candidates whose application is received by October 1, 2026. The search will continue until the appropriate candidate is found. Applicants should contact Dr. Nir Yakoby, chairperson of Department of Biology, yakoby@camden.rutgers.edu, with position related questions.</div> Biology Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 6758 26FA0534 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/273848 2026-04-28T15:44:19-04:00 2026-04-28T15:44:20-04:00 Department of Medicine: Hepatologist (GI) <div><strong>Clinical Care Responsibilities:</strong></div><ol><li>Clinical practice with 90% effort focused on direct patient care in the practice of hepatology and gastroenterology. Clinical practice will be concentrated on diagnosis, monitoring, management and endoscopic procedures on patients with or being evaluated for clinical problems related to the liver. It will consist of 7 half-day sessions per week (5 half-days of outpatient clinic per week, one of which may be fellow’s clinic or gastroenterology focused clinic) and 2 half days of endoscopy per week (particularly patients needing screening for or management of esophageal varices but also general gastrointestinal upper and lower endoscopy including screening colonoscopies). 10 to 12 weeks of inpatient hepatology service at Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital, New Brunswick per year (20% effort). During the RWJUH inpatient service, 2 half-days of endoscopy or outpatient clinics will be performed in the AM).<ul><li>Note that for candidates who are trained in liver transplantation, there will be an option of 20% effort at University Hospital, Newark on the liver transplant services. This will consist of 5 full weeks of inpatient care (i.e. including weekend duties) (10% effort), one half-day of clinic per month and weekly attendance (by Zoom or in person) on the weekly afternoon liver transplantation conference (10% effort).</li></ul></li><li>Establish and maintain physician office hours in order to be accessible to new consults and follow up patients, adjusting as needed at designated GI offices.</li><li>Be accountable for overall care of patients who are consulted or admitted (inpatient and same day procedure) under Physician’s name.</li><li>Provide complete and timely consults as requested by other specialists.</li><li>Provide clear instructions, explanations, and options available regarding diagnosis, treatment, medications, and follow-up to patients, family members, and other health care team members.</li><li>Provide GI night and weekend on-call coverage during inpatient service (estimated at 2 nights per Monday – Thursday weekdays and 50% of weekends while on inpatient service and otherwise as is necessary to cover clinical needs.</li><li>Attend monthly meetings with key personnel to review data, outcomes, protocols, policies, procedures, and staffing to continuously monitor and improve the care rendered.</li><li>Attend departmental physician staff meetings, M&amp;M Conference, liver masses/tumor board meetings, fellowship selection committee, and other departmental meetings deemed appropriate by the Division Chief or the Department of Medicine Chair</li><li>Identify opportunities to participate in research trials and publications</li><li>Safeguard patient confidentiality at all times. Limit work/patient related discussions to private areas.</li><li>Complete required medical documentation included in patients charts in accordance with the Medical Staff Bylaws.</li><li>Provide accurate and complete information required for billing</li><li>Submit clinical charges and patient notes in timely manner.</li><li>Effectively communicate with patients, family members, and other health care team members.</li></ol><div><strong>Academic Responsibilities at Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School</strong></div><ol><li>Supervise and teach fellows, residents and housestaff, and medical students.</li><li>Perform clinical or translational research or quality improvement and academic program building in areas of interest, preferably related to liver diseases.</li><li>Pursue leadership activities in medical societies and associations, particularly in leading gastroenterology, endoscopy and internal medicine societies.</li><li>Participate in or develop CME programs, especially as related to gastrointestinal and biliary malignancies, advanced endoscopy or other clinical areas of expertise.</li><li>Participate in the academic activities of the Gastroenterology and Hepatology Division as well as the educational, patient care, research/quality improvement and other activities of the Department of Medicine.</li><li>Attend Division and Department meetings including but not limited to faculty meetings, Grand Rounds and Fellow recruitment sessions.</li><li>Participate in appropriate Department of Medicine and Medical School committees.</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned by the Division Chief and/or Department Chair.</li></ol> RWJ - Medicine Gastroenterolog RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7772 26FA0154 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/265903 2025-12-31T09:00:53-05:00 2025-12-31T09:00:54-05:00 Research-Track Assistant Professor, Associate Professor or Professor (Multiple Positions) <div>The Department of Psychiatry at Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School (RWJMS) seeks Research-Track faculty at any rank to expand our research portfolio. Research-track faculty are matched to a specific research group/lab and work to support the research initiatives of that group/lab under supervision of the principal investigator and/or center director. The Department of Psychiatry has a very robust research portfolio, with over $25 million in awards in the last fiscal year. Department research is generally conducted among the Rutgers Addiction Research Center (<a href=\"https://addiction.rutgers.edu/\"><strong>https://addiction.rutgers.edu/</strong></a>), the Center for Psychiatric Health &amp; Genomics (<a href=\"https://cphg.rutgers.edu/\"><strong>https://cphg.rutgers.edu/</strong></a>), the Division of Addiction Psychiatry (<a href=\"https://rwjms.rutgers.edu/department/psychiatry/divisions\"><strong>https://rwjms.rutgers.edu/department/psychiatry/divisions</strong></a>), the Center for Advanced Human Brain Imaging Research (<a href=\"https://sites.rutgers.edu/cahbir/\"><strong>https://sites.rutgers.edu/cahbir/</strong></a>), and individual labs including basic science and animal models.</div><div><br></div><div>Research-Track faculty will perform research activities on behalf of the Department of Psychiatry in strategic growth areas, function collaboratively with a multidisciplinary team, and maintain effective communication with staff and administration. Research-Track faculty are expected to have developed sufficient expertise and skills to contribute immediately to the research initiatives of the program they join without an expectation of significant training. Research-Track faculty may be asked to contribute to, and/or submit as principal investigator, applications for extramural funding in their research area of expertise to financially support their position. The Research-Track faculty position is contingent upon continued funding availability.</div> RWJ - Psychiatry Research RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7826 24FA1301 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279664 2026-08-17T16:28:17-04:00 2026-08-17T16:28:18-04:00 Assistant Nurse Manager <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking an Assistant Nurse Manager (ANM) for the Crisis Receiving Stabilization Center (CRSC) within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Assistant Nurse Manager (ANM) is to be responsible for supervising the provision and management of patient care services for an assigned shift or unit on a consistent basis. The ANM serves as a resource for nursing care across the system on an as needed basis and works with other healthcare professionals to optimize patient outcomes. The ANM promotes quality patient care, patient safety and customer satisfaction. The ANM serves as the resource person for staff in explaining and executing policy and procedure. The ANM functions as a member of the interdisciplinary team; participates in quality improvement activities, educational activities and supports research endeavors. The role is consistent with the scope and standards outlined by the American Psychiatric Nurses Association for Psychiatric-Mental Health Nursing.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Assures the completion of admission nursing assessment and on-going risk assessments in accordance with specific unit standards and regulatory requirements.</li><li>Supervises staff in assessing, planning, implementing and evaluating delivery of care.</li><li>Collaborates with treatment teams, clients, family and significant others in the development of individualized plans of care, on an as needed basis in an effort to promote wellness and recovery.</li><li>Assists with patient care responsibility when required.</li><li>Facilitates effective communication inter and intra departmentally to coordinate efforts, resolve operations problems and improve quality of patient care.</li><li>Assists in interpreting and translating the theoretical concepts of nursing into the delivery of nursing services for all age groups.</li><li>Plans and implements safe staffing based upon the defined staff plan.</li><li>Demonstrates respect and regard for the dignity of all patients, families, visitors and fellow employees to ensure a professional, responsible and courteous environment.</li></ul> UBHC - CRSC Newark RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8817 Newark NJ 25ST2089 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279985 2026-08-25T17:08:09-04:00 2026-08-25T17:08:09-04:00 Temporary Research Assistant (Research) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Temporary Research Assistant (Research) in the Department of Medicine – Infectious Disease within the New Jersey Medical School (NJMS).<br><br>The Temporary Assistant (Research) will perform data management and programming tasks. The data management tasks include using SAS programming language for quality assurance of collected data (clinical, laboratory, demographic), using Tableau software for creating and maintain dashboards, routine data management tasks for data transmitted from the international sites, manuscript development, proposal assistance and other relevant scientific activities.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>Works with Data Managers and research coordinators to develop SAS scripts for quality assurance and quality control activities.</li><li>Works with our staff and stakeholders to create ad hoc databases for analysis using programming language.</li><li>Creates and maintains interactive dashboards on Tableau under DOMC staff supervision.</li><li>Works with investigators, statisticians and study coordinators in design and set-up of case report forms (CRFs) for specific clinical, translational, and basic science protocols.</li><li>Assists study coordinators and data managers in preparing appropriate and detailed standard operating procedures, training manuals and other materials for study conduct and data collection in the clinic, field and laboratory.</li><li>Reviews incoming completed case report forms (CRFs) for accuracy and completion from the field sites.&nbsp;</li></ul> NJMS - Medicine Infectious Dis RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7442 Newark NJ 26ST1658 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277770 2026-06-25T11:14:52-04:00 2026-06-25T11:14:53-04:00 Technician I PT Days (multiple vacancies) UCHC Northern State Prison <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Full Time Technician I for Northern State Prison, located in Newark, NJ. The Technician I participates as a member of the clinical and administrative medical team at the Prison.<br><br>Among the duties for the position are:<br><br><br></div><ul><li>Takes vital signs, height and weight and documents in electronic medical records (EMR).</li><li>Assists the physician/associate practitioner with procedures, including preparing the inmate for the examination.</li><li>Obtains specimen collection and handling, including, but not limited to, drawing blood.</li><li>Assists with the cleaning, sterilization and securing of equipment within the Health Service Unit.</li><li>Maintains or assists in maintaining the supply stock in the Health Service Unit by ordering in a timely and appropriate manner.</li><li>Maintains the supply stock in the examination rooms.</li><li>Aggregates the orders of all medications and forwards to the pharmacy provider / local pharmacy.</li></ul> UCHC Northern State Prison Phy_DUP RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7679 Newark NJ 26ST0685 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275349 2026-05-19T08:37:09-04:00 2026-05-19T08:37:09-04:00 Myeloma Clinical Scholar, Faculty Physician (Associate/Professor) <div>Rutgers Cancer Institute seeks an <strong>mid- to senior-level academically oriented</strong> <strong>hematologist/oncologist</strong> for a clinical research position with a<strong> clinical focus in myeloma</strong>, a record of original clinical research, and exceptional clinical and leadership skills. Unique opportunities exist for collaborations between clinical enterprise at RWJ Barnabas Health and research programs at Rutgers Cancer Institute. Research programs at Rutgers Cancer Institute include: <a href=\"https://cinj.org/research/research-programs\"><strong>Cancer Metabolism and Immunology, Genomic Instability and Cancer Genetics, Cancer Pharmacology, Clinical Investigations and Precision Therapeutics, and Cancer Prevention and Control</strong></a><strong>. </strong>There are a broad range of teaching opportunities with medical students, house staff, and fellows. Academic rank (Associate Professor/Professor) and clinical research support commensurate with experience. <strong>Uniquely qualified candidates may be considered for additional leadership responsibilities as Section Head for Hematologic Malignancy.</strong><br><br></div><div>As a National Cancer Institute (NCI) Designated Comprehensive Cancer Center, Rutgers Cancer Institute is a leader in high-intensity cancer care, offering comprehensive hematology/oncology clinical programs. Partnering with RWJBarnabas Health, the state's largest health care delivery system, we provide sophisticated oncology care to patients close to home. This integrated cancer care model offers access to advanced diagnostic and treatment options, including clinical trials, immunotherapy, proton therapy, precision medicine, CAR T-cell therapy, and cardio-oncology. Become part of our innovative team and make history as we unveil the groundbreaking Jack and Sheryl Morris Cancer Center—a 12-story, 520,000 square foot freestanding cancer hospital, the first of its kind in New Jersey. Explore the state-of-the-art facility <a href=\"https://cinj.org/about-cinj/jack-sheryl-morris-cancer-center\"><strong>here</strong></a> and discover more about our groundbreaking initiatives at <a href=\"https://cinj.org/\"><strong>www.cinj.org</strong></a>.</div><div><br>The academic appointment will be within the Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School and located in New Brunswick, NJ. Faculty members are expected to support the educational goals of the school, engaging in teaching activities for medical students and residents, as well as delivering targeted lectures in their area of expertise.<br><br></div><div>Apply now and contribute to our commitment to excellence in patient care, research, and education! For questions on this position or to learn more about our available positions<strong>, </strong>please contact the Rutgers Cancer Institute Faculty Recruitment Office at <a href=\"mailto:facultyaffairs@cinj.rutgers.edu\"><strong>cinjcareers@rutgers.edu</strong></a>.<br><br><a href=\"https://www.cinj.org/about-cinj/faculty-opportunities\"><strong>See all our open faculty positions here</strong></a>!</div> CINJ - Medical Heme Malig RBHS Chancellor-L2 Cancer Institute of New Jersey-L3 7908 24FA1087 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266304 2025-12-31T09:48:20-05:00 2025-12-31T09:48:20-05:00 Postdoctoral Associate <div>The Abraira laboratory in the Dept. Cell Biology &amp; Neuroscience at Rutgers University is seeking a motivated and dedicated Postdoctoral Fellow to join our dynamic team studying the neuroscience of somatosensation, specifically utilizing mouse genetics. The selected candidate will have the unique opportunity to engage with cutting-edge research methodologies and techniques to decode the mysteries of the somatosensory system.</div> DLS - Keck Center New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 7061 25FA0717 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280147 2026-08-31T08:33:47-04:00 2026-08-31T08:33:48-04:00 Technician I PT Days UCHC SWSP Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Full Time Technician I for Southwoods State Prison, located in Bridgeton, NJ. The Technician I participates as a member of the clinical and administrative medical team at the Prison.<br><br>Among the duties for the position are:<br><br>Takes vital signs, height and weight and documents in electronic medical records (EMR).</div><ul><li>Assists the physician/associate practitioner with procedures, including preparing the inmate for the examination.</li><li>Obtains specimen collection and handling, including, but not limited to, drawing blood.</li><li>Assists with the cleaning, sterilization and securing of equipment within the Health Service Unit.</li><li>Maintains or assists in maintaining the supply stock in the Health Service Unit by ordering in a timely and appropriate manner.</li><li>Maintains the supply stock in the examination rooms.</li><li>Aggregates the orders of all medications and forwards to the pharmacy provider / local pharmacy.</li></ul> UCHC-South Woods Psn-Ancillary RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7685 Bridgeton NJ 26ST0547 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278561 2026-07-10T10:33:25-04:00 2026-07-10T10:33:26-04:00 Technician I PT Eves UCHC ADTC <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Part Time UCHC Technician I for the Adult Diagnostic Treatment Center located in Avenel, NJ. The UCHC Technician I participates as a member of the clinical and administrative medical team at the Prison.<br><br>Among the duties for this position are:<br><br></div><ul><li>Takes vital signs, height and weight and documents in electronic medical records (EMR).</li><li>Assists the physician/associate practitioner with procedures, including preparing the inmate for the examination.</li><li>Obtains specimen collection and handling, including, but not limited to, drawing blood.</li><li>Assists with the cleaning, sterilization and securing of equipment within the Health Service Unit. Maintains or assists in maintaining the supply stock in the Health Service Unit by ordering in a timely and appropriate manner.</li><li>Maintains the supply stock in the examination rooms.</li><li>Aggregates the orders of all medications and forwards to the pharmacy provider / local pharmacy.</li></ul> UCHC Adult Treatment Center Ph RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7674 Avenel NJ 26ST0906 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/268102 2026-01-27T19:49:45-05:00 2026-01-27T19:49:46-05:00 Tenured or Tenure-Track Open Rank Faculty Position, Basic/Translational Science, in the Rutgers Addiction Research Center/ Brain Health Institute <div>The Brain Health Institute (BHI; <a href=\"https://brainhealthinstitute.rutgers.edu\"><strong>https://brainhealthinstitute.rutgers.edu</strong></a>) and Rutgers Addiction Research Center (RARC; <a href=\"https://addiction.rutgers.edu\"><strong>https://addiction.rutgers.edu</strong></a>) are recruiting a tenured or tenure track faculty member at Assistant/Associate/Professor level to expand our research portfolio in the basic/translational science of substance use disorders, broadly defined to include preclinical or human subjects-based research programs. The specific area of research is open, and can include but is not limited to animal behavior, animal or human psychopharmacology, neuroimaging, biomarker development, and/or interventions development/therapeutics.<br><br>The RARC, an initiative of the BHI, is an academic research center that brings together researchers from across the Rutgers campuses, medical schools, and health systems for collaborative, interdisciplinary work focused on tackling addiction. With over 150 faculty who work across the domains of Basic Science; Epidemiology, Etiology, &amp; Prevention; Treatment &amp; Recovery; and Public Policy, the RARC is the only comprehensive addiction center in New Jersey. The RARC creates opportunities for collaboration and community, bringing together faculty with a passion for innovative, cross-disciplinary research who are employing cutting edge approaches. These activities are supported by the largest university-based human cell and DNA repository in the world as well as recently established centers focused on human brain imaging, computational neuroscience, gene editing, etc.</div> Brain Health Institute RBHS Chancellor-L2 Brain Health Institute-L3 8146 22FA1093 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280314 2026-09-02T09:28:37-04:00 2026-09-02T09:28:39-04:00 Post Doctoral Associate (Multi-omics Life Course Research) <div>The Department of Biostatistics and Epidemiology at the Rutgers School of Public Health located in Piscataway, NJ is seeking a Post Doctoral Associate to join an interdisciplinary research program focused on pregnancy, life-course cardiometabolic health, and the developmental origins of health and disease.<br><br></div><div>The Post Doctoral Associate will work with longitudinal pregnancy and birth cohort data to investigate how metabolic and molecular characteristics during pregnancy contribute to maternal and offspring health across the life course. Current projects integrate epidemiologic data with metabolomics, proteomics, and other high-dimensional molecular measures to study pregnancy cardiovascular health, adverse pregnancy outcomes, placental biology, and later cardiometabolic disease.<br><br></div><div>The associate will have opportunities to lead manuscripts, develop independent research questions, contribute to NIH-funded and collaborative studies, present findings at scientific meetings, and participate in grant development. The position will provide training and mentorship in life-course epidemiology, pregnancy and perinatal epidemiology, and the analysis of high-dimensional molecular data.<br><br></div><div>This is a 12-month full-funded position, with additional years dependent on funding and satisfactory performance.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Lead analyses of longitudinal epidemiologic and molecular data.</li><li>Develop and apply statistical approaches for metabolomics, proteomics, and related high-dimensional data.</li><li>Prepare first-author manuscripts and scientific presentations.</li><li>Collaborate with epidemiologists, biostatisticians, clinicians, and laboratory scientists.</li></ul> SPH - Epidemiology RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Public Health-L3 7710 Piscataway NJ 26ST1608 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279120 2026-07-27T11:45:56-04:00 2026-07-27T11:45:57-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Postdoctoral Associate for the Brain Health Institute (BHI) within Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences (RBHS).<br><br>The primary purpose of the Postdoctoral Associate is to work on research project investigating the neural mechanisms of sensory perception, learning, and decision-making. The laboratory uses state-of-the-art behavioral, neurophysiological, circuit, and computational approaches to examine neural activity in awake-behaving rodents performing auditory and audiovisual tasks. These approaches include high-channel count silicon-probe electrophysiology, optogenetics and opto-tagging, viral circuit tools, anatomical tract tracing, immunohistochemistry and imaging, and quantitative analysis of behavioral and neural data. The Postdoctoral Associate will perform research on cortical and downstream circuit mechanisms that support sensory-guided behavior using psychophysical training, in vivo multichannel recordings, circuit perturbations, histological validation, and computational analysis.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Trains and tests rodents (gerbils) on auditory and audiovisual psychophysical tasks to assess auditory perception, learning, and decision-making.</li><li>Performs anatomical tract tracing, AAV-based labeling, immunohistochemistry, imaging, and analyses of the neural circuits involved in auditory processing and decision-making.</li><li>Performs stereotaxic surgical procedures, including craniotomies, implants, viral injections, and related recovery and animal care procedures.</li><li>Performs high-channel-count in vivo electrophysiological recordings in awake-behaving animals, including silicon probe and optogenetic/opto-tagging approaches.</li><li>Performs research using viral transfection and circuit manipulation techniques, including optogenetics and designer receptors exclusively activated by designer drugs (DREADDs), as appropriate to the project.</li><li>Develops and applies computational workflows for electrophysiology, imaging, and behavioral data analysis using Python, MATLAB, ImageJ/FIJI, DeepLabCut, or related tools.</li><li>Maintains accurate records of experimentation, animal procedures, data analysis, and research progress.</li><li>Analyzes, organizes, and presents data at laboratory meetings, departmental seminars, and major scientific meetings; contributes to manuscript and grant preparation.</li></ul> Brain Health Institute RBHS Chancellor-L2 Brain Health Institute-L3 8146 Piscataway NJ 26ST1257 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/271802 2026-03-26T20:20:20-04:00 2026-03-26T20:20:21-04:00 Rutgers Business School - Nwk and NB - Adjunct Summer 2027 <div>The Rutgers Business School at Rutgers – Newark and New Brunswick is accepting applications for part-time instructors for the Summer 2027 term, with courses beginning in May 2027 to August 2027. We are seeking qualified candidates who will contribute to the University’s educational mission, as well as the academic objectives and goals of the Rutgers Business School, combining learning and enterprise.</div><div><br></div><div>Our academic units and programs consist of Accounting and Information Systems, Administrative Studies, Finance and Economics, Marketing, Business Fashion, Management and Global Business, Management Systems and Information Science, Supply Chain Management, Healthcare Analytics and Intelligence, Information Technology and Analytics, Quantitative Finance, Business Innovation, Executive MBA, MBA programs (various concentrations), Doctoral Programs, International Programs…just to name a few.<br><br>Successful candidates will be responsible for the following:</div><ul><li>Instructing/Co-instructing courses at the graduate and/or undergraduate level (may include traditional lecture, hybrid, and/or fully online courses)</li><li>Prepare course materials (e.g., syllabi, presentations, hand-outs, reading materials, etc.)</li><li>Provide advisement and constructive feedback to students as well as instruction regarding student work and academic standards</li><li>Respond to student emails and inquiries</li><li>Adhere to grade submission policies and deadlines</li><li>Adhere to University policies and regulations</li><li>Practice innovative educational methodology</li></ul> Human Resources Newark Newark Chancellor-L2 Rutgers Business School-L3 6942 26FA0294 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279546 2026-08-12T14:55:15-04:00 2026-08-12T14:55:15-04:00 Post-Doc Jain Lab <div>We have an exciting opportunity to join our team as a Postdoc.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>A full-time Postdoc position is available in the lab of Dr. Devanshi Jain in the Genetics Department at Rutgers University, New Jersey. We study germline development, specifically molecular mechanisms of the meiotic cell cycle. Our work involves genetic mouse models, combined with molecular, cellular, and biochemical analyses.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>A successful candidate will work closely with the principal investigator as well as other members of the lab. Successful applicants must be highly motivated and passionate about research, be able to independently lead a research project, have excellent communication skills, and work efficiently and collaboratively as part of a team.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>We request a minimum 2-year commitment. PhD in genetics/molecular/cell biology field is required.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Jain Lab website: https://thejainlab.org</div> Human Genetics Institute of NJ New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 8177 26FA0712 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279769 2026-08-20T09:53:15-04:00 2026-08-20T09:53:16-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate <div><strong>A postdoctoral position</strong> is immediately available to study cell metabolism in liver diseases and liver cancer. The projects are built upon our publications on nitrogen metabolism and ammonia handling in several cancer types (PMID: 26603296, 31665640, 36256480, 41512056). This position will have the opportunity to gain strong training in cancer metabolism, cell growth signaling, and mouse models. The position is aiming at publishing high-profile papers and pursuing an independent career. Candidates with strong motivation and a Ph.D. background in molecular biology/cell biology/biochemistry are encouraged to apply.<br><br></div><div>Applicants may apply to this job posting and include a cover letter, CV, and the names and contacts of three references. <strong>Questions should be directed to</strong>: Wei-Xing Zong, PhD, Department of Chemical Biology, the Cancer Institute of New Jersey, Rutgers University, 164 Frelinghuysen Road, Piscataway, New Jersey 08854. <br><strong>Email:</strong> zongwx@pharmacy.rutgers.edu.</div><div><strong>Lab website:</strong> https://sites.rutgers.edu/wei-xing-zong/</div> Chemical Biology RBHS Chancellor-L2 Ernest Mario School of Pharmac-L3 6717 26FA0287 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277319 2026-06-17T10:47:54-04:00 2026-06-17T10:47:55-04:00 Clerical Assistant <div>Rutgers University–Newark (RU-N), an urban public research university and anchor institution located in Newark, New Jersey, a city of promise, is seeking a Clerical Assistant. Reporting to the Chief of Staff and Vice Chancellor, this position provides general clerical and office support to ensure the smooth day-to-day operations of the unit. The role supports calendar coordination, front office coverage, and routine administrative functions, while maintaining a professional and customer-focused environment.<br><br></div><div>This position is responsible for, but not limited to, the following:</div><ul><li>Provides calendar and scheduling support for assigned principal(s), including coordinating meetings, managing appointments, and maintaining accurate calendars</li><li>Serves as the first point of contact for the office, greeting visitors and responding to routine inquiries in a professional and welcoming manner</li><li>Assists with basic meeting logistics, including scheduling space and preparing meeting materials as needed</li><li>Maintains kitchen and general office supply inventory, ensuring shared spaces are organized, stocked, and operational</li><li>Coordinates routine supply orders and monitors inventory levels in accordance with established procedures</li><li>Provides clerical support, including filing, organizing documents, and performing basic data entry tasks</li><li>Supports general office operations and assists with routine administrative tasks as assigned</li><li>Performs duties with professionalism and handles information in accordance with university policies and guidelines</li></ul> Newark Chancellor Newark Chancellor-L2 Newark Chancellor-L3 6602 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274113 2026-05-01T08:44:54-04:00 2026-05-01T08:44:54-04:00 Lecturers, UG Liberal Studies <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the Faculty of Arts &amp; Sciences, Undergraduate Liberal Studies Department, seeks new lecturers to teach various topics within the discipline for courses in Fall 2026, Winter, 2027, Spring 2027, and/or Summer 2027.The instructor will present course material during the assigned course times, hold office hours, administer exams, assign grades, and coordinate any other requirements related to course instruction.</div> English Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 6762 26FA0436 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266087 2025-12-31T09:25:08-05:00 2025-12-31T09:25:09-05:00 Associate Professor of Transplant & Hepatobiliary Surgery <div>The Department of Surgery at Rutgers New Jersey Medical School is actively recruiting an Experienced Abdominal Transplant Surgeon for a full time faculty position. Independent Experience in Liver Transplant is required. In addition mastery in organ procurement including donation after circulatory death is required. Experience in Normothermic Regional Perfusion and Machine Perfusion is desirable. Clinical and Translational research interests and experience is also desirable. Academic rank and additional leadership opportunities commensurate with experience and accomplishments.<br><br>&nbsp;Opportunities to participate in Renal and Pancreas Transplant are secondary and available in affiliated programs in the RWJ Barnabas Health System.&nbsp; Rutgers University is an ADA, AA/EEO employer. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, citizenship, disability or protected veteran status. Interested candidates should submit a current CV, your complete contact information, and contact information for four professional references to the email address below. Personal statements summarizing teaching experience, clinical and research interests, and contributions to diversity are encouraged.</div> NJMS - Surgery RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7495 25FA0760 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280061 2026-08-27T08:52:50-04:00 2026-08-27T08:52:51-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Post-Doctoral Associate in the Public Health Research Institute within the New Jersey Medical School (NJMS).<br><br>Under the direction of the Principal Investigator, the Post-Doctoral Associate conducts studies of the mechanism of fungal pathogenesis and fungal vaccine research in the human fungal pathogen Cryptococcus neoformans. By applying molecular biology, biochemistry and Immunology, will aim to investigate the molecular basis of Cryptococcus-host interactions and characterize fungal antigen-mediated immune protection with a goal to develop novel antifungal vaccines. The Postdoctoral Associate will design and conduct highly specialized molecular research in the area of Cryptococcus pathogenesis and immunology under the direction of the Principal Investigator. Collecting data and preparing reports for peer- reviewed scientific publications and conference presentations, and contributes to the writing of grants.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>Conducts research activities on projects to investigate the molecular mechanisms of Cryptococcus-host interactions, focusing on identification and characterization of antigens required for vaccine-mediated protection and fungal pathogenesis, independently or as assigned, followed by appropriate reports, recommendations and conclusions.</li><li>Interfaces with internal and external collaborators on the research projects.</li><li>Generates, compiles and presents statistical data with appropriate conclusions, recommendations, etc. pertinent to research activity.</li><li>Assists with training new students and visitors in research area focused on Cryptococcus pathogenesis and fungal immunology.</li><li>Oversees daily research lab operations within the Lab.</li><li>Keeps abreast of all pertinent federal, state and Rutgers’ regulations, laws and policies as they presently exist and as they change or are modified.&nbsp;</li></ul> NJMS - PHRI Center RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7422 Newark NJ 26ST1670 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278288 2026-07-06T14:09:16-04:00 2026-07-06T14:09:17-04:00 Research Teaching Specialist V <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Research Teaching Specialist V within the section of Pediatric Population Science at the Rutgers Cancer Institute, Division of Pediatric Hematology/Oncology.<br><br>Under direct supervision of the Principal Investigator, the purpose of the Research Teaching Specialist V position is to engage in research lab activities. The Research Teaching Specialist V will support highly specialized and technical research within the lab.<br><br>Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Participates in aspects of research and ensures compliance with study protocols. Monitors progress of projects. Reports to the Principal Investigator on project progress, problems, and the need for adjustments.</li><li>Supports recruitment, screening, enrollment, and consenting of participants for studies per project timelines. Ensures participant completion of study activities per protocol. Maintains study recruitment, accrual, and participation documents.</li><li>Assists with creating surveys using survey software programs as directed. Under the direction of the PI, abstracts information from medical records per protocol, maintaining confidentiality of data.</li><li>As directed, engages in data collection, including conducting semi-structured qualitative interviews and administering surveys per study protocol.</li><li>Supports study data entry, data management, preliminary data screening, and data cleaning throughout the project, as assigned.</li><li>As directed, provides support in other data processing and analysis. Prepares reports containing findings, analysis, conclusion and recommendations (i.e., grants, summaries, etc.), as requested.</li><li>Enhances recruitment and data collection efforts given participants’ busy schedules, research activities may require flexible (i.e., evening or weekend) activities on occasion per project demands. Any changes to the work schedule will be discussed with the PIs in advance.</li><li>Assists with progress reports, administrative, regulatory, and study accrual/progress updates for all assigned studies.</li><li>Under the instruction of the Principal Investigator, drafts materials for IRB submissions and renewals.</li><li>Under the direction of the Principal Investigator, supports targeted literature searches.</li><li>Helps maintain the lab website.</li><li>As directed, provides support in the preparation of presentations and assists in the preparation of manuscripts and grants.</li></ul> CINJ - Pediatric Population Sc RBHS Chancellor-L2 Cancer Institute of New Jersey-L3 8187 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1420 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266433 2026-01-04T21:35:58-05:00 2026-01-04T21:35:59-05:00 Lecturers, Data Science <div>The Graduate Program in Data Science at Rutgers University-Camden seeks new lecturers for Spring 2026 and/or Summer 2026 semester(s) to teach various Data Science related courses at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. For any assigned course, the instructor will be required to create an up to date, inclusive syllabus and curriculum, present course material during the assigned course times, hold regular office hours, administer assessments and exams, assign grades, and coordinate with the graduate program director any other requirements related to course instruction.</div> Mathematics Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 6765 25FA1013 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280204 2026-08-31T12:46:24-04:00 2026-08-31T12:46:25-04:00 Director, Marketing & Communications <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Director, Marketing &amp; Communications for the Undergraduate Admissions Office within the Division of Enrollment Management. Reporting to the Interim Co-Executive Director of Undergraduate Admissions (and ultimately to the Assistant Vice Chancellor for Enrollment Management), the Director of Marketing &amp; Communications serves as a member of the Undergraduate Admissions leadership team and plays a critical role in achieving annual and long-term enrollment goals.</div><div><br></div><div>Among the key duties of the position are the following:</div><ul><li>Serves as the division's senior marketing strategist for undergraduate recruitment, collaborating with university partners to ensure brand alignment, effective audience engagement, and the achievement of enrollment priorities.</li><li>Leads a fast-paced team responsible for delivering a high volume and diverse portfolio of outreach and engagement initiatives, including an email campaign comprising more than 2,500 communications annually, print publications, interactive presentations, web content, social media, and digital marketing.</li><li>Develops and implements a cohesive, distinctive marketing and communications strategy from concept through execution and delivery.</li><li>Cultivates data-informed, high-impact, and results-oriented marketing practices that support the recruitment and enrollment of an increasingly talented and diverse student body.</li><li>Advances and executes marketing and communication strategies designed to engage and strengthen relationships with key audiences, including prospective students, applicants, admitted students, enrolling students, parents and families, school counselors, educators, and internal stakeholders.</li><li>Collaborates with other Enrollment Management units to develop and implement communications initiatives that advance divisional priorities, support student success, promote operational objectives, and ensure a consistent and coordinated Enrollment Management message.</li><li>Establishes a culture of accountability through the use of analytics and performance metrics, ensuring continuous improvement and alignment with institutional enrollment objectives.</li><li>Identifies and leverages market trends and emerging communications channels, continuously evolving Undergraduate Admissions' outreach and marketing strategies to remain innovative and competitive.</li><li>Leads, supervises, and develops a team of marketing and communications professionals and oversees the Marketing &amp; Communications budget.</li></ul> Undergraduate Admissions - NB New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Enrollment Management Admin NB-L3 8379 Piscataway NJ 26ST1627 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278702 2026-07-13T09:05:13-04:00 2026-07-13T09:05:14-04:00 Manager, Information Systems & Technology (Infrastructure) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Manager, Information Systems &amp; Technology (Infrastructure) within the Information Systems and Technology Department at the Rutgers Cancer Institute.<br><br>The Manager, Information Systems &amp; Technology (Infrastructure) collaborates with researchers, IT staff, and external partners to evaluate and implement technologies that enhance research productivity. This position is accountable for maintaining service reliability, driving infrastructure improvements, and supporting emerging technology needs across the Rutgers Cancer Institute.<br><br>Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Participates in strategic planning, management, deployment and development of appropriate resources to optimize infrastructure, project, and support services for all research technologies and systems, including server infrastructure, scientific instruments, high performance computing, AI, and cloud computing infrastructure and services.</li><li>Administers and maintains enterprise storage and server infrastructure, including platforms such as Box and RDS, ensuring high availability, optimal performance, and data security through proactive system upgrades, patch management, and vulnerability remediation in compliance with established security standards.</li><li>Identifies financial resources needed for projects. Provides budget reports and updates as needed to department leadership and assists with budget oversight to optimize fiscal resources.</li><li>Serves as the primary liaison with Rutgers OIT and OARC teams while providing senior-level technical guidance and escalation support and designing scalable infrastructure solutions to meet research and operational needs.</li><li>Governs data lifecycle management for RCI systems, ensuring secure access, transmission, and storage of data in compliance with institutional policies and federal regulations, including HIPAA.</li><li>Recommends and participates in creating new IST policies and procedures for research technology operations, including change management and contingency planning. Ensures compliance with current policies and procedures, educates and trains as necessary.</li><li>Creates and maintains standard operating procedures (SOP’s) as they relate to systems, redundancy, standard operations, and disaster recovery.</li><li>Provides technical support and troubleshooting for research technology systems and infrastructure.</li><li>Recommends staffing needs including the hiring, firing, promoting, demoting, performance evaluations, transfers and/or disciplining of employees, as well as other personnel actions according to University policies and procedures.</li><li>Develops and maintain disaster recovery and business continuity plans for research technology operations.</li><li>Conducts periodic testing of contingency plans to ensure they remain effective and up-to-date.</li><li>Oversees relevant purchasing, contractual and fiscal activities with external vendors to ensure proper vendor project performance and compliance.</li><li>Stays abreast of the latest server/cloud technologies.</li></ul> CINJ - IST Central Core RBHS Chancellor-L2 Cancer Institute of New Jersey-L3 7933 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1511 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274064 2026-04-30T12:51:30-04:00 2026-04-30T12:51:30-04:00 Lecturers, Teacher Education <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the Faculty of Arts and Sciences, Education and Teacher Prep Department, seeks new lecturers to teach various topics within the discipline for courses in Fall 2026, Winter 2027, Spring 2027 and/or Summer 2027. The instructor will present course material during the assigned course times, hold office hours, administer exams, assign grades, and coordinate any other requirements related to course instruction.</div> Education Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 6761 26FA0418 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266015 2025-12-31T09:13:53-05:00 2025-12-31T09:13:54-05:00 Clinical Instructor (Part-Time) <div>The Department of Restorative Dentistry at Rutgers School of Dental Medicine is seeking PART-TIME general dentists for a faculty position at the rank of Clinical Instructor. The successful candidate will have a .20 FTE - .40 FTE commitment to teaching. Specific responsibilities include participation in both didactic and clinical teaching of Restorative Dentistry (Operative Dentistry, Fixed Prosthodontics, and Removable Prosthodontics) to our pre-doctoral dental students, as well as participation in other predoctoral educational programs of the Department. The successful candidate will possess strong leadership and teamwork skills.<br><br></div><div>Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Interviews of qualified candidates will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.<br><br></div><div><strong>Essential Duties and Responsibilities:</strong></div><div>· Clinical Teaching</div><div>· Preclinical Laboratory Teaching</div><div>· Seminars</div><div>· Lectures</div><div>· Other duties as assigned by Chair</div> RSDM - Restorative Dentistry RBHS Chancellor-L2 Rutgers School of Dental Medic-L3 7550 22FA0793 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279740 2026-08-20T08:46:32-04:00 2026-08-20T08:46:33-04:00 Technician I FT Eves UCHC GSYCF <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Full Time Technician I for Garden State Youth Correctional Facility located in Yardville, NJ. The Technician I participates as a member of the clinical and administrative medical team at the Prison.<br><br>Among the duties for the position are:<br><br></div><ul><li>Takes vital signs, height and weight and documents in electronic medical records (EMR).</li><li>Assists the physician/associate practitioner with procedures, including preparing the inmate for the examination.</li><li>Obtains specimen collection and handling, including, but not limited to, drawing blood.</li><li>Assists with the cleaning, sterilization and securing of equipment within the Health Service Unit.</li><li>Maintains or assists in maintaining the supply stock in the Health Service Unit by ordering in a timely and appropriate manner.</li><li>Maintains the supply stock in the examination rooms.</li><li>Aggregates the orders of all medications and forwards to the pharmacy provider / local pharmacy.</li></ul> UCHC Garden State Youth Nursin RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7690 Yardville NJ 26ST0188 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280039 2026-08-26T14:10:37-04:00 2026-08-26T14:10:38-04:00 Screening Clinician <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Screening Clinician for the Acute Psychiatric Services (APS) within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Screening Clinician position is to perform psychiatric emergency services, screening, and screening outreach assessments as well as other mental health services. Demonstrates competence in providing generic crisis assessment of individuals of all ages (birth through 65+ years) and in determining the need for any additional professional consultation. Demonstrates competence in devising an appropriate intervention/disposition plan.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Identifies the appropriate level of care disposition from skill based knowledge of the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, Fifth Edition (DSM-5) criteria, clinical expertise, and departmental criteria.</li><li>Serves assigned shifts providing on-site, outreach screening and commitment evaluations in an effective and skillful manner.</li><li>Utilizes person, family and agency information to determine an appropriate screening outcome for persons served.</li><li>Completes all documentation within required timeframe.</li><li>Maintains comprehensive and up-to-date knowledge of eligibility and admission criteria for units, programs, and contracts served by the department.</li><li>Effectively contributes to and supports an environment that enhances the positive self-image of persons served and preserves their human dignity.</li><li>Actively and enthusiastically participates and contributes to smooth functioning and operations of unit.</li><li>Maintains the level of competency necessary to be able to conduct the initial evaluations of the commitment process.</li><li>Regularly attends and participates in in-service meetings and other designated training events that will enhance clinical skills, as documented by continuing education reports.</li><li>Keeps abreast of developments in theory and technique related to the field as indicted by contributions to discussions in clinical meetings.</li></ul> UBHC - Emergency Screening Psy RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8029 Piscataway NJ 25ST2465 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277998 2026-06-30T10:21:07-04:00 2026-06-30T10:21:08-04:00 Business System Analyst II <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Business System Analyst II in the Enterprise Applications &amp; Research Computing (EARC) with the Office of Information Technology (OIT).<br><br>The Business System Analyst II provides oversight, planning, and support of the Document Management (Perceptive Content, Docusign) and Banner SIS suite of applications and integrations with other University systems. Serves as a liaison between the business community and the OIT organization to provide solutions to meet user needs and drive process efficiency and collaboration. Possesses expertise in the business units supported and understands their operations as well as the OIT organization’s systems and capabilities. Reviews, analyzes, and evaluates business systems and user needs. Identifies system and business process strengths and weaknesses to determine opportunities to automate processes and functions. Gathers and documents high level business requirements into functional specifications for the OIT organization and manages changes to such specifications. Documents requirements, defines scope and objectives, and formulates systems to parallel overall business strategies. Assists in the business redesign and documentation as needed for new technology. Educates the OIT organization on the direction of the business. Negotiates agreements and commitments by facilitating communication between business units and OIT, from initial requirements to final implementation. Possesses an understanding of technological trends and uses this knowledge to bring solutions to the business units supported in to enhance the enterprise’s competitive edge. May make recommendations for buy versus build decisions.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Work with University departments to understand their requirements through site visits, interviews, analysis, and documentation. Include in consulting with the business, considerations of legal, security, and compliance requirements.</li><li>Leads the gathering and assessment of clients’ IT business needs and requirements, providing gap and future recommendations to improve business processes and efficiency. Is proactive in understanding clients’ processes, key drivers/measures of success, and the short-/long-term direction of technology.</li><li>Acts as the clients’ liaison with OIT—and with outside vendors, contractors and consultants—to define and establish IT service and support requirements. Facilitates interaction between stakeholders and actively resolves conflicts.</li><li>Advocates for the technology needs of the client. Builds OIT’s understanding of clients’ strategies, goals and processes; and communicates OIT’s technology strategies, plans and status to clients along with information on emerging technologies.</li><li>Analyzes and identifies the operational and financial impacts of new solutions and service requests, including the value to OIT and the return-on-investment for the University.</li></ul> Enterprise Application Service EVP & Chief Admin Officer OIT - VP & Chief Information O-L3 6882 Somerset NJ 26ST1423 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275701 2026-05-22T07:16:03-04:00 2026-05-22T07:16:03-04:00 Dining Services Student Worker (Woody's) <div>Join the Rutgers Dining team as a Dining Services Student Worker in one of our dining halls or retail operations across the New Brunswick, Piscataway and Camden campuses. Rutgers Dining Services strives to be the best in culinary excellence and as a Dining Services Worker you play a critical role in the customer experience. From assisting in the preparation and service of food, to maintaining the presentation of the dining halls, to assisting guests, we have a variety of roles and will find the right one for you!<br><br>Dining Service Workers earn a paycheck and more:</div><ul><li>Student employee meal privileges</li><li>Flexible schedules (10-20 hours/week) that work around your classes and activities</li><li>Convenient on-campus locations</li><li>Valuable work experience to add to your resume</li><li>Learn important job skills including interpersonal communications, team dynamics, dependability and time management</li><li>A fun and welcoming environment</li></ul> Woody's New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Student Affairs - New Brunswic-L3 6680 Piscataway NJ 26ST1141 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266355 2025-12-31T09:53:25-05:00 2025-12-31T09:53:26-05:00 Post-Doctoral Associate <div>The Center for Advanced Infrastructure and Transportation is conducting research to develop durable, sustainable, resilient and smart transportation infrastructure. We are currently accepting applications for a Postdoctoral Associate position in these research areas.</div><div><br>The successful candidate will report to Prof. Hao Wang and Prof. Nenad Gucunski at CAIT and will work independently associated with different projects related to non-destructive testing and evaluation of civil infrastructure. The candidate is expected to perform both fundamental and applied researches and need publish research findings in journal and conferences. The candidate will also assist in the development and writing of research proposals for external funding</div> Advanced Infrastructure Center New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Engineering-L3 6709 25FA0694 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280175 2026-08-31T10:12:30-04:00 2026-08-31T10:12:31-04:00 Principal Secretary <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Principal Secretary for the Expanded Food and Nutrition Education Program (EFNEP). Reporting to the Program Associate I of the Camden County Expanded Food and Nutrition Education Program (EFNEP), the Principal Secretary facilitates the orderly and timely flow of daily documents; organizes and performs diversified office duties in a high volume, fast-paced environment, including confidential clerical support for the NJ EFNEP Camden County Office. The Principal Secretary will be housed in the Camden County Cooperative Extension Office.</div><div><br>Among the key duties of the position are the following:</div><ul><li>Manages multiple tasks with accuracy.</li><li>Arranges meetings and associated logistics.</li><li>Prepares written communications and compiles documents for evaluation reporting.</li><li>Responds to internal and external inquiries.</li><li>Greets and directs visitors to proper destination; arranges schedules, appointments, and reservations.</li><li>Distributes mail, takes dictation and maintains records and files.</li><li>Aids clerical back-up-support (in-line with the realm of this position’s duties) for all secretarial lines for the NJ EFNEP work units on an as-needed basis, (i.e., in the case of Secretarial staff shortages due to illness, vacations, etc.).</li><li>Provides confidential and coordinating secretarial/clerical support to a university administrator or office.</li><li>Designs word processing routines to access, manipulate, and transmit files for specific uses. Performs a variety of additional advanced and basic word processing assignments.</li></ul> EFNEP New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 6972 Camden NJ 26ST1043 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278612 2026-07-10T12:39:53-04:00 2026-07-10T12:39:54-04:00 Technician I PT Days UCHC NJSP (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Part Time Technician I for New Jersey State Prison, located in Trenton., NJ. The Technician I participates as a member of the clinical and administrative medical team at the Prison.<br><br>Among the duties for the position are:<br><br><br></div><ul><li>Takes vital signs, height and weight and documents in electronic medical records (EMR).</li><li>Assists the physician/associate practitioner with procedures, including preparing the inmate for the examination.</li><li>Obtains specimen collection and handling, including, but not limited to, drawing blood.</li><li>Assists with the cleaning, sterilization and securing of equipment within the Health Service Unit.</li><li>Maintains or assists in maintaining the supply stock in the Health Service Unit by ordering in a timely and appropriate manner.</li><li>Maintains the supply stock in the examination rooms.</li><li>Aggregates the orders of all medications and forwards to the pharmacy provider / local pharmacy.</li></ul> UCHC New Jersey State Prison A RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7683 Trenton NJ 26ST0881 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/268858 2026-02-09T13:56:09-05:00 2026-02-09T13:56:10-05:00 Ophthalmologist - Comprehensive <div>The Institute of Ophthalmology and Visual Science at Rutgers New Jersey Medical School invites applications for a Comprehensive Ophthalmologist to assist with the general eye clinic. Rank and salary are commensurate with experience. We seek individuals with strong clinical expertise, commitment to resident education, and commitment to the development of a nationally recognized program in clinical and/or translational research. The institute is a highly productive clinical and academic enterprise with ~75% of faculty members at or above accredited, outstanding residency training program, has a catchment area that includes New Jersey, and serves a level 1 trauma center (University Hospital).</div> NJMS - Ophthalmology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7456 26FA0089 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280389 2026-09-03T12:21:43-04:00 2026-09-03T12:21:44-04:00 Mental Health Specialist III - Part Time <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a part-time Mental Health Specialist III for the Child &amp; Adolescent Services – Partial Hospitalization within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Partial Hospital Mental Health Specialist III position is to provide daily direct care services to the program’s consumers as directed by the unit supervisor. Demonstrates competence in recognizing the unique needs and behaviors of children with emotional and/or developmental needs. Provides appropriate assistance and renders service in accordance with UBHC policies and procedure in a culturally competent and Person Centered manner. Actively participates in crisis interventions.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Engages consumer/patient in appropriate intervention based on service plan and supervisory directions.</li><li>Interacts and communicates with individuals served in a wellness and recovery focused manner.</li><li>Completes all required documentation within prescribed time frames as monitored by tracking reports.</li><li>Assists in facilitating concrete needs for students and parents and facilitates referral on an ongoing basis.</li><li>Documents interventions, and interactions with parents and students in accordance with unit policies.</li><li>Engages with students and families by supporting children and families’ community based activities, as demonstrated by attending social and recreational functions.</li></ul> UBHC - PH Child & Adolescent RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8058 Newark NJ 26ST1414 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279277 2026-08-03T10:41:19-04:00 2026-08-03T10:41:20-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Post-Doctoral Associate in the Department of Medicine within the New Jersey Medical School (NJMS).<br><br>Under the direction of the Principal Investigator, the Post-Doctoral Associate will conduct genetic, microbiological, biochemical and animal studies to identify compounds that inhibit or kill <em>Mycobacterium tuberculosis </em>and to better understand their targets and mechanisms of action. The Fellow will also investigate the cellular mechanisms of drug synergy in <em>M. tuberculosis.<br><br></em>Among the key duties of this position are the following:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>Uses conventional and novel methods including advanced robotics to screen libraries of M. tuberculosis for drug tolerance and drug resistance phenotypes.</li><li>Performs MIC testing, kill curves and other microbiological tests to characterize M. tuberculosis and other BSL2 and BSL3 pathogens including select agents.</li><li>Designs and tests novel prodrugs against tuberculosis and other BSL2 and BSL3 pathogens.</li><li>Performs genetic manipulations of M. tuberculosis and other mycobacteria including the development of resistant mutants, cloning, and gene knockouts.</li><li>Performs microbiological and genetic characterization different M. tuberculosis strains and M. tuberculosis mutants.</li><li>Performs biological experiments with inhibited M. tuberculosis.&nbsp;</li></ul> NJMS - Emerging Pathogen Affil RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7485 Newark NJ 26ST1584 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275934 2026-05-27T17:44:51-04:00 2026-05-27T17:44:51-04:00 Assistant Professor of Plastic Surgery <div>The Division of Plastic Surgery in the Department of Surgery at the Rutgers New Jersey Medical School is recruiting a fellowship trained plastic surgeon. The attending surgeon will be expected to support the clinical, academic, education, and research missions of the Division of Plastic &amp; Reconstructive Surgery, Department of Surgery, and Rutgers New Jersey Medical School.</div> NJMS - Surgery RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7495 26FA0495 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/272994 2026-04-15T11:24:33-04:00 2026-04-15T11:24:34-04:00 Assistant Professor - Cardiothoracic/Liver Transplant Anesthesiologist <div>The Department of Anesthesiology at Rutgers, New Jersey Medical School, seeks a full-time Cardiothoracic/Liver Transplant anesthesiologist for a non-tenure track position. The academic rank and administrative title will be determined based on the candidate’s qualifications. We offer a highly competitive compensation package, excellent benefits, and a robust retirement plan.<br><br></div><div>The attending anesthesiologist will work one-on-one with a senior resident in all cardiac/liver surgeries. Additionally, they will cover two operating rooms with the CRNAs/residents for non-cardiac cases.<br><br></div><div>Duties include providing on-site anesthesia services to adult patients undergoing cardiac and liver transplant surgeries at the University Hospital; intraoperative and didactic teaching of the residents; participation in Faculty Development programs; work collaboratively with the members of the surgical services both clinically and administratively; and engagement in research that forwards the discipline both academically and clinically.<br><br></div><div>Qualified applicants must: 1. Have a medical doctorate or equivalent, 2. Hold or be eligible for medical licensure in the state of New Jersey, and 3. Be a BC/BE Anesthesiologist.</div><div>The effective day of the appointment is August 1, 2026</div><div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmation Action Employer and is compliant with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Diversity as a core value of RBHS, embodies inclusiveness, mutual respect, and multiple perspectives and serves as a driver for excellence for achieving equity in health and health care. For more information, please visit <a href=\"http://recruitment.rutgers.edu/TheRUCommitment-2.htm\"><strong>http://recruitment.rutgers.edu/TheRUCommitment-2.htm</strong></a> and for the University’s commitment to equal employment opportunity and affirmative, please go to <a href=\"https://policies.rutgers.edu/sites/default/files/60.1.8%20-%20current.pdf\"><strong>https://policies.rutgers.edu/sites/default/files/60.1.8%20-%20current.pdf</strong></a>. <strong>We encourage applications from women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities.</strong></div><div>The University Hospital, a primary teaching hospital of the Rutgers New Jersey Medical School, is a widely recognized tertiary care center and Level 1 Trauma Center. Newark is a vibrant city in the larger New York area (20 minutes from Manhattan) surrounded by the idyllic communities of Northern New Jersey.</div> NJMS - Anesthesiology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7432 26FA0327 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/264764 2025-12-08T18:32:17-05:00 2025-12-08T18:32:17-05:00 CoAd Non-Teaching: AI in Rail Transportation <div>A researcher is being sought to support ongoing work to investigate the use of artificial intelligence (AI) in rail transportation applications from a strategic visioning perspective. The successful candidate must demonstrate a robust understanding of and experience with AI science, AI<br>applications in transportation infrastructure, and translating complex scientific topics into easy-to-understand summaries and visuals.<br><br></div> Advanced Infrastructure Center New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Engineering-L3 6709 25FA1230 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279627 2026-08-17T10:35:17-04:00 2026-08-17T10:35:18-04:00 Dining Services Worker B <div>Rutgers, The State University is seeking a Dining Services Worker B for Livingston Dining Commons.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Performs general food service utility duties in various dining hall facilities.</li><li>Assists cooks, bakers, and Dining Services supervisors in tasks involving sanitary food handling.</li><li>Provides dining room services, including cash register duties.</li></ul> Livingston Dining Commons New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Student Affairs - New Brunswic-L3 6676 Piscataway NJ 26ST1391 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279884 2026-08-24T13:59:54-04:00 2026-08-24T13:59:56-04:00 Military/Veteran Peer Support Specialist III Per Diem <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Military/Veteran Peer Support Specialist III (Per Diem) for the Military Services within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>Under the supervision, provides person centered, culturally competent, and “consumer friendly” services to individuals who contact the Call Center. Receives telephone, chat, and text requests for service, undertakes review of the service need of the caller or consumer, and responds by offering peer support and appropriate referrals and disposition.</div><div><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Provides “customer friendly” services, taking initiative in engaging individuals served in an empathic and concerned manner.&nbsp;</li><li>Provides direct care services consistent with philosophy of UBHC.</li><li>Reviews service requests/referrals for all populations, and responds in accordance with prescribed departmental procedures.&nbsp;</li><li>Documents contacts, interventions, and interactions with callers in a timely manner and in accordance with established policies.&nbsp;</li><li>Maintains knowledge of Center and Unit policies and procedures.</li><li>Demonstrates good work habits.</li></ul> UBHC - Military Services RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8040 Piscataway NJ 26ST1252 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277754 2026-06-25T10:57:53-04:00 2026-06-25T10:57:54-04:00 Technician I PT Eves UCHC EMCFW(Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Part Time Technician I for Edna Mahan Correctional Facility located in Clinton, NJ. The Technician I participates as a member of the clinical and administrative medical team at the Prison.<br><br>Among the duties for the position are:<br><br></div><ul><li>Takes vital signs, height and weight and documents in electronic medical records (EMR).</li><li>Assists the physician/associate practitioner with procedures, including preparing the inmate for the examination.</li><li>Obtains specimen collection and handling, including, but not limited to, drawing blood.</li><li>Assists with the cleaning, sterilization and securing of equipment within the Health Service Unit.</li><li>Maintains or assists in maintaining the supply stock in the Health Service Unit by ordering in a timely and appropriate manner.</li><li>Maintains the supply stock in the examination rooms.</li><li>Aggregates the orders of all medications and forwards to the pharmacy provider / local pharmacy</li></ul> UCHC-Edna Mahan Corr-Ancillary RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7682 Clinton NJ 26ST0573 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274932 2026-05-13T11:20:43-04:00 2026-05-13T11:20:44-04:00 Summer 2026: Lecturer, Educational Psychology <div>The Rutgers University, Graduate School of Education, invites applications for Lecturer (Formerly PTL) teaching positions in the department of Educational Psychology during the Summer 2026 Session (May 26, 2026 through August 12, 2026).<br><br>Successful applicants will instruct undergraduate or graduate level courses in at least one of the the following content areas:<br><br>-School Counseling and Counseling Psychology<br><br>-College Student Affairs and Higher Education<br><br>-Educational Psychology: Learning &amp; Cognition and/or Human Development<br><br>-Gifted Education<br><br>-Special Education<br><br>-Educational Statistics, Measurement, and/or Evaluation<br><br>Courses will be offered in a range of modalities beyond traditional settings, including hybrid and online formats. Course appointments are in the New Brunswick area, as well as, hybrid/online format.</div> Education Psychology New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Graduate School of Education-L3 6813 25FA0912 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266227 2025-12-31T09:37:56-05:00 2025-12-31T09:37:57-05:00 Department of Medicine: Oncology Hospitalist <div>Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital New Brunswick is seeking a full time Hospitalist to join our Oncology Division with Rutgers Cancer Institute of NJ (CINJ), the state’s only NCI-designated Comprehensive Cancer Center and Rutgers-Robert Wood Johnson Medical School, The State University of New Jersey.</div><div>In this position, the hospitalist with manage primarily oncology patients on our solid oncology and liquid oncology services with close collaboration with the oncologists who practice at CINJ. Through the well-established, multidisciplinary team the overall goal it to have close collaboration with the outpatient oncology practices for patients who require the acute inpatient level of care. The hospitalist with engage in the inpatient care, assist with the transitions of care back to the ambulatory setting, and work closely with the surgical and medical oncologic support staff, inclusive of advanced practice providers.</div><div>Ideal candidates will be joining this busy and growing practice as we look towards expansion in the oncologic care that service the states only NCI-designated Comprehensive Cancer Center. A core function of the hospitalists will be to support the team-based approach, inclusive of communication with case managers, social workers, bed managers and ensure appropriate patience centered transitions of care. In addition, the candidate will work closely with the palliative care teams to assist in the patient and family communications and care planning.</div><div>In addition to clinical care, the academic institution and collaboration with Robert Wood Johnson Medical School allows the unique opportunities to engage in clinical and research programs, clinical trials research, cancer chemoprevention, clinical and basic pharmacology, novel cell therapy constructs, and participation in a broad range of teaching initiatives.</div> RWJ - Medicine Operational RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 8254 25FA1041 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280102 2026-08-27T16:08:31-04:00 2026-08-27T16:08:32-04:00 Research Scientist II (GIS) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Research Scientist II (GIS) within the Office of the Director/Cancer Epidemiology Services/NJ State Cancer Registry at the Rutgers Cancer Institute.<br><br>The primary role of the Research Scientist II (RS II) under direction of the Supervising Research Scientist, Deputy Director, or Director is to assist with the design and conduct of research studies on cancers and assists in the analysis of cancer surveillance data using the New Jersey State Cancer Registry (NJSCR). The RS II will also provide advanced expertise in health geography, Geographic Information Science (GIScience), epidemiology, geospatial analysis, and population health and lead analytic and geospatial initiatives at the New Jersey State Cancer Registry (NJSCR) designed to improve understanding of cancer patterns, disparities, and neighborhood influences on cancer outcomes; integrate cancer registry data with census, environmental, and other relevant contextual datasets; and producing mapping and visualization tools that support surveillance, research, and public health action.</div><div><br>Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Serves as CES Team Lead/Project Lead on geospatial cancer research studies, assisting the NJSCR principal investigator, deputy director, and Supervising Research Scientists (SRS) with the development and implementation of epidemiologic and geographic cancer research studies, using state-of-the-art geographic information systems (GIS) tools and methodologies.</li><li>Provides subject-matter expertise on GIS methods, neighborhood measures, contextual effects, and population health data integration.</li><li>Manages geocoded cancer datasets and oversee linkages with census, environmental, demographic, and neighborhood contextual data (e.g., socioeconomic indices, segregation measures, redlining, rurality).</li><li>Conducts geospatial and epidemiologic analyses to assess cancer outcomes, spatial patterns, temporal trends, and disparities across racial/ethnic, socioeconomic, and geographic groups using specialized tools and programming applications such as SQL, SAS, R, Python, ArcGIS, or QGIS accurately and efficiently.</li><li>Constructs, cleans, and analyzes longitudinal residential histories to examine mobility, life-course exposures, and neighborhood change.</li><li>Develops high-quality GIS outputs, including static maps, analytic spatial layers, and interactive web-based mapping tools for internal and external users.</li><li>Prepares scientifically sound NJSCR-specific statement of work, Scientific Review Board, Institutional Review Board applications, protocols, data use agreements, and other documents (Local Context Supplement, Data Linkage Agreement, Research Agreement) in coordination with senior management, research collaborators, and sponsors, if applicable. Ensure timely submission of SRB, IRB, and associated Modifications and Continuing Reviews. Monitor and track all study documentation to ensure timely execution and compliance and that information is correctly documented in their respective tracker databases.</li><li>Develops and negotiates project budgets reports, tracks invoicing, payments, and spending on projects. Monitors that studies are correctly documented in the tracker databases.</li><li>Manages day-to-day activities of geospatial cancer research projects and studies under supervision of the SRS or deputy director.</li><li>Act as the primary liaison with the principal investigator, providing progress reports, communicating problems and questions, collaborating on publications, and transmitting data securely.</li></ul> CINJ - Cancer Registry & Resea RBHS Chancellor-L2 Cancer Institute of New Jersey-L3 7944 New Brunswick NJ 26ST0269 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278435 2026-07-08T15:26:58-04:00 2026-07-08T15:26:59-04:00 Peer Support Specialist III (IRTS Southern/Northern/Statewide) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Peer Support Specialist III (IRTS Southern/Northern/Statewide) for the Case Management Services within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The Peer Support Specialist III will serve as a role model to demonstrate recovery and wellness principles and provide non-clinical recovery support and to engage and empower individuals to pursue and maintain their health and wellness, live a self-directed life, access community resources, and reach their full potential.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Initiates contact with individuals served.</li><li>Validates individuals served experiences and feelings.</li><li>Relates their own recovery stories, and with written permission, the recovery stories of others to inspire hope.</li><li>Understands their own personal values and culture and how these may contribute to biases, judgments, and beliefs.</li><li>Assists and supports individuals served to set goals and to dream of future possibilities.</li><li>Develops and maintains up-to-date information about community resources and services.</li></ul> UBHC - Community-Based Service RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8011 Piscataway NJ 25ST2047 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267494 2026-01-17T14:10:29-05:00 2026-01-17T14:10:30-05:00 Instructor (Part Time) - 2026 <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking instructors to teach non-credit courses for the Center for Government Services. The instructor will teach in one or more of the following NJ government related areas:<br><br></div><ul><li>Affordable Housing Professional Certification Program</li><li>Assessment Administration Program</li><li>Elected Officials Program</li><li>Financial Management Program</li><li>Municipal Attorneys</li><li>Municipal Clerks Program</li><li>NJ Educational Facility Management Program</li><li>NJ Local Housing Authority and Redevelopment Agency Program</li><li>Planning &amp; Zoning Program</li><li>Professional Development Program</li><li>Public Purchasing Program</li><li>Public Safety Program</li><li>Public Works Program</li><li>School Transportation Supervisors Certification Program</li><li>Tax Collection Program</li><li>Train-the-Trainer Program</li></ul><div><br>Successful candidates will be responsible for the following:</div><ul><li>Instruct/co-instruct non-credit courses in one or more of the areas/programs listed above (may include traditional lecture, hybrid, and/or fully online formats)</li><li>Prepare course materials (e.g., syllabi, presentations, hand-outs, reading materials, etc.)</li><li>Provide constructive feedback to students as well as critical instruction that meets program standards and goals</li><li>Respond to student emails and inquiries</li><li>Adhere to grade submission policies and deadlines (if applicable)</li><li>Adhere to University policies and regulations</li><li>Practice innovative educational methodology</li></ul> DoCS - CGS University Academic Affairs-L2 Division of Continuing Studies-L3 6688 26FA0042 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280255 2026-08-31T16:24:19-04:00 2026-08-31T16:24:20-04:00 Mental Health Clinician III <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Mental Health Clinician III for the Child &amp; Adolescent Partial Hospital within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Mental Health Clinician III is to provide comprehensive evaluation, assessment and therapeutic intervention to address the psychological, emotional and social needs of individuals served by the unit. Duties include formulating evaluations, developing and implementing treatment plans, conducting individual, group, and family therapy and providing case management functions.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Actively participates in and contributes to smooth functioning of the department and demonstrates initiative and flexibility regarding work assignments.</li><li>Consistently ensures the individuals served rights to fair and equitable treatment, self-determination, individuality, privacy and civil rights are maintained.</li><li>Consistently provides individual, group and family therapy based on sound clinical judgment as indicated by supervisory observation and feedback from individuals served, families and fellow team members.</li><li>Adapts the assessment and treatment processes to accommodate variations in readiness for treatment/change, and implications of age, cultural, medical, economic or other relevant factors.</li><li>Consistently identifies appropriate resources for individuals served and families based on assessed needs, performs case management functions and completes all forms, correspondence and reports necessary to ensure overall coordination of treatment services via linkages, service procurement, referrals, patient advocacy and state/community systems.</li><li>Formulates clinically appropriate and timely treatment plans that reflect input from individuals served and caregivers as appropriate with realistic, measurable, observable objectives. Takes into account the individuals’ strengths and potential limitations and are clearly oriented toward wellness and recovery.</li><li>Formulates clinically appropriate and timely discharge plans and documents in discharge instructions consistent with Clinical Records standards in accordance with prescribed time frames.</li></ul> UBHC - Child & Adolescent PH P RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8803 Newark NJ 26ST1324 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278889 2026-07-16T10:48:16-04:00 2026-07-16T10:48:17-04:00 Program Coordinator <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Program Coordinator for the Access Center within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>Supervises all the day-to-day aspects of the New York State United Teacher (NYSUT) program, represents NYSUT at events and act as the liaison to funding agencies collaborating agencies, and referrals sources as needed and/or required by this position. Supervises the activities and staff of the NYSUT program serving the members of the New York State United Teachers. Ensures the quality of the telephone-based counseling and crisis interventions are provided. Ensures compliance with relevant funding agency and regulatory agency requirements.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Participates as a key member of the management team and is responsible for overseeing, managing and preparing documentation needed by the program and National Call Center leadership.</li><li>Oversees the day-to-day operation of NYSUT peer line to ensure all calls are being answered in a timely manner and that staff are responding in accordance to established departmental protocol.</li><li>Supervises staff as assigned.</li><li>Develops and supports marketing of the NYSUT peer line services.</li><li>Oversees, manages and prepares paperwork and documentation needed by UBHC and external funding agencies and the Federal Government</li><li>Serves as liaison within the collaborating agencies, external funding sources, and other departments within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.</li></ul> UBHC - Access Center RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7985 Remote NJ 26ST1527 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/271110 2026-03-18T17:45:06-04:00 2026-03-18T17:45:06-04:00 Coadjutant Researcher Rutgers Artificial Intelligence and Data Science (RAD) Collaboratory <div>The Rutgers Artificial Intelligence and Data Science (RAD) Collaboratory is seeking two experienced videographers, and an experienced photographer to capture and edit content for the March 24th RAD Symposium which will take place from 9am-4pm. This is an event which will include attendance and presentations from high-level executives, and will include focused panel discussions with industry leaders, a poster session, presentations and a networking portion.<br><br><br></div><h1>Responsibilities:</h1><div>* Collaborate with department to define tasks, setup equipment and manage production<br>* Captures high quality photos and videos of every aspect of the event<br>* Transports, sets up, and operates production equipment<br>* Responsible for editing and delivering the final product back to RAD</div><div>* Setting up and taking down equipment<br>* Ensure that the equipment is present and working</div> Quantitative Biomedicine Inst New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 6749 26FA0259 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279477 2026-08-10T13:20:56-04:00 2026-08-10T13:20:57-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Licensed Practical Nurse for the department of Surgery at the Robert Wood Johnson Medical School.<br><br>The Rutgers–Robert Wood Johnson Medical School Licensed Practical Nurse, in collaboration with physicians, nursing staff, and other members of the healthcare team, provides focused, technical nursing care to clinical and office operations.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Provides and documents nursing care within the scope of practice for colorectal surgery patients in face-to-face and telephone encounters; provides input to the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status to the physician and other members of the healthcare team as appropriate and in a timely manner.</li><li>May be required to travel to offsite locations to assist providers during clinic hours, including Steeplechase Cancer Center.</li><li>Assists physicians and advanced practice nurse during scheduled office hours, including preparation and setup of clinic exam and procedure rooms for patient visits. Assists in office procedures. Reviews and prepares patient charts prior to office visits for essential paperwork and test results.</li><li>Places orders and obtains insurance precertification for prescribed clinical testing for special procedures (CT, MRI, Ultrasound etc.) Provide patients with results of prescribed clinical tests after discussing them with the appropriate physicians.</li><li>Coordinates pre-operative testing and medical clearance prior to surgical procedures. Calls patients to check in pre- and post-operatively.</li><li>Completes return to work/school letters and disability paperwork for patients.</li></ul> RWJ - Surgery General RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7835 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1601 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279750 2026-08-20T08:58:08-04:00 2026-08-20T08:58:09-04:00 Technician I FT Eves UCHC MSCF <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Full Time Technician I for Midstate Correctional Facility located in Wrightstown NJ. The Technician I participates as a member of the clinical and administrative medical team at the Prison.<br><br>Among the duties for the position are:<br><br><br></div><ul><li>Takes vital signs, height and weight and documents in electronic medical records (EMR).</li><li>Assists the physician/associate practitioner with procedures, including preparing the inmate for the examination.</li><li>Obtains specimen collection and handling, including, but not limited to, drawing blood.</li><li>Assists with the cleaning, sterilization and securing of equipment within the Health Service Unit.</li><li>Maintains or assists in maintaining the supply stock in the Health Service Unit by ordering in a timely and appropriate manner.</li><li>Maintains the supply stock in the examination rooms.</li><li>Aggregates the orders of all medications and forwards to the pharmacy provider / local pharmacy.</li></ul> UCHC Midstate Correction Physi RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7680 Wrightstown NJ 26ST0893 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/276778 2026-06-09T15:53:07-04:00 2026-06-12T15:32:14-04:00 Tenure-Track/Tenured Faculty Position in Interpersonal Communication  (Open Rank) <div>The Department of Communication at Rutgers University’s School of Communication and Information seeks a full-time faculty member in interpersonal communication. The search is open rank but prioritizes early career scholars. The appointment will begin Fall 2027.&nbsp;</div><div>We are looking for a scholar of interpersonal communication who conducts applied empirical research in complex social and relational contexts. We welcome applicants who approach their scholarship from a diverse range of empirical perspectives (e.g., quantitative analysis, qualitative analysis, conversation analysis). Research and teaching interests should address contemporary communication problems such as facilitating difficult or high-stakes conversations in personal, family, professional, or community contexts. This might include such topics as discussing social problems and differences, engaging in interpersonal influence, managing conflict, communicating support or advice, or negotiating human relationships in personal or professional contexts, in face-to-face or technologically mediated channels. The candidate should have a research program that is theory-driven, data-informed, and communication-centered. We prioritize applicants who are active in the communication discipline.&nbsp;</div><div>Our faculty members employ a wide range of empirical and methodological approaches in their research. We encourage applications from candidates whose scholarship intersects with and/or complements one or more of the department’s research foci (interpersonal communication, language and social interaction, health communication, organizational communication, communication and technology, and computational social science) and/or other areas within the school, such as media studies and information science. For more about the Department of Communication and the School of Communication and Information (SC&amp;I), see <strong>comminfo.rutgers.edu</strong>.&nbsp;</div><div>We look forward to welcoming a new colleague who will contribute to our thriving undergraduate and master’s-level programs and our highly regarded interdisciplinary school-wide Ph.D. program.&nbsp;</div> Communication New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School  Communicatn & Info Sci-L3 7088 26FA0590 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266452 2026-01-04T21:40:47-05:00 2026-01-04T21:40:48-05:00 Assistant Professor in Social Psychology, Tenure-Track <div>The Department of Psychology at Rutgers University-New Brunswick, NJ, plans to hire a tenure-track Assistant Professor in SOCIAL PSYCHOLOGY, with a start date of September 1, 2026. We seek a candidate who has a strong research program in any area of social psychology. We welcome applications from candidates whose research is in one or more of the following areas: intergroup relations, motivation, relationships, and health. Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Social Psychology or a related field by the time of appointment, will be expected to develop and maintain an active, extramurally funded research program, and teach and mentor at the undergraduate and graduate level in the field of social psychology.<br><br></div><div>Applicants should submit a CV, research statement, teaching philosophy, representative reprints, and 3 letters of recommendation to: https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/259298. Candidates are also encouraged to address (in these statements or separately) ways in which their work includes open science practices, their commitment to service, and/or ways in which their research, courses, or service will contribute to the goals in the <a href=\"https://sas.rutgers.edu/about/strategic-plan\"><strong>SAS strategic plan</strong></a>. Review of applications will begin on October 18, 2025, and continue until the position is filled, but timely submission of materials is recommended for full consideration. Applicants may contact Calvin Lai, Ph.D., Chair of the Search Committee, with questions or concerns about the application or review process, at <a href=\"mailto:calvin.lai@rutgers.edu\"><strong>calvin.lai@rutgers.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div><div><strong>Equal Employment Opportunity Statement:</strong></div><div>It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, affectional or sexual orientation, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information (including the refusal to submit to genetic testing), or any other category protected by law. As an institution, we value diversity of background and opinion, and prohibit discrimination or harassment on the basis of any legally protected class in the areas of hiring, recruitment, promotion, transfer, demotion, training, compensation, pay, fringe benefits, layoff, termination or any other terms and conditions of employment. For additional information, please see the Non-Discrimination Statement at the following web address: <a href=\"https://uhr.rutgers.edu/non-discrimination-statement\"><strong>https://uhr.rutgers.edu/non-discrimination-statement</strong></a><br><br></div> Psychology New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 8128 25FA0835 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280213 2026-08-31T13:25:23-04:00 2026-08-31T13:25:24-04:00 Behavioral Health Aide - per diem - Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a per diem Behavioral Health Aide within the Inpatient Services Department for Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the per diem Behavioral Health Aide is to provide continuous, direct, one-to-one observation and support for patients experiencing acute mental health symptoms. Assists in maintaining a safe and supportive environment for patients.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Provides constant, uninterrupted one-to-one observation for assigned patients who are at risk for self-harm, harm to others, aggression, or emotional distress.</li><li>Assists in maintaining a safe and supportive environment by promptly reporting escalating patient behaviors, mood changes, and concerning activities to the clinical care team.</li><li>Completes and documents accurate, timely, and objective safety observations in accordance with organizational policy, regulatory requirements, and established observation intervals (including every 15-minute checks as assigned).</li><li>Maintains a calm and professional demeanor during patient escalation or crisis situations and utilizes approved verbal redirection and de-escalation techniques.</li><li>Assists patients with basic activities of daily living, ambulation, meals, hydration, and comfort measures as directed.</li><li>Assists with patient orientation to the unit environment, reinforcing unit expectations, behavioral standards, safety protocols, and patient rights as directed by clinical leadership.</li><li>Fosters respectful, culturally responsive, and compassionate interactions with patients, families, visitors, and interdisciplinary team members while maintaining professional boundaries and confidentiality.</li></ul> UBHC - Acute Psychological Ser RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7987 Piscataway NJ 26ST1689 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278711 2026-07-13T10:32:41-04:00 2026-07-13T10:32:42-04:00 Lecturers, Various Disciplines, School of Business <div>Rutgers University-Camden, School of Business, seeks new Lecturers (part-time faculty) to teach courses during the AY 2026/2027 academic year in a variety of disciplines to include:<br>- Introduction to Business<br>- Statistics<br>- Information Technology<br>- Optimization and Modeling<br>- Business of Sports<br>- Business Communications<br>- Marketing Analytics<br>- Introduction to Business<br>Courses are delivered during the day, on-campus (face-to-face) at the Rutgers-Camden campus or at our offsite locations - at Camden County Community College (Blackwood, NJ), Mercer County Community College (West Windsor, NJ), Brookdale Community College (Lincroft, NJ). Some online teaching opportunities are available.&nbsp;<br>The successful candidate/s will be responsible for building his or her own course section which entails: modifying the existing syllabus, vetting the appropriate textbook, present course materials during the assigned course times, designing assessments, and organizing the course within Canvas, Rutgers’s Learning Management System. All in accordance with the school's guidelines.<br>While teaching the course, the candidate is expected to attend class as scheduled, respond to student inquiries within a reasonable time frame, as appropriate make weekly announcements regarding course content and upcoming deadlines, provide timely feedback on student work, facilitate student interactions, offer virtual office hours as needed, and comply with grade submission policies and deadlines.</div> School of Business Camden Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 School of Business Camden-L3 8078 26FA0672 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/269508 2026-02-19T09:56:49-05:00 2026-02-19T09:56:50-05:00 Tenure Track Physician Scientist <div>During the first three years of their appointment, successful candidate(s) will devote the majority of their effort to their research portfolio, with limited time allocated to other duties (e.g., patient care, teaching, mentorship, and service). After this start-up period, the balance of research and other duties will depend on career goals, the extent to which time is covered by extramural funding sources, and expectations of their Division.&nbsp;</div> RWJ - Medicine Chairman RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7768 26FA0151 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280457 2026-09-04T13:06:37-04:00 2026-09-04T13:06:38-04:00 Senior Director of Administration (Pediatrics) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Senior Director of Administration for the department of Pediatrics at the Robert Wood Johnson Medical School.<br><br>Primarily responsible to develop, implement, direct and provide overall management of the administrative infrastructure for a complex and widely dispersed academic department to ensure support to the chairs' academic, research and clinical programs ,whether university or hospital based. Scope of position requires administrative leadership in general administration, financial management, organizational development, labor relations, marketing, operations management, information systems management, and overall policy and procedure development and implementation. Overarching responsibility is ensuring the departments' very best selection and use of resources for maintaining and developing departments' programs.&nbsp;</div><div><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Develops, implements and constantly renews and refreshes overall administrative program to support the program objectives of the chairs.&nbsp;</li><li>Develops, implements and manages annual departmental budgets including clinical, academic and research components to support the objectives of the departments. Provides overall ·guidance for all departmental/divisional major procurement decisions and ongoing spending policies to meet budgetary objectives.&nbsp;</li><li>Provides administrative directions and leadership for divisional staff.&nbsp;</li><li>Encourages, fosters and requires development of standardized administrative practice throughout the departments with satellite practices.&nbsp;</li><li>Develops and ensures implementation of overall clinical practice process standards and objectives.&nbsp;</li><li>Works with chairs to refine practice incentive programs to best fit departmental programmatic goals.</li><li>Develops and implements physician productivity monitoring systems.&nbsp;</li><li>Develops and manages departments' administrative organization to maintain best fit of resources and environmental demands.&nbsp;</li></ul> RWJ - Pediatrics RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7801 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1726 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279402 2026-08-07T11:23:06-04:00 2026-08-07T11:23:07-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Postdoctoral Associate for the Outpatient Services in Newark within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.&nbsp;<br><br>Under direction, the Postdoctoral Associate provides therapeutic interventions for the psychological and social needs of individuals served. The Postdoctoral Associate will provide psychological testing as required by the program to increase our understanding of the issues experienced by the individuals we serve. Supports the integration of evidence-based practices and provide therapeutic interventions based upon the principles of wellness and recovery.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Contributes to and supports goals and objectives of the Unit and UBHC.&nbsp;</li><li>Provides direct care, psychotherapeutic interventions/services in accordance with UBHC program/unit policies, accreditation standards, licensing regulations and billing requirements.&nbsp;</li><li>Completes and monitors clinical records in compliance with UBHC program policies, accreditation standards, licensing regulations and billing requirements.&nbsp;</li><li>Takes a lead clinical role in the department, including the professional development of staff, students and interns as assigned by supervisor.&nbsp;</li><li>Attends to professional development by remaining current in knowledge of trends and development in mental health.&nbsp;</li><li>Participates in research activities, development, implementation, and evaluation of programs.&nbsp;</li></ul> UBHC - Outpatient Newark RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8059 Newark NJ 26ST1597 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/276125 2026-05-29T12:11:41-04:00 2026-05-29T12:11:42-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the School of Art &amp; Sciences, Biology Department, the Center for Computational and Integrative Biology (CCIB), and the Yakoby Lab, invites applications for a Post-Doctoral Associate position. This position is supported by NIH funded grant. The position is renewable based on availability of continuing funding.<br>We are seeking a highly motivated individual who is interested in generating new platforms to investigate the co-evolution of the the epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR) and its ligand across Drosophila species. The successful candidate will use a combination of molecular, genetic, biochemical, and computational approaches to study how EGFR signaling levels evolved across species. The successful candidate must have experience with genome engineering (i.e. CRISPR/Cas9), and broad use of molecular biology and biochemical tools to validate genomic alternations. The successful applicant is expected to independently conduct their own research project, and be involved in other laboratory projects related to gene regulation and tissue patterning. The candidate should be excited to work in an interdisciplinary program.<br>Questions about this position should be sent to Dr. Nir Yakoby, yakoby@camden.rutgers.edu</div> Biology Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 6758 26FA0535 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/273855 2026-04-28T16:38:13-04:00 2026-04-28T16:38:13-04:00 MGSA – Department of Music – (Fall 2026) <div>The Department of Music, Mason Gross School of the Arts, Rutgers University invites applications for part-time instructional and academic support for undergraduate and graduate courses in a variety of areas, including and not limited to: aural skills, composition, general music, jazz studies, music technology, music theory, and musicology. Applications are also being accepted for private lesson studio teachers.<br><br></div><div>Academic support positions include piano accompaniment, chamber music coaching, student teaching supervision, and other departmental academic support tasks.</div> Music New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Mason Gross School of Arts Dea-L3 6865 26FA0403 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/265912 2025-12-31T09:01:27-05:00 2025-12-31T09:01:28-05:00 Postdoctoral Associate in Cell & Structural Biology <div>The Dai laboratory in the Department of Cell Biology and Neuroscience and the Institute for Quantitative Biomedicine at Rutgers University is seeking applications for a postdoctoral associate position. We are recruiting a motivated individual to contribute to the development of the new methodology of cellular tomography and cryo-focused ion beam milling for multiple collaborative projects. Research areas of primary interest include protein aggregation in neurodegenerative diseases and the structure and dynamics of membrane proteins. The lab is hosted in the Institute for Quantitative Biomedicine, co-located with the RCSB Protein Data Bank. In addition to the Rutgers Cryo-electron Microscopy and Nanoimaging Facility, core facilities housed within the Institute include protein NMR spectroscopy, mass spectrometry, and hardware for high-performance computing.&nbsp;</div> Quantitative Biomedicine Inst New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 6749 25FA0462 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279666 2026-08-18T08:34:14-04:00 2026-08-18T08:34:15-04:00 Physician Specialist-Oral Surgeon UCHC Statewide (Per Diem) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care (UCHC) is seeking a Physician Specialist-Oral Surgeon Per Diem located at Trenton, NJ. The Physician Specialist-Oral Surgeon performs surgery on mouth, jaws, and related head and neck structure to execute difficult and multiple extractions of teeth, to remove tumors and other abnormal growths, to correct abnormal jaw relations by mandibular or maxillary revision, to prepare mouth for insertion of dental prosthesis, or to treat fractured jaws; and interrelates and works effectively with inmates, other members of the dental staff, medical and nursing staff, correctional staff at all levels, administrative and support staff.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Clinically examine, evaluate and diagnose conditions in patients referred by General Dentists through an</li><li>internal referral process in the NJ DOC facilities.</li><li>Provide follow-up consultations and care for patients treated clinically.</li><li>Administers local anesthetics.</li><li>Removes impacted, damaged, and non-restorable teeth.</li><li>Performs surgery on the mouth and jaws in order to treat conditions such as jaw growth problems</li></ul><div><br></div> UCHC Northern State Prison Nur RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7701 Trenton NJ 26ST0281 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279991 2026-08-26T07:52:58-04:00 2026-08-26T07:52:59-04:00 Coadjutant <div>Seeking a Coadjutant to conduct research in support of the Newark Public Safety Collaborative's (NPSC) mission to democratize access to data and analysis. The position will obtain, evaluate, validate, and ground-truth place-based environmental feature data from large datasets and other sources. Responsibilities include extracting and integrating data from official databases, conducting GIS-based research and analysis, assessing data quality and accuracy, resolving discrepancies across sources, and documenting findings to support NPSC's research and evaluation activities.<br><br>This is a grant funded position.<br><br></div><div>For more info about NPSC please visit https://newarkcollaborative.org/.</div> School of Criminal Justice Newark Chancellor-L2 School of Criminal Justice-L3 6871 26FA0735 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277773 2026-06-25T11:17:15-04:00 2026-06-25T11:17:16-04:00 Technician I Per Diem-UCHC NSP (multiple vacancies) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Per Diem I for Northern State Prison, located in Newark, NJ. The Technician I participates as a member of the clinical and administrative medical team at the Prison.<br><br>Among the duties for the position are:<br><br></div><ul><li>Takes vital signs, height and weight and documents in electronic medical records (EMR).</li><li>Assists the physician/associate practitioner with procedures, including preparing the inmate for the examination.</li><li>Obtains specimen collection and handling, including, but not limited to, drawing blood.</li><li>Assists with the cleaning, sterilization and securing of equipment within the Health Service Unit.</li><li>Maintains or assists in maintaining the supply stock in the Health Service Unit by ordering in a timely and appropriate manner. Maintains the supply stock in the examination rooms.</li><li>Aggregates the orders of all medications and forwards to the pharmacy provider / local pharmacy.</li></ul> UCHC New Jersey State Prison N RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7693 Newark NJ 26ST0699 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275416 2026-05-19T13:09:15-04:00 2026-05-19T13:09:16-04:00 PLT/CoAd - Douglass Residential College <div>Instructors may be responsible for teaching courses offered by Douglass Residential College at any credit threshold. In-person instructional appointments are in-person on the New Brunswick campus. Non-instructional appointments may include a combination of in-person and hybrid/online formats. Non-instructional appointments may also include student support, event support, and data analytics.<br><br></div> Douglass Residential College New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Academic Affairs-L3 8111 26FA0496 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266307 2025-12-31T09:48:25-05:00 2025-12-31T09:48:25-05:00 Coadjutant (Non-Teaching) Fall 2025 <div>Research Assistant to synthesize, purify and characterize specialty ionic liquids. The successful candidate will hold at least an Associate’s Degree and be a continuing student majoring in Chemistry or Biology.<br><br>Job Duties:<br>1. Synthesis of functionalized imidazolium, pyrrolidinium and other types of specialty ionic liquids bearing sulfonylimide and other anions.<br>2. Purification of ionic liquids using standard organic procedures.<br>3. Structure confirmation of ionic liquids using Nuclear Magnetic Resonance Spectroscopy.<br>4. Water content determination of ionic liquids using Karl Fischer Titration.<br>5. Measurement of temperature dependent viscosity and conductivity of ionic liquids.<br>6. Measurement of density.<br>7. Measurement of thermal profiles using Differential Scanning Calorimetry.<br>8. Maintaining a laboratory notebook with records of all procedures, observations and results.<br>9. Compiling data and delivering oral and poster presentations at local and national scientific meetings.<br>10. Write up of all experimental procedures, results and analyses for publication in peer-reviewed journals.<br><br>Hiring for multiple positions.</div> Chemistry & Chemical Biology New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 7001 25FA0821 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280149 2026-08-31T08:35:56-04:00 2026-08-31T08:35:57-04:00 Technician I PT Nights UCHC SWSP <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Part Time Technician I for Southwoods State Prison, located in Bridgeton, NJ. The Technician I participates as a member of the clinical and administrative medical team at the Prison.</div><div><br>Among the duties for the position are:<br><br></div><ul><li>Takes vital signs, height and weight and documents in electronic medical records (EMR).</li><li>Assists the physician/associate practitioner with procedures, including preparing the inmate for the examination.</li><li>Obtains specimen collection and handling, including, but not limited to, drawing blood.</li><li>Assists with the cleaning, sterilization and securing of equipment within the Health Service Unit.</li><li>Maintains or assists in maintaining the supply stock in the Health Service Unit by ordering in a timely and appropriate manner.</li><li>Maintains the supply stock in the examination rooms.</li><li>Aggregates the orders of all medications and forwards to the pharmacy provider / local pharmacy.</li></ul> UCHC-South Woods Psn-Ancillary RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7685 Bridgeton NJ 26ST0549 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278563 2026-07-10T10:34:59-04:00 2026-07-10T10:35:00-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse PT Nights UCHC ADTC STU <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Part Time Licensed Practical Nurse for the Adult Diagnostic Treatment Center located in Avenel, NJ<br><br>The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment. Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.</div><div><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs.</li><li>Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.</li><li>Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.</li><li>Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.</li><li>Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.</li><li>Documents all aspects of patient care.</li></ul> UCHC Adult Treatment Center Ph RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7674 Avenel NJ 26ST0910 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/268225 2026-01-29T13:27:19-05:00 2026-01-29T13:27:20-05:00 Department Chair - Clinical and Preventive Nutrition Sciences <div>Rutgers University School of Health Professions (SHP) is seeking a Chair for the Department of Clinical and Preventive Nutrition Sciences (DCPNS). SHP is the largest school of health professions in the nation with over 25 academic programs ranging from certificate to doctorate across the health care landscape. Reporting to the Dean of the School of Health Professions (SHP), The Department of Clinical and Preventive Nutrition Sciences (DCPNS) Chair is responsible for education, research, and administrative leadership of the department, inclusive of the Master of Science in Clinical Nutrition-for Aspiring Dietitians and the Doctor of Clinical Nutrition Programs.<br><br></div><div><strong>Primary Responsibilities</strong></div><ul><li>Provides leadership and administration of the department, including budgeting, oversight of expenditures, personnel, facilities planning, resource allocation, academic and program planning, and policy implementation.</li><li>Oversees the operation of departmental academic programs, including the maintenance of applicable accreditations.</li><li>Reviews the budget, program, and departmental plans, and ensures ongoing communication with the members of the department.</li><li>Provides supervision of program directors, faculty, and staff, including workload assignments, and conducts the annual evaluations.</li><li>Makes recommendations regarding appointments, reappointments, promotions, leaves, dismissals, and acceptance of resignations of faculty and staff in accordance with the policies and procedures of the University and School.</li><li>Offers mentorship and support for faculty professional development, research, and scholarly productivity, including establishing annual goals and objectives for individual faculty members.</li><li>Develops department strategic and operational plans.</li><li>Conducts an annual review of the department's educational, research/scholarship, and service activities, and submits an annual report of accomplishments to the Dean.</li><li>In conjunction with the Vice Chair of Research, oversees faculty and student research to ensure compliance with applicable regulations, policies, and procedures regarding research.</li><li>Participates in graduate student research advisement.</li><li>Participates in departmental student disciplinary actions in accordance with university and school policies.</li><li>Fosters collaborations within the School, Rutgers Health, the University, and national and international partners.</li><li>Engages in research, grant writing, publications, presentations, and other scholarly activities on a national and international level.</li><li>Oversees all clinical operations within the department.</li><li>Participates in graduate course development, teaching, and interprofessional education.</li><li>Teaches academic courses at a level of workload consistent with (or takes into account) all other duties.</li><li>Develops strategies for Departmental publicity, websites, articles, and promotional materials.</li><li>Serves on university, school, and department committees as needed.</li><li>Participates and provides leadership on professional committees, professional organizations or editorial boards, on a national and/or international level.</li><li>Makes recommendations to the Dean regarding related course and program offerings and all other issues of concern to the department.</li><li>Oversees scheduling of classes, sequencing of courses, and scheduling of faculty, adjunct faculty, and staff.</li><li>Oversees and approves payment of adjunct faculty and work study students.</li><li>Represents department and is a liaison to other departments, schools, and bodies.</li><li>Performs other duties assigned by the Dean.</li></ul><div><br></div> SHP - Clinical & Preventive Nu RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Health Professions-L3 7570 25FA1233 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280323 2026-09-02T12:24:05-04:00 2026-09-02T12:24:06-04:00 Senior Incident Response Analyst <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a <strong>Senior Incident Response Analyst </strong>for the Office of Information Technology. This position will report tothe Associate Director.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Performs daily operations of the incident detection and response program, which includes finding evidence of threats or suspicious behavior and leveraging data to improve controls and processes.</li><li>Monitors information security incidents throughout Rutgers' computing environment.</li><li>Serves as an escalation point for Incident Response Analysts.</li><li>Provides expert-level analytic, investigative and forensic support of complex security incidents to detect and remediate security threats on networks, workstations, servers, and other connected devices.</li><li>Provides expert level advice and services to business units throughout the University while participating in all phases of Rutgers’ Integrated Incident Response Program (Prepare, Detect &amp; Analyze, Contain, Eradicate, Recovery, Report, Remediate).</li></ul> OIT - Enterprise Infrastructur EVP & Chief Admin Officer OIT - VP & Chief Information O-L3 7280 Piscataway NJ 26ST1709 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279164 2026-07-28T13:08:02-04:00 2026-07-28T13:08:03-04:00 Post-Doc Ellison Lab <div>This position is for a Research Associate who will act as a project manager for the Ellison and Brand labs. Responsibilities include performing laboratory and computational experiments, writing and/or contributing to scientific manuscripts, and mentoring students and trainees. Performing experiments and data analysis in order to achieve research aims. Writing and contributing to scientific manuscripts to publish findings . Mentoring trainees so that they may complete their own research projects.&nbsp;</div> Human Genetics Institute of NJ New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 8177 26FA0678 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/271839 2026-03-27T11:02:38-04:00 2026-03-27T11:02:39-04:00 Assistant Professor - Maternal – Fetal Medicine (Ob/Gyn) <div>This position will treat women with maternal or fetal issues pre-conception, through their pregnancy, and beyond with a focus on improving maternal or fetal options. Oversight and experience with level II ultrasound and intrapartum procedures are required. Experience and training in fetal medicine is preferred. Plans and participates in medical care to both inpatients and outpatients seen in University Hospital, our Ambulatory Practice, and other sites collaborating with Rutgers-NJMS. In addition to clinical duties, the successful applicant will be responsible for lectures and didactic clinical instruction for our fully accredited MFM fellowship program as well as our obstetrics and gynecology residents and NJMS medical students.</div> NJMS - Obstetrics & Gynocology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7455 26FA0296 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279552 2026-08-12T16:06:56-04:00 2026-08-12T16:06:57-04:00 Habilitation Counselor - Camden Residential <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Habilitation Counselor for the Camden Residential Program within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Habilitation Counselor is to provide day-to-day direct care, face-to-face case management and supportive services to individuals who reside in UBHC Housing programs as directed by the Program Supervisor in accordance with all regulatory requirements.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Assumes direct care responsibilities for individuals served in the Residential program and provides face-to-face supportive counseling, crisis intervention, psycho-education, skills building, and case management services as indicated.</li><li>Involves individuals served and family/significant others in jointly formulating Residential Treatment/Individualized Recovery Plans reflecting measurable goals and objectives based on individual’s input, clinical assessment, and treatment team recommendations in accordance with all regulatory requirements.</li><li>Collaborates effectively with other departments, staff, referral sources, other service providers and social support networks to provide services and rehabilitative care for individuals served.</li><li>Completes Individualized Residential Treatment/Recovery Plans one week before due date and obtains all necessary signatures by Plan due date as monitored by documentation tracking.</li><li>Ensures that all relevant attendance records and logs reflect the individual’s attendance.</li><li>Collaborates effectively with members of the department and with external departments, staff, referral sources, other service providers and social support networks to provide services and rehabilitative care for consumers individuals and families.</li><li>Demonstrates positive participation in all department team and staff meetings and with other treatment providers.</li></ul> UBHC - Community-Based Service RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8011 Collingswood NJ 26ST0882 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279776 2026-08-20T13:02:30-04:00 2026-08-20T13:02:31-04:00 Staff Nurse <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Staff Nurse for the department of Otolaryngology at the Robert Wood Johnson Medical School.<br><br>The Staff Nurse, in collaboration with physicians, nursing staff, and other members of the healthcare team, oversees, coordinates, and provides focused, episodic care to Rutgers Health patients. This care encompasses health promotion, health maintenance, or management of health-related problems that is delivered in face-to-face or telephone encounters. Additional responsibilities include delegation, direction, and supervision of the activities of Rutgers Health LPNs and non-nursing clinical staff to meet the needs of Rutgers Health patients.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Explains procedures and treatments to patient to gain cooperation, understanding and allay apprehension.</li><li>Responsible for assisting with patients who are medically complex and/or have sensitive medical or social issues.</li><li>Reviews plan of care, meds/tests with physicians as needed.</li><li>Contacts pharmacy for prescription renewals for patients.</li><li>Responsible for setting up and downloading 24-hour ambulatory blood pressure monitors.</li></ul> RWJ - Otolaryngology HNS RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 8266 New Brunswick NJ 26ST0039 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277369 2026-06-17T14:54:53-04:00 2026-06-17T14:54:54-04:00 Gallery Attendant (Temporary) <div>Rutgers University- Newark (RU-N), an urban public research university and anchor institution, located in Newark, New Jersey, a city of promise, is seeking a Gallery Attendant for Express Newark, who will report to the Gallery Director. As a hospitality position, the Gallery Attendant is required to have an outgoing personality. This can be a fulfilling job for art enthusiasts because you are surrounded by artworks all day and have the opportunity to speak to guests about them.<br><br>The position responsibilities include and are not limited to the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Serve as the front reception for the galleries</li><li>Greet visitors to the gallery, answer the telephone, respond to emails, and undertake clerical tasks</li><li>Assist with the preparation of materials for art-making workshops</li><li>Help guests navigate the various exhibition zones of the Paul Robeson Galleries, Express Newark, and the campus of Rutgers University – Newark</li><li>Ensure works of art are secure</li></ul> RCC Gallery - Newark Newark Chancellor-L2 Provost-L3 7215 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274116 2026-05-01T08:56:19-04:00 2026-05-01T08:56:19-04:00 Applied Music Instructors, VMPA <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the Faculty of Arts &amp; Sciences, Department of Visual, Media, and Performing Arts (VMPA), may be hiring Applied Music Instructors to teach lessons in voice and various instruments within the discipline for courses in Fall 2026 and/or Spring 2027; including the preparation for student juries, assign grades and coordinate any other requirements related to course instruction.</div> Fine Arts Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 6757 26FA0438 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266139 2025-12-31T09:29:40-05:00 2025-12-31T09:29:41-05:00 Open Rank Faculty - Psychiatric Rehabilitation and Counseling Professions <div>This is an open rank, 12-month faculty position. The successful candidate will contribute to the education of students who will become mental health practitioners specializing in the rehabilitation of individuals diagnosed with serious mental illness.<br><br></div><div><strong>Essential Duties and Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Serve as a primary instructor teaching undergraduate psychiatric rehabilitation students and contributing to the education of rehabilitation counseling students</li><li>Develop curricula materials for on-campus and web-based courses</li><li>Collaborate with internal and external stakeholders on developing and implementing funding proposals related to the Department’s educational and research agenda</li><li>Pursue a scholarly agenda, contributing to presentations and peer reviewed publications</li><li>Participate in professional association, community service and university service activities</li><li>Understands and adheres to legacy UMDNJ’s compliance standards as they appear in legacy UMDNJ’s Corporate Compliance Policy and Code of Conduct and Conflict of Interest Policy.</li><li>Keeps abreast of all pertinent federal, state and legacy UMDNJ regulations, laws and policies as they presently exist and as they change or are modified.</li></ul><div><br></div> SHP - Psychiatric Rehabilitati RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Health Professions-L3 7581 25FA1104 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280066 2026-08-27T09:55:50-04:00 2026-08-27T09:55:50-04:00 Mental Health Clinician III <div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Mental Health Clinician III in the PH Adult Newark of Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>Under direction, the primary purpose of the Mental Health Clinician III is to provide comprehensive evaluation, assessment and therapeutic intervention to address the psychological, emotional and social needs of individuals served by the unit. Duties include formulating evaluations, developing and implementing treatment plans, conducting individual, group, and family therapy and providing case management functions.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Contributes to and supports goals and objectives of the Department and UBHC.</li><li>Consistently behaves in accordance with established department and UBHC policies and procedures as observed by supervisor.</li><li>Actively participates in and contributes to smooth functioning of the department and demonstrates initiative and flexibility regarding work assignments as observed by supervisor and administration feedback.</li><li>Effectively contributes to and supports an environment that enhances the positive self-image of individuals served and preserves their human dignity as observed by supervisor.</li><li>Maintains effective, open communication with members of the treatment team as evidenced by supervisory observation and team members’ feedback.</li></ul> UBHC - PH Adult Newark RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8056 Newark NJ 26ST0034 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278312 2026-07-06T16:42:07-04:00 2026-07-06T16:42:08-04:00 Habilitation Counselor <div>&nbsp;Carries out the treatment plan as developed with input from the patient, family, significant others, and the approval of the treatment team. Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Habilitation Counselor for the&nbsp; Child &amp; Adolescent Services – School Based Program within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.&nbsp;<br><br>The primary purpose of the Habilitation Counselor is to participate as a member of a team in developing and maintaining a comprehensive referral process for children and families. Demonstrates competency in recognizing the needs and behaviors of patients (age 5 – 18 years).&nbsp;<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Spends appropriate or designated percentage of time in direct service with school personnel, families and/or children.</li><li>Engages with students and families via school and home visitation and follow-up as necessary to develop effective assessments and referrals to community based agencies to meet the needs of the families.</li><li>Provides case management services for patients assigned to caseloads. Demonstrates ability to recognize the unique needs of children and families.&nbsp;</li><li>Carries out the treatment plan as developed with input from the patient, family, significant others, and the approval of the treatment team.&nbsp;</li><li>Maintains a thorough knowledge of available medical, financial and community resources,.</li><li>Enters documentation of any and all relevant information in patient's chart within 1-5 working days of contact as indicated by random review of records.&nbsp; &nbsp;</li><li>Properly identifies problems and seeks reasonable solutions.</li><li>Consistently researches new resources to determine whether they would be appropriate for UBHC patients.&nbsp;</li></ul> UBHC - NJ4S Program RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8768 Piscataway NJ 26ST1477 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279479 2026-08-10T14:30:17-04:00 2026-08-10T14:30:17-04:00 Supervising Mental Health Specialist <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Supervising Mental Health Specialist for Addiction Services within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>Participates as a member of a treatment team in providing patient care and services to adolescent patients and or children (ages 4 years 21 years). Collaborates with the clinical and administrative leadership of the program offering comprehensive mental health care to patients and their families. Primarily responsible for providing patient care, leadership, training, and supervision to assigned staff.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Provides administrative supervision to Mental Health Specialists and assigned Staff.</li><li>Interacts with patients in a therapeutic manner according to their developmental level.</li><li>Participates in the observation and treatment of patients.</li><li>Maintains knowledge of policies and procedures.</li><li>Maintains cooperative working relationship with others and assumes appropriate leadership functions.</li><li>Performs routine driving as assigned.</li></ul> UBHC - Addiction Services RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 9266 Plainfield NJ 26ST1069 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279752 2026-08-20T09:00:06-04:00 2026-08-20T09:00:07-04:00 Technician I Per Diem UCHC MSCF (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking Per Diem Technician I for Midstate Correctional Facility located in Wrightstown NJ. The Technician I participates as a member of the clinical and administrative medical team at the Prison.<br><br>Among the duties for the position are:<br><br></div><ul><li>Takes vital signs, height and weight and documents in electronic medical records (EMR).</li><li>Assists the physician/associate practitioner with procedures, including preparing the inmate for the examination.</li><li>Obtains specimen collection and handling, including, but not limited to, drawing blood.</li><li>Assists with the cleaning, sterilization and securing of equipment within the Health Service Unit.</li><li>Maintains or assists in maintaining the supply stock in the Health Service Unit by ordering in a timely and appropriate manner.</li><li>Maintains the supply stock in the examination rooms.</li><li>Aggregates the orders of all medications and forwards to the pharmacy provider / local pharmacy.</li></ul> UCHC Midstate Correction Physi RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7680 Wrightstown NJ 26ST0981 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/276964 2026-06-11T13:20:54-04:00 2026-06-11T13:20:55-04:00 Clerical Assistant <div>Rutgers University – Newark, an urban public research anchor institution, located in Newark, New Jersey, a city of promise, is seeking a Clerical Assistant. The Part-Time Billing Clerk is responsible for accurate and timely billing, invoicing, and payment processing. This role supports the Business Office &amp; The Senior Program Coordinator by ensuring students’ accounts are billed correctly, records are maintained accurately, and billing discrepancies are resolved efficiently.<br><br></div><div>This position is responsible for and not limited to the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Prepare review and process invoices and/or billing statements</li><li>Verify bill data for accuracy and completeness</li><li>Enter billing information into the accounting or billing system. Ex. Notations for each student's account with the date the invoices were sent.</li><li>Respond to internal /external billing inquiries.</li><li>Maintain organized and confidential bill records</li><li>Identify and resolve any billing discrepancies</li><li>Support month-end or periodic reposting as assigned</li><li>Perform other administrative duties as needed</li></ul><div><br><br></div><div><br></div> Business Services - Newark Newark Chancellor-L2 Administration & Finance-L3 6628 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274080 2026-04-30T14:46:42-04:00 2026-04-30T14:46:42-04:00 Lecturers, Gender Studies <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the Faculty of Arts &amp; Sciences, Gender Studies Program, invites applications for lecturer positions within the discipline for courses in Fall 2026, Winter 2027, Spring 2027 and/or Summer 2027. We seek candidates with effective teaching experience who can teach online (Canvas), on campus, and/or at off campus locations and who can teach introductory and advanced courses in women's studies, gender, masculinities, transgender studies, and queer/LGBTQIA+ studies. The position may carry with it an opportunity to participate in campus programming planning around gender studies. Gender Studies offers an undergraduate academic major and minor and with courses in masculinities, queer studies, and women's studies. For information about the program see https://genderstudies.camden.rutgers.edu.</div> Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 8076 26FA0420 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266019 2025-12-31T09:14:02-05:00 2025-12-31T09:14:03-05:00 Diagnostic Radiologist--Per Diem <div>The Department of Radiology at New Jersey Medical School (NJMS) at Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is recruiting a per diem diagnostic radiologist to work at University Hospital and/or satellite facility of NJMS at Rutgers. The successful applicant will be expected to read a full spectrum of radiology services which may include the following: General Radiography, CT, MRI, Mammography and Nuclear Medicine.</div> NJMS - Radiology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7492 25FA0626 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279743 2026-08-20T08:49:02-04:00 2026-08-20T08:49:02-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse PT Eves UCHC GSYCF (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking Part Time Licensed Practical Nurse (Medical) for Garden State Youth Correctional Facility, located in Yardville, NJ<br><br>The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs. Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.</li><li>Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.</li><li>Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.</li><li>Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.</li><li>Documents all aspects of patient care.</li></ul> UCHC Garden State Youth Physic RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7676 Yardville NJ 26ST0193 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280041 2026-08-26T14:12:31-04:00 2026-08-26T14:12:32-04:00 Mental Health Specialist II Per Diem (Multiple Positions) <div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Mental Health Specialist II in the Emergency Screening<strong> </strong>in the Acute Psychiatric Services (APS) - Piscataway of Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>Under the supervision of the Program Coordinator, will provide services which support the delivery of clinical services in the Unit.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Takes primary responsibility for answering telephone calls from consumers.</li><li>Documents all telephone calls in the Acute Psychiatric Services (APS) telephone log or Electronic Medical Record (EMR).</li><li>Maintains confidentiality of information in accordance with Rutgers UBHC policy, University policy, Joint Commission standards and the Department of Mental Health and Addiction Services (DMHAS) requirements.</li><li>Refers consumer calls to a clinician as directed by the Program Coordinator.</li><li>Conducts initial triage of consumers and families when they arrive onsite five (5) minutes after arrival and provides immediate report to the Program Coordinator.</li></ul> UBHC - Emergency Screening Psy RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8029 Piscataway NJ 26ST0052 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278006 2026-06-30T11:05:25-04:00 2026-06-30T11:05:26-04:00 Hospitalist Admitter/Rounder <div>Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital (RWJUH) New Brunswick is seeking a full time Hospitalist Admitter to join our Hospitalist Division with Rutgers-Robert Wood Johnson Medical School, The State University of New Jersey.</div><div><br></div><div>In this position, the Admitter will primarily manage admitted patients to the hospitalist medicine service in close collaboration with consultants and subspecialists who practice at RWJUH. Working on a well-established, multidisciplinary team, the hospitalist’s main goal is to partner with the emergency department physicians, observation unit physicians, and intensivists for patients who require admission to the hospitalist service for acute inpatient levels of care on medical surgical and intermediate care units. The hospitalist will coordinate the inpatient care, assist with transitions of care back to the ambulatory setting, and work closely with the medical and surgical support staff, inclusive of advanced practice providers.</div><div><br></div><div>Ideal candidates will be joining a busy and growing practice delivering comprehensive care. A core function of the hospitalist will be to support a team-based approach, inclusive of communication with case managers, social workers, bed managers, and others to ensure appropriate patient-centered transitions of care. Moreover, the hospitalist will work extensively with the case management, social work, bed management, and pharmacy teams to assist in patient and family communications and care planning.</div><div>In addition to providing clinical care, our academic institution in collaboration with Robert Wood Johnson Medical School creates unique opportunities for physicians to engage in clinical and research programs, faculty development, quality improvement activities, and participation in a broad range of teaching initiatives.</div> RWJ - Medicine General Interna RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7773 26FA0640 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275707 2026-05-22T07:23:34-04:00 2026-05-22T07:23:35-04:00 Dining Services Student Worker (The Atrium) <div>Join the Rutgers Dining team as a Dining Services Student Worker in one of our dining halls or retail operations across the New Brunswick and Piscataway campuses. Rutgers Dining Services strives to be the best in culinary excellence and as a Dining Services Worker you play a critical role in the customer experience. From assisting in the preparation and service of food, to maintaining the presentation of the dining halls, to assisting guests, we have a variety of roles and will find the right one for you!<br><br>Dining Service Workers earn a paycheck and more:</div><ol><li>Student employee meal privileges.</li><li>Flexible schedules (10/20 hours/week) that work around your classes and activities.</li><li>Convenient on-campus locations.</li><li>Opportunities to advance to leadership positions such as Captain, Meal Manager and Student Unit Manager.</li><li>Valuable work experience to add to your resume.</li><li>Learn important job skills including interpersonal communications, team dynamics, dependability and time management.</li><li>A fun and welcoming environment.</li></ol> The Atrium New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Student Affairs - New Brunswic-L3 8704 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1144 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266376 2026-01-01T00:03:23-05:00 2026-01-01T00:03:25-05:00 Instructor - Part-time for Non-credit Classes - Environmental <div>The Office of Continuing Professional Education, part of NJAES-Cooperative Extension, invites applications for instructors to teach non-credit courses (half-day through multi-day) to adult learners on the New Brunswick campus; however, courses may also run at various locations throughout the State of New Jersey and/or in an online format. Instructors will develop and present course material during the assigned course times, coordinate materials with Program Coordinator, and follow-up with necessary paperwork. Course topics are primarily but not limited to: Environmental Science; Food Science/Safety; Recycling/Solid Waste Management; Stormwater Management; Landscape/Horticulture; Pesticide Safety; Environmental Policy; and Drinking Water/Wastewater. **Evergreen Posting to 12/31/2026**</div> Continuing Professional Educat New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 6966 25FA1180 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280179 2026-08-31T10:36:49-04:00 2026-08-31T10:36:50-04:00 Assistant Nurse Manager <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking an Assistant Nurse Manager for the Inpatient Units and Acute Psychiatric Services (APS) Department within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Assistant Nurse Manager is to be responsible for supervising the provision and management of patient care services for an assigned shift or unit on a consistent basis. The ANM serves as a resource for nursing care across the system on an as needed basis and works with other healthcare professionals to optimize patient outcomes. The ANM promotes quality patient care, patient safety and customer satisfaction. The ANM serves as the resource person for staff in explaining and executing policy and procedure. The ANM functions as a member of the interdisciplinary team; participates in quality improvement activities, educational activities and supports research endeavors. The role is consistent with the scope and standards outlined by the American Psychiatric Nurses Association for Psychiatric-Mental Health Nursing.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Assures the completion of admission nursing assessment and ongoing risk assessments in accordance with specific unit standards and regulatory requirements.</li><li>Supervises staff in assessing, planning, implementing and evaluating delivery of care.</li><li>Supervises all high risk situations to assure standards of practice are met on a consistent basis.</li><li>Facilitates effective communication inter and intra departmentally to coordinate efforts, resolve operations problems and improve quality of patient care.</li><li>Assists in interpreting and translating the theoretical concepts of nursing into the delivery of nursing services for all age groups.</li><li>Develops nursing policies and procedures that support unit/hospital objectives and comply with established guidelines.</li><li>Plans and implements safe staffing based upon patient acuity and defined staff plan.</li><li>Demonstrates respect and regard for the dignity of all patients, families, visitors and fellow employees to ensure a professional, responsible and courteous environment.</li></ul> UBHC - Acute Psychological Ser RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7987 Piscataway NJ 26ST1682 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278616 2026-07-10T12:44:52-04:00 2026-07-10T12:44:53-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse PT Nights UCHC NJSP <div>Rutgers University Correctional Healthcare is seeking a Part Time Licensed Practical Nurse for New Jersey State Prison, located in Trenton NJ<br><br>The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment. Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs.</li><li>Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.</li><li>Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.</li><li>Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.</li><li>Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.</li><li>Documents all aspects of patient care.</li></ul> UCHC New Jersey State Prison A RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7683 Trenton NJ 26ST0870 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/268860 2026-02-09T14:01:32-05:00 2026-02-09T14:01:33-05:00 Physician Specialist-Per Diem- Clinical Assistant Professor <div>This per diem position will take call, round, and see patients in the hospital as needed for approx. 12 weeks per year</div> NJMS - Neurology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7454 25FA1154 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280408 2026-09-03T14:35:45-04:00 2026-09-03T14:35:46-04:00 Research Support Associate <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Research Support Associate for the department of Biochemistry &amp; Molecular Biology at the Robert Wood Johnson Medical School.<br><br>Under the direction of the Principal Investigator, the Research Support Associate assists in single-molecule biophysical analysis of force-producing enzymes.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Prepares samples and carry out single-molecule biophysical assays on force-producing enzymes.</li><li>Assists with daily maintenance of various cell cultures.</li><li>Supports general molecular biology and recombinant protein preparation.</li><li>Uses and maintains custom-built instrumentation for optical and magnetic tweezers.</li><li>Uses and improves custom-written LabVIEW and MATLAB scripts for data acquisition and analysis.</li><li>Maintains clear and comprehensive laboratory records.</li><li>Performs statistical analyses of research data.</li><li>Analyzes and processes experimental data for publication and grant application.</li></ul> RWJ - Biochemistry & Molecular RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7782 Piscataway NJ 26ST1719 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279289 2026-08-03T14:29:53-04:00 2026-08-03T14:29:55-04:00 Department Nurse Manager UCHC NJSP <div>University Correctional Healthcare (UCHC) is seeking a Department Nurse Manager for the New Jersey State Prison, located in Trenton, NJ. The Department Nurse Manager performs supervisory responsibilities for nurses across shifts on an assigned unit(s) at a facility on a consistent basis. Collaborates with physicians, other health care personnel and interdepartmental personnel to ensure that the mission and objectives of the facility’s health program are realized. Maintains the standards of nursing practice/care and actualizes the philosophy, goals and objectives of the Nursing Service to staff, inmates and families.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Assists in interpreting and translating the theoretical concepts of nursing into the delivery of nursing services for adults (18 to 64 years) and geriatrics (65+) inmates within the Department of Corrections.</li><li>Assists in the participation of the structuring of organized nursing services.</li><li>Implements nursing functions within the context of UCHC.</li><li>Uses information systems to retrieve, implement and retain essential records and services.</li><li>Directs and supervises nursing and health care services in the context of the service.</li><li>Provides for cost-effective use of resources and participates in budget preparation in the context of a unit.</li><li>Assists with orientations and development of self, staff and nursing students.</li><li>Participates and provides leadership in quality assurance and quality improvement activities and provides training to staff and correctional officers.</li><li>Participates in decision making for organized nursing services</li></ul> UCHC New Jersey State Prison A RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7683 Trenton NJ 26ST0856 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275981 2026-05-28T12:06:29-04:00 2026-05-28T12:06:30-04:00 Lecturers in Engineering Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 <div>The School of Engineering at Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking multiple part-time instructors (Lecturer/Coadjutant) for the Fall 2026 and/or Spring 2027 semester to teach first year introduction to engineering course sequence 14:440:101/102. The successful candidates will cover the full range of duties associated with teaching, including, but not limited to, preparing course material; teaching during the assigned course times; supervising a group of teaching and learning assistants; holding office hours and providing appropriate out-of-class time for students; responding to student e-mails; conducting and grading assessments of students through assignments, exams, and other means, in a timely manner; and submitting final grades. Course appointments may require instruction during the day, in the evenings, online, or any combination of these. Prior college teaching experience in the course topic area is preferred. For questions regarding the position, please contact Professor Katie Barillas (katie.barillas@rutgers.edu) at SoE Undergraduate Education. In your application, please include (1) a cover letter, (2) your curriculum vitae, (3) the names and contact information of at least three references, and (4) a teaching statement providing evidence of effective and inclusive teaching. You may also upload any evidence of your teaching experience such as sample syllabus or course materials, results of student instructional ratings, or published work. Consideration of candidates will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled.</div> Academic Programs New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Engineering-L3 7105 26FA0523 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/273066 2026-04-15T16:25:26-04:00 2026-04-15T16:25:27-04:00 Post-Doc Assocaite - Verzi <div>The position will conduct state-of-the-art epigenomics and single cell assays using mouse genetic or organoid models to investigate gene regulatory mechanisms related to intestinal health including diet, nutrition, inflammation, regeneration, stem cell biology, and colon cancer.</div> Human Genetics Institute of NJ New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 8177 26FA0353 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/264977 2025-12-11T12:18:56-05:00 2025-12-11T12:18:57-05:00 Postdoctoral Associate - Astrophysics (Rutgers-CCA Flatiron Research Fellow) <div>The Rutgers University Department of Physics and Astronomy invites applications for a postdoctoral research position starting on, or after, 7/01/2026. The position is to be offered jointly with the Center for Computational Astrophysics (CCA) at the Simons Foundation Flatiron Institute in New York City. For full consideration, applicants are encouraged to submit their materials by January 10, 2026.<br><br></div><div>The successful applicant will work at the galaxy-interstellar medium interface under the guidance of Professor Blakesley Burkhart, in collaboration with other members of the CCA and Rutgers science staff, and contribute to a research program on star formation, galaxy formation, the interstellar medium, and fluid dynamics. The successful candidate will be expected to work on all or a subset of the above topics, be proficient in working with large data-sets (observational or numerical), machine learning, and running/analyzing numerical simulations.<br><br></div><div>The initial appointment will be for two years at Rutgers University followed by a third year appointment held at CCA as a Flatiron Research Fellow. There is a possibility of an additional year’s extension at CCA, contingent on performance. The successful candidate will benefit from the rich scientific atmospheres at Rutgers and CCA. Weekly visits between the scientific communities at Rutgers and CCA are highly encouraged. The postdoc will have opportunities to participate in observational work, help mentor graduate students, attend journal clubs/coffee meetings/colloquia at CCA and Rutgers. Funds for conference travel and professional development will be provided.<br><br></div> Physics & Astronomy New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 8126 25FA1006 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279631 2026-08-17T11:09:07-04:00 2026-08-17T11:09:08-04:00 Laboratory/Technical Assistant (Casual) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Laboratory/Technical Assistant for the Waksman Student Scholars Program within the Waksman Institute.<br><br>This role will support operation of the Waksman Students Scholars Program (WSSP), a year-round high school science outreach program. High school students in the WSSP isolate plasmid DNA clones generated from a species of plants and investigate the genes using molecular biology techniques in the laboratory and analysis of DNA sequences using online bioinformatics programs. The individual will report directly to the WSSP Program Directors.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Reviews the student's analysis of DNA clones and provides feedback and guidance both in person during the summer programs at Waksman Institute and on-line during the academic year.</li><li>Performs BLAST analyses and searches of the bioinformatic databases on the students’ DNA sequences.</li><li>Analyzes 1000 “unknown” sequences, reviews the quality of the sequence data and perform searches of the bioinformatic databases to compare with the students’ answers.</li><li>Organizes and submits “unknown” DNA sequences analyzed by high school students for publication on the NCBI DNA databases.</li></ul> Waksman Institute of Microbiol New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 6726 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279909 2026-08-24T16:09:38-04:00 2026-08-24T16:09:39-04:00 Graduate Assistant <div>Rutgers School of Health Professions (SHP) is seeking a Graduate Assistant to work in the Dean's Office.<br><br>The purpose of this Graduate Assistant position is to work with the AI in Education project members of the SHP Scholarship of Teaching and Learning (SoTL) Laboratory to design, build, and maintain a next-generation learning platform that leverages large language models, AI agents, and cloud technologies to support healthcare education and research. The position combines software engineering, AI integration, and technical research, working collaboratively with interdisciplinary teams to create scalable, secure, and innovative simulation experiences that enhance learning, assessment, and clinical training.</div><div><br>Essential duties and responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Design, develop, and maintain full-stack Al -powered web applications and platform components supporting the Rutgers Virtual Health Simulator (VHS), including front end interfaces, backend services, APIs, databases, and cloud infrastructure.</li><li>Research, prototype, integrate, and optimize Large Language Models (LLMs), AI agents, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipelines, and related Al technologies to support clinical educational simulations, intelligent tutoring, clinical research analytics, and personalized learning experiences.</li><li>Develop scalable backend services, data pipelines, and secure application architectures for storing, processing, and managing simulation data, user interactions, analytics, and educational content while ensuring system reliability, security, and compliance with institutional policies.</li><li>Collaborate with faculty, clinicians, instructional designers, and interdisciplinary research teams to translate educational and research objectives into technical requirements, software solutions, and platform enhancements.</li><li>Evaluate emerging Al technologies, conduct technical research, develop proof-of-concept implementations, and prepare technical documentation, architecture diagrams, and software documentation to support ongoing platform development and future research initiatives.</li><li>Participate in software testing, debugging, deployment, performance optimization, system maintenance, and continuous improvement activities using modem software engineering, DevOps, and cloud development practices.</li><li>Provide support in research studies including data collection, analysis, documentation, and technical assistance for ongoing projects.</li></ul> School of Health Professions RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Health Professions-L3 7567 Newark NJ 26ST1645 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277756 2026-06-25T10:59:48-04:00 2026-06-25T10:59:49-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse PT Days EMCFW UCHC (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Part Time Licensed Practical Nurse for Edna Mahan Correctional Facility, located in Clinton, NJ<br><br>The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br>* Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs.<br>* Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.<br>* Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.<br>* Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.<br>* Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.<br>* Documents all aspects of patient care.</div> UCHC-Edna Mahan Corr-Ancillary RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7682 Clinton NJ 26ST0575 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274937 2026-05-13T11:25:27-04:00 2026-05-13T11:25:28-04:00 Fall Semester 2026:  Lecturer, Educational Psychology <div>The Rutgers University, Graduate School of Education, invites applications for Lecturer (formerly Part Time Lecturers) teaching positions in the department of Educational Psychology during the Fall 2026 Semester, September 1, 2026 through December 22, 2026.<br><br>Successful applicants will instruct undergraduate or graduate level courses in at least one of the the following content areas:<br><br>-School Counseling and Counseling Psychology<br><br>-College Student Affairs and Higher Education<br><br>-Educational Psychology: Learning &amp; Cognition and/or Human Development<br><br>-Gifted Education<br><br>-Special Education<br><br>-Educational Statistics, Measurement, and/or Evaluation<br><br>Courses will be offered in a range of modalities beyond traditional settings, including hybrid and online formats. Course appointments are in the New Brunswick area, as well as, hybrid/online format.</div> Education Psychology New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Graduate School of Education-L3 6813 25FA0514 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266229 2025-12-31T09:38:02-05:00 2025-12-31T09:38:02-05:00 Chair - Emergency Medicine <div>Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School seeks a Chair of Emergency Medicine.&nbsp; This position is a senior leadership role responsible for advancing the strategic, clinical, educational, and research missions of the department. The Chair is responsible for fostering excellence in patient care, advancing innovative research, promoting top-tier education and training programs, and championing equity and inclusion. The Chair will serve as a key member of the institution’s leadership team, collaborating across disciplines to achieve strategic goals. This leader will establish the department as a national model for integrated academic and clinical excellence in Emergency Medicine.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Reporting directly to the Dean and working closely with the Senior Associate Dean for Clinical Affairs and other members of the Dean's Executive Team, the Chair directs and coordinates the clinical, teaching and research efforts within the department. This position requires a leader who will build a strong, collaborative relationship with the school's principal hospital affiliate that facilitates the growth and recognition of an academic medical center, and serve as a role model and catalyst of intellectual attainment. In addition, the Chair will advise on personnel matters, participate in activities of faculty committees, support faculty pursuit of research and scholarly activity, and develop and manage the departmental budget. The chair will also advise the Dean on academic, clinical and financial matters. Working closely with Emergency Medicine Department Administrators, the chair will be responsible for the supervision of approximately 31 clinical faculty, 21 APPs, 1 Ph.D. researcher and 5 staff members.&nbsp;</div> RWJ Medical School RWJ-Finance Office-L2 RWJ Medical School-L3 7861 25FA1225 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280104 2026-08-27T16:16:04-04:00 2026-08-27T16:16:04-04:00 Classroom Assistant II-ELRA Preschool <div>The Classroom Assistant II is a full-time position responsible for supporting the daily operation of the Infant/Toddler classroom and assisting in creating a safe, nurturing, structured, and developmentally appropriate learning environment for young children. This position supports the planning and implementation of daily routines, classroom activities, transitions, meals, rest periods, outdoor play, and instructional experiences that promote children’s social, emotional, cognitive, language, and physical development. The Classroom Assistant follows classroom instructional plans, individualized child-care routines, daily schedules, and developmental activities established and supervised by the Program Manager. The position supports children’s physical, social-emotional, language, cognitive, and motor development through responsive interactions, supervised play, caregiving routines, and age-appropriate learning activities.<br><br>This is a grant funded position contingent upon the availability of funds to support it.&nbsp;</div> Community Leadership Cntr Cam Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Community Leadership Cntr Cam-L3 6634 Camden NJ 26ST1674 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278459 2026-07-09T08:54:34-04:00 2026-07-09T08:54:35-04:00 Assistant/Associate/Full Professor <div>The newly launched Rutgers Center for NeuroMetabolism (CNM), in collaboration with the Child Health Institute of New Jersey (CHINJ), the Department of Neuroscience and Cell Biology (NCB), and the Rutgers Brain Health Institute (BHI), are seeking to recruit an open rank, tenure-track/tenured faculty positions at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. Located within the transformative Rutgers Helix complex, the CNM is poised to lead groundbreaking research at the intersection of neuroscience and metabolism, focusing on disorders such as obesity, type 2 diabetes, eating disorders, and related inflammatory, vascular, or gastrointestinal diseases. The CNM aims to build a world-class research program within one of the nation’s leading academic medical centers. We seek dynamic researchers to join a thriving and collaborative community with access to cutting-edge resources, generous start-up packages, and opportunities for impactful research and mentorship. The Child Health Institute of New Jersey (CHINJ) is a state-of-the-art research institute with over a dozen research laboratories with more than 80 faculty, fellows, students, and technicians. CHINJ is located on the Rutgers University—New Brunswick campus and includes 40,000 square feet of state-of-the-art laboratories and office space as well as sophisticated facilities for modeling pediatric diseases. CHINJ is part of the Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School (RWJMS).<br><br></div><div>We seek researchers with expertise in neurometabolism with a focus on mechanisms underlying metabolic, neurological, and psychiatric disorders, as well as their translational potential for clinical therapies. The ideal candidate will bring innovative perspectives to a collaborative environment, leveraging Rutgers’ resources to drive discoveries from bench to bedside.Tenure-track appointments will be made through appropriate departments (e.g. Neuroscience and Cell Biology, Pediatrics, Medicine and Psychiatry) at RWJMS, with full access to graduate training programs and research resources. Successful candidates will be provided with excellent start-up packages and will be expected to develop and maintain strong, externally funded research programs, and participate in collaborative projects with other Departments and Institutes on the campus.<br><br></div><div><strong>Why Join Rutgers CNM?</strong></div><ul><li><strong>Exceptional Resources:</strong> Access to exceptional core facilities, including a state-of-the-art vivarium with 24/7 activity monitoring system, behavioral testing cores, metabolic core, imaging core, and cutting-edge lab facilities at the Helix.</li><li><strong>Generous Start-Up Packages:</strong> Competitive support to establish or expand your research program.</li><li><strong>Collaborative Ecosystem:</strong> Work alongside renowned researchers within a supportive and forward-thinking environment.</li><li><strong>Access to global talent:</strong> The CNM faculty has access to graduate students from multiple PhD programs, including Neuroscience, Molecular Bioscience, Biomedical Engineering, Endocrinology and Animal Sciences, Behavioral Neuroscience, and Toxicology. Additionally, CNM faculty has access to amazing top undergraduate students from the Rutgers Honors College, Cell Biology and Neuroscience, and General Biology. Furthermore, Rutgers is attractive to globally talented postdoctoral fellows due to the excellence in research, the geological location, and the diverse cultures.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Successful faculty candidates will be expected to perform the following duties:</strong></div><ul><li><strong>Develop and maintain a nationally and internationally recognized research program</strong> supported by external grant funding, leveraging cutting-edge, interdisciplinary, and translational approaches.</li><li><strong>Foster collaborations</strong> with faculty in the CNM, the CHINJ, the Departments of Neuroscience and Cell Biology, Pediatrics and Psychiatry, the Brain Health Institute of New Jersey, and the broader Rutgers Health and Rutgers University community</li><li><strong>Engage in mentorship and teaching</strong> by participating in Rutgers graduate and medical student training programs.</li><li><strong>Contribute to the academic community</strong> through: Participation in seminars and faculty meetings; Mentoring opportunities for trainees and junior faculty; Involvement in institute-wide community activities</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Essential Duties and Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Understands and adheres to Rutgers<strong> </strong>compliance standards as they appear in the Rutgers Corporate Compliance Policy and Code of Conduct and Conflict of Interest Policy.</li><li>Keeps abreast of all pertinent federal, state and Rutgers<strong> </strong>regulations, laws and policies as they presently exist and as they change or are modified as outlined in Rutgers compliance policies.</li><li>Ensures that all staff are trained and evaluated on their knowledge of and adherence to compliance policies and procedures specific to their jobs.</li><li>Outstanding human relations and leadership skills and the ability to function in a team environment are required. Knowledge of how to accomplish superior performance in a unionized environment is preferred</li></ul> RWJ - Child Health Institute RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7852 25FA0414 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267547 2026-01-20T11:35:04-05:00 2026-01-20T11:35:04-05:00 Co Adj Non-Teaching (Coaching Facilitator) <div>The New Jersey Tiered Systems of Support for Early Reading (NJTSS-ER) Project provides professional development to school districts to facilitate implementation of NJTSS-ER with students in kindergarten through third grade. With funding from a recent New Jersey Department of Education grant, Rutgers University is seeking a co-adjunct staff member to provide guidance on NJTSS-ER support coaching. The person in this position will also facilitate development and integration of coaching support materials and training.<br>One of the most complex aspects of this position involves exercising professional judgment pertaining to appropriate coaching approaches and the use of data to inform the coaching process. This person must be able to independently assess practices and procedures, establish protocols for analyzing student learning data, and determine appropriate next steps. Discretion is essential in determining how to approach coaching that promotes educator reflection and growth while also aligning with NJTSS-ER priorities. This person must also be able to navigate varying levels of district/school/educator readiness and school culture, tailoring strategies to meet individual educator needs while ensuring fidelity to research-based reading and writing practices. This requires balancing content expertise and pedagogical knowledge to influence instructional supports that ultimately improve student outcomes.</div><div>&nbsp;</div> Inclusive Schools Project New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Graduate School of Applied & P-L3 6826 26FA0043 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280261 2026-09-01T07:58:04-04:00 2026-09-01T07:58:05-04:00 Research Teaching Specialist III (Virology and Bacteriology) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Research Teaching Specialist III (Virology and Bacteriology) in the Department of Medicine within the New Jersey Medical School (NJMS).&nbsp;<br><br>The Research Teaching Specialist III will be responsible for daily oversight of development and testing new assays safely in the BSL3/ABSL3 environment while adhering to the CDC guidelines, federal, state, and local regulations, and institutional guidelines. Will perform research with BSL2/BSL3 bacteria and viruses and Select Agents in in-vitro and in- vivo models. Will also assist the BSL3 Director and Deputy Lab Manager to oversee the lab duties as assigned.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>Collaborates with principal investigators, research teams, and faculty on ongoing research projects involving bacterial and viral research.</li><li>Cultures and quantitates pathogenic and non-pathogenic bacteria and viruses including SARS-COV-2, M.Tuberculosis requiring work in the BSL3/ABSL3 facilities including Tier 1 agents.</li><li>Performs detailed MICs and DNA/RNA extraction of above-described pathogens using various systems and performs preliminary analysis.</li><li>Assists in the development and testing of new assays.</li><li>Assist in preparing IACUC approvals, renewals and submissions.</li><li>Assists design of animal studies for IBC, IACUC, and for grant submission.&nbsp;</li></ul> NJMS - Medicine Infectious Dis RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7442 Newark NJ 26ST1702 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278895 2026-07-16T12:38:58-04:00 2026-07-16T12:38:58-04:00 Postdoctoral Researcher in Theoretical and Computational Chemistry <div>The group of Dr. Chong Sun in the Department of Chemistry and Chemical Biology is seeking a postdoctoral researcher to join interdisciplinary projects at the intersection of theoretical chemistry, machine learning and quantum information science. Candidates with experience in method development and high-performance computing are especially encouraged to apply. A Ph.D. in chemistry, physics, computer science, or a related field is required. The position offers a flexible start date, competitive salary, and full benefits. To apply, please submit a CV with a full publication list, a cover letter, and three reference letters.&nbsp;</div> Chemistry & Chemical Biology New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 7001 26FA0657 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/271252 2026-03-20T10:05:05-04:00 2026-03-20T10:05:05-04:00 Co Adj - Non Teaching <div>| The Graduate School of Applied and Professional Psychology (GSAPP), Office of Professional Development and Continuing education (OPDCE), is currently seeking a mental health professional with expertise in a particular content area and the ability to instruct a continuing education workshop.</div> Applied Psychology Center New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Graduate School of Applied & P-L3 8116 26FA0267 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280070 2026-08-27T10:18:30-04:00 2026-08-27T10:18:31-04:00 SR RESEARCH ANIMAL WORKER <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Sr Research Animal Worker for the Animal Care Program, Department of Animal Science.</div><div><br>Among the key duties of the position are the following:</div><ul><li>Performs diversified duties to support the operation of the Animal Care Program with the daily care of livestock animals used in research, teaching and outreach on the Cook Campus agricultural animal farm.</li><li>Guides and instructs student workers in the performance of their duties.</li></ul> Animal Care New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 7156 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1672 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278321 2026-07-07T09:39:30-04:00 2026-07-07T09:39:31-04:00 Management Assistant <div>Rutgers School of Health Professions (SHP) is seeking a Management Assistant to work in the Research and MSST Division of the SHP-Dean’s Office-Administration.<br><br></div><div>Under direction of Sr. Director, Research Administration, the Management Assistant provides high-level administrative support to the School of Health Professions’ Office of Research and Methodology and Statistics Support Team (MSST). The Management Assistant is responsible for providing administrative support to research faculty and staff. Additionally, the Management Assistant executes assignments and tasks requiring data collection, information gathering and analysis, data entry/retrieval, and database maintenance. The Management Assistant also coordinates activities and events for assigned projects and programs.<br><br>Essential duties and responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Assists in sending out communications for events, meetings, and other communications to SHP Faculty from our Research Office.</li><li>Processes grant-related expenses (i.e. consultants, supplies, travel) and non-grant related expenses for Tenure Track Research Faculty, including some select Research Faculty.</li><li>Manages the procurement of supplies and equipment, maintains the facilities supply inventory and associated databases. Monitors spaces for required maintenance and distributes supplies as needed.</li><li>Assists School’s Work-In-Progress Seminar Series.</li><li>Assists Associate Dean for Research in administrative coordination, scheduling, meeting coordination, meeting summaries, and helps with basic document preparation.</li></ul> School of Health Professions RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Health Professions-L3 7567 Newark NJ 26ST1478 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266835 2026-01-06T16:12:52-05:00 2026-01-06T16:12:53-05:00 Research Teaching Specialist IV (Biostatistics and Epidemiology) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Research Teaching Specialist IV in the EPI &amp; Health Outcome Department at the Rutgers Cancer Institute.&nbsp;<br><br>Under the direction of the Principal Investigator, the Research Teaching Specialist IV provides data management and programming support to fulfill the needs of faculty conducting cancer epidemiology research. This position reports to the Chief of Cancer Epidemiology and Health Outcomes Section.<br><br>Among the key duties for this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>As assigned, carries out various data cleaning, management, and programming tasks relating to relevant research activities.&nbsp;</li><li>Assists in all phases of research studies as assigned by the Principal Investigators conducting epidemiological and related research and communicates with primary data collection staff to resolve discrepancies in recorded data.&nbsp;</li><li>May assist in organizing and conducting specialized research activities for a particular research project.&nbsp;</li><li>Assists with the instructing and training of students, fellows and research staff in data analysis and relevant research projects as assigned by the Principal Investigators.&nbsp;</li><li>As directed, conducts data processing and statistical analyses.&nbsp;</li><li>Develops and maintains analytical datasets, syntax, and data dictionaries for research projects. &nbsp;</li></ul> CINJ - EPI & Health Outcome RBHS Chancellor-L2 Cancer Institute of New Jersey-L3 7912 New Brunswick NJ 25ST1731 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280222 2026-08-31T13:42:52-04:00 2026-08-31T13:42:53-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse FT Eves UCHC GSYCF <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking Full Time Licensed Practical Nurse (Medical) for Garden State Youth Correctional Facility, located in Yardville, NJ<br><br>The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs. Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.</li><li>Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.</li><li>Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.</li><li>Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.</li><li>Documents all aspects of patient care.</li></ul> UCHC Garden State Youth Physic RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7676 Yardville NJ 26ST1692 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278727 2026-07-13T12:01:34-04:00 2026-07-13T12:01:35-04:00 Temporary Research Assistant <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Temporary Research Assistant within Radiation Oncology at the Rutgers Cancer Institute.&nbsp;<br><br>Under the direction of the Principal Investigator or designee, the Temporary Research Assistant will assist in research on the lab grant deliverables. The incumbent will review, provide quality control, and analyze study data.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Works under the direction of the PI or his/her designee. Responsible for executing laboratory tasks as outlined by the Principal Investigator or a senior member of laboratory team.&nbsp;</li><li>Performs functions as directed for experiments that are proposed in the grant, under the direction of the principal investigator and other designated lab members.&nbsp;</li><li>Maintains department database on a computer. Candidate must have competent computer skills and be able to utilize equipment and technology in support of the assigned project(s).&nbsp;</li><li>Must possess effective oral and written communication skills and ability to summarize scientific research process and communicate project findings.&nbsp;</li></ul> CINJ - Feng Tumor Suppresion RBHS Chancellor-L2 Cancer Institute of New Jersey-L3 8559 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1518 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/269635 2026-02-23T09:40:15-05:00 2026-02-23T09:40:15-05:00 Clinical Assistant Professor/Oncology <div>Hackensack University Medical Center is a 781-bed teaching and research hospital and is part of Hackensack Meridian Health, which is affiliated with Rutgers University–New Jersey Medical School. Hackensack University Medical Center is the largest provider of inpatient and outpatient services in the state of New Jersey. This is a long-standing partnership with the medical center and the position has the full support of the physician and nursing staff at the John Theurer Cancer Center. There are multiple faculty members at Hackensack University Medical Center in the areas of Organ Transplant, Infectious Disease and Pediatrics. There are also hospital-based clinical practitioners. The department considers this a priority hire to maintain the continuity and quality of our service to and collaboration with site and the John Theurer Cancer Center.</div> Pharmacy Practice & Administra RBHS Chancellor-L2 Ernest Mario School of Pharmac-L3 6720 25FA1132 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280459 2026-09-04T13:39:23-04:00 2026-09-04T13:39:24-04:00 Mental Health Specialist II - Part Time - NJ Hopeline <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Mental Health Specialist II (Part Time) for the NJ Hopeline within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>Performs functions in support of the Unit’s mission providing streamlined, prompt, and “customer friendly” services to clients of the 988 Lifeline Services. Receives telephone, chat and/or text requests for service, undertakes assessment of the service need of the client and responds by offering support and appropriate referrals or disposition. Demonstrates competency in recognizing the unique needs of clients and applying relevant assessment and support skills with regard to a wide range of issues.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Interacts with client in a therapeutic manner.</li><li>Participates in ensuring that all service requests are handled in an effective and “client friendly” manner.</li><li>Assesses service requests/referrals and responds in accordance with prescribed procedures.</li><li>Assesses client’s condition in order to make/authorize an appropriate disposition.</li><li>Assumes overall responsibilities for completion of all request and documentation for disposition.</li><li>Documents assessments, interventions, and interactions with clients in a timely manner and in accordance with established policies.</li></ul> UBHC - NJ Hopeline RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8707 Remote NJ 26ST1296 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279408 2026-08-07T12:42:59-04:00 2026-08-07T12:43:00-04:00 Mental Health Specialist III - Per Diem - Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a per diem Mental Health Specialist III for the Addiction Services Department within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Mental Health Specialist III position is to serve as a team member in providing and maintaining a safe therapeutic milieu. This position provides support and assistance to an interdisciplinary team. Actively participates in group and treatment-related activities and crisis interventions.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Provides direct care responsibilities for consumers/patients as assigned.</li><li>Engages consumer/patient in appropriate treatment intervention based on service plan and supervisory directions.</li><li>Interacts and communicates with consumer/patient in therapeutic manner.</li><li>Assists with consumer admission, transfer, and discharge procedures.</li><li>Consistently demonstrates session/group facilitation management skills.</li><li>Maintains appropriate consumer/patient records as mandated by University Behavioral Health Care policy and applicable accrediting organization standards.</li><li>Responsible for transporting individuals served to treatment related activities.</li></ul> UBHC - Addictions RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8003 Plainfield NJ 26ST1012 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/276310 2026-06-02T11:29:20-04:00 2026-06-09T11:46:37-04:00 Post Doctoral Associate <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a highly qualified candidate for a Postdoctoral Research Associate position in the Department of Kinesiology and Health, School of Arts and Sciences. The Postdoctoral Associate will work with Dr. Peixuan Zheng on a DoD/DoW funded project investigating cognitive health, vascular function, and physical activity in people with multiple sclerosis and healthy controls, as well as assist with other research projects in the Physical activity &amp; Neuroscience Research Laboratory. This position provides an excellent opportunity to contribute to innovative, multidisciplinary research at the intersection of exercise science, brain health, wearable devices/real-world behavior, vascular physiology, novel biomarkers for neurovegetative disease in a stimulating, supportive, and mentored environment.</div> DLS Kinesiology & Health New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 8131 26FA0520 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/273901 2026-04-29T10:38:44-04:00 2026-04-29T10:38:45-04:00 Assistant/Associate Professor of Medicine-Hospital Medicine <div>This position serves as an attending for the Division of Hospital Medicine in the Department of Medicine. This Hospitalist position can be classified as day shift or night shift and candidates must be board certified/eligible in Hospital Medicine.<br><strong>Multiple Positions Available.</strong><br><br></div><div>Candidates will be expected to participate fully in the patient care, teaching, research and service activities of the Department of Medicine and Division of Hospital Medicine. Ideal candidates will possess excellent clinical and communication skills, a strong commitment to serving a multicultural diverse patient population and teaching/faculty experience with a passion for training students and residents, and a commitment to scholarship.<br><br></div><div><strong>C</strong>andidates must also submit a cover letter, three letters of reference, a current CV, and complete contact information.<br><br></div> NJMS - Medicine Academic Medic RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7440 23FA1116 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/265914 2025-12-31T09:01:33-05:00 2025-12-31T09:01:34-05:00 Co-Adjutant Researcher - York Lab <div>The Laboratory for Biomolecular Simulation Research (<a href=\"http://lbsr.rutgers.edu/\"><strong>http://lbsr.rutgers.edu</strong></a>) and Institute for Quantitative Biomedicine (<a href=\"https://iqb.rutgers.edu/\"><strong>https://iqb.rutgers.edu/</strong></a>) at Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is seeking 2 high-level software development scientists</div><div><br>in a joint project with <a href=\"https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/\"><strong>Nvidia</strong></a>, world leader in artificial intelligence (AI) computing, and <a href=\"https://tandemai.com/\"><strong>Tandem AI</strong></a>, an advanced technology company providing access to the most advanced tools in drug discovery. This is an exciting opportunity for a talented scientist to gain valuable experience developing software infrastructure for drug discovery. At Rutgers, the LBSR is directed by Professor Darrin York, and is dedicated to the development and application of innovative biomolecular simulation tools for enzyme design and drug discovery (<a href=\"https://theory.rutgers.edu/\"><strong>https://theory.rutgers.edu/</strong></a>). The successful candidate will develop web pages and front-ends to showcase new drug discovery tools and databases used to train innovative machine learning models. This is an outstanding opportunity for an ambitious computer scientist/software engineer to be involved as a lead in a project of this scope and impact and is ideally suited for individuals with career aspirations to lead efforts in drug discovery or related new start-up company efforts.</div> Quantitative Biomedicine Inst New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 6749 25FA0471 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279668 2026-08-18T10:11:11-04:00 2026-08-18T10:11:12-04:00 Program Support Specialist (Clerkship for Clinical Education Activities) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Program Support Specialist for the Office of Education at the Robert Wood Johnson Medical School.<br><br>Under the supervision of the Assistant Dean for Education and the direction of the discipline specific Clerkship Director, assists with the development, implementation and monitoring of educational programs within the department. Provides administrative and program support to the Clerkship/Elective/Sub-internship and Boot Camp Directors. Reports to Assistant Dean for Education. The Program Support Specialist for Clinical Education Activities will support to all departmental clinical activities: clerkships, electives, sub-internships, bootcamps departmental activities for physical diagnosis in PCM 2 New Brunswick Site, summative clinical skills assessment and departmental-specific activities in Introduction to the Clerkship Experience.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Provides administrative support to departmental Clerkship, Electives, Sub-internship and Boot Camp Directors and/or the Chief of Education Division as it pertains to all undergraduate clinical medical education activities.</li><li>Liaison to students, faculty, residents, community faculty, affiliated sites and school administration for any issues or questions relating to the Clerkship, Electives, Sub-internships Boot Camp.</li><li>Maintains and update web-based course platform (AMP) syllabus and related course material.</li><li>Serves as first support contact for students with issues/problems relating to CATS and AMP.</li><li>Prepares all student activity schedules for each clinical rotation, including weekly floor assignments, scrub sessions (if required), computer training, tutorial sessions, simulation sessions, and exam reviews. (150-190 students/year).</li></ul> RWJ - Education RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7748 New Brunswick NJ 26ST0731 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279999 2026-08-26T09:06:12-04:00 2026-08-26T09:06:13-04:00 Research Teaching Specialist V <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Research Teaching Specialist V for the Center for Advanced Biotechnology and Medicine (CABM) within Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences (RBHS).<br><br>The primary purpose of the Research Teaching Specialist V is to investigate how host-microbe interactions influence health and disease through multidisciplinary approaches integrating molecular biology, immunology, microbiology, and experimental model systems. Under the direction of the Principal Investigator, the Research Teaching Specialist V will perform cellular and molecular biology experiments related to the ongoing investigatory activities of the laboratory, contribute to laboratory setup, assist with maintaining laboratory organization and research operations, and participate in collaborative research projects.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Conduct research under the direction of the Principal Investigator and actively participate in laboratory meetings.</li><li>Assist in establishing laboratory protocols and standard operating procedures and support the setup, organization, and operation of a newly established research laboratory.</li><li>Assist in the day-to-day maintenance of laboratory space, equipment, supplies, instrumentation, and inventory, ensuring a safe and efficient research environment.</li><li>Prepare laboratory reagents, buffers, media, and solutions.</li><li>Perform and assist with molecular, cellular, biochemical, microbiological, and animal research techniques, including sterile technique, cell culture, bacterial culture, PCR, genotyping, immunostaining, microscopy, protein biochemistry methods, mouse handling, colony management, tissue collection and processing, and related experimental procedures in accordance with established laboratory protocols.</li><li>Maintain accurate laboratory records and documentation, organize and analyze experimental data, and assist with the preparation of figures, presentations, manuscripts, and laboratory reports.</li><li>Assist the Principal Investigator in training laboratory personnel and trainees in laboratory techniques, standard operating procedures, and safe laboratory practices.</li><li>Support laboratory administrative activities, including ordering, receiving, shipping, inventory management, and coordination of laboratory resources.</li></ul> RBHS RBHS Chancellor-L2 CABM-L3 7883 Piscataway NJ 26ST1655 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277775 2026-06-25T11:19:18-04:00 2026-06-25T11:19:19-04:00 Staff Nurse FT Nights UCHC EMCFW <div>Rutgers University Correctional Healthcare is seeking a Full Time UCHC Staff Nurse for Edna Mahan Correctional Facility located in Clinton, NJ. The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus. Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br><br>Among the duties are:</div><ul><li>Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the inmate-patient including adults (18 to 64 years), and geriatrics (65+) within the framework established by the correctional system.</li><li>Utilizes effective communication skills by demonstrating respect, concern and courtesy in all interpersonal relationships.</li><li>Uses current knowledge to promote a safe environment for providing health care to inmate-patients.</li></ul> UCHC-Edna Mahan Corr-Ancillary RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7682 Clinton NJ 26ST0703 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275520 2026-05-20T13:44:19-04:00 2026-05-20T13:44:20-04:00 Dining Services Student Worker - Server Position - (Henry's Diner) <div>Join the Rutgers Dining team as a Dining Services Student Worker in one of our dining halls or retail operations across the New Brunswick and Piscataway campuses. Rutgers Dining Services strives to be the best in culinary excellence and as a Dining Services Worker you play a critical role in the customer experience. From assisting in the preparation and service of food, to maintaining the presentation of the dining halls, to assisting guests, we have a variety of roles and will find the right one for you!<br><br>Dining Service Workers earn a paycheck and more:<br>1. Student employee meal privileges.<br>2. Flexible schedules (10/20 hours/week) that work around your classes and activities.<br>3. Convenient on-campus locations.<br>4. Opportunities to advance to leadership positions such as Captain, Meal Manager and Student Unit Manager.<br>5. Valuable work experience to add to your resume.<br>6. Learn important job skills including interpersonal communications, team dynamics, dependability and time management.<br>7. A fun and welcoming environment.</div> Henry's Diner New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Student Affairs - New Brunswic-L3 6681 Piscataway NJ 26ST1101 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266311 2025-12-31T09:48:33-05:00 2025-12-31T09:48:33-05:00 Hill Assistant Professorships and other Postdoctoral Positions <div>The Rutgers Mathematics Department offers various postdoctoral positions in Mathematics. These include several Hill or Triennial Assistant Professorships, which are three-year non-tenure track, non-renewable, Post-Doctoral Research instructorships. Subject to availability of funding, the Department expects to have five of these positions that will start in Fall of 2026. Hill Assistant Professorships carry a teaching load of three single-semester courses per year, while Triennial Assistant Professorships carry a teaching load of four single-semester courses per year. Candidates should have received a Ph.D. by the time the position starts, and show outstanding promise of research ability in pure or applied mathematics as well as a capacity for effective teaching. In addition, various postdoctoral research positions may become available, which may or may not carry teaching responsibilities.<br><br></div><div>Applicants should complete the online form associated with this listing and submit a curriculum vitae. In addition, you should register as a job applicant at mathjobs.org https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/27217and complete the application, with the requested supporting documents, for position PD26 under the Rutgers University-New Brunswick listing.<br><br>All job offers are contingent upon successful pre-employment background screening prior to commencement of employment. The academic year salary for a postdoctoral fellow will not be less than $63,968 based on the most recent collective bargaining agreement between the faculty union (AAUP-AFT) and Rutgers University.</div> Mathematics New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 8125 25FA0930 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280151 2026-08-31T08:38:16-04:00 2026-08-31T08:38:17-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse FT Days - UCHC SWSP Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking Full Time Licensed Practical Nurse (Medical) for Southwoods State Prison, located in Bridgeton, NJ<br><br>The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs.</li><li>Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.</li><li>Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.</li><li>Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.</li><li>Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.</li><li>Documents all aspects of patient care.</li></ul> UCHC-South Woods Psn-Ancillary RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7685 Bridgeton NJ 26ST0174 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278566 2026-07-10T10:37:28-04:00 2026-07-10T10:37:29-04:00 Staff Nurse PT Days UCHC ADTC <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Part Time Staff Nurse for the Adult Diagnostic Treatment Center, located in Avenel, NJ. The UCHC Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus; works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment; frequently functions guided by nursing protocols; and functions as a team leader as assigned.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the inmatepatient including adults (18 to 64 years), and geriatrics (65+) and their family within the framework established by the correctional system.</li><li>Utilizes effective communication skills by demonstrating respect, concern and courtesy in all interpersonal relationships.</li><li>Attends appropriate in-services and continuing education offerings to obtain and maintain necessary skills.</li><li>Participates in offering education to inmates, security officers and other members of the health care team.</li><li>Participates in in-service meetings and educational programs either as attendee or as a teacher, as arranged and approved by supervisor.</li></ul> UCHC Adult Treatment Center Ph RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7674 Avenel NJ 26ST0901 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/268250 2026-01-29T14:54:29-05:00 2026-01-29T14:54:29-05:00 Adjunct Instructor (Per Diem) Epidemiology <div>Multiple Instructors needed for graduate courses in Epidemiology and Biostatistics at Rutgers School of Public Health during the Fall 2026 Semester to accommodate our expanding enrollment. Applicants should have experience teaching epidemiology/and or Biostatistics at the graduate level.</div> SPH - Epidemiology RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Public Health-L3 7710 22FA1383 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280332 2026-09-02T14:20:53-04:00 2026-09-02T14:20:54-04:00 Assistant Dean III-Nursing Student Success Coach and Retention Specialist <div>Rutgers University-Camden, School of Nursing seeks an Assistant Dean III- Nursing Student Success Coach &amp; Retention Specialist. Under the direction of the Associate Dean for Undergraduate Programs, the Assistant Dean III applies a whole-person, student-centered framework to identify at-risk undergraduate nursing students and implement targeted coaching strategies that promote academic success, progression, and retention within the undergraduate program. Providing individualized and group-based academic coaching, including nursing content support, to strengthen clinical reasoning, clinical judgment, and professional development. The role develops and delivers structured interventions using in-person and technology-enhanced modalities, including synchronous and asynchronous approaches.<br><br>The Assistant Dean III, Nursing Student Success Coach and Retention Specialist collaborates with administrators, faculty, advisors, data analytics professionals, and student support services to design and implement data-informed retention initiatives that support undergraduate student success and align with established program goals and priorities. The position supports student engagement with learning tools and educational resources to improve academic performance and program outcomes.<br><br></div><div>Using established data sources and student performance indicators, the position monitors student progress, identifies trends, and implements targeted interventions. The role utilizes the Navigate Early Alert System to manage student cases, coordinate outreach, and schedule coaching appointments. The position also facilitates appropriate referrals to campus and community resources to address non-academic factors that influence student success.<br><br></div><div>In addition, the role manages the Nursing Tutoring Center, including tutor recruitment, training, and student scheduling, to ensure high-quality academic support services aligned with program needs. The role initiates and manages academic remediation courses and structured support strategies for students requiring additional academic support, ensuring alignment with established program expectations and student success goals.<br><br></div><div>This position works closely with administration and advisors to identify and address programmatic needs related to student success, contributing data-informed insights to support decision making and continuous improvement efforts. The role serves as an ex officio member of assigned committees, providing expertise and input related to student success, retention, and academic support strategies.<br><br></div><div>The Assistant Dean III-Nursing Student Success Coach and Retention Specialist serves as a resource to faculty and staff by sharing best practices related to academic coaching, student support strategies, and retention efforts. The position participates in student-facing programming, including orientation, recruitment events, and embedded student success courses.</div><div>This role maintains accurate records, reports, and documentation related to student progression and retention and supports ongoing program assessment and improvement efforts. All initiatives and interventions are developed and implemented in alignment with established undergraduate program goals and in collaboration with academic leadership.<br><br></div><div>The position requires strong organizational, analytical, and interpersonal skills, as well as the ability to work collaboratively across units to achieve defined student success outcomes.</div> School of Nursing Camden Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 School of Nursing Camden-L3 6631 Camden NJ 26ST1559 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279186 2026-07-29T10:25:08-04:00 2026-07-29T10:25:08-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the School of Arts &amp; Sciences, Department of Biology, invites applications for a Postdoctoral Associate, in the laboratory of Dr. Maria E. Solesio. The research will focus on elucidating the mechanisms driving mitochondria to dysfunction and failure in neurodegeneration and aging, using cellular models. Successful candidates will participate in the initiation of the different research projects available in the laboratory and are expected to independently conduct their own research project.<br><br>If you have any questions about this position or the department, please contact Dr. Maria Solesio m.solesio@rutgers.edu.</div> Biology Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 6758 26FA0693 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/272139 2026-04-01T14:20:09-04:00 2026-04-01T14:20:09-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate in African American and African Diaspora Literary Studies <div>The Department of English at Rutgers University, which has a long history of scholarship and teaching in African American Literature and Literature of the African Diaspora, invites applications for the Cheryl A. Wall Postdoctoral Associate in African American and African Diaspora Literary Studies. We welcome applications from scholars pursuing research in these fields, broadly, and are especially interested in scholars engaged in black feminist critical approaches to literary and cultural study. Scholarship and teaching intersecting with African American poetics, black ecologies, performance studies, sound studies, black queer studies, or the black radical tradition are also especially welcome.</div><div><br>The Postdoctoral Associate fellowship position has the possibility of renewal for a second year and includes an annual salary of $60,000 and health benefits.<br><br></div><div>The recipients will each teach one course per academic year, serve as informal mentors to graduate students in the field, and participate in the intellectual life of the department.</div><div>Applications must be submitted by April 17, 2026. Interested parties may direct inquiries to Professor Carter Mathes at: cmathes@english.rutgers.edu.</div> English New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 7008 26FA0298 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279558 2026-08-13T09:10:39-04:00 2026-08-13T09:10:40-04:00 Clinical Services Representative I <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Clinical Services Representative I for the department of Surgery at the Robert Wood Johnson Medical School.<br><br>Performs a variety of billing and collection duties in support of clinic and/or business operations. Provides guidance to Clinic Services Representatives II at a variety of clinic sites, as needed. Functions as a senior staff member handling more complex issues and problems.&nbsp;<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Acts as the first point of contact with patients to resolve basic inquiries, involving insurance companies and third party companies relating to billing, insurance payments, payment arrangements, etc.&nbsp;</li><li>Collects co-payments or self-pay balances from patients. Researches complex billing issues and consults with management for resolution in accordance with established guidelines.&nbsp;</li><li>Verifies and updates patient demographic, insurance and other information by utilizing various database systems (e.g., PATCOM, WebMD, IDX, Navinet, etc.)&nbsp;</li><li>Responsible for patient registration, check-out, and/or charge entry transactions.&nbsp;</li><li>Monitors accuracy of billing records and assists in auditing of same, as required. Ensures that information provided to patients, co-workers, insurance companies, etc. is accurate and current.&nbsp;</li><li>Provides coverage across clinic and administrative assignments, as required by business and operational needs.&nbsp;</li></ul> RWJ - Surgery Colon Rectal RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7836 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1614 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279791 2026-08-21T00:01:11-04:00 2026-08-21T00:01:13-04:00 Admissions Officer (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers University – Newark, an urban public research anchor institution, located in Newark, New Jersey, a city of promise, is seeking an Admissions Officer. Reporting to the Director of Recruitment and Outreach, the Admissions Officer, promotes the University’s mission by empowering prospective students, families, and educators with the information and tools needed to understand and navigate the college admissions process at Rutgers University – Newark. The Admissions Officer will primarily work with first-year students, they will be cross trained to work with, recruit, and enroll transfer students as well. This position involves frequent evening and weekend hours. The Admissions Officer must have regular access to and use of a personal vehicle, as travel is required.<br><br>This position is responsible for and not limited to the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Develops and implement strategic recruitment efforts, application and selection processes for undergraduate students to achieve the general university enrollment goals, as well as goals related to specific schools, colleges, departments, and applicant types.</li><li>Provides exceptional service to prospective students, their families, and other constituencies and public speaking is a frequently used and required skill.</li><li>Communicates clearly and effectively with all colleagues through regular and planned communication and/or meetings so that information and updates are passed on accurately and timely to those who require it.</li><li>Manage other duties as assigned, demonstrate their capability to learn new information, understand it, and implement it to be effective in the position.</li></ul> Admissions Newark Newark Chancellor-L2 Enrollment Management Newark-L3 6714 Newark NJ 26ST1613 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277418 2026-06-18T10:37:13-04:00 2026-06-18T10:37:14-04:00 Assistant Professor <div>&nbsp;The Department of Psychiatry at the Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School (RWJMS) has an opening for a full time Academic Psychiatrist. The position is at the Assistant Professor level.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Responsibilities include providing inpatient consultation at our primary teaching hospital, Robert Wood Johnson Barnabas University Hospital as well as direct clinical care to outpatients with psychiatric disorders who are being treated within Rutgers Health.&nbsp; &nbsp; Teaching medical students, residents and allied professionals is a core responsibility.&nbsp;</div> RWJ - Psychiatry RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7823 26FA0603 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274118 2026-05-01T09:06:10-04:00 2026-05-01T09:06:12-04:00 Coadjutants, VMPA (Non-Teaching Positions) <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the Faculty of Arts &amp; Sciences, Department of Visual, Media, and Performing Arts, is seeking co-adjutants (non-teaching) to perform a variety of roles within Animation, Graphic Design, Painting, Photography, Sculpture/Intermedia: Art &amp; Technology, Art History, Museum Studies, Music, Theater, Filmmaking, and Dance.<br>Responsibilities may include:<br>• Non-teaching co-adjutant roles such as accompanist, music director, or stage, costume, sound, or lighting designer.<br>• Non-credit instructor roles to support the Rutgers Pre-College Arts Program for high school students.<br>These courses provide students with professional development opportunities beyond the high school curriculum and prepare them for potential future careers in the arts.<br>Duties include: assisting with instruction, coordinating related course requirements, and supporting course delivery as needed.<br>Note: Hiring for Pre-College positions is contingent upon sufficient student enrollment.</div> Fine Arts Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 6757 26FA0440 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266144 2025-12-31T09:29:49-05:00 2025-12-31T09:29:49-05:00 Postdoctoral Associate: Use of Industrial Byproducts in Transportation Infrastructure <div>The Rutgers Center for Advanced Infrastructure and Transportation (CAIT) invites applications for a Postdoctoral Associate in the broad area of innovative materials for transportation infrastructure with applications in civil (geotechnical/material) engineering, industrial scale economics, and transportation infrastructure performance. The successful candidate will lead research activities into the use and value of industrial byproducts in transportation infrastructure in support of a United States Department of Transportation funded initiative. The candidate will collaborate closely with several research groups at Rutgers as well as with national and international academic, governmental, and industrial partners.</div> Advanced Infrastructure Center New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Engineering-L3 6709 25FA0936 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280263 2026-09-01T08:38:32-04:00 2026-09-01T08:38:33-04:00 System Programmer/Administrator IV (Platform Systems Engineer) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a System Programmer/Administrator IV (Platform Systems Engineer) in the Enterprise Infrastructure &amp; Service Delivery/ Platform Systems Engineering within the Office of Information Technology (OIT).<br><br>Reporting to the IT Manager of the Platform Systems Engineering group within Enterprise Infrastructure, the System Programmer/Administrator IV is focused on designing, engineering, and evolving the core Linux-based platforms that support enterprise systems and engineering workloads. While strong Linux administration skills are required, the position emphasizes strategic platform engineering, automation strategy, and infrastructure architecture.</div><div>The ideal candidate understands how large-scale systems fit together, can design automation-driven environments, and helps guide the technical direction of platform infrastructure. Experience with container platforms, particularly Kubernetes, along with automation frameworks and familiarity with AI-related infrastructure or tooling is highly valued.</div><div>This role is ideal for someone who enjoys thinking beyond day-to-day administration and contributing to the design, evolution, and automation of large-scale platform infrastructure.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Design and engineer scalable Linux-based platform infrastructure across on-premises and cloud environments.</li><li>Manage, support, and operate container orchestration platforms such as Kubernetes or OpenShift in production environments, including cluster deployment and configuration, upgrades, scaling, monitoring, troubleshooting, and ensuring overall platform reliability and performance.</li><li>Develop and expand infrastructure automation using tools such as Ansible Automation Platform, Terraform, GitLab, and similar technologies.</li><li>Architect and implement infrastructure as code frameworks that standardize system deployment and configuration.</li><li>Ability to work independently, troubleshoot complex infrastructure issues, and take ownership of platform reliability and improvements.</li><li>Lead initiatives that improve platform reliability, scalability, and operational efficiency.</li></ul> OIT - Enterprise Infrastructur EVP & Chief Admin Officer OIT - VP & Chief Information O-L3 7280 Piscataway NJ 26ST1704 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278937 2026-07-17T11:09:18-04:00 2026-07-17T11:09:19-04:00 Graduate Assistant (6) Positions <div>Rutgers School of Health Professions is seeking a Graduate Assistant to work in the Department of Health Informatics.<br><br>The Graduate Assistant role is designed to support the teacher with various aspects of online teaching, including grading, working individually with students to improve their performance, and answering questions about the course content.<br><br></div><div>Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Facilitate online lessons, tutorials or discussions in concert with the Instructor.</li><li>Grade assignments, exams, quizzes, and projects.</li><li>Maintain and update student grades as an Excel Sheet to be submitted to the Instructor.</li><li>Assist the Instructor in preparing and sharing reading materials, supplementary notes.</li><li>Perform other related duties as assigned.</li></ul> SHP - Health Informatics RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Health Professions-L3 7582 Piscataway NJ 26ST1539 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/271477 2026-03-24T10:17:32-04:00 2026-03-24T10:17:32-04:00 Post Doctorial Associate <div>Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy, Pharmacy Practice, and Pharmacy Administration – Health Outcomes, Policy &amp; Economics, Rutgers University is part of Rutgers Biomedical Health Sciences (RBHS) and participates in interdisciplinary professional education and training partnership with Rutgers School of Public Health and the Robert Wood Johnson Medical School.<br><br>Though certain responsibilities of the resident are required, the program has the flexibility to develop activities consistent with the resident’s background and career goals. In general, the resident responsibilities include: 1. Attend daily rounds and make appropriate recommendations to inter-disciplinary treatment teams 2. Design, monitor, and evaluate treatment goals for patients that consider patient-, disease-, and drug-specific information and ethical considerations 3. Present educational in-services on pharmacy topics to patients, pharmacy staff, and inter-disciplinary treatment team 4. Lead inpatient and outpatient pharmacy medication education groups 5. Supervise pharmacy students on Advanced Pharmacy Practice Experience (APPE) rotations. 6. Present didactic lectures to pharmacy students at the Rutgers Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy 7. Complete a research project related to the provision of pharmacy care, as well as presenting this research at a national conference.</div> Pharmacy Practice & Administra RBHS Chancellor-L2 Ernest Mario School of Pharmac-L3 6720 26FA0269 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279492 2026-08-11T09:53:00-04:00 2026-08-11T09:53:01-04:00 Mental Health Specialist IV <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Mental Health Specialist IV within the&nbsp; Acute Psychological Services of Rutgers University Behavioral Healthcare.&nbsp;<br><br>The Mental Health Specialist IV participates as a member of the unit team providing care to assigned patients under the direct supervision of the Registered Nurse.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>Assists the Registered Nurse in planning patient care.</li><li>Provides care based on the patient’s established care plan, under the supervision of the registered nurse.</li><li>Observes patient’s behaviors and when necessary notifies appropriate staff.</li><li>Assists in maintaining a safe, therapeutic environment that respects patients’ rights.</li><li>Assists the patients with activities of daily living, encouraging independent behavior, when appropriate.</li><li>Collects routine urine specimens, takes vital signs including blood pressure and weighs patients as directed by the registered nurse.&nbsp;</li></ul> UBHC - Acute Psychological Ser RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7987 Piscataway NJ 26ST1602 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279754 2026-08-20T09:04:10-04:00 2026-08-20T09:04:10-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse PT Days UCHC MSCF (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Healthcare is seeking Part Time Licensed Practical Nurse for Midstate Correctional Facility located in Wrightstown, NJ.The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment. Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs.</li><li>Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.</li><li>Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.</li><li>Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.</li><li>Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.</li><li>Documents all aspects of patient care.</li></ul> UCHC Midstate Correction Physi RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7680 Wrightstown NJ 26ST0887 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277046 2026-06-12T12:27:55-04:00 2026-06-12T12:27:55-04:00 Post–Doctoral Associate <div>The Aging &amp; Brain Health Alliance in the Center for Molecular and Behavioral Neuroscience (CMBN), at Rutgers University-Newark seeks a Post-Doctoral Associate with training in neuroscience, cognitive science, psychology, public health, kinesiology, or a related field, and an interest in interdisciplinary research on aging and Alzheimer's disease prevention. The Post-Doctoral Associate will contribute to NIH-funded studies of cognitive aging and Alzheimer's disease risk in older African Americans, including the Pathways to Healthy Aging in African Americans longitudinal cohort study and the Exercise to Improve Brain Health in Older African Americans randomized controlled trial. The fellow will work within a multidisciplinary team integrating cognitive neuroscience, neuropsychology, genetics, neuroimaging, exercise science, public health, sleep research, and biomarker science to investigate factors that promote cognitive resilience and reduce dementia risk. The position provides advanced training in cognitive aging, neuropsychological assessment, longitudinal data analysis, community-engaged science, grant development, and academic career advancement.</div> CMBN Newark Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences Newa-L3 6804 26FA0605 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274087 2026-04-30T15:08:02-04:00 2026-04-30T15:08:03-04:00 Lecturers, Honors College <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the Faculty of Arts &amp; Sciences, Honors College, seeks lecturers in the areas of literature, art, political science, criminal justice, music, fine art, mathematics, biology, chemistry, global studies, psychology, religion, sociology, philosophy to teach Honors College seminars. The ideal candidate will have expertise teaching at the university level, a commitment to innovative teaching strategies, and competencies in multiple Rutgers-Camden categories of general education.</div> Honors College Camden Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Provost Office Camden-L3 8632 26FA0423 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266026 2025-12-31T09:15:00-05:00 2025-12-31T09:15:00-05:00 Abdominal / Body Imager <div>The Department of Radiology at New Jersey Medical School at Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is recruiting a full-time Abdominal/Body Imager. The successful candidate must be fellowship trained in abdominal/body imaging or demonstrate experience in abdominal/body imaging, must possess an M.D. or D.O. degree, and be ABR eligible or certified in Diagnostic Radiology. J1 Waiver sponsorship is available. The position will offer a market competitive salary and excellent benefits.<br><br></div><div>We are seeking a candidate at the Assistant Professor level or higher to join our section; new graduates are also encouraged to apply. We serve a diverse community with a wide range of interesting cases. We are a collegial department that values education of residents, clinical excellence, and faculty personal growth and well-being.</div><div>The Department of Radiology has 25 clinical and research faculty members, and 38 diagnostic radiology residents who provide patient care for all the major divisions of contemporary imaging. The Department is responsible for all aspects of diagnostic imaging at University Hospital, a tertiary care center as well as the Doctor’s Office Center, an outpatient facility on campus. University Hospital is a liver transplant center and a Level 1 trauma center comprising of state-of-the-art equipment and employs medical and dental professionals who are specialists in their field. We take care of a diverse patient population with a wide variety of interesting cases. University Hospital is a Liver Transplant Center and Level 1 Trauma center.</div><div><br><br></div><div>All applicants interested in this position should direct inquiries to Natalie Colimon-Fitzgerald, MBA, Director of Administration, Department of Radiology (<a href=\"mailto:nc204@njms.rutgers.edu\"><strong>nc204@njms.rutgers.edu</strong></a>), or Dr. Humaira Chaudhry MD, Chair, (<a href=\"mailto:chaudhhu@njms.rutgers.edu\"><strong>chaudhhu@njms.rutgers.edu</strong></a>, 973-972-5188) or Inessa Goldman MD, Division Chief of Abdominal Imaging (iag35@njms.rutgers.edu).</div> NJMS - Radiology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7492 25FA0716 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280044 2026-08-26T14:19:40-04:00 2026-08-26T14:19:41-04:00 Mental Health Specialist IV - per diem - (Multiple Positions) <div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is seeking a per diem Mental Health Specialist IV in the Acute Psychiatric Services of Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the per diem Mental Health Specialist IV is to provide services which support the delivery of clinical services in the Unit.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Provides telephone coverage for the unit.</li><li>Documents all telephone calls in the Acute Psychiatric Services (APS) telephone log or Electronic Medical Record (EMR).</li><li>Maintains confidentiality of information in accordance with Rutgers UBHC policy, University policy, Joint Commission standards and the Department of Mental Health and Addiction Services (DMHAS) requirements.</li><li>Refers consumer calls to a clinician as directed by the Program Coordinator.</li><li>Assists in the provision of direct care for individuals in the ECEB.</li><li>Assists consumers and/or families in the completion of registration paperwork</li></ul> UBHC - Emergency Screening Psy RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8029 Piscataway NJ 26ST1370 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278050 2026-06-30T15:25:29-04:00 2026-06-30T15:25:30-04:00 Mental Health Specialist III -Part-Time - Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a part-time Mental Health Specialist for the Inpatient Units within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the part-time Mental Health Specialist III is to participate as a member of the unit team providing care for all age groups in accordance with facility policy and procedure. Demonstrates leadership skills and assists the Staff Nurse with staff assignments, orientation of new staff and formulation of patient groups<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Assists the Staff Nurse with MHS IV assignments, orientation of new staff and formulation of patient groups when required.</li><li>Assists the Staff Nurse in planning patient care.</li><li>Provides care based on the patient’s established care plan, under the supervision of the Staff Nurse.</li><li>Observes patient’s behaviors and when necessary notifies appropriate staff.</li><li>Assists in maintaining a safe, therapeutic environment that respects patients’ rights.</li><li>Assists the patients with activities of daily living, encouraging independent behavior, when appropriate.</li><li>Collects routine urine specimens, takes vital signs including blood pressure and weighs patients as directed by the Staff Nurse.</li><li>Assists patients and observes patients during mealtimes in the cafeteria and on the unit.</li></ul> UBHC - Acute Psychological Ser RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7987 Piscataway NJ 26ST1437 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266378 2026-01-01T00:03:30-05:00 2026-01-01T00:03:35-05:00 Instructor - Part-time for Non-Credit Classes - Workforce Development <div>The Office of Continuing Professional Education, part of NJAES-Cooperative Extension, invites applications for instructors to teach non-credit courses (half-day through multi-day) to adult learners at various locations throughout New Jersey and/or online. Instructors will develop and present course material during the assigned course times, coordinate materials with Program Coordinator, and follow-up with necessary paperwork. Course topics include but are not limited to: Soft Skills, such as Diversity, Leadership and Management, Communications; and Computer Skills, such as Microsoft applications and Adobe software. We welcome new course ideas in certifications as well as management, leadership, and supervisory skills. **Evergreen Posting to 12/31/2026**</div> Continuing Professional Educat New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 6966 25FA1179 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280182 2026-08-31T10:38:18-04:00 2026-08-31T10:38:19-04:00 Research Assistant, Per Diem <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Research Assistant, Per Diem within the Population Sciences, Behavioral Sciences Section at the Rutgers Cancer Institute.<br><br>The Arana Research Lab at Rutgers Cancer Institute is seeking a Research Assistant, Per Diem to conduct research on understanding and improving cancer outcomes for Hispanic cancer survivors. The Research Assistant, Per Diem will provide support in recruitment, data collection, data management, study material development, participant tracking, retention, patient communications, and incentives.</div><div><br>Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Works under the direction of the Principal Investigator.</li><li>Assists with recruitment, including community outreach and engagement in English and Spanish.</li><li>Assists with data collection and data management.</li><li>Conducts qualitative data analysis under the supervision of the Principal Investigator.</li><li>Possesses effective oral and written communication skills and the ability to publish scientific research papers and abstracts.</li><li>Acts as a role model for corporate integrity, customer service and improved quality.</li></ul> CINJ - Sec Behavioral Sciences RBHS Chancellor-L2 Cancer Institute of New Jersey-L3 7946 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1508 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278620 2026-07-10T12:49:10-04:00 2026-07-10T12:49:11-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse Per Diem UCHC NJSP (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Healthcare is seeking Per DIem Licensed Practical Nurse for Midstate Correctional Facility located in Wrightstown, NJ. The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment. Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs.</li><li>Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.</li><li>Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.</li><li>Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.</li><li>Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.</li><li>Documents all aspects of patient care.</li></ul> UCHC New Jersey State Prison N_DUP RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7697 Trenton NJ 26ST1282 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/268942 2026-02-10T15:13:58-05:00 2026-02-10T15:13:59-05:00 Emergency Radiologist- Assistant Professor-Multiple Positions <div>The Department of Radiology at New Jersey Medical School at Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is recruiting a full-time Emergency Radiologist (Multiple positions). The successful applicant will be fellowship trained in Emergency Radiology, Abdominal/Body Imaging, Neuroradiology, or demonstrate experience in Emergency Radiology. Candidates must possess an M.D. or D.O. degree and either hold, or be eligible for, ABR certification in Diagnostic Radiology. J-1 Waiver sponsorship is available.<br><br></div><div>We are seeking a candidate at the Assistant Professor level or higher to join our section; new graduates are also encouraged to apply. We serve a diverse community with a wide range of interesting cases. We are a collegial department that values education of residents, clinical excellence, and faculty personal growth and well-being.<br><br></div><div>The Department of Radiology has 44 clinical and research faculty members who provide patient care for all the major divisions of contemporary imaging. The department has undergone a recent residency program merger, with a total of 40 diagnostic radiology residents.</div><div>The department is responsible for all aspects of diagnostic imaging at University Hospital, a tertiary care medical center. University Hospital is a designated stroke center, liver transplant center and a Level 1 trauma center with state-of-the-art equipment and employs medical and dental professionals who are specialists in their field.<br><br></div><div>The position will offer a competitive market salary and excellent benefits. J1Waiver candidates and new graduates with interest in education are also encouraged to apply.<br><br></div><div>All applicants interested in this position should direct inquiries to Natalie Colimon-Fitzgerald, MBA, Director of Administration, Department of Radiology (nc204@njms.rutgers.edu), or Dr. R. Joshua Dym, Section Head of Emergency Radiology, (rjd253@njms.rutgers.edu).<br><br><em>It is university policy to provide equal employment opportunity to all its employees and applicants for employment regardless of their race, creed, color, national origin, age, ancestry, nationality, marital or domestic partnership or civil union status, sex, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, disability status, liability for military service, protected veteran status, affectional or sexual orientation, atypical cellular or blood trait, genetic information (including the refusal to submit to genetic testing), or any other category protected by law. As an institution, we encourage all qualified applicants to apply. For additional information please see the Non-Discrimination Statement at the following web address: </em><a href=\"http://uhr.rutgers.edu/non-discrimination-statement\"><strong><em>http://uhr.rutgers.edu/non-discrimination-statement</em></strong></a><em>.</em></div> NJMS - Radiology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7492 25FA1272 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280418 2026-09-03T15:39:48-04:00 2026-09-03T15:39:49-04:00 Research Field Worker Casual <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Research Field Worker for the School of Environmental and Biological Sciences.<br><br>Among the key duties of the position are the following:</div><ul><li>Measures bioplastic plasticulture durability and crop yield.</li><li>Monitors surface temperatures, soil temperatures, plant growth, chlorophyll, and microbial soil populations.</li><li>Maintains crop production; transplant habanero and other peppers and tomatoes.</li><li>Performs data entry of findings and results.</li></ul> Agriculture & Natural Resource New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 6967 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279328 2026-08-05T10:44:56-04:00 2026-08-05T10:44:57-04:00 Post-doctoral Research Associate <div>The Center for Urban Policy Research (CUPR) seeks Postdoctoral Associates to support externally funded projects aimed at accelerating building and grid decarbonization for a sustainable energy transition. CUPR has multiple ongoing projects funded by the New Jersey Board of Public Utilities, the US Department of Energy, the US Environmental Protection Agency, the National Science Foundation, and others that include a mix of research design, fieldwork, data science, simulation modeling, writing, and presentations. The overarching goal of the Postdoctoral Associate will be to systematically investigate, evaluate, and address both technical and non-technical (political, behavioral, social) obstacles to building a grid decarbonization. The successful candidate will work with a team of approximately 20 researchers in the built environment group at CUPR and will contribute research skills and training at the intersection of engineering, economics, and public policy with knowledge and experience of buildings and energy systems. Specific postdoc duties will depend on the successful candidate’s skills and interests, matched to project needs, with time allocated to pursue independent, discretionary work.</div><div>Responsibilities are expected to include a subset of:</div><div>(1) Use advanced energy modeling to analyze energy efficiency, demand flexibility, and electrification measures in the building stock.</div><div>(2) Use advanced community-scale energy models to analyze high-performance buildings and geothermal energy systems.</div><div>(3) Assess technical and non-technical barriers to the adoption of clean energy technologies.</div><div>(4) Conduct analyses of existing codes, standards, and policies related to building decarbonization, including econometric analyses of economic impacts.</div><div>(5) Conduct analyses of utility rates and rate impacts on households and other populations with emphasis on low- and moderate-income populations and affordable housing settings.</div><div>(6) Author peer-reviewed publications and public reports on research findings.</div><div>(7) Maintain a database of research materials, datasets, and codebooks.</div> Rutgers Center Green Building New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Bloustein Schl Plng & Pub Polc-L3 6620 26FA0701 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275990 2026-05-28T12:21:07-04:00 2026-05-28T12:21:08-04:00 Lecturers (Adjunct Faculty) for the Master’s Program in Communication and Media  (Fall 2026) <div>The School of Communication and Information seeks part-time lecturers for its master’s program in Communication and Media. Please see the description of our program at https://comminfo.rutgers.edu/academics/graduate/mcm and the list of courses we offer at https://comminfo.rutgers.edu/academics/courses?courses=&amp;program=31. Within your cover letter, please let us know which courses in our program you feel most prepared to teach. Please submit a cover letter, resume/curriculum vitae, and names and contact information for at least three references. You may also upload any evidence of your teaching experience such as sample syllabi or course materials, results of student instructional ratings, or published work.</div> Communication New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School  Communicatn & Info Sci-L3 7088 26FA0375 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/273117 2026-04-16T12:45:51-04:00 2026-04-16T12:45:51-04:00 Internal Medicine; Primary Care Faculty <div>Outpatient care in the General Internal Medicine practice. This will include seeing patients in the CAB practice, as well as outpatient satellite locations of the Division, possibly including the Executive Health Program:<br><br></div><ul><li>Complete all charting and billing in a timely manner</li><li>Participate in education and training of Medical Students, Residents and all academic and clinical activities of the division as assigned by the Division Chief.</li><li>Participate in clinical research as opportunities as available.</li><li>Participate in appropriate Department of Medicine and Medical School committees.</li><li>Attend Division and Department meetings including but not limited to faculty meetings, Grand Rounds and Resident recruitment sessions</li><li>Other duties as assigned by the Division Chief and/or Department Chairman.</li></ul> RWJ - Medicine General Interna RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7773 26FA0332 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/265410 2025-12-17T13:28:25-05:00 2025-12-17T13:28:25-05:00 Post Doctoral Associate (Zander) <div>The Zander laboratory at the Waksman Institute of Microbiology is looking for an individual that investigates powdery mildew resistance in hemp. Furthermore, the individual will also optimize a hemp transformation and genome editing platform. Research is carried out in the Zander laboratory, that conducts molecular, genetic and (epi)genomic research to better understand the role of transcription factors and the epigenome dynamics. The individual needs to conduct research on questions related to powdery mildew resistance and susceptibility in hemp. By using genetic, genomic and biochemical methods, the individual will identify/analyze/characterize molecular determinants for powdery mildew resistance in hemp. The individual will report directly to the laboratory Principle Investigator (PI).<br><strong><br>KEY DUTIES &amp; RESPONSIBILITIES</strong><br><br><strong>90 %</strong> <strong>1.</strong> Conduct grant-funded research as directed by the PI (Dr. Zander). This research will include performing genetic, (epi)genomics and proteomic analyses in hemp. It is expected that the research findings will be published, with the individual contributing to the writing and production of the resulting manuscript. It is expected that the research findings will be provided as preliminary data for grant proposals, with the individual contributing to the writing and production of such proposals as well as the presentation of results at scientific meetings.</div><div><strong>10 % 2.</strong> Train and oversee undergraduate researchers within the lab on related projects. This training will include showing undergraduates the methodologies of plant genetics, genomics, recombinant DNA techniques, protein biochemistry, Powerpoint oral presentation of data, poster presentation of data, proper record and notebook keeping, and basic laboratory techniques. It is expected that trained students will have clear guidance and training on projects, and that they will grow towards independence under this mentorship.</div><div><strong>Expected outcomes:</strong></div><div>• Assigned projects completed on time and within budgetary guidelines</div><div>• Analyses conducted using standard and specialized methods and in accordance with established procedures</div><div>• Detailed documentation of all procedures and results</div><div>• Clear communication of all procedures and results</div><div>• Work conducted independently (with supervision as necessary)</div> Waksman Institute of Microbiol New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 6726 25FA1250 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279635 2026-08-17T11:31:35-04:00 2026-08-17T11:31:36-04:00 NTT Associate Teaching Professor <div>The Division of Life Sciences, Rutgers, The State University, Piscataway/New Brunswick campus, has an opening for non-tenure track CY Associate Teaching Professor.&nbsp; The Teaching Professor will serve as the Director of Introductory Biology Programs with responsibility for overseeing our large General Biology courses along with the Prep for General Biology and the Bio Practice Group courses.&nbsp; The Director works with the faculty teaching in the introductory courses to guide curricular development, supervise administrative staff, manage course budgets, review the course schedule, coordinate the assessment, and serve as the primary point of contact for stakeholders and partners in undergraduate instruction.&nbsp; In addition, as a Teaching Professor, it is expected that the candidate will teach two courses in both the fall and spring as well as have teaching responsibility in the summer. &nbsp;<br><br></div> DLS Undergraduate Instruction New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 7064 26FA0689 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279925 2026-08-25T11:06:12-04:00 2026-08-25T11:06:13-04:00 SENIOR EOF COUNSELOR <div>Rutgers University-Newark, an urban public research university and anchor institution, located in Newark, New Jersey, a city of promise, is seeking a Senior EOF Counselor. Reporting to the Assistant Dean/ Assistant Director of Counseling Services in the Educational Opportunity Fund (EOF) program at Rutgers University-Newark, the position responsibilities include and are not limited to the following.<br><br>This position is responsible for and not limited to the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Assists the programmatic development and implementation of the EOF Program, and assures successful levels of academic achievement and graduation for an assigned caseload of Rutgers University – Newark undergraduate students.</li><li>Provides orientation to the campus culture as well as academic, career, financial aid, and personal counseling.</li><li>Serves as a liaison and maintains contact with faculty, school academic advisors, residence life, student life, financial aid, student accounting, registrar’s office, admissions office, the Learning Resource and Writing Centers, and other internal and external special programs.</li><li>Develops, initiates, and administers special projects and services for the summer program’s academic component and specified EOF populations to promote leadership, holistic growth, and achievement.</li><li>Conducts outreach on behalf of EOF students with outside community constituents, agencies, and schools.</li><li>Teaches a credit-bearing during the summer bridge program and during the academic year that focuses on strategies for academic success.</li></ul> Academic Foundations Center Newark Chancellor-L2 Provost-L3 6802 Newark NJ 26ST1648 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277759 2026-06-25T11:02:01-04:00 2026-06-25T11:02:01-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse Mental Health PT Eves-UCHC EMCFW <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Part Time Licensed Practical Nurse Mental Health for Edna Mahan Correctional Facility, located in Clinton, NJ<br><br>The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br>* Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs.<br>* Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.<br>* Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.<br>* Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.<br>* Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.<br>* Documents all aspects of patient care.</div> UCHC Edna Mahan Correction Med RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7659 Clinton NJ 26ST0578 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274943 2026-05-13T11:29:05-04:00 2026-05-13T11:29:06-04:00 Fall Semester 2026: Lecturer, Educational Theory, Policy, and Administration <div>The Graduate School of Education, Rutgers University invites applications for Lecturers (formerly Part Time Lecturers) in the department of Educational Theory, Policy and Administration during the Fall 2026 Semester, September 1, 2026 through December 22, 2026.<br><br>Successful applicants will instruct undergraduate or graduate level courses in social and philosophical foundations of education, educational policy, social studies education, and/or educational leadership. Specific courses might include history of education; philosophy of education; gender in education; race, ethnicity and inequality; urban education; sociology of education; public school finance; policy analysis; school leadership; and queer issues in schools, among others.<br><br>Courses will be offered in a range of modalities beyond traditional settings, including hybrid and online formats as well as synchronous and asynchronous instruction. Course appointments are in the New Brunswick area, as well as, hybrid/online format.</div> Education Theory, Policy & Adm New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Graduate School of Education-L3 6814 25FA0512 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266237 2025-12-31T09:38:58-05:00 2025-12-31T09:38:59-05:00 Spring Semester 2026:  Lecturer, Educational Psychology <div>The Rutgers University, Graduate School of Education, invites applications for Lecturer (formerly Part Time Lecturers) teaching positions in the department of Educational Psychology during the Spring 2026 Semester, February 1, 2026 through June 30, 2026.<br><br>Successful applicants will instruct undergraduate or graduate level courses in at least one of the the following content areas:<br><br>-School Counseling and Counseling Psychology<br><br>-College Student Affairs and Higher Education<br><br>-Educational Psychology: Learning &amp; Cognition and/or Human Development<br><br>-Gifted Education<br><br>-Special Education<br><br>-Educational Statistics, Measurement, and/or Evaluation<br><br>Courses will be offered in a range of modalities beyond traditional settings, including hybrid and online formats. Course appointments are in the New Brunswick area, as well as, hybrid/online format.</div> Education Psychology New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Graduate School of Education-L3 6813 25FA0914 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280110 2026-08-28T10:32:44-04:00 2026-08-28T10:32:45-04:00 Mental Health Specialist III <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Mental Health Specialist III for the Acute Psychiatric Services Department within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Mental Health Specialist III is to participate as a member of the unit team providing care for all age groups in accordance with facility policy and procedure. Demonstrates leadership skills and assists the Staff Nurse with staff assignments, orientation of new staff and formulation of patient groups.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Assists the Staff Nurse in planning patient care.</li><li>Provides care based on the patient’s established care plan, under the supervision of the Staff Nurse.</li><li>Observes patient’s behaviors and when necessary notifies appropriate staff.</li><li>Assists in maintaining a safe, therapeutic environment that respects patients’ rights.</li><li>Assists the patients with activities of daily living, encouraging independent behavior, when appropriate.</li><li>Assists patients and observes patients during mealtimes in the cafeteria and on the unit.</li><li>Monitors the milieu for changes in patient behavior. Also, observes interaction between patients and visitors.</li></ul> UBHC - Acute Psychological Ser RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7987 Piscataway NJ 26ST1262 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278478 2026-07-09T10:40:18-04:00 2026-07-09T10:40:19-04:00 Mental Health Clinician II <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Mental Health Clinician II&nbsp; Adult Partial Hospital in Cherry Hill within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>Under direction, the Mental Health Clinician II serves as the senior mental health practitioner who provides lead functions for the program, to include screening of intakes and referrals, care coordination, ensuring completion of program specific documentation and/or comprehensive assessment and therapeutic intervention for the psychological and social needs of child and adolescent (ages 3-17 years) and/or adult individuals served (18 and over), including development of treatment plans, conducting individual, group, and family therapy, and providing case management. Assists with the provision of clinical supervision to licensing candidates as assigned.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Contributes to and supports goals and objectives of the Unit and UBHC.&nbsp;</li><li>Assesses treatment needs and provides evidence based treatment services and/or case management as clinically indicated to assigned individuals served (individuals, groups and families) that is consistent with the service design and philosophy of the program and in accordance with accepted professional and ethical standards of UBHC.&nbsp;</li><li>Maintains and oversees the maintenance of assigned individuals’ clinical record in compliance with UBHC, The Joint Commission (TJC) and other applicable regulatory and accreditation standards that meets quality and program standards.&nbsp;</li><li>Provides assigned lead functions for the department.&nbsp;</li><li>Attends to professional self-development by remaining current in knowledge of trends and development in mental health, addictions or co-occurring disorders.&nbsp;</li><li>Participates in development, implementation, and evaluation of program services.&nbsp;</li></ul> UBHC - PH Adult Cherry Hill RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8015 Camden NJ 26ST1503 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267729 2026-01-21T18:13:17-05:00 2026-01-21T18:13:18-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor (Reproductive Endocrinology & Infertility) <div>The Department of Obstetrics, Gynecology and Reproductive Health at Rutgers – New Jersey Medical School has a full time position available at the Assistant or Associate Professor level, depending on experience, for a Board Certified or Board Eligible Physician, as a REI subspecialist, in the Division of Reproductive Endocrinology and Infertility. Rank and salary commensurate with experience. We seek faculty who will join a highly collaborative REI team in providing the full scope of care across the subspecialty, educating the next generation of physicians, and advancing the field through cutting-edge research. Faculty provide clinical REI/GYN services at University Hospital as well as at RBHS affiliates. Services provided include infertility care and assisted reproductive technologies at our recently renovated, state-of the art IVF lab, fertility preservation services, reproductive surgery, hormone therapy, evaluation and management of PCOS/androgen disorders and other disorders of the reproductive endocrine system. Our faculty perform research across the spectrum of basic, translational science and clinical trials; candidates who qualify and are interested in protected research time should consider applying. In addition, the Division has a longstanding, ACGME-accredited REI fellowship program and the applicant must have strong interest in teaching and supervising fellows, residents and medical students.</div> NJMS - Obstetrics & Gynocology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7455 26FA0054 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279804 2026-08-21T10:29:52-04:00 2026-08-21T10:29:52-04:00 Experiential Learning and Employer Development Co-Adjunct <div>Career Exploration and Success seeks a highly qualified employer-relations, recruiting, or experiential-learning professional to serve as an Experiential Learning and Employer Development Co-Adjunct during the Fall semester.<br><br></div><div>This is a fixed-term, three-month Class 8 non-teaching academic-support appointment focused exclusively on developing employer-provided experiential-learning and career opportunities for Rutgers–New Brunswick students. The co-adjutant will recruit and cultivate employers that can provide internships, applied learning experiences, and full-time employment opportunities through the Rutgers Scarlet Service Internship Program (RSSI), Industry Connect, and designated career and internship fairs.<br><br></div><div>The co-adjunct is responsible for:</div><ul><li>Recruiting and vetting employers for approximately 120 RSSI internship experiences.</li><li>Developing employer relationships that produce internships, applied learning experiences, and full-time employment opportunities through Industry Connect.</li><li>Recruiting employers offering internships, experiential-learning opportunities, and entry-level positions for designated career and internship fairs.</li><li>Evaluating prospective employer opportunities for alignment with applicable program requirements and student career-readiness objectives.</li><li>Communicating program expectations, participation requirements, and relevant deadlines to prospective employer partners.</li><li>Maintaining accurate records of employer outreach, employer participation, and opportunities developed.</li><li>Coordinating with designated Career Exploration and Success staff regarding employer eligibility, recruitment progress, and program deadlines.</li><li>Providing a final accounting of the employers recruited and the internship, experiential-learning, and full-time opportunities developed during the appointment.</li></ul><div><br>The successful candidate must possess excellent employer-outreach, relationship-development, communication, and project-management skills. The candidate must be able to cultivate professional relationships independently, evaluate prospective opportunities against established program requirements, maintain accurate records, and meet time-sensitive employer-recruitment goals.<br><br></div><div>The appointment is limited to the defined employer-development and experiential-learning responsibilities described above. It does not include continuing staff responsibilities, general coordinator coverage, staff supervision, routine departmental administration, or other duties as assigned.<br><br></div><div>The workload may fluctuate according to RSSI, Industry Connect, and career-fair recruitment cycles. The appointment begins on [start date], concludes on [end date], and carries no expectation of continued employment. Any subsequent appointment is contingent upon program needs, satisfactory performance, available funding, and required university approvals.<br><br></div><div>The fixed salary for this three-month appointment is $21,176.48, subject to final university approval.</div> Career Exploration & Success New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Undergraduate Education-L3 7231 26FA0727 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277426 2026-06-18T11:40:45-04:00 2026-06-18T11:40:45-04:00 Co Adj – Non Teaching <div>The Graduate School of Applied and Professional Psychology (GSAPP), Department of Clinical Psychology is currently seeking licensed psychologists (NJ) with expertise in either Psychodynamic or CBT treatment approaches to provide training/supervision for our doctoral students participating in either of two first-year courses (Learning Theory &amp; CB Foundations 18:820:507; Analytic Foundations18:820:509). The courses provide the foundation for both theoretical orientations and each student sees a case associated with each class. Supervision groups will meet once a week, in-person at GSAPP or remotely (depending on instructor preference), for 90 minutes. The psychologist will provide group clinical supervision for 2-4 students with one case each through the GSAPP clinic. Supervision commences around October 1st, and continues until the close of the spring term (around May 15), for a total of approximately 30 supervisory sessions. Communication and coordination between course instructors and the group supervisors is expected If you have any questions or would like additional information about these opportunities, please contact Dr. Nicole Cain, Chair of the Clinical Department, at nicole.cain@rutgers.edu.&nbsp;</div> Clinical Psychology New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Graduate School of Applied & P-L3 6827 26FA0624 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274162 2026-05-01T12:52:27-04:00 2026-05-01T12:52:27-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Postdoctoral Associate in the Center for Immunity and Inflammation within the New Jersey Medical School (NJMS).<br><br>Under the direction of the Principal Investigator, the primary purpose of the Postdoctoral Associate position is to perform specialized research activities and design and execute advanced experimental procedures in an immunology-focused laboratory independently.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Designs, discusses, and performs diverse experimental models and techniques related to the study of innate cells.</li><li>Contributes to general laboratory operations, including breeding and genotyping of mice and general maintenance of animal colonies.</li><li>Develops new ideas for promotion current research for the NJMS –Center for Immunity and Inflammation.</li><li>Operates and maintains experimental equipment.</li><li>Records and analyzes data from experiments.</li></ul> NJMS - Immunity & Infection Ce RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7451 Newark NJ 26ST0933 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266165 2025-12-31T09:31:51-05:00 2025-12-31T09:31:52-05:00 Director of the Center for Autism Research at Rutgers Brain Health Institute <div>The Rutgers Brain Health Institute (BHI) is recruiting an outstanding tenure-eligible investigator to serve as the Director of Rutgers Center for Autism Research, Education and Services<em> </em>(RUCARES). RUCARES is devoted to innovative research, education, and service with a focus on diagnosing, treating, and supporting children and adults with autism spectrum disorder (ASD). The center was established in 2020 under the leadership of the inaugural Director, Dr. Wayne Fisher, to foster the growth of autism research, education and services at Rutgers. Over the last six years, led by RUCARES, NIH funding for autism related research at Rutgers has grown more than 7-fold. RUCARES has also partnered with Children Specialized Hospital (CSH), to improve the health outcomes for all New Jersey individuals and families affected by autism. RUCARES, and its clinical arm CSH-RUCARES, are the first centers of their kind in New Jersey. In addition to the severe behavior program which offers highly effective clinical services to treat autistic children with severe behavior problems, CSH-RUCARES was recently awarded the New Jersey Autism Center of Excellence (NJACE) grant to support both clinical and basic research on autism.<br><br>The ideal candidate for the Director of RUCARES will be a research leader in autism spectrum disorders with a strong, externally-funded research program who utilizes basic <strong><em>or </em></strong>clinical approaches to address key questions regarding autism and related disorders. One of the primary roles of the Director of RUCARES will be to coordinate and nurture existing research and clinical activities, while striving to grow Rutgers into a world leader in basic and clinical autism research. Applicants must have a PhD, MD or equivalent degree, with an independent research program focused on autism spectrum disorders. The applicant also must demonstrate strong leadership skills. Investigators in basic science or clinical research are encouraged to apply. We offer a highly competitive salary and excellent start-up packages to establish the Director’s own research program and to grow the center.<br><br></div><div>Rutgers has considerable strengths in basic, clinical and translational autism research, with over 50 principal investigators working to develop new autism treatments. The department of pediatrics in New Brunswick and Newark have a full complement of pediatric medical subspecialists who actively collaborate with pediatric surgical specialists in clinical care and academic endeavors. Rutgers faculty and students also work closely with the autism community in NJ, providing educational intervention services, developing policy and performing public outreach through the Boggs Center on Developmental Disabilities and the Douglass Developmental Disabilities Center.<br><br></div><div>The Rutgers Brain Health Institute (BHI) is an internationally recognized institute for basic, translational, and clinical research into the biological bases of human brain function and dysfunction. BHI supports over 300 neuroscience faculty labs engaged in basic and clinical research at Rutgers. BHI has created multiple centers of excellence in autism, Alzheimer’s, addiction, human brain imaging and computational cognitive neuropsychiatry with outstanding core facilities, including a new research-dedicated 3T Prisma MRI scanner and a human behavioral testing core developed and operated in collaboration with Princeton University. Rutgers offers tremendous collaborative opportunities with over 300 neuroscience faculty labs engaged in basic, clinical and translational research, and proximity to the New York, Princeton and Philadelphia neuroscience communities. Applicants should submit a CV and statement of research accomplishments and plans and names of at least three references to Dr Jennifer Mulle, Chair of search committee, at <a href=\"mailto:bhi@bhi.rutgers.edu\"><strong>bhi@bhi.rutgers.edu</strong></a> .</div> Brain Health Institute RBHS Chancellor-L2 Brain Health Institute-L3 8146 25FA0459 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280074 2026-08-27T11:13:32-04:00 2026-08-27T11:13:33-04:00 Mental Health Specialist III UBHC <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Mental Health Specialist III for the Inpatient Units within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Mental Health Specialist III is to participate as a member of the unit team providing care for all age groups in accordance with facility policy and procedure. Demonstrates leadership skills and assists the Staff Nurse with staff assignments, orientation of new staff and formulation of patient groups.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Assists the Staff Nurse in planning patient care.</li><li>Provides care based on the patient’s established care plan, under the supervision of the Staff Nurse.</li><li>Observes patient’s behaviors and when necessary notifies appropriate staff.</li><li>Assists in maintaining a safe, therapeutic environment that respects patients’ rights.</li><li>Assists the patients with activities of daily living, encouraging independent behavior, when appropriate.</li><li>Monitors the milieu for changes in patient behavior. Also, observes interaction between patients and visitors.</li><li>Accompanies patients for medical evaluation outside of the facility.</li></ul> UBHC - Acute Psychological Ser RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7987 Piscataway NJ 26ST1654 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278324 2026-07-07T09:49:19-04:00 2026-07-07T09:49:20-04:00 Seasonal Marine Field Worker <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Seasonal Marine Field Worker for the School of Environmental and Biological Sciences, Haskin Shellfish Research Laboratory, Port Norris, New Jersey.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Assists with monitoring of Delaware Bay oyster fishery.</li><li>Monitors includes field collection aboard research and commercial fishing vessels as well as laboratory processing (measuring, shucking, oyster disease/pathology analysis) of oyster dredge samples.</li><li>Performs data entry and audit associated with these tasks will also be required.</li><li>Provides support as needed to additional projects by assisting with tasks like animal care, video analysis, and Living Shoreline installation.</li></ul> Haskin Shellfsh Research Labor New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 7171 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267009 2026-01-08T14:31:29-05:00 2026-01-08T14:31:30-05:00 Salesforce Developer <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Salesforce Developer for the Office of Information Technology. Under the direction of a Project Manager/Associate Director for Enterprise Application Services (EAS), provides analytical and programming support for Enrollment Management office and other university administrative and academic offices. This position serve as one of the platform developers for the enterprise Salesforce.com environment.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Develops solutions within the Salesforce or CRM platform or software that integrates with Salesforce to meet stakeholder requirements for existing and new functionality.</li><li>Works with project managers, business analysts and other developers to design, develop, test and deploy solutions including dashboards, interfaces, and integrations.</li><li>Assists with necessary system upgrades in all Salesforce environments as well as testing all impacted areas and workflows.</li><li>Works with our institutional management team to establish suitable processes to support administrative, development, and change management activities.</li><li>Assists in training of new users, and grow the Salesforce.com skill set across the organization.</li><li>Works with members of the user community to define and document development requirements.</li><li>Assists with the evaluation, scope and completion of new development requests.</li><li>Understands and adheres to Rutgers’ compliance standards as they appear in RBHS’s Corporate Compliance Policy, Code of Conduct and Conflict of Interest Policy.</li><li>Performs other related duties as assigned.</li></ul> Enterprise Application Service EVP & Chief Admin Officer OIT - VP & Chief Information O-L3 6882 Somerset NJ 26ST0032 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280226 2026-08-31T14:16:15-04:00 2026-08-31T14:16:16-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse PT Eves SWSP <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Part Time Licensed Practical Nurse for Southwoods State Prison, located in Bridgeton, NJ<br><br>The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs.</li><li>Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.</li><li>Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.</li><li>Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.</li><li>Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.</li><li>Documents all aspects of patient care.</li></ul> UCHC-South Woods Psn-Ancillary RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7685 Bridgeton NJ 26ST1694 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278772 2026-07-14T09:23:28-04:00 2026-07-14T09:23:28-04:00 Post Doctoral Associate <div>The Department of Environmental Sciences is seeking a Postdoctoral Associate to conduct research on applied climatology. This position will work with the Office of the New Jersey State Climatologist to evaluate compound climate risks across the state, including combined flooding from sea level rise, storm surge, and inland rainfall, storm-induced extreme winds and precipitation, and sequential synoptic weather systems or predecessor events. The position will involve developing probabilistic frameworks to characterize compound hazard frequency and severity under current and future climate states. The position offers the candidate the opportunity to work with stakeholders across New Jersey and the mid-Atlantic region and to provide physical insights for risk assessment on topics such as sea level, air quality, and agricultural impacts, among others. Successful candidates will be involved with observational data analysis, numerical modeling of natural hazards, and outreach to local stakeholders. Candidates will present research findings through publications, publicly available data visualization tools, academic presentations, and public engagement.</div> Environmental Science New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 7137 26FA0669 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/269869 2026-02-25T15:57:43-05:00 2026-02-25T15:57:43-05:00 Research Associate - Biological Structure Annotation Specialist (Biocurator) <div>The RCSB Protein Data Bank (RCSB PDB, rcsb.org), the US data center for the global PDB archive, serves thousands of Data Depositors in the Americas and makes 3D macromolecular structure data available at no charge and without usage restrictions to many millions of rcsb.org users worldwide.</div><div>The primary objectives of <strong>Deposition/Biocuration Services:</strong></div><div>● Provide expert deposition, validation, biocuration, and remediation services to Data Depositors worldwide</div><div>● Maintain data quality and uniformity in the PDB archive which is critical to research and education</div><div>● Develop and promote community-endorsed data standards for archiving and exchange of global structural biology data</div><div>The RCSB PDB at Rutgers University in Piscataway, NJ has an opening for a Biological Structure Annotation Specialist (Biocurator) to analyze, curate, and validate macromolecular structures from the dynamically expanding structural biology community. The Biocurator also participates in exciting projects with significant impact on the scientific community, communicates daily with members of the research community, and participates in fun outreach activities.</div> Quantitative Biomedicine Inst New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 6749 26FA0165 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280464 2026-09-04T14:14:17-04:00 2026-09-04T14:14:18-04:00 Clinical Services Representative I <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Clinical Services Representative I within the Department of Orthodontics at the Rutgers School of Dental Medicine (RSDM).<br><br>Under general supervision, the Clinical Services Representative I carries out a variety of front desk services related to cash collection. The incumbent serves as a receptionist, maintain appointment books, requests chart, post payments, enters and updates patient demographic and insurance information and collect copayments.<br><br>Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following:</div><ul><li>Registers patients presenting for treatment at Rutgers School of Dental Medicine. Enters all biographic and insurance information into appropriate computer system. Checks patient identification as required by RSDM policies. Audits patient data, such as address, is current.</li><li>Obtains a copy of the patients’ Medicaid/Medicaid HMO card each month, verifies and updates information as needed.</li><li>Ensures that the designated insurance copayment is collected before patient is seen by student.</li><li>Responsible for the collection and posting of patients' payments. Ensures that the patients' payments are recorded properly. Prepares computer receipts for patients.</li><li>Responds with good customer service to patient inquiries or transfers, as appropriate, to a financial coordinator.</li><li>Prepares and balances receipts daily for the bank deposit. Endorses all checks with Rutgers University stamp and ensures that deposit is placed in a secure lock bag.</li><li>Proves cash collections daily according to the procedures established by the Head Cashier.</li><li>Directs patients to the correct area of the dental school (Special Needs, Pediatric Dentistry, Oral Med, etc.).</li><li>Informs students of their patients’ arrival. Takes messages for students and advises them of patient appointments.</li><li>Requests charts for patients of record who will be seen the next day.</li></ul> RSDM - Orthodontics RBHS Chancellor-L2 Rutgers School of Dental Medic-L3 7547 Newark NJ 26ST1727 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279420 2026-08-07T13:36:23-04:00 2026-08-07T13:36:24-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate - Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Postdoctoral Associate for the Behavioral Research and Training Institute (BRTI)– Center for Integrated Care within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Postdoctoral Associate is to be responsible for research and clinical activities with the Behavioral Research and Training Institute.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Conceptualizes, designs and implements research and program evaluation projects in support of the lab’s mission.</li><li>Based on a thorough knowledge of the field and the research literature, identifies research projects that would contribute to increasing the body of knowledge related to integrated behavioral health, addiction, psychology.</li><li>Translates research ideas into concrete, specific and implementable research projects that meet the standards of scientific inquiry and that comport with University requirements.</li><li>Assists the AVP in the preparation of research proposals to obtain grant support from federal, state and local units of government, as well as foundations.</li><li>Provides technical assistance to research lab based on needs assessment and data collection.</li><li>Under the supervision of the AVP, manages and coordinates research projects.</li><li>Prepares manuscripts summarizing the center’s research projects for submission to professional journals and publications.</li></ul> UBHC - BRTI Institute RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8044 Piscataway NJ 26ST1398 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/276404 2026-06-03T12:34:18-04:00 2026-06-03T12:34:18-04:00 Associate Professor of Transplant Surgery <div>Job Description<br><br></div><div>Duties and Responsibilities:<br><br></div><div>Looking for an Abdominal Transplant Surgeon to join a growing abdominal organ transplant program within an academic medical center. The candidate should have expertise in kidney and pancreas transplantation, including organ transplantation and recovery, with a focus on clinical excellence, multidisciplinary care, education, and programmatic growth.<br><br></div><div>As an attending at Rutgers, Robert Wood Johnson Medical School and Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital in New Brunswick, responsibilities will include all aspects of patient care and medical record completion, teaching of students, residents, and fellows via clinical patient rounds, Grand Rounds, and departmental conferences; participation in community education programs and lecture series; submission of abstracts/manuscripts for publication; and other duties as assigned by the Division Chief, Chair, or Dean. Position duties will be to function as an Abdominal Transplant Surgeon within the transplant program.<br><br></div><ul><li>Performing kidney and pancreas transplant surgeries, procurements, and related procedures</li><li>Managing all phases of donor and transplant recipient care in inpatient and outpatient settings</li><li>Participating in transplant candidate selection committees and the development of clinical protocols</li><li>Supporting quality improvement, clinical outcomes, and regulatory performance initiatives</li><li>Participating in clinical research, scholarship, and innovation activities</li><li>Teaching and mentoring medical students, residents, fellows, and other trainees in office, inpatient, and operative settings</li><li>Collaborating with multidisciplinary transplant teams to provide comprehensive, patient-centered care</li><li>Supporting strategic growth, regional visibility, and long-term sustainability of the abdominal organ transplant program</li><li>Participating in national and regional transplant societies and professional organizations.</li></ul> RWJ - Surgery General RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7835 26FA0527 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274040 2026-04-30T11:23:48-04:00 2026-04-30T11:23:48-04:00 Lecturers, Africana Studies <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the Faculty of Arts &amp; Sciences, Africana Studies Program, is seeking lecturers to teach various topics for courses in Fall 2026, Winter 2027, Spring 2027 and/or Summer 2027. The instructor will present course material during the assigned course times, hold office hours, administer exams, assign grades and coordinate any other requirements related to course instruction.</div> Africana Studies Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 9012 26FA0405 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/265918 2025-12-31T09:02:29-05:00 2025-12-31T09:02:29-05:00 Post Doc Associate - RCEI - Lockwood <div>Performs complex evidence synthesis or computational simulation modeling of biodiversity data. Documents the work performed maintains all databases that result from research output and develops information for research papers. Consult with the Director of the Rutgers Climate and Energy Institute (RCEI), other RCEI staff, and members of the leadership team in the preparation of proposals, grant applications, and annual progress reports. Is responsible for the preparation of a wide variety of peer-reviewed publications, and acts as a point of contact for both internal and external collaborators. Completes work independently, with broadly defined work objectives and limited review of overall results. Performs professional work that requires specialized knowledge of biodiversity research, and has a solid understanding, use, and application of concepts, theories, principles, practices, terminology, and applied bases of biodiversity research.</div> Rutgers Climate & Energy Insti New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 8722 24FA1342 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279679 2026-08-18T13:57:49-04:00 2026-08-18T13:57:50-04:00 Patient Navigator <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Patient Navigator in the Department of Medicine- Infectious Disease within the New Jersey Medical School (NJMS).<br><br>The Patient Navigator provides clients with medical case management services as defined by the Health Resource Services Administration (HRSA). Provides client-centered services that link clients with health care, psychosocial, and other services. Coordinates and follows-up to ensure that medical treatments have been provided. Ensures timely and coordinated access to medically appropriate levels of health and support services and continuity of care, through ongoing assessment of the client’s and other key family members’ needs and personal support systems. Ensures that comprehensive medical case management is provided including the provision of treatment adherence counseling to ensure readiness for, and adherence to, complex HIV/AIDS treatments. Key activities include (1) initial assessment of service needs; (2) development of a comprehensive, individualized service plan; (3) provision of services required to implement the plan; (4)monitoring to assess the efficacy of the plan; and (5) periodic re-evaluation and adaptation of the plan as necessary over the life of the client.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Orients clients and provides information about the available services of the ID Practice.</li><li>Performs a biopsychosocial assessment and develops a care plan to address the client’s needs initially and at a minimum every six months.</li><li>Develops assessments of clients’ medical and bio-psychosocial needs including, but not limited to medical care, housing, support groups, home health care, respite care, legal services, employment training, entitlements, food, substance abuse treatment and counseling, etc.</li><li>Develops service plans including referrals to appropriate service providers, community-based organizations, and entitlements for the client, family members, and/or partner(s). Assists with facilitating access to services in an empowering way that allows client to have control.</li><li>Conducts ongoing monitoring including regular reassessment, plan modifications, referrals, and recommendations, as well as client’s needs, risks and progress as appropriate.</li><li>Coordinates/facilitates and follows-up on medical treatments and patient referrals for core medical services and other services as needed.</li></ul> NJMS - Medicine Infect Disease RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7443 Newark NJ 26ST1623 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280006 2026-08-26T09:43:57-04:00 2026-08-26T09:43:57-04:00 Non-Credit Instructor – 2026 <div>The Center for Continuing and Professional Development under the Division of Lifelong Learning and Innovation seeks qualified part time instructors for the center’s array of non-credit programs and initiatives. Candidates would contribute to the division’s educational mission of lifelong learning and its objective of providing an educational experience that connects instruction and training with the skill sets to succeed in their current career or pursue a new path. Potential areas of industry include, but are not limited to, customer service, workforce development, information technology, information technology &amp; management, managing programs, communication and leadership, managing people and projects, project management, strategic planning, training and employee development, leadership coaching, paralegal, healthcare, programming and coding, and other areas of professional development and training.<br><br>Successful candidates will be responsible for the following:<br><br>• Instructing/co-instructing course(s) for non-credit programs (may include traditional lecture, hybrid, and/or fully online courses)<br>• Prepare course materials (i.e., syllabi, presentations, hand-outs, reading materials, etc.)<br>• Provide constructive feedback to students as well as critical instruction regarding course/program work<br>• Respond to student emails and inquiries<br>• Adhere university and program regulations, policies, and deadlines<br>• Practice innovative educational methodology</div> DoCS - CCPD University Academic Affairs-L2 Division of Continuing Studies-L3 7289 26FA0737 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277780 2026-06-25T11:23:37-04:00 2026-06-25T11:23:37-04:00 Staff Nurse Mental Health Per Diem Mulitiple Vacancies UCHC NSP <div>University Correctional Healthcare (UCHC) is seeking a per diem Mental Health Staff Nurse (RN) for the Northern State Prison in Newark, New Jersey. The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus. Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment. Frequently functions guided by nursing protocols. Functions as a team leader as assigned. Demonstrates competency in assessment and identification of the psychological and physical health of adults (18 to 64 years), and geriatrics (65+) all population groups and their personal strengths. Identifies inmate-centered goals and nursing objectives and implements prescribed interventions and solutions for the identified problems.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the inmate-patient including adults (18 to 64 years), and geriatrics (65+) within the framework established by the correctional system.</li><li>Uses psychiatric standards of nursing practice and classification of mental disorders: to develop inmate treatment plans with specific goals and interventions delineating nursing actions unique to each inmate’s needs.</li><li>Implements nursing actions that promote, maintain or restore physical and mental health of all age groups.</li><li>Evaluates inmate responses in collaboration with multi-disciplinary care providers to ensure quality inmate care.</li><li>Performs additional duties that are directly related to the workings of the milieu and its safety, as demonstrated by documentation in specific paperwork and by supervisory observations.</li></ul> UCHC Nursing Per Diem Medical RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7664 Newark NJ 26ST0764 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275526 2026-05-20T13:50:28-04:00 2026-05-20T13:50:29-04:00 Dining Services Student Worker (Three Chili's Truck) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Dining Services Student Worker (Three Chilli's Truck). Rutgers Dining Services strives to be the best in culinary excellence and as a Dining Services Worker you play a critical role in the customer experience. From assisting in the preparation and service of food, to maintaining the presentation of the dining halls, to assisting guests, we have a variety of roles and will find the right one for you!<br><br>Dining Service Workers earn a paycheck and more:</div><ol><li>Student employee meal privileges.</li><li>Flexible schedules (10/20 hours/week) that work around your classes and activities.</li><li>Convenient on-campus locations.</li><li>Opportunities to advance to leadership positions such as Captain, Meal Manager and Student Unit Manager.</li><li>Valuable work experience to add to your resume.</li><li>Learn important job skills including interpersonal communications, team dynamics, dependability and time management.</li><li>A fun and welcoming environment.</li></ol> Three Chilies New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Student Affairs - New Brunswic-L3 8457 Piscataway NJ 26ST1103 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266313 2025-12-31T09:48:36-05:00 2025-12-31T09:48:36-05:00 Postdoctoral Associate <div>DIMACS, the Center for Discrete Mathematics and Theoretical Computer Science, invites applications for postdoctoral associate positions for 2026-2028. The postdoc will be mentored by a faculty member at Rutgers or a DIMACS partner institution, and able to participate in the wide variety of activities at DIMACS, while working on an original research program. Topics include but are not limited to artificial intelligence, computing theory (algorithms, complexity), data science, statistics, discrete mathematics (graph theory, combinatorics), game theory, machine learning, optimization, privacy, and security. Activities often address applications in wide-ranging areas, including biology, robotics, cyber &amp; physical security, economics, voting, engineering, ecology, sociology, epidemiology, sustainability, and computational social choice. Applicants should be recent PhD graduates in computer science, mathematics, statistics, economics, information science, operations research, or a related field.<br><br>Positions provide salary, health benefits, and an allowance for travel. Applicants should provide a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, a research statement highlighting their current, past and planned future research, a teaching statement if intending to teach, and the names/e-mail addresses of three references.<br><br>DIMACS fosters research and education programs on topics that lie at the interface of discrete mathematics and theoretical computer science and their wide-ranging applications. It was founded as an NSF Science and Technology Center in 1989. DIMACS’s partners include Rutgers University, AT&amp;T Labs - Research, Columbia University, Georgia Tech, IBM Research, Microsoft Research, NEC Laboratories America, New Jersey Institute of Technology, Nokia Bell Labs, Peraton Labs, Princeton University, Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute, and Stevens Institute of Technology.<br><br>Research and education areas at DIMACS include algorithms, combinatorics, complexity, privacy and security, discrete and computational geometry, optimization, graph theory, data science, artificial intelligence, and machine learning, with applications in sustainability, epidemiology, genetics, networks, transportation, security, and economics. Many DIMACS activities relate to specific topics of current interest represented by the DIMACS Special Focus programs. Postdoctoral Associates at DIMACS are encouraged to collaborate with DIMACS members and visitors and to participate in all of the research and educational activities of DIMACS.<br><br>We are strongly committed to increasing the diversity of our Center. We believe that research and society benefit from a diverse workplace and strongly encourage applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and students with non-traditional backgrounds.<br><br></div> DIMACS New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 6729 25FA1030 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280153 2026-08-31T08:40:18-04:00 2026-08-31T08:40:19-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse PT Days UCHC SWSP <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Part Time Licensed Practical Nurse for Southwoods State Prison, located in Bridgeton, NJ<br><br>The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs.</li><li>Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.</li><li>Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.</li><li>Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.</li><li>Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.</li><li>Documents all aspects of patient care.</li></ul> UCHC-South Woods Psn-Ancillary RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7685 Bridgeton NJ 26ST0550 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278570 2026-07-10T10:58:15-04:00 2026-07-10T10:58:17-04:00 Technician I  PT Days UCHC BSP (multiple vacancies) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Part Time UCHC Technician I for Bayside State Prison, located in Leesburg, NJ. The UCHC Technician I participates as a member of the clinical and administrative medical team at the Prison.<br><br>Among the duties for this position are:<br><br></div><ul><li>&nbsp;Takes vital signs, height and weight and documents in electronic medical records (EMR).</li><li>&nbsp;Assists the physician/associate practitioner with procedures, including preparing the inmate for the examination.</li><li>&nbsp;Obtains specimen collection and handling, including, but not limited to, drawing blood.</li><li>&nbsp;Assists with the cleaning, sterilization and securing of equipment within the Health Service Unit.</li><li>&nbsp;Maintains or assists in maintaining the supply stock in the Health Service Unit by ordering in a timely and appropriate manner. Maintains the supply stock in the examination rooms.• Aggregates the orders of all medications and forwards to the pharmacy provider / local pharmacy.</li></ul><div><br></div> UCHC Bayside State Prison Anci RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7684 Leesburg NJ 26ST0663 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/268289 2026-01-30T10:18:43-05:00 2026-01-30T10:18:44-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor- General Internal Medicine <div>The Department of Medicine at Rutgers New Jersey Medical School seeks qualified candidates at the Assistant/Associate Professor level for a full-time academic position in the Division of General Internal Medicine.<br><br></div><div>The position will be responsible for the full spectrum of care in the inpatient and outpatient areas for the Division of General Internal Medicine and the Department of Medicine. This position includes patient care, teaching and scholarship, with administrative oversight for managing ambulatory practices.<br><br></div> NJMS - Medicine Academic Medic RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7440 26FA0070 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280352 2026-09-03T08:53:42-04:00 2026-09-03T08:53:43-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate, Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Postdoctoral Associate for the department of Pathology &amp; Laboratory Medicine at the Robert Wood Johnson Medical School.<br><br>The Postdoctoral Research Associate works independently on research projects, with supervision from a Research Mentor, and on developing teaching skills, with supervision from a Teaching Mentor, to support the general functioning of their biomedical research laboratory, and to fulfill the research and teaching requirements of the Rutgers IRACDA, INSPIRE Postdoctoral Training Program.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Eligible applicants must apply to the program and receive approval from the INSPIRE Admissions Committee. Application and eligibility information can be found on the INSPIRE website: https://rwjms.rutgers.edu/research/inspire/home.</li><li>Must take part in all of the research, writing and teaching training provided for INSPIRE IRACDA Fellows.</li><li>Must take part in all of the research and teaching evaluation surveys provided for the INSPIRE IRACDA fellows.</li><li>Does biomedical research with Research mentor, and publishes the findings, in support of developing an independent academic research career.</li><li>Works with a Teaching Mentor at INSPIRE Partner School to teach and mentor undergraduate student, in support of developing an independent academic research career.</li></ul><div><br></div> RWJ - Pathology Research RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7799 Piscataway NJ 26ST1572 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279210 2026-07-30T15:35:51-04:00 2026-07-30T15:35:52-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate - Pharmacoepidemiology/Health Informatics <div>Postdoctoral Research Associate- The Postdoctoral Research Associate will join a multidisciplinary research team focused on cognitive aging and health and Alzheimer’s disease and related dementias. Reporting to the Principal Investigator on grant-funded projects, the individual will play a key role in supporting laboratory operations and advancing ongoing research initiatives.<br><br></div><div>Primary responsibilities include:</div><ul><li>Designing and executing observational cohort studies examining drug-drug interactions and dementia risk using large-scale EHR and administrative claims data.</li><li>Leading statistical analysis (methods may include IPTW-weighted Cox regression, active comparator new-user designs, self-controlled case series, propensity scoring).</li><li>Developing and extending an AI-based drug safety signal prioritization platform.</li><li>Supporting grant preparation and contributing to grant aims.</li><li>Collaborating with mentors in pharmacoepidemiology methods and adjacent clinical research domains.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>The candidate must demonstrate a strong record of accomplishment in a relevant area of research, as evidenced by peer-reviewed publications. Expertise in pharmacoepidemiology methods and specific dementia/drug safety and interactions is highly desirable. In addition to experimental work, the Postdoctoral Research Associate will contribute to mentoring and training staff and students, assist in experimental design and planning, and help introduce and develop new technical approaches within the group. The individual will collaborate with other research teams involved in NIH-funded projects, and participate in group meetings</div> Institute for Health, Health C RBHS Chancellor-L2 Institute for Health, Health C-L3 8086 26FA0692 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/272443 2026-04-06T12:34:36-04:00 2026-04-06T12:34:37-04:00 Lecturers/Adjuncts- Summer Session <div>The Department of Biochemistry &amp; Microbiology is seeking Lecturers/Adjuncts to teach summer session undergraduate courses and labs. The Lecturer will present course materials during the assigned courses times, hold office hours, help proctor, grade exams and assignments, develop homework/exam questions and coordinate any other requirements related to the instruction of the course. Additional duties may include assisting students with laboratory activities.<br><br></div> Biochemistry & Microbiology New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 7135 26FA0315 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279565 2026-08-13T10:01:26-04:00 2026-08-13T10:01:27-04:00 Peer Support Specialist III <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Peer Support Specialist III for the Outpatient Monmouth Junction Department within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The Peer Support Specialist III is a member of a team offering person centered, culturally competent instrumental, information and emotional support either in person or by phone. The Peer Support Specialist III uses lived experience and basic peer support skills to engage and empower persons served to support their wellness. Offers insight into the experience of living with a mental and/or substance use disorder and relevant recovery supports in order to assist staff in identifying program environments and treatment approaches that are conducive to recovery.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Uses his/her own lived experiences with mental and/or substance use recovery as a vehicle to establish rapport and build relationships with the individuals served and/or their family member(s).</li><li>Engages consumers in the community to enhance commitment to recovery.</li><li>Follows supervisory direction and is receptive to feedback from supervisor.</li><li>Demonstrates initiative and flexibility with respect to job assignments.</li><li>Completes Employee Health update as required.</li><li>Understands and adheres to Rutgers’ compliance standards as they appear in RBHS’s Corporate Compliance Policy, Code of Conduct and Conflict of Interest Policy.</li></ul> UBHC - Outpatient Monmouth Jun RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8023 Monmouth Junction NJ 26ST0397 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267838 2026-01-23T09:36:25-05:00 2026-01-23T09:36:25-05:00 Non-Credit Instructor (Part Time) - 2026 <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking non-credit part time instructors for the Center for Mathematics, Science, and Computer Education. We seek qualified instructors who can contribute to the University’s educational mission and bridge the gap between the classroom and the industry. Successful candidates will instruct/co-instruct on a wide variety of topics in K-12 STEM education.<br><br>Candidates will be responsible for the following:<br>• Instructing/co-instructing mathematics, STEM, STEAM, maker education, or coding workshops for teachers and/or students at the K-12 level<br>• Prepare course materials (i.e., syllabi, presentations, hand-outs, reading materials, etc.)<br>• Provide constructive feedback to participants.<br>• Practice innovative educational methodology</div> DoCS - CMSCE University Academic Affairs-L2 Division of Continuing Studies-L3 8084 26FA0063 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280266 2026-09-01T08:51:55-04:00 2026-09-01T08:51:56-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Postdoctoral Associate for the Child Health Institute of NJ at the Robert Wood Johnson Medical School.<br><br>Under the direction of the Principal Investigator, the Postdoctoral Associate will be responsible for the design, analysis, interpretation, and presentation of experiments regarding the study of molecular mechanisms of the regulation of synaptic transmission in mammalian brain and human neurons derived from human tissue. In addition, the postdoc will perform molecular, cellular and/or electro-physiological experiments.<br><br>The Postdoc will participate in lab meetings, research in progress seminars, and presentations at conferences. The Postdoctoral Associate will prepare manuscripts based on their research, aid in developing the PI’s grant applications, and will apply for personal grant funding.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Under the direction of the Principal Investigator, will perform whole-cell patch clamp electrophysiology in brain slices and cell cultures.</li><li>Performs behavioral tests in mice.</li><li>Performs in vivo 2p imaging in head-fixed mice.</li><li>Compiles and analyzes data with appropriate conclusions and recommendations in support of further CHI research.</li><li>Communicates with the PI and present the data in a timely manner.</li></ul> RWJ - Child Health Institute RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7852 New Brunswick NJ 25ST1989 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278939 2026-07-17T12:16:20-04:00 2026-07-17T12:16:21-04:00 Open Rank Faculty - Clinical Laboratory & Medical Imaging Sciences <div>Rutgers University’s School of Health Professions (SHP) invites applications for an open-rank, full-time, 12-month, non-tenure-track faculty position in the Clinical Laboratory Sciences (CLS) Division of the Department of Clinical Laboratory and Medical Imaging Sciences (CLMIS). The successful candidate will join a comprehensive academic unit that offers the Master of Science in CLS (MS-CLS) and the Doctor of Clinical Laboratory Science (DCLS). The MS-CLS program and DCLS pre-residency curriculum are delivered entirely online. Interprofessional education and collaboration are actively encouraged within the Department of CLMIS and SHP, fostering a distinctive environment for faculty growth and scholarly engagement.<br><br>Primary Responsibilities</div><ul><li>Develop, deliver, and continuously improve graduate-level online CLS courses in molecular diagnostics, clinical immunology, clinical chemistry, and related disciplines.</li><li>Advise and mentor graduate students, including supervision of capstone projects, applied research, and DCLS residency experiences.</li><li>Engage in scholarly activities, including CLS research, educational scholarship, quality improvement/implementation science initiatives, and contributions to the professional literature.</li><li>Contribute to service by participating on committees, supporting program assessment and accreditation efforts, and assisting with student recruitment and outreach.</li></ul> SHP - CLMIS RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Health Professions-L3 7592 26FA0514 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/271483 2026-03-24T10:18:54-04:00 2026-03-24T10:18:55-04:00 Post Doctorial Associate <div>Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy, Pharmacy Practice, and Pharmacy Administration – Health Outcomes, Policy &amp; Economics, Rutgers University is part of Rutgers Biomedical Health Sciences (RBHS) and participates in interdisciplinary professional education and training partnership with Rutgers School of Public Health and the Robert Wood Johnson Medical School.<br><br>Though certain responsibilities of the resident are required, the program has the flexibility to develop activities consistent with the resident’s background and career goals. In general, the resident responsibilities include: 1. Attend daily rounds and make appropriate recommendations to inter-disciplinary treatment teams 2. Design, monitor, and evaluate treatment goals for patients that consider patient-, disease-, and drug-specific information and ethical considerations 3. Present educational in-services on pharmacy topics to patients, pharmacy staff, and inter-disciplinary treatment team 4. Lead inpatient and outpatient pharmacy medication education groups 5. Supervise pharmacy students on Advanced Pharmacy Practice Experience (APPE) rotations. 6. Present didactic lectures to pharmacy students at the Rutgers Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy 7. Complete a research project related to the provision of pharmacy care, as well as presenting this research at a national conference</div> Pharmacy Practice & Administra RBHS Chancellor-L2 Ernest Mario School of Pharmac-L3 6720 26FA0271 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279499 2026-08-11T10:58:10-04:00 2026-08-11T10:58:10-04:00 Coadjutant- Casual NonTeaching, School of Communication and Information (AY27) <div>School of Communication and Information seeks Program/Research/Instructional Assistants and Graders: These assistants work with a department chair, program director, or faculty member to support administrative and instructional duties; may create documents, organize events, update websites, maintain departmental/program data, work with a researcher on a specific area of inquiry; may record and analyze data, conduct literature reviews, abstract information, develop research protocols, conduct focus groups and interviews, complete IRB forms; may attend classes, take attendance, set up equipment and materials in the classroom, hold regular office hours, offer review sessions periodically through the semester, update online course materials, prepare materials for distribution to the class, grade papers and exams according to a rubric supplied by the teacher, and/or run automated grading sheets.</div> School  Communicatn & Info Sci New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School  Communicatn & Info Sci-L3 8093 26FA0705 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279756 2026-08-20T09:07:14-04:00 2026-08-20T09:07:15-04:00 Technician I PT Eves UCHC BSP (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Part Time Technician I for Bayside State Prison, located in Leesburg, NJ. The Technician I participates as a member of the clinical and administrative medical team at the Prison.<br><br>Among the duties for the position are:<br><br><br></div><ul><li>Takes vital signs, height and weight and documents in electronic medical records (EMR).</li><li>Assists the physician/associate practitioner with procedures, including preparing the inmate for the examination.</li><li>Obtains specimen collection and handling, including, but not limited to, drawing blood.</li><li>Assists with the cleaning, sterilization and securing of equipment within the Health Service Unit.</li><li>Maintains or assists in maintaining the supply stock in the Health Service Unit by ordering in a timely and appropriate manner.</li><li>Maintains the supply stock in the examination rooms.</li><li>Aggregates the orders of all medications and forwards to the pharmacy provider / local pharmacy.</li></ul> UCHC Bayside State Prison Anci RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7684 Leesburg NJ 26ST0665 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277077 2026-06-12T15:33:17-04:00 2026-06-12T15:33:18-04:00 Mental Health Clinician III - Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Mental Health Clinician III for the Brief Treatment within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>Under direction, the primary purpose of the Mental Health Clinician III is to provide comprehensive evaluation, assessment and therapeutic intervention to address the psychological, emotional and social needs of individuals served by the unit. Duties include formulating evaluations, developing and implementing treatment plans, conducting individual, group, and family therapy and providing case management functions.<br><br>Among the key duties of the position are the following:</div><ul><li>Consistently behaves in accordance with established department and UBHC policies and procedures as observed by supervisor.</li><li>Under supervision, provides psychotherapeutic interventions/services in accordance with accepted professional and ethical standards of licensing/regulatory bodies and UBHC.</li><li>Formulates clinically appropriate evaluations consistent with Clinical Records standards in accordance with prescribed time as indicated by periodic record review.</li><li>Participates meaningfully in supervision/consultation as demonstrated by integration of supervisory material in clinical practice as observed by supervisor.</li><li>Participates in development, implementation, and evaluation of programs.</li><li>Completes Employee Health Update as required.</li></ul> UBHC - Addictions RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8003 Plainfield NJ 25ST1990 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274089 2026-04-30T15:17:16-04:00 2026-04-30T15:17:17-04:00 Capstone Advisor, Graduate Liberal Studies <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the Faculty of Arts &amp; Sciences, Graduate Liberal Studies Program, seeks Capstone Project Advisors for graduate liberal studies students for the 2026-2027 AY. This will be a Coadjutant role.</div> Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 8076 26FA0425 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266032 2025-12-31T09:16:35-05:00 2025-12-31T09:16:36-05:00 General Anesthesiologist (2 Positions Available) <div>The Department of Anesthesiology at Rutgers, New Jersey Medical School, seeks two qualified General Anesthesiologist for full-time positions as Assistant Professor, Non-Tenure Track. The effective day of the appointments is February 1, 2026. Candidates on H1B or equivalent visa are welcome to apply.</div><div><br></div><ul><li>Duties include on-site anesthesia services to adult patients at University Hospital; intraoperative and didactic teaching of residents; participation in Faculty Development programs; working collaboratively with the members of the surgical services both clinically and administratively; contributing to research that forwards the discipline academically and clinically.</li></ul><div><br></div><ul><li>Qualified applicants must:</li></ul><ol><li>Have a medical doctorate or equivalent,</li><li>Hold or be eligible for medical licensure in New Jersey,</li><li>Be a BC/BE Anesthesiologist.</li></ol><div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmation Action Employer and is compliant with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Diversity as a core value of RBHS, embodies inclusiveness, mutual respect, and multiple perspectives and serves as a driver for excellence for achieving equity in health and health care. For more information, please visit <a href=\"http://recruitment.rutgers.edu/TheRUCommitment-2.htm\"><strong>http://recruitment.rutgers.edu/TheRUCommitment-2.htm</strong></a> and for the University’s commitment to equal employment opportunity and affirmative, please go to <a href=\"https://policies.rutgers.edu/sites/default/files/60.1.8%20-%20current.pdf\"><strong>https://policies.rutgers.edu/sites/default/files/60.1.8%20-%20current.pdf</strong></a>. <strong>We encourage applications from women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities.</strong></div><div>We offer excellent benefits and a highly competitive salary.<br><br>The University Hospital, a primary teaching hospital of the Rutgers New Jersey Medical School, is a widely recognized tertiary care center and Level 1 Trauma Center. Located in the vibrant city of Newark, just 20 minutes from Manhattan, you’ll be surrounded by the idyllic communities of Northern New Jersey.</div> NJMS - Anesthesiology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7432 25FA0693 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280046 2026-08-26T14:25:12-04:00 2026-08-26T14:25:12-04:00 Laboratory/Technical Assistant (Semenova Lab) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a seasonal Laboratory/Technical Assistant (Semenova Lab) for the Waksman Institute.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Assists with experiments investigating RNA-targeting type VI CRISPR-Cas systems.</li><li>Performs molecular cloning and plasmid analysis.</li><li>Conducts bacterial cell transformations and growth experiments.</li><li>Prepares RNA samples for RNA sequencing and downstream analyses.</li><li>Supports overall laboratory operations, including supply and equipment ordering.</li></ul> Waksman Institute of Microbiol New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 6726 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278054 2026-06-30T16:56:11-04:00 2026-06-30T16:56:12-04:00 Open Rank Associate Professor/Professor in Fluid Biomarkers <div>Under the direction of the <strong>Herbert and Jacqueline Krieger Klein Alzheimer’s Research Center </strong>at the Brain Health Institute (BHI), we seek a faculty level expert in fluid biomarkers for a tenure-track position at the Associate or Full Professor level at BHI, and Robert Wood Johnson Medical School (RWJMS) within <a href=\"https://academichealth.rutgers.edu/\"><strong>Rutgers Health</strong></a>. We seek a faculty member who is experienced in the identification, validation, and utilization of fluid biomarkers in the diagnosis, prognosis, and treatment of Alzheimer’s disease (AD) and AD related disorders (ADRD). The successful candidate will work as part of a multi-disciplinary team including neurologists, neuropsychologists, neuroimaging experts and neuropathologists. The AD center will develop a research cohort of individuals at high risk for dementia. This cohort will be extensively phenotyped for clinical, cognitive, genetic, neuroimaging, behavioral, digital and blood biomarker measures. In addition to scientific leadership, responsibilities will also include mentorship of young investigators. Applicants must have experience in conducting large-scale longitudinal fluid biomarker studies, and an interest in studying the earliest stages of AD. The successful candidate will be responsible for leading and conducting cutting-edge research in fluid biomarkers associated with ADRD.</div><div>Qualifying tenure-track applicants must have an established scholarly record demonstrating ability to develop and lead a program of independent, NIH (or other extramurally) funded research. Successful applicant(s) will serve as a core member(s) within the Herbert and Jacqueline Krieger Klein Alzheimer’s Center at BHI, with a primary appointment in one of the relevant departments at RWJMS, including Psychiatry, Neurology and Neurosurgery. The Herbert and Jacqueline Krieger Klein Alzheimer’s Center is a new center within BHI at Rutgers University with the mission of establishing an interdisciplinary, integrated program to provide comprehensive research focused on prevention and treatment of ADRD. This center is the first of its kind in New Jersey, and the successful applicant will be integral to its development. Ideal candidates will bring vision and experience in modern aging and memory research and enthusiasm for team science and collaboration.</div><div><br></div><div>Applicants representing diverse backgrounds of all sorts are highly encouraged to apply. Rutgers University is committed to diversity, equity and inclusion. The AD research center is actively working to ensure that our faculty composition reflects diversity. We especially welcome applications from backgrounds underrepresented in STEM (including women, Black, Latinx, Indigenous and LGBTQ+ scientists).<br><br></div><div>To become a part of our vibrant community applicants should submit a CV and a brief statement of research accomplishments and plans to Dr. Michal Beeri at <a href=\"mailto:mbeeri@ifh.rutgers.edu\"><strong>mbeeri@ifh.rutgers.edu</strong></a> and copy to <a href=\"mailto:bhi@bhi.rutgers.edu\"><strong>bhi@bhi.rutgers.edu</strong></a></div> Brain Health Institute RBHS Chancellor-L2 Brain Health Institute-L3 8146 25FA0019 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266390 2026-01-04T21:31:11-05:00 2026-01-04T21:31:12-05:00 Postdoctoral Associate <div>A Postdoctoral Associate position is available at the Animal Sciences Department in the laboratory of Dr. Igor Shmarakov. Candidate must have a Ph.D. degree in an area relevant to biochemistry, cell biology, or physiology. The ideal candidate will have strong communication skills, a publication record consistent with career level, and an interest in understanding the molecular basis of retinoid metabolism and signaling. Experience in animal models of lung injury, lung cell isolation, lung organoid cultures, immunofluorescent staining of tissues and cells, gene expression analysis by qRT-PCR and immunoblot, lipid extraction and analysis using HPLC, analysis of datasets generated by bulk or single-cell RNA sequencing. Salary will be commensurate with NIH and Rutgers guidelines. The position is based in the Shmarakov laboratory, an interdisciplinary and energetic research group housed on the Cook campus of Rutgers University in New Brunswick, NJ. As a postdoctoral associate, the candidate would have abundant opportunities to interact with members of the vibrant community with a research focus on lipid metabolism and signaling, endocrinology, respiratory toxicology, and lung injury within Rutgers University and the Department of Animal Sciences. The campus is also in close proximity to the cultural and scientific offerings of both NYC and Philadelphia.</div> Animal Science New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 7134 24FA1004 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280185 2026-08-31T10:45:29-04:00 2026-08-31T10:45:30-04:00 Forensic Mental Health Clinician UCHC ADTC <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care (UCHC) is seeking a Forensic Mental Health Clinician for Adult Diagnostic Treatment Center, located in Avenel, NJ. Reporting to the Clinician Supervisor, the Forensic Mental Health Clinician completes specialized psychological testing and assessment of clinical needs of adult inmates sentenced to the Department of Corrections.<br><br>Among the key duties for this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Arrives at DSM IV diagnoses with precision and accuracy through psychological testing and evaluation sessions.</li><li>Provides crisis intervention, individual and group psychotherapy and psycho-education programming as clinically indicated to assigned inmates.</li><li>Involves inmates and Department of Corrections staff in developing achievable and understandable psychosocial treatment plans.</li><li>Advocates for appropriate resources for inmates based on assessed needs.</li><li>Manages caseload demands effectively while considering both qualities of care and the security needs of the Department of Corrections.</li><li>Assumes overall case management responsibilities for assigned inmates including coordination of treatment and liaison with community agencies; maintains appropriate inmate records.</li><li>Demonstrates competency in psychological testing and in recognizing the unique needs and behaviors of adult inmates and seniors</li></ul> UCHC Adult Diagnosis & Treatme RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7651 Avenel NJ 26ST0355 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278623 2026-07-10T12:51:59-04:00 2026-07-10T12:51:59-04:00 Staff Nurse PT Eves UCHC NJSP (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Part Time Staff Nurse for the New Jersey State Prison located in Trenton, New Jersey.<br><br>The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus for inmates in the New Jersey Department of Corrections.<br><br>Duties include:<br>* Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the resident-patient including adolescents (13-17 years), adults (18 to 64 years) and their family within the framework established by the correctional system.<br>* Performs assessments of resident-patient in a variety of settings such as initial intake area, health care unit for sick call, emergency situations in housing, chronic care clinics and infirmary.<br>* Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br>* Identifies inmate-centered goals and nursing objectives and implements prescribed interventions and solutions for the identified problems.<br>* Plans nursing care by identification of resident-patient needs based on assessments. Makes appropriate, timely referrals and initiates appropriate nursing care based on institutional policies and procedures.<br>* As team leader or charge nurse, delegates duties to other health care team members based on their skill, knowledge and experience and guides the provision of care by others.</div> UCHC New Jersey State Prison A RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7683 Trenton NJ 26ST0878 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/269107 2026-02-12T10:22:27-05:00 2026-02-12T10:22:27-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor/Professor <div><strong>Pediatric Pulmonary Medicine Faculty</strong></div><div>The Department of Pediatrics, Rutgers-Robert Wood Johnson Medical School, Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences is seeking a candidate for a faculty position in the Division of Pulmonary Medicine and Cystic Fibrosis Center. The division has a comprehensive Cystic Fibrosis Center (pediatric and adult), a comprehensive sleep disorders program, technology dependent center, aero digestive, asthma and general pulmonary clinics. The position will have both clinical and academic responsibilities. In support of our academic endeavors, we have a state-of-the-art Pediatric Clinical Research Center, we have an active CFF TDN Center and Rutgers RBHS has a Clinical and Translational Science Award. The candidate will be expected to provide ambulatory and inpatient care including bronchoscopies. Responsibilities include developing a strong clinical and teaching base for medical students, residents and fellows. Candidates will be expected to participate in research projects and start up grant funding is available for qualified applicants. Candidates must be a graduate of an accredited medical school program including formal specialty training in Pediatric Pulmonology. Candidates must be board certified in Pediatrics with board eligibility in pulmonary medicine or Board certified in Pediatric Pulmonology. Training and Board certification in Sleep medicine is an asset.</div><div>The inpatient clinical services of the division of pediatric pulmonary medicine are conducted at the Bristol-Myers Squibb Children’s Hospital (BMSCH) of the Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital in New Brunswick, NJ. This is a 105-bed acute care hospital located on the only pediatric academic health campus in the state of New Jersey. The BMSCH is ranked as one of America’s Best Hospitals by U.S. News and World Report. Outpatient services are provided in New Brunswick and East Brunswick.<br><br></div><div>The Department of Pediatrics has a full complement of pediatric medical and surgical subspecialists. The Child Health Institute of New Jersey houses our research faculty. The Department of Pediatrics includes physicians and basic scientists who conduct collaborative research with an emphasis on mechanisms of disease, novel therapies, epidemiology and/or outcomes research in the areas of relevance to childhood diseases. The Department provides a collaborative setting for the study of basic mechanisms of disease and outcomes research that would provide new insights into the treatment of childhood diseases. The Robert Wood Johnson School of Medicine is consistently ranked as one of the highly NIH-funded academic universities and Rutgers is a member of the Association of American Universities comprising the top comprehensive research universities in North America. Adjacent to the Children’s hospital is the PSE&amp;G Children’s Specialized Hospital which is one of the country’s largest inpatient acute rehabilitation hospitals for children. Across the street is the Rutgers Cancer Institute of New Jersey – the only NCI designated center in the state of New Jersey as well as the Ronald MacDonald House. As the state’s premiere institution, located in central Jersey, there are many opportunities to collaborate across campuses with all the health professional schools and biomedical science schools at the Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences.<br><br><br><br></div><div>If interested, please send current CV to:<br><br></div><div>M. Douglas Baker, MD</div><div>Professor of Pediatrics</div><div>Executive Vice Chair</div><div>Department of Pediatrics, RWJMS</div><div><a href=\"mailto:mb1913@rwjms.rutgers.edu\"><strong>mb1913@rwjms.rutgers.edu</strong></a></div><div>Office: 732.235.7991</div><div><a href=\"mailto:mb1913@rwjms.rutgers.edu\"><strong>mb1913@rwjms.rutgers.edu</strong></a></div> RWJ - Pediatrics Pulmonary RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7811 26FA0123 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280423 2026-09-03T16:09:10-04:00 2026-09-03T16:09:11-04:00 Assistant / Associate Professor Position in Finance <div>The Finance and Economics Department of the Rutgers Business School at Newark and New Brunswick, Rutgers University, is seeking a full-time faculty member at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor (without tenure), subject to funding availability. Candidate must already have a Ph.D. in finance or economics, should have a track record of publications in top-tier finance and economics journals, and have demonstrated effective teaching at the university level.<br><br>The successful candidate will have scholarly activities in either empirical asset pricing or corporate finance with strong econometric skills. The successful candidate is expected to teach in both the undergraduate and graduate programs of the Department, especially courses such as Corporate Finance, Investment Analysis, Asset Pricing, Derivatives, Analysis of Fixed Income and Econometrics.<br><br>Posting will be open until filled.</div> Finance & Economics Newark Chancellor-L2 Rutgers Business School-L3 6935 26FA0699 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279352 2026-08-06T11:10:28-04:00 2026-08-06T11:10:29-04:00 Custodian <div>Rutgers University- Newark (RU-N), an urban public research university and anchor institution, located in Newark, New Jersey, a city of promise is seeking a Custodian. Under the direction of the Area Operations Manager and or Group Leader the individual assigned to this work area is responsible for performing all custodial duties necessary to maintain the area in a clean and habitable condition.<br><br>This position is responsible for and not limited to the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Cleans, dusts, strips, scrubs, waxes, and buff floors, rooms, toilets, offices, and all interiors of buildings; replenishes linen inventory.</li><li>Maintains perimeter of outside buildings, i.e. policing grounds removing trash, leaves etc. Inspects the interior and exterior of buildings for custodial and general physical security, checks lighting, and replaces light bulbs as needed.</li><li>Detects faulty operation of custodial equipment and building systems and reports questionable conditions to supervisor.</li></ul> Housing Newark Newark Chancellor-L2 Campus Operations-L3 7220 Newark NJ 26ST1591 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275992 2026-05-28T12:33:32-04:00 2026-05-28T12:33:33-04:00 Lecturers (Adjunct Faculty) for the Undergraduate Program in Information Technology and Informatics (Fall 2026) <div>The Department of Library and Information Science seeks part-time lecturers for its undergraduate program in Information Technology and Informatics. Please see the description of our program at https://comminfo.rutgers.edu/academics/undergraduate/information-technology-and-informatics-major and the list of courses we offer at https://comminfo.rutgers.edu/academics/courses?courses=&amp;program=27. Within your cover letter, please let us know which courses in our program you feel most prepared to teach. Please submit a cover letter, resume/curriculum vitae, and names and contact information for at least three references. You may also upload any evidence of your teaching experience such as sample syllabi or course materials, results of student instructional ratings, or published work.<br><br>We welcome applicants with backgrounds in any area of our curriculum, and are especially interested in professionals with interests and abilities to teach in following areas:<br><br>· Information assurance and cybersecurity<br><br>· Web design and development, especially full-stack development and front-end Javascript frameworks.<br><br>· Programming fundamentals, data management, and analytics with Python.</div> Library & Information Science New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School  Communicatn & Info Sci-L3 7090 26FA0373 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/273256 2026-04-20T09:08:59-04:00 2026-04-20T09:08:59-04:00 CoAd Non-Teaching <div>The candidate will serve as the lead architect in the creation of sophisticated, data-driven instructional units that translate New Jersey's complex regional weather and climate patterns into accessible middle and high school curricula. By integrating localized datasets, she will develop comprehensive units that explore the state's hydrological landscape, specifically focusing on the critical environmental and socio-economic variables associated with drought cycles and flood mitigation. These materials will be rigorously aligned with Next Generation Science Standards (NGSS), ensuring they provide immediate value to educators seeking high-quality, state-specific resources. To ensure pedagogical excellence, she will manage a full-cycle development process-moving from initial construction through active classroom piloting and evidence-based refinement. This iterative approach incorporates direct feedback from stakeholders to guarantee that the final products are both classroom-practical and student-centric. Ultimately, Dr. Holzer will oversee the digital dissemination of these resources via The Office of the New Jersey State Climatologist website, acting as a key advocate for New Jersey's climate literacy by providing schools statewide with open-access, professional-grade tools for environmental education.</div> Environmental Science New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 7137 26FA0365 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/265491 2025-12-18T11:16:32-05:00 2025-12-18T11:16:33-05:00 RBS - Part Time Instructor (Non-Credit) - 2026 <div>The Rutgers Business School is seeking part-time instructors to teach for its non-credit programs and centers. We are looking for qualified instructors that can contribute to our school's mission, connect the classroom and the industry, and provide a positive learning experience.<br><br>Successful candidates will instruct/co-instruct on a variety of topics, including, but not limited to: accounting, accounting information systems, financial accounting, government accounting, taxation, administrative studies, finance, economics, real estate, marketing, management, management science and information systems, operational management, strategic leadership, supply chain, and much more.<br><br>Candidates will be responsible for the following:</div><ul><li>Instructing/Co-instructing for non-credit courses and workshops</li><li>Preparing course materials (e.g., syllabi, presentation, reading materials, documents, etc.)</li><li>Provide constructive feedback and advisement to participants</li><li>Practice innovative educational methodology and pedagogy</li><li>Generating necessary final reports for program directors</li></ul><div><br>Some positions may be grant funded.</div> Human Resources Newark Newark Chancellor-L2 Rutgers Business School-L3 6942 25FA1258 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279640 2026-08-17T11:56:58-04:00 2026-08-17T11:56:58-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Postdoctoral Associate within Radiation Oncology/Cancer Biology at the Rutgers Cancer Institute.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Postdoctoral Associate position is to conduct independent laboratory research under the direction of the principal investigator. Incumbent is expected to carry out various experimental and bioinformatics studies in the area of the lab. The focus of the Lab is in the area of differential protein expression in the human vascular endothelium, associated with normal or diseased tissues, offers the potential for developing novel diagnostic, imaging, and therapeutic strategies. Our program uses peptide- and antibody-based combinatorial library selection to discover, validate, and exploit the vascular biochemical diversity of endothelial cell surfaces towards identifying new vascular targeted pharmacologics for clinical translation.&nbsp;</div><div><br>Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Performs independent research relevant to the interest and field of differential protein expression in the human vascular endothelium, associated with normal or diseased tissues, offers the potential for developing novel diagnostic, imaging, and therapeutic strategies.&nbsp;</li><li>Publishes reports of key findings in a timely manner.&nbsp;</li><li>Keeps detailed records of procedures and experiments. Compiles and presents statistical data with appropriate conclusions and recommendations pertinent to the research.&nbsp;</li><li>Prepares grant proposals based on the research conducted and maintains an up to date understanding of the relevant literature.&nbsp;</li><li>Gives oral presentations of the research at lab meetings and conferences.&nbsp;</li><li>Assists with the instructing and training of students, fellows, technicians, and laboratory assistants as required.&nbsp;</li><li>Publishes scientific research papers/articles using effective oral and written communication skills.</li></ul> CINJ - RadOnc Offsite Newark RBHS Chancellor-L2 Cancer Institute of New Jersey-L3 8358 Newark NJ 26ST1621 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279945 2026-08-25T12:23:22-04:00 2026-08-25T12:23:22-04:00 Graduate Assistant (3) Positions <div>Rutgers School of Health Professions (SHP) is seeking a Graduate Assistant to work in the Department of Psychiatric Rehabilitation &amp; Counseling Professions.<br><br>The graduate assistant is an individual engaged in doctoral studies within the department who contributes to both its teaching and research missions under the supervision of department faculty members. The main responsibilities include assisting with teaching and research activities.<br><br>To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed are representative of the knowledge, skill and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Ability to read, write, speak, understand and communicate in English sufficiently to perform the duties of the position.</div><div><br>Essential duties and responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Directly responsible for providing support to faculty mentor.</li><li>Fulfills course work and research for their PhD at RBHS-SHP, research, publication and dissemination efforts as determined by chairperson or faculty mentor.</li><li>Assists associate dean in providing faculty development support activities as directed.</li><li>Teaches course and study sections and assists with teaching as assigned including course preparation, delivering lessons, and student evaluation.</li><li>Prepares and teaches entire undergraduate and graduate courses as assigned in areas of expertise with the guidance of a teaching mentor.</li><li>Assists faculty members in their preparation, teaching, and evaluation of students in their courses.</li><li>Engages in research activities under the direction of a faculty mentor including but not limited to data entry, analysis, data collection and storage, obtaining consents, and study activities.</li><li>Other responsibilities may include minor administrative assistance, student advisement, presentations at state or national meetings</li></ul> SHP - Psychiatric Rehabilitati RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Health Professions-L3 7581 Piscataway NJ 26ST1651 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277761 2026-06-25T11:04:01-04:00 2026-06-25T11:04:02-04:00 Staff Nurse PT Days UCHC NSP (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Part Time Staff Nurse for the Northern State Prison located in Newark, NJ<br><br>The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus for inmates in the New Jersey Department of Corrections.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br>* Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the resident-patient including adolescents (13-17 years), adults (18 to 64 years) and their family within the framework established by the correctional system.<br>* Performs assessments of resident-patient in a variety of settings such as initial intake area, health care unit for sick call, emergency situations in housing, chronic care clinics and infirmary.<br>* Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br>* Identifies inmate-centered goals and nursing objectives and implements prescribed interventions and solutions for the identified problems.<br>* Plans nursing care by identification of resident-patient needs based on assessments. Makes appropriate, timely referrals and initiates appropriate nursing care based on institutional policies and procedures.<br>* As team leader or charge nurse, delegates duties to other health care team members based on their skill, knowledge and experience and guides the provision of care by others</div> UCHC Northern State Prison Phy_DUP RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7679 Newark NJ 26ST0675 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274973 2026-05-13T14:30:14-04:00 2026-05-13T14:30:15-04:00 Food Services Worker - Casual <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Food Service Worker – Casual for the Dining Services.<br><br>Among the key duties of the position are the following:</div><ul><li>Performs general utility work in the various dining facilities at Rutgers University, including food prep, service and maintenance.</li></ul> Dining Services New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Student Affairs - New Brunswic-L3 8110 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266254 2025-12-31T09:41:16-05:00 2025-12-31T09:41:17-05:00 Postdoctoral Associate - M-EASE project <div>The Modeling Equitable and Accessible Spaces for Everyone (M-EASE) project in the Department of Psychology and Center for Cognitive Science is seeking a post-doctoral associate for an NSF-funded project on the social, environmental and linguistic factors that affect human wayfinding. Working with the PI and co-PIs in computer science, psychology, applied math and architecture/design, the postdoctoral fellow will be intimately involved in all aspects of the research, including the conceptualization, design, performance, analysis, and modeling of the results of VR experiments, and the preparation of manuscripts for publication. A doctoral degree in cognitive psychology, cognitive science, computer science/engineering, language sciences or a related field is required, as well as strong quantitative and programming skills. Experience with virtual reality development, machine learning, or advanced data analyses and modeling are highly desirable.</div> Psychology New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 8128 25FA0682 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280127 2026-08-28T15:25:20-04:00 2026-08-28T15:25:21-04:00 Mental Health Specialist III <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Mental Health Specialist III within Community Based Services – Residential at Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Mental Health Specialist III is to ensure the safety of residents and assist them in carrying out activities of daily living.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Assumes individual service coordination responsibilities for individuals served.</li><li>Documents events occurring on shift as per supervisory directive.</li><li>Demonstrates awareness of relevant organization and residential policies, procedures and requirements.</li><li>Demonstrates respect to supervisory feedback to enhance performance skills.</li><li>Effectively contributes to and supports an environment that enhances the positive self-image of consumer/resident and preserves their human dignity.</li><li>Completes Employee Health Update as required.</li></ul> UBHC - Community-Based Service RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8011 Collingswood NJ 26ST1677 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278492 2026-07-09T11:03:12-04:00 2026-07-09T11:03:13-04:00 Community Coordinator <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Community Coordinator for the Outpatient in Monmouth Junction within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Community Coordinator is to serve as a trusted liaison between the community and CCBHC, promoting access to health and social services, improving health outcomes, and supporting individuals and families in navigating complex systems of care. The Community Coordinator provides culturally responsive outreach, education, care coordination, and advocacy to reduce barriers to services and advance health equity. The Community Coordinator plays a critical role in addressing social determinants of health, supporting transitions of care, promoting recovery-oriented practices, and ensuring continuity of services consistent with person-centered treatment planning.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Conducts community outreach to identify individuals in need of services.</li><li>Builds trusting relationships with individuals served, families, and community partners.</li><li>Provides education on health topics, prevention strategies, and available resources.</li><li>Participates in community events, health fairs, and stakeholder meetings.</li><li>Connects individuals and families to healthcare, public health programs, and social services.</li><li>Promotes healthcare linkage by assisting with appointment scheduling.</li><li>Assists to transport and accompany clients to healthcare, public health programs, and social service-related appointments as deemed necessary to ensure successful engagement and positive outcomes.</li><li>Supports individuals served by ensuring they understand their treatment plans and rights.</li><li>Shares community insights to improve program effectiveness.</li><li>Advocates on behalf of individuals served to reduce systemic barriers.</li></ul> UBHC - Outpatient Monmouth Jun RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8023 Monmouth Junction NJ 26ST0811 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279570 2026-08-13T10:59:56-04:00 2026-08-13T10:59:57-04:00 Mental Health Clinician II <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Mental Health Clinician II in the Outpatient Services within Rutgers University Behavioral Healthcare.<br><br>Under direction, the Mental Health Clinician II serves as the senior mental health practitioner who provides lead functions for the OCD IOP program, to include screening of intakes and referrals, care coordination, ensuring completion of program specific documentation and/or comprehensive assessment and therapeutic intervention for the psychological and social needs of adult individuals served (18 and over), including development of treatment plans, conducting individual, group, and family therapy, and providing case management. Assists with the provision of clinical supervision to licensing candidates as assigned.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Contributes to and supports goals and objectives of the Unit and UBHC.</li><li>Demonstrates knowledge of University Behavioral Health Care’s vision, mission and values as they relate to service provision, daily activities, decisions and quality improvement priorities and consistently behaves in accordance with established policies and procedures as observed by supervisor.</li><li>Effectively contributes to and supports an environment that enhances the positive self-image of individuals served and their families and preserves their human dignity, right to fair and equitable treatment, self-determination, individuality, privacy and civil rights as observed by supervisor and with minimal complaints and positive feedback from peers, patients and their families.</li><li>Actively and enthusiastically participates in ensuring the smooth functioning and operation of the program, and participates in UBHC-wide meetings, performance improvement activities, committees and task forces as assigned and as observed by supervisor and program administration.</li><li>Consistently ensures that individuals served, families and system partners understand and adhere to procedures while at UBHC.</li></ul> UBHC - Edison RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8002 Edison NJ 25ST2349 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279821 2026-08-21T12:25:10-04:00 2026-08-21T12:25:11-04:00 Statewide Associate Medical Director UCHC Administration <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Statewide Medical Director located in Trenton, NJ . The Associate Statewide Medical Director, under the direction of the Statewide Medical Director, is responsible for providing medical services to inmates of the Department of Corrections, which are consistent with community standards of care.</div><div>Provides overall clinical and teaching responsibilities for University Correctional HealthCare (UCHC) and directly supervises the UCHC Medical Providers. Oversees the provision of clinical service at all the sites. Serves as a liaison for clinical matters with medical providers outside the system and is available to provide on-call services and on-site clinical services as may be indicated.</div><div>Demonstrates competency in recognizing the unique needs of all inmates/residents, ages 18-65+, and in applying relevant<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Assists the Medical Director in all aspects of the delivery of medical services to ensure access to care andvclinical quality is performed at or above established thresholds.</li><li>Communicates directly with admitting and attending physicians to determine the earliest time when an inmate admitted to the hospital can be transferred to the New Jersey Department of Corrections (NJDOC) preferred Hospital and/or return to an infirmary setting within NJDOC.</li><li>Provides direct supervision and direction to Supervising Physicians, to include evaluation, annual performance review, and disciplinary review under the supervision of the Medical Director.</li><li>Provides clinical leadership that includes medical evaluations, treatment planning, and treatmentto inmates within University Correctional Health Care (UCHC</li></ul><div><br></div> UCHC Administration RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7673 Trenton NJ 26ST1129 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277581 2026-06-23T11:37:45-04:00 2026-06-23T11:37:46-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate for the Center for Climate, Health and Healthcare (CCHH) <div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Postdoctoral Associate for the Center for Climate, Health and Healthcare (CCHH) within the Institute for Health, Health Care Policy and Aging Research (IFH). The CCHH Postdoctoral Associate position will work with an established Principal Investigator with a track record of publications and supportive mentorship. The PI and applicant will work together to achieve research and career goals in a supportive environment. The position provides opportunities to work on various quantitative or qualitative research and academic projects focused on climate and health outcomes, health service use and access across the life span, community health, health promotion/prevention/equity, healthcare sustainability/resilience, or other topic areas related to the mission of the Center based on the available funding sources. Projects include examining multi-level drivers of health and other exposures of interest and disparities therein. The postdoctoral research scientist will have the opportunity to explore additional research questions for their career development.<br><br></div><div>The Postdoctoral Associate may analyze and interpret data on health outcomes, treatment need, and/or utilization, as well as health and social drivers, from a variety of administrative and population data sources. They will contribute to the development of peer-reviewed manuscripts, scientific presentations, and grants. They will work collaboratively in teams and engage in other activities as needed. There will also be opportunities to pursue independent research and career development (e.g., grant writing training) in health services and climate-related studies.</div> Institute for Health, Health C RBHS Chancellor-L2 Institute for Health, Health C-L3 8086 26FA0629 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274385 2026-05-06T11:10:42-04:00 2026-05-06T11:10:42-04:00 Postdoctoral Research Associate - Traffic Engineering <div>The Center for Advanced Infrastructure and Transportation (CAIT) within the School of Engineering at Rutgers University, is seeming a Postdoctoral Associate in Traffic Engineering, specializing in Intelligent Transportation Systems (ITS). This is a pivotal role requiring a blend of technical expertise, project management, and collaboration skills. The successful candidate will contribute significantly to the development, deployment, maintenance, and enhancement of ITS projects in the DataCity Smart Mobility Testing Ground program.</div> Advanced Infrastructure Center New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Engineering-L3 6709 26FA0445 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266169 2025-12-31T09:32:28-05:00 2025-12-31T09:32:29-05:00 Post Doctoral Associate (Zander Lab) <div>The Zander laboratory at the Waksman Institute of Microbiology looks for an individual that investigates stimulus-induced 3D epigenome reprogramming in crop and medicinal plant species. Furthermore, the individual will develop cistrome mapping tools for various plant species. Research is carried out in the Zander laboratory, that conducts molecular, genetic and (epi)genomic research to better understand the role of transcription factors and the epigenome dynamics. The individual is needed to conduct research on questions related to transcription factor DNA-driven 3D epigenome dynamics in immune responses. By using genetic, genomic and biochemical methods, the individual will identify/analyze/characterize molecular determinants for chromatin looping in plants. The individual will report directly to the laboratory Principle Investigator (PI).</div> Waksman Institute of Microbiol New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 6726 25FA0903 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280076 2026-08-27T11:19:57-04:00 2026-08-27T11:19:58-04:00 Mental Health Specialist II UBHC <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Mental Health Specialist II for the Acute Psychiatric Services (APS) Department within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Mental Health Specialist II is to provide services which support the delivery of clinical services in the Unit.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Takes primary responsibility for answering telephone calls from consumers.</li><li>Conducts initial triage of consumers and families when they arrive onsite five (5) minutes after arrival and provides immediate report to the Program Coordinator.</li><li>Assists Public Safety in their search for consumers and belongings when they are admitted to the Extended Care Evaluation Bed (ECEB) area.</li><li>Provides direct care for individuals in the ECEB.</li><li>Maintains appropriate client records in a timely manner as mandated by Center policy.</li><li>Assumes responsibility for managing the transfer of consumers into and out of the Unit.</li><li>Assists consumers and/or families in the completion of registration paperwork as required.</li><li>Assists the Program Coordinator in transporting the Unit vehicles for servicing as needed.</li></ul> UBHC - Emergency Screening Psy RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8029 Piscataway NJ 26ST1643 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278355 2026-07-07T14:27:06-04:00 2026-07-07T14:27:07-04:00 Habilitation Counselor - Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Habilitation Counselor for Essex Children’s Mobile Response and Stabilization Services at Rutgers, University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Habilitation Counselor is to provide assessments for the Children’s Mobile Response and Stabilization Services (CMRSS) program in designated catchment area that meet quality and quantity standards within UBHC and the Children’s System of Care (CSoC). Performs functions in support of the UBHC mission providing streamlined, prompt, and “consumer friendly” crisis response services. Receives telephone requests for service, undertakes crisis assessment of the service needs of the client or customer, responds by outreach to the family, assesses the youth and family strengths and current crisis situation, makes appropriate referrals for time-limited stabilization services, monitors effectiveness of services and makes linkages for aftercare. Demonstrates competency in recognizing the unique needs and applying relevant crisis stabilization approaches for children and adolescent and their families.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Responds to families telephone referrals, inquiries, and other contacts with professionals, outside agencies and other parties in a professional and cordial manner, per caller feedback.</li><li>Demonstrates proficiency in utilizing computer systems to accurately retrieve and input information in accordance with established protocols.</li><li>Provides face to face interventions in the community including, but not limited to, families’ homes, schools, group homes, foster homes, shelters, and the detention center.</li><li>Assists families in effectively managing crisis/dangerous situations and can formulate a crisis/safety plan.</li><li>Acquires familiarity with agencies in the designated catchment area that provides services to children, adolescents and their families that can provide crisis stabilization services and providing ongoing support/resources for the family.</li><li>Develops community based, time-limited, crisis stabilization resources within designated catchment area specific to children with emotional or behavioral disturbances and their families’ needs and requests to maximize service transitions.</li><li>Assists in the development of a continuum of crisis stabilization providers in designated catchment area.</li></ul> UBHC - Emergency Screening New RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8052 Newark NJ 26ST0509 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267059 2026-01-09T13:12:59-05:00 2026-01-09T13:12:59-05:00 Data Collector <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Data Collector for the National Institute for Early Education Research (NIEER). Responsibilities for this position will include scheduling appointments with schools, administering the assessments, reporting the number of completed assessments on a weekly basis to the Project Coordinator(s), returning completed assessments to NIEER and data entry and cleaning.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Completes reliability requirements for the assessments and classroom observations required for the specific project assigned.</li><li>Communicates with assigned child care programs, preschools, or schools to schedule data collection dates.</li><li>Maintains active communication with programs as necessary to facilitate data collection.</li><li>Administers assessments or observations in designated classrooms, as trained.</li><li>Monitors participation completion of study daily and follow-up surveys.</li><li>Administers semi-structured interviews to teachers, as needed.</li><li>Provides daily reports on completed work.</li><li>Reports the number of completed assessments to the Project Coordinator(s) and return completed assessments to NIEER on a weekly basis.</li><li>Ensures the accuracy, integrity, and confidentiality of data and adherence to study protocols.</li><li>Enters data as trained by coordinators and assist in data cleaning and/or entering.</li><li>Participates in the recruitment, screening, and scheduling of participants for study visits.</li><li>Supports coordinators in project management tasks related to data collection.</li><li>Handles special projects assigned based on demonstrated knowledge and job skills.</li></ul> NIEER New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Graduate School of Education-L3 6818 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280232 2026-08-31T14:23:44-04:00 2026-08-31T14:23:45-04:00 Technician I FT Eves UCHC ADTC <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Full Time UCHC Technician I for the Adult Diagnostic Treatment Center located in Avenel, NJ. The UCHC Technician I participates as a member of the clinical and administrative medical team at the Prison.<br><br>Among the duties for this position are:<br><br><br></div><ul><li>Takes vital signs, height and weight and documents in electronic medical records (EMR).</li><li>Assists the physician/associate practitioner with procedures, including preparing the inmate for the examination.</li><li>Obtains specimen collection and handling, including, but not limited to, drawing blood.</li><li>Assists with the cleaning, sterilization and securing of equipment within the Health Service Unit.</li><li>Maintains or assists in maintaining the supply stock in the Health Service Unit by ordering in a timely and appropriate manner. Maintains the supply stock in the examination rooms.• Aggregates the orders of all medications and forwards to the pharmacy provider / local pharmacy.</li></ul><div>.</div> UCHC Adult Treatment Center Ph RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7674 Avenel NJ 26ST1696 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278806 2026-07-14T13:36:49-04:00 2026-07-14T13:36:50-04:00 Staff Nurse Mental Health PT Days UCHC NSP (Multiple Vacancies) <div>University Correctional Healthcare (UCHC) is seeking a Part Time Mental Health Staff Nurse (RN) for the Northern State Prison in Newark, New Jersey. The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus. Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment. Frequently functions guided by nursing protocols. Functions as a team leader as assigned. Demonstrates competency in assessment and identification of the psychological and physical health of adults (18 to 64 years), and geriatrics (65+) all population groups and their personal strengths. Identifies inmate-centered goals and nursing objectives and implements prescribed interventions and solutions for the identified problems.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the inmate-patient including adults (18 to 64 years), and geriatrics (65+) within the framework established by the correctional system.</li><li>Uses psychiatric standards of nursing practice and classification of mental disorders: to develop inmate treatment plans with specific goals and interventions delineating nursing actions unique to each inmate’s needs.</li><li>Implements nursing actions that promote, maintain or restore physical and mental health of all age groups.</li><li>Evaluates inmate responses in collaboration with multi-disciplinary care providers to ensure quality inmate care.</li><li>Performs additional duties that are directly related to the workings of the milieu and its safety, as demonstrated by documentation in specific paperwork and by supervisory observations.</li></ul> UCHC Northern State Prison Med RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7656 Newark NJ 26ST0765 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/270190 2026-03-04T10:13:35-05:00 2026-03-04T10:13:35-05:00 Postdoctoral Associate <div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey is seeking a Postdoctoral Associate in the Department of Biochemistry &amp; Microbiology within the School of Environmental and Biological Sciences. The Laboratory of Dr. Debashish Bhattacharya has an open Postdoctoral Associate position in the field of algal and seaweed multi-omics and metabolic engineering in support of multiple ongoing projects.<br><br>Under the direction of Dr. Bhattacharya the individual will be responsible for the independent conduct of a significant element of a larger research activity in algal and seaweed biotechnology, computational biology, and genetics aimed at developing platforms for generating valuable bioproducts from the brown seaweed <em>Sargassum</em> with a focus on bioprospecting using microbiome data. This Postdoctoral Associate will identify carbohydrate active enzymes to be used for downstream applications by collaborators and design and conduct highly specialized and technical research and aid graduate students with their research programs.<br><br>The Bhattacharya Lab at Rutgers University leverages many experimental approaches including multi-omics, physiology, live culture, and computational approaches to ask fundamental questions about algal and seaweed biology, adaptation, and conservation and algal plastid origin and evolution as well as algal extremophile biology. The candidate will have the opportunity to join a highly motivated and broadly trained laboratory that seeks to both generate basic knowledge and develop conservation tools.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Performs various research and technical operations independently or as assigned, relating to investigatory activities of a laboratory, followed by appropriate reports, recommendations and conclusions.</li><li>Assists and conducts independent research relevant to the interest and field of algal and seaweed multi-omics and biotechnological research with living and preserved samples.</li><li>Participates in the development of performance standards, selection of methodology and instrumentation and coordination of the analytical, biochemical, physiology, genetics, and instrumentation functions with the research areas to ensure conformance with the goals and objectives of the PI’s lab.</li><li>Conducts a continuous program of research and development regarding the analytical and instrumentation functions of the laboratory, constantly evaluating existing procedures where required to keep methodology and procedures current.</li><li>Contributes to the supervision of the work performed by graduate and undergraduate students and other postdoctoral fellows.</li></ul><div><br>This is a grant funded position, continuation of employment in this position is contingent upon adequate grant funds.</div> Biochemistry & Microbiology New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 7135 26FA0173 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280471 2026-09-04T14:37:22-04:00 2026-09-04T14:37:22-04:00 Mental Health Specialist II- Part Time- NJ Hopeline <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Mental Health Specialist II (Part Time) for 988 Lifeline Services within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>Performs functions in support of the Unit’s mission providing streamlined, prompt, and “customer friendly” services to clients of the 988 Lifeline Services. Receives telephone, chat and/or text requests for service, undertakes assessment of the service need of the client and responds by offering support and appropriate referrals or disposition. Demonstrates competency in recognizing the unique needs of clients and applying relevant assessment and support skills with regard to a wide range of issues.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Interacts with client in a therapeutic manner.</li><li>Participates in ensuring that all service requests are handled in an effective and “client friendly” manner.</li><li>Assesses service requests/referrals and responds in accordance with prescribed procedures.</li><li>Assesses client’s condition in order to make/authorize an appropriate disposition.</li><li>Assumes overall responsibilities for completion of all request and documentation for disposition.</li><li>Documents assessments, interventions, and interactions with clients in a timely manner and in accordance with established policies.</li></ul> UBHC - NJ Hopeline RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8707 Remote NJ 26ST1293 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279424 2026-08-07T13:58:06-04:00 2026-08-07T13:58:07-04:00 Mental Health Clinician II <div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Mental Health Clinician II in the 988 Lifeline Services - 988 Chat &amp; Text Backup of Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>Under direction, the Mental Health Clinician II serves as the senior mental health practitioner who provides lead functions for the program, to include screening of intakes and referrals, care coordination, ensuring completion of program specific documentation and/or comprehensive assessment and therapeutic intervention for the psychological and social needs of child and adolescent (ages 3-17 years) and/or adult individuals served (18 and over), including development of treatment plans, conducting individual, group, and family therapy, and providing case management. Assists with the provision of clinical supervision to licensing candidates as assigned.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Contributes to and supports goals and objectives of the Unit and UBHC.</li><li>Demonstrates knowledge of University Behavioral Health Care’s vision, mission and values as they relate to service provision, daily activities, decisions and quality improvement priorities and consistently behaves in accordance with established policies and procedures as observed by supervisor.</li><li>Effectively contributes to and supports an environment that enhances the positive self-image of individuals served and their families and preserves their human dignity, right to fair and equitable treatment, self-determination, individuality, privacy and civil rights as observed by supervisor and with minimal complaints and positive feedback from peers, patients and their families.</li><li>Actively and enthusiastically participates in ensuring the smooth functioning and operation of the program, and participates in UBHC-wide meetings, performance improvement activities, committees and task forces as assigned and as observed by supervisor and program administration.</li><li>Consistently ensures that individuals served, families and system partners understand and adhere to procedures while at UBHC.</li></ul> UBHC - BRTI Institute RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8044 Piscataway NJ 25ST2636 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/276577 2026-06-05T11:45:35-04:00 2026-06-05T11:45:36-04:00 Assistant Professor of Surgery <div>Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School (RWJMS) in New Brunswick, NJ is seeking a full-time Assistant Professor of Surgery. The successful candidate will join an established group of nationally known surgeons. Our current staff of 6 cardiac surgeons performs approximately 2000 cardiac surgical procedures annually. The position supports the work of primary surgeons, procurement coverage, and acute care needs. The appointee will participate in the full spectrum of a cardiac surgical practice. In addition, the appointee will have the opportunity to acquire skills in advanced techniques including minimally invasive valve surgery and valve repair; aortic surgery; transplantation and mechanical support; robotics; and catheter-based approaches to aortic disease and valvular repair/replacement. RWJMS is an international leader in minimally invasive valve surgery, transcatheter valvular procedures, mechanical support, and earned 3-STS stars for both CABG and AVR. Prior to the start of employment, qualified applicants must 1) have a medical doctorate or equivalent, 2) hold or be eligible for medical licensure in the State of New Jersey, and 3) have completed an accredited fellowship or equivalent training in CT Surgery. The candidate would be expected to meet requirements for an appointment as an Assistant Professor of Surgery in the Department of Surgery and will be compensated commensurately. This practice will be exclusively based at Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital (RWJUH). RWJUH is the primary teaching hospital for Rutgers RWJMS. RWJUH is the premier academic medical center in New Jersey, serving a catchment of more than 5 million people. Its Centers of Excellence include cardiovascular care from minimally invasive heart surgery to transplantation, cancer care, stroke care, neuroscience, orthopedics, and women and children's care, including The Bristol-Myers Squibb Children's Hospital (BMSCH), Rutgers Cancer Institute of New Jersey (CINJ), and a level 1 Trauma Center.</div> RWJ - Surgery Cardiac RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 8636 26FA0539 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274042 2026-04-30T11:35:44-04:00 2026-04-30T11:35:45-04:00 Course Developers/Non-teaching Coadjutant, CELG <div>Rutgers University-Camden, Center for Executive Leadership in Government (CELG), is seeking Course Developers for the for academic year 2026-2027. Programs are designed for training managers in non-profit, government, and public service organizations. The training provided includes professional certification and/or professional development for managers.<br>The position/s will collaborate with content experts and instructors preparing materials to be used in the creation of an online version; provide pedagogical support for new instructors building modules including public sector specific examples for cases and course framing content. Collaborates with other team members to develop project plans that ensure work is consistent with the mission and goals of CELG, and meets deliverables as projected. Completed work will meet the standards defined by CELG for each work product. Complete work will be delivered to the Associate Director, CELG for review and approval. Ownership of the final product will belong to Rutgers University and may not be produced or used without Rutgers approval.<br>The position/s will be responsible for non-credit course content development, course administration and content delivery, material development, revisions, updates, online materials and audio/visual/presentations for the following programs:<br>• Mini Master in Public Administration<br>• Public Leadership<br>• Strategic Communications<br>• Elevating Personal Leadership Skills<br>• Technology for Public Managers<br>• Human Resources and the Public Manager<br>• Grant Writing<br>• Other courses and seminars as needed</div> Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 8076 26FA0408 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/265920 2025-12-31T09:02:48-05:00 2025-12-31T09:02:48-05:00 Postdoctoral Instructor in Mathematics <div>Subject to availability of funding, the Mathematics Department expects to offer one or more postdoctoral research and instructor positions that will begin in fall of 2025. Most of these positions are expected to be three-year non-tenure track, non-renewable, Post-Doctoral positions with an annual teaching load of 3 single semesters courses. Candidates should have received a PhD and show outstanding promise of research in pure or applied mathematics as well as a capacity for effective teaching.</div><div>Applicants should complete the online form associated with this listing and submit a curriculum vitae. In addition, you should register as a job applicant at mathjobs.org and complete the application, with the requested supporting documents, for position PD25 under the Rutgers University-New Brunswick listing (<a href=\"https://nam02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.mathjobs.org%2Fjobs%2Flist%2F25895&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cmb1186%40math.rutgers.edu%7C720a3a5fa1974cee5c5408dd07f7818d%7Cb92d2b234d35447093ff69aca6632ffe%7C1%7C0%7C638675481794517894%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=RApwutTZlWocGvszWs8jCFrWe4YwxRiWuslDz0dhd0A%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/25895</strong></a>). Rutgers University is an exciting, large public state university with one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation.<br><br> Review of applications begins December 1, 2024 and continues until any potential openings are filled. Applications received after December 1, 2024 are still welcome, but may not receive full consideration.</div> Mathematics New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 8125 24FA1240 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279685 2026-08-18T14:28:56-04:00 2026-08-18T14:28:57-04:00 Temporary Research Assistant (Logistics) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Temporary Research Assistant in the Department of Medicine- Infectious Diseases within the New Jersey Medical School (NJMS).&nbsp;<br><br>Under the direction of the Director Research Operations, and the Programmer Analyst, the Temporary Research Assistant is responsible for overseeing and facilitating clinical supply logistics for the DOMC group.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>Works with international sites in shipment coordination, import/export documentation, quality assurance and quality control (QA/QC) activities during protocol conduct.</li><li>Works with investigators, and study coordinators in coordination and set-up of shipments for specific clinical, translational and basic science protocols.</li><li>Work with study coordinators to develop appropriate and detailed standard operating procedures, training manuals and other materials for shipment coordination and supply management in the clinic, field and laboratory.</li><li>Reviews shipping documents for accuracy and completion, from the field sites.</li><li>Maintains shipment tracking databases as per operating procedures and under guidance of database programmer and study coordinator(s).</li><li>Works with import companies to facilitate US Customs clearance and delivery to Rutgers laboratories and assist with or other study related tasks as needed and directed.&nbsp;</li></ul> NJMS - Medicine Infectious Dis RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7442 Newark NJ 26ST1626 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280011 2026-08-26T10:06:04-04:00 2026-08-26T10:06:05-04:00 Temporary Research Assistant (Junior Data Manager) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Temporary Research Assistant (Junior Data Manager) in the Department of&nbsp; Medicine- Infectious Diseases within the New Jersey Medical School (NJMS).<br><br>Under the direction of the Data Operations and Management Center (DOMC) Director and Program Manager, the Temporary Research Assistant (Junior Data Manager) is responsible for off-site study coordination and data management oversight of protocols positioned at international sites. The Junior Data Manager will provide study coordination of speciﬁc protocols and will develop case report forms consistent with clinical protocols and investigator input. The Junior Data Manager sets up SOPs for data collection sites to provide data capture and performs quality assurance audits to validate data in preparation for analysis by biostatisticians.<br><br>Among the key duties of the position are the following:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>Works with investigators and DOMC staff to develop REDCap case report forms (CRFs) consistent with the approved protocol to capture clinical and laboratory data.</li><li>Facilitates and coordinates orientation and trains volunteers/staff on instruments administration, data-gathering software, and data collection.</li><li>Maintains and manages research databases using SAS software. Works with statisticians in creating the appropriate databases from collected data for analyses.</li><li>Monitors data quality per standard operating procedures for each protocol with minimal supervision.</li><li>Coordinates QA/QC with international on-site staff and Rutgers Study Coordinators.&nbsp;</li></ul> NJMS - Medicine Infectious Dis RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7442 Newark NJ 26ST1660 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277782 2026-06-25T11:25:50-04:00 2026-06-25T11:25:51-04:00 Staff Nurse Mental Health FT Eves UCHC EMCFW <div>University Correctional Healthcare is seeking a Full Time UCHC Staff Nurse for Edna Mahan Correctional Facility, located in Clinton, NJ. The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus. Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br><br>Among the duties are:</div><ul><li>Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the inmate-patient including adults (18 to 64 years), and geriatrics (65+) within the framework established by the correctional system.</li><li>Utilizes effective communication skills by demonstrating respect, concern and courtesy in all interpersonal relationships.</li><li>Uses current knowledge to promote a safe environment for providing health care to inmate-patients.</li></ul> UCHC Edna Mahan Correction Med RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7659 Clinton NJ 26ST0965 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275543 2026-05-20T14:21:20-04:00 2026-05-20T14:21:21-04:00 Dining Services Student Worker (Kilmer's Market) <div>Join the Rutgers Dining team as a Dining Services Student Worker in one of our dining halls or retail operations across the New Brunswick and Piscataway campuses. Rutgers Dining Services strives to be the best in culinary excellence and as a Dining Services Worker you play a critical role in the customer experience. From assisting in the preparation and service of food, to maintaining the presentation of the dining halls, to assisting guests, we have a variety of roles and will find the right one for you!<br><br>Dining Service Workers earn a paycheck and more:</div><ol><li>Student employee meal privileges.</li><li>Flexible schedules (10/20 hours/week) that work around your classes and activities.</li><li>Convenient on-campus locations.</li><li>Opportunities to advance to leadership positions such as Captain, Meal Manager and Student Unit Manager.</li><li>Valuable work experience to add to your resume.</li><li>Learn important job skills including interpersonal communications, team dynamics, dependability and time management.</li><li>A fun and welcoming environment.</li></ol> Kilmer's Market New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Student Affairs - New Brunswic-L3 6682 Piscataway NJ 26ST1107 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266331 2025-12-31T09:51:08-05:00 2025-12-31T09:51:08-05:00 Postdoctoral Associate <div>The postdoc will carry out cutting-edge neuroscience research in a vibrant research environment, performing experiments and data analysis, authoring publications and grant proposals, training personnel, and contributing to the positive atmosphere of the Margolis laboratory in the Department of Cell Biology and Neuroscience.</div> DLS Cell Biology & Neuroscienc New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 7060 25FA0749 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280155 2026-08-31T08:42:32-04:00 2026-08-31T08:42:32-04: