ntion organizations.</li><li>Serves as a community resource person on unintentional poisoning injury and poison center services.</li><li>Develops and maintains relationships with community-based organizations, and represents the poison control center on coalitions, work groups, committee meetings, and special events.</li></ul> NJMS - Emergency Medicine NJPI RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7486 Newark NJ 26ST1667 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278138 2026-07-01T12:16:22-04:00 2026-07-01T12:16:30-04:00 Research Associate (Non-Tenure Track) <div>Rutgers University-Camden, School of Arts and Sciences, Department of Biology, invites applications for a Non-Tenure Track (NTT) Research Associate position. This is a research track faculty position for one-year, and is contingent upon continued funding availability.<br>The successful position will lead an research program focused on elucidating the mechanisms that drive mitochondrial dysfunction in neurodegeneration and aging, using cellular and animal models.<br>Beyond primary research, the candidate will take a leadership role in laboratory management, ensuring operational efficiency and providing mentorship and technical training to junior researchers and students.<br>Research-Track faculty are expected to have developed sufficient expertise and skills to contribute immediately to the research initiatives of the program they join without an expectation of significant training. Research-Track faculty may be asked to contribute to, and/or submit as principal investigator, applications for extramural funding in their research area of expertise to financially support their position.<br>If you have any questions about this position or the department, please contact the Dr. Maria E. (Marien) Solesio, PhD (m.solesio@rutgers.edu).</div> Biology Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 6758 26FA0653 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266393 2026-01-04T21:31:20-05:00 2026-01-04T21:31:21-05:00 Extension Specialist in Equine Management <div>The Rutgers New Brunswick Department of Animal Sciences invites qualified candidates to apply for a 12-month tenured open-rank faculty position in the Extension Specialist title series within the Department of Animal Sciences. This position builds up the established strengths and traditions of the Rutgers Equine Science Center and the equine research program within Animal Sciences by focusing on equine physiology and possibly using the horse as a model for understanding the human-animal bond. Eligible candidates should have a background in equine science and management, with research areas including but not limited to horse and human interaction, behavior and welfare, nutrition, reproduction, exercise physiology, pasture and forage management, as well as experience in extension outreach to support equine stakeholders.<br><br>The Extension Specialist hired in this area will lead and expand targeted outreach initiatives, develop and deliver science-based educational programs, and collaborate with stakeholders to address emerging challenges in equine management. This includes: designing and implementing statewide equine management workshops focused on physiology, nutrition, welfare, and pasture systems; creating decision-support tools and resources for equine farm owners to improve environmental sustainability and economic viability; translating research findings into practical applications for horse owners and industry professionals; and supporting data-driven policy development by engaging with state agencies and industry groups on equine-related issues. The successful candidate will develop an externally funded research program that focuses on the core disciplines of animal science in areas mentioned above. Contributions to the Animal Sciences teaching program will include: developing and teaching new undergraduate and graduate courses in equine physiology, health, behavior, and management; supervising student-led research projects and internships; and integrating experiential learning opportunities such as field visits, hands-on labs, and community-based projects into the curriculum.<br><br></div><div>In general, the successful candidate should complement existing faculty in the Department of Animal Sciences, SEBS, NJAES, and RCE, demonstrating a willingness to collaborate with faculty, staff, and students to promote the university's mission and values, and serve on department, college, and university committees as fitting a tenured position This position requires someone who builds connections and collaborations with industry and also with other faculty across disciplines and departments within NJAES/SEBS, as well as across Rutgers, including the Department of Psychology and Graduate School of Applied and Professional Psychology. Additional efforts could be realized with applied academic synergies with the Rutgers Brandt Behavioral Health Treatment Center and Retreat located adjacent to the Best Management Practice Demonstration Horse Farm at Ryders Lane. In addition, NJ offers connections with the Shreiber School of Veterinary Medicine at Rowan University.<br><br></div><div>Rutgers is an equal opportunity employer. Individuals covered by Section 503 of the Vocational Rehabilitation Act of 1973 or Section 402 of the Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act of 1974 may self-identify. If you wish to self-identify, please do so in the cover letter transmitting your CV.<br><br><strong>Proposed Start Date: </strong>September 1, 2026</div><div><br></div><div><strong>To apply: </strong>Submit the following documents:<br><br></div><ul><li>CV</li><li>Personal statement: Please address your value in this position to the Department and to the Land Grant Mission and the mission of Rutgers (<a href=\"https://www.rutgers.edu/about-rutgers\"><strong>https://www.rutgers.edu/about-rutgers</strong></a>).</li><li>Statement of Values: Provide a statement that describes examples of you experiences in leadership, mentoring, and/or community engagement that resonate with the values and mission of Rutgers University as a land grant university serving a diverse state and student body.</li><li>Research and Teaching Statement</li><li>Extension portfolio</li><li>Names/contacts of professional 3 references.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Questions can be directed to Dr. Carey A. Williams, Interim Director, Equine Science Center, Search Committee Chair, <a href=\"mailto:carey.williams@rutgers.edu\"><strong>carey.williams@rutgers.edu</strong></a>.<br><br></div><div><strong>Materials are due Dec. 1st, 2025.</strong></div><div><br></div> Animal Science New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 7134 25FA0917 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280187 2026-08-31T10:47:16-04:00 2026-08-31T10:47:17-04:00 Forensic Mental Health Clinician UCHC NJSP <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care (UCHC) is seeking a Forensic Mental Health Clinician for the New Jersey State Prison located in Trenton, NJ. Reporting to the Clinician Supervisor, the Forensic Mental Health Clinician completes specialized psychological testing and assessment of clinical needs of adult inmates sentenced to the Department of Corrections.<br><br>Among the key duties for this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Arrives at DSM IV diagnoses with precision and accuracy through psychological testing and evaluation sessions.</li><li>Provides crisis intervention, individual and group psychotherapy and psycho-education programming as clinically indicated to assigned inmates.</li><li>Involves inmates and Department of Corrections staff in developing achievable and understandable psychosocial treatment plans.</li><li>Advocates for appropriate resources for inmates based on assessed needs.</li><li>Manages caseload demands effectively while considering both qualities of care and the security needs of the Department of Corrections.</li><li>Assumes overall case management responsibilities for assigned inmates including coordination of treatment and liaison with community agencies; maintains appropriate inmate records.</li><li>Demonstrates competency in psychological testing and in recognizing the unique needs and behaviors of adult inmates and seniors</li></ul> UCHC New Jersey State Prison M RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7660 Trenton NJ 26ST0471 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278627 2026-07-10T13:00:55-04:00 2026-07-10T13:00:56-04:00 Staff Nurse PT Days UCHC NJSP Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Part Time Staff Nurse for the New Jersey State Prison, located in Trenton, NJ<br><br>The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus for inmates in the New Jersey Department of Corrections.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br>* Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the resident-patient including adolescents (13-17 years), adults (18 to 64 years) and their family within the framework established by the correctional system.<br>* Performs assessments of resident-patient in a variety of settings such as initial intake area, health care unit for sick call, emergency situations in housing, chronic care clinics and infirmary.<br>* Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br>* Identifies inmate-centered goals and nursing objectives and implements prescribed interventions and solutions for the identified problems.<br>* Plans nursing care by identification of resident-patient needs based on assessments. Makes appropriate, timely referrals and initiates appropriate nursing care based on institutional policies and procedures.<br>* As team leader or charge nurse, delegates duties to other health care team members based on their skill, knowledge and experience and guides the provision of care by others.&nbsp;</div> UCHC New Jersey State Prison A RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7683 Trenton NJ 26ST1023 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/269313 2026-02-16T17:47:39-05:00 2026-02-16T17:47:40-05:00 Clinical Assistant Professor- Per Diem - Emergency Medicine <div>The Department of Emergency Medicine at Rutgers, New Jersey Medical School, seeks qualified candidates for <strong>Per Diem</strong> positions as Clinical Assistant Professor, Non-Tenure Track, to assist with weekday and weeknight urgent coverage (up to 6 calls/month) in the Emergency Department at University Hospital. Candidates will also participate in the education of medical students, residents and fellows.</div> NJMS - Emergency Medicine RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7494 26FA0143 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280433 2026-09-04T09:11:40-04:00 2026-09-04T09:11:41-04:00 Program Manager (Cancer Surveillance Data Systems Informatics) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Program Manager of Cancer Surveillance Data Systems Informatics within the Office of the Director, New Jersey State Cancer Registry at the Rutgers Cancer Institute.<br><br>The Program Manager of Cancer Surveillance Data Systems and Informatics at the New Jersey State Cancer Registry oversees all operational and programmatic aspects of data collection, data processing, and systems integration for New Jersey’s statewide cancer surveillance system. The incumbent works closely with the Director of Cancer Epidemiology Services/New Jersey State Cancer Registry, Deputy Director of Cancer Surveillance Research, Rutgers information technology, and other senior staff to manage and fulfill deliverables of the Center of Excellence for Cancer Surveillance, which was formed through a partnership between the New Jersey Department of Health and the Rutgers Cancer Institute.<br><br>The Program Manager of Cancer Surveillance Data Systems and Informatics also works closely with partners from local, state, and national agencies, including but not limited to the New Jersey Department of Health, the National Cancer Institute’s Surveillance, Epidemiology, and End Results (SEER) Program; the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention’s National Program of Cancer Registries (NPCR); the North American Association of Central Cancer Registries (NAACCR); and the National Cancer Registrar’s Association (NCRA).</div><div><br>Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following:</div><ul><li>Assists Director in strategic project planning, and direction of data/informatics activities and projects to ensure excellence in cancer surveillance statewide. Recommends, drafts, and executes renewals, revisions, and amendments to cancer surveillance operational regulations and statutes as necessary.</li><li>Responsible for and contributes to national dialogue for developing cancer surveillance and registry standards, procedures, and best practices through active participation in NAACCR, SEER, NPCR, and NCRA. Works with local providers, hospitals, and registrars, Department of Health, SEER, NPCR, NAACCR and other state and national agencies to assure the highest quality cancer surveillance data are collected in a timely and effective manner. Ensures compliance with SEER, NPCR, and NAACCR and other established guidelines, as well as contract and cooperative agreement deliverables.&nbsp;</li><li>Manages and coordinates all workflow, data management, permission structure and activities related to the New Jersey State Cancer Registry (NJSCR) database management system. Identifies new approaches to improve efficiency of extracting and utilizing NJSCR data.</li><li>Manages data collection and quality assurance activities of the NJSCR. Ensures compliance with state and federal reporting requirements for the collection of cancer data including the monitoring of completeness and timeliness of reporting, as well as confidentiality of all data.</li><li>Manages the development of an efficient and multi system surveillance information system capable of harmonizing data from multiple sources and in varying file formats and quality.</li><li>Manage, train, hire, discipline, cross train and develop staff to support NJSCR initiatives. Cultivates staff and skillsets to support NJSCR future state and needs. Complete performance appraisals, coaching, and disciplinary actions as necessary. Assigns all permission levels to staff, as well as increases access as necessary/when warranted or needed.&nbsp;</li><li>Represents the New Jersey State Cancer Registry operationally at state, regional and national planning meetings, both in-person and virtually.</li><li>Provides content expertise and assistance to Director (or designee) in support of special epidemiologic studies that use New Jersey State Cancer Registry surveillance data for research.</li></ul> CINJ - Cancer Registry Operati RBHS Chancellor-L2 Cancer Institute of New Jersey-L3 7894 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1721 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279358 2026-08-06T11:39:21-04:00 2026-08-06T11:39:22-04:00 Assistant Professor of Professional Practice <div>The Department of Management Science and Information Systems at Rutgers Business School–Newark and New Brunswick invites applications for a full-time (100%), non-tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor of Professional Practice, with an anticipated start date of January 2027.</div> Management Science & Informati Newark Chancellor-L2 Rutgers Business School-L3 6939 26FA0360 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275994 2026-05-28T12:34:41-04:00 2026-05-28T12:34:41-04:00 Lecturers (Adjunct Faculty) for the Undergraduate Program in Digital Communication, Information, and Media (Fall 2026) <div>The School of Communication and Information seeks lecturers for its undergraduate program in Digital Communication, Information, and Media. Please see the description of our program at https://comminfo.rutgers.edu/academics/undergraduate/dcim and the list of courses we offer at https://comminfo.rutgers.edu/academics/courses?courses=&amp;program=29. Within your cover letter, please let us know which courses in our program you feel most prepared to teach. Please submit a cover letter, resume/curriculum vitae, and names and contact information for at least three references. You may also upload any evidence of your teaching experience such as sample syllabi or course materials, results of student instructional ratings, or published work.</div> School  Communicatn & Info Sci New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School  Communicatn & Info Sci-L3 8093 26FA0371 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/273309 2026-04-20T13:17:50-04:00 2026-04-20T13:17:51-04:00 Assistant Professor <div>The Department of Psychiatry at the Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School (RWJMS) has an opening for a full time Academic Psychiatrist. The position is at the Assistant Professor level, commensurate with experience.<br><br>The Assistant Professor will provide direct clinical care at the Child &amp; Adolescent Psychiatry Partial Hospitalization Programs and the Brandt Center at Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br></div> RWJ - Psychiatry RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7823 26FA0378 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/265504 2025-12-18T12:07:17-05:00 2025-12-18T12:07:17-05:00 NTT Lecturer at the rank of Assistant Teaching Professor <div>The Department seeks applications for two one-year, possibly-renewable teaching positions at the rank of NTT Lecturer at the rank of Assistant Teaching Professor available beginning January 1, 2026, subject to the availability of funding, with the possibility of appointment at a higher level for well-qualified candidates. <br><br>This position has a teaching load of 4-4 (four undergraduate mathematics courses in each of the fall and spring semesters), with possible teaching reductions for administrative, advising or other departmental duties. Applicants should have received a Ph.D. and show outstanding evidence of teaching at the undergraduate level. Ideally, candidates will have had at least three years teaching experience by the time the position starts. <br><br>The academic year salary for an assistant resp. associate resp. full teaching professor will not be less than $82,110 based on the most recent collective bargaining agreement between the faculty union (AAUP-AFT) and Rutgers University.<br><br>Applicants should complete the online form associated with this listing and submit a curriculum vitae. In addition, you should register as a job applicant at mathjobs.org<br><br><a href=\"https://nam02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.mathjobs.org%2Fjobs%2Flist%2F27867&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cmb1186%40math.rutgers.edu%7C3ddfe3129bb44be744cd08de3c1f1053%7Cb92d2b234d35447093ff69aca6632ffe%7C1%7C0%7C639014301281205755%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=Foyx%2B74nHLY83pu4n%2BAt2c06LOgcLgLnvmbQQZLyEzc%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/27867</strong></a><br><br>and complete the application, with the requested supporting documents, for position TF26B under the Rutgers University-New Brunswick listing. Review of applications begins on December 22, 2025.</div> Mathematics New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 8125 25FA1243 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279644 2026-08-17T12:09:20-04:00 2026-08-17T12:09:21-04:00 Supervising Physician UCHC EMCFW <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Supervising Physician for Edna Mahan Correctional Facility, located in Clinton, NJ. The Supervising Physician is responsible for providing medical services to inmates of the Department of Corrections, which are consistent with community Standards of Care. Provides clinical supervision to the assigned physicians and medical nurse practitioners. Serves as liaison for clinical matters with medical providers outside of the system and be available to provide on- call services.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Responsible for providing clinical and professional supervision, management, and monitoring of physicians and nurse practitioners/physician assistants of assigned State Prison.<ul><li>Oversees the clinical work of physicians and nurse practitioners/physician assistants in the assigned State Prison by conducting regular peer reviews in documentation, medication usage, and consult request patterns, as assigned.</li><li>Hosts quarterly meetings for physicians and nurse practitioners/physician assistants in the region to review CQI issues, policies, and problems.</li><li>Participates in annual performance evaluations of physicians and nurse practitioners within a region.</li></ul></li><li>Works in concert with the Medical Director and the regional nurse managers to develop and maintain appropriate medical services within the assigned State Prison</li><li>Assists in the development and implementation of UCHC policies and procedures.<ul><li>Participates in UCHC continuous quality improvement program.<ul><li>Corrective action plans.</li><li>Continuing medical education.</li><li>Algorithms/models for best practices.</li></ul></li><li>Participates in the formal preparation for health care reviews (such as National Commission of Correctional HealthCare inspections).</li><li>Performs routine administrative functions and organizational responsibilities.<ul><li>Maintains monthly provider clinic schedule for the assigned State Prison, which will be provided to the medical and mental health staff in a concise, clear, and timely manner.</li><li>Responsible for time off request approval, time sheet review and approval, and monitoring paid time off and adherence to time and attendance policy for physicians and nurse practitioners/physician assistants of the assigned State Prison.</li></ul></li><li>Responsible for ensuring that physicians and nurse practitioners/physician assistants adhere to all Rutgers, UCHC, and NJDOC conduct and policies, including but not limited to dress codes, time and attendance policies, and all applicable policies.</li><li>Directly responsible for ensuring and documenting progressive discipline of all physicians and nurse practitioners/ physician assistants of the assigned state prison, including but not limited to termination of appointments in collaboration with the Medical Director</li></ul></li></ul> UCHC-Edna Mahan Corr-Ancillary RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7682 Clinton NJ 26ST0946 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279954 2026-08-25T14:04:38-04:00 2026-08-25T14:04:39-04:00 Military/Veteran Peer Support Specialist III <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Military/Veteran Peer Support Specialist III<br>for the Military Services within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>Under the supervision, provides person centered, culturally competent, and “consumer friendly” services to individuals who contact the Call Center. Receives telephone, chat, and text requests for service, undertakes review of the service need of the caller or consumer, and responds by offering peer support and appropriate referrals and disposition.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Provides “customer friendly” services, taking initiative in engaging individuals served in an empathic and concerned manner.</li><li>Provides direct care services consistent with philosophy of UBHC.</li><li>Reviews service requests/referrals for all populations, and responds in accordance with prescribed departmental procedures.&nbsp;</li><li>Documents contacts, interventions, and interactions with callers in a timely manner and in accordance with established policies.&nbsp;</li><li>Maintains knowledge of Center and Unit policies and procedures.</li><li>Contributes to and supports the mission, vision, values, goals and objectives of UBHC.</li></ul> UBHC - Military Services RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8040 Piscataway NJ 26ST0842 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277763 2026-06-25T11:06:00-04:00 2026-06-25T11:06:01-04:00 Staff Nurse PT Nights UCHC NSP <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Full Time Staff Nurse for Northern State Prison located in Newark, NJ<br><br>The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus for inmates in the New Jersey Department of Corrections.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br>* Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the resident-patient including adolescents (13-17 years), adults (18 to 64 years) and their family within the framework established by the correctional system.<br>* Performs assessments of resident-patient in a variety of settings such as initial intake area, health care unit for sick call, emergency situations in housing, chronic care clinics and infirmary.<br>* Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br>* Identifies inmate-centered goals and nursing objectives and implements prescribed interventions and solutions for the identified problems.<br>* Plans nursing care by identification of resident-patient needs based on assessments. Makes appropriate, timely referrals and initiates appropriate nursing care based on institutional policies and procedures.<br>* As team leader or charge nurse, delegates duties to other health care team members based on their skill, knowledge and experience and guides the provision of care by others.</div> UCHC Northern State Prison Phy_DUP RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7679 Newark NJ 26ST0677 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275326 2026-05-18T15:23:03-04:00 2026-05-18T15:23:04-04:00 Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Pediatric Critical Care <div>The Division of Pediatric Critical Care Medicine at Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School is seeking a BE/BC academic focused pediatric critical care physician to join our group. The right faculty member will be entering as a clinical scholar with appropriate support to allow them to pursue the goal of establishing independence for their scholarly work over 2-3 years.</div><div>As part of the RWJBarnabas Health system, members of our group mainly cover a 20-bed multidisciplinary medical surgical unit at the Bristol Myers Squibb Children’s Hospital at Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital New Brunswick and a 4 bed unit which can flex to 10 at the Unterberg Children’s Hospital at Monmouth Medical Center. Our clinical programs include high level general pediatric surgery, neurosurgery, ENT surgery, a level 1 pediatric trauma program, solid organ transplantation, bone marrow transplant, palliative care medicine, pediatric ground and air transport, and extracorporeal support. We staff and support a Pediatric sedation program.</div><div>We have high camaraderie and teamwork amongst our division members and are looking for the right person to join our group.</div><div>Requirements are:</div><div>· Proven potential for academic growth</div><div>· Team centered approach</div><div>· Strong procedural skillset</div><div>· Adaptability</div><div>· Evidence based practice</div><div>· Teaching ability</div><div>Members of our group are in leadership positions throughout our health care system. We have a strong clinical research center to support any research endeavor.</div><div>This position is open to applicants at all levels from early to senior levels. Salary is commensurate with experience. We are an EOE employer.</div><div>If interested, please submit your application to the Rutgers website listed below.</div><div><a href=\"https://jobs.rutgers.edu/\"><strong>https://jobs.rutgers.edu/</strong></a><strong><br><br></strong><br></div><div>Simon Li MD MPH MBA, Division Chief</div><div>Professor and Chief, Division of Pediatric Critical Care Medicine</div><div>Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School</div><div>New Brunswick, NJ 08901</div><div>sl1799@rwjms.rutgers.edu</div> RWJ - Pediatrics Critical Care RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7813 26FA0487 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266263 2025-12-31T09:42:16-05:00 2025-12-31T09:42:16-05:00 Post Doctorial Associate <div>Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy, Pharmacy Practice, and Pharmacy Administration – Health Outcomes, Policy &amp; Economics, Rutgers University is part of Rutgers Biomedical Health Sciences (RBHS) and participates in interdisciplinary professional education and training partnership with Rutgers School of Public Health and the Robert Wood Johnson Medical School.<br><br>Though certain responsibilities of the resident are required, the program has the flexibility to develop activities consistent with the resident’s background and career goals. In general, the resident responsibilities include: 1. Attend daily rounds and make appropriate recommendations to inter-disciplinary treatment teams 2. Design, monitor, and evaluate treatment goals for patients that consider patient-, disease-, and drug-specific information and ethical considerations 3. Present educational in-services on pharmacy topics to patients, pharmacy staff, and inter-disciplinary treatment team 4. Lead inpatient and outpatient pharmacy medication education groups 5. Supervise pharmacy students on Advanced Pharmacy Practice Experience (APPE) rotations. 6. Present didactic lectures to pharmacy students at the Rutgers Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy 7. Complete a research project related to the provision of pharmacy care, as well as presenting this research at a national conference.</div> Pharmacy Practice & Administra RBHS Chancellor-L2 Ernest Mario School of Pharmac-L3 6720 25FA0630 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280367 2026-09-03T10:20:31-04:00 2026-09-03T10:20:32-04:00 Coordinator Budgetary Services <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Coordinator Budgetary Services. in the Department of Medicine- Global Tuberculosis Institute (GTBI) within the New Jersey Medical School (NJMS).<br><br>The Coordinator Budgetary Services coordinates the general accounting activities of the Unit to ensure that financial transactions are properly processed and accounted. Develops and implements accounting systems and procedures; ensures accurate and timely preparation of financial reports, account analyses and assists in preparation of expenditures and revenue forecasts. Deals with clinical and health department agreements.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Formulates, recommends and implements accounting procedures and controls for the unit.</li><li>Analyzes present accounting systems and procedures for possible improvements.</li><li>Responsible for general ledger accounting and maintenance of Chart of Accounts.</li><li>Develops or improves methods of processing invoices and issuance of checks for payment.</li><li>Prepares Unit's budget.</li><li>Analyzes monthly statistical and operating results.</li></ul> NJMS - Medicine Tuberculosis C RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7448 Newark NJ 26ST1714 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279228 2026-07-31T09:49:22-04:00 2026-07-31T09:49:23-04:00 Temporary Research Assistant <div>The Rutgers School of Public Health is seeking a Temporary Research Assistant.&nbsp; The Temporary Research Assistant will assist with a study that aims to determine the feasibility and acceptability of a mobile health mindfulness app in order to eventually improve the overall care and mental health of caregivers and the older adults they care for. The TRA will serve as an assistant for a research study with caregivers of older adults with cognitive impairment ordementia. Will be responsible for the data collection and subject recruitment for the study under the supervision of the Principal Investigator.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Supports Principal Investigator with subject recruitment throughout New Brunswick.</li><li>Orients participants to the mHealth app</li></ul> SPH - Social & Behavioral Heal RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Public Health-L3 7713 Piscataway NJ 26ST1575 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/272658 2026-04-08T12:47:30-04:00 2026-04-08T12:47:31-04:00 Assist–Assoc Prof, Division Director of Pediatric Critical Care <div>Rutgers Health – New Jersey Medical School Department of Pediatrics offers an outstanding opportunity for a Pediatric Intensivist (to serve as Division Director of the PICU) to join our faculty of more than 30 full-time clinicians and scientists at the Assistant or Associate Professor level.</div> NJMS - Pediatrics Critical Car RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7473 26FA0323 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279585 2026-08-14T09:55:38-04:00 2026-08-14T09:55:39-04:00 Staff Nurse (RN) - Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Staff Nurse (RN) for the Crisis Receiving Stabilization Center (CRSC) within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Staff Nurse (RN) is to provide essential, goal-directed nursing care for individuals served in mental health or substance use crises, adhering to departmental policies and regulatory standards. Responsibilities include conducting assessments, developing crisis care plans, administering medications, and collaborating with the interdisciplinary team to stabilize and support patients.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Assesses individuals served needs in order to provide quality care to assigned individuals served.</li><li>Documents initial nursing assessment and individualized, goal directed plan of care considering the psychological, social, physical health and safety needs of the patient, in accordance with unit standards.</li><li>Identifies and documents patient, family and significant other learning needs upon admission.</li><li>Develops, discusses and communicates a realistic, individualized plan of care for each patient, in collaboration with the patient, family and significant other in an effort to promote wellness and recovery.</li><li>Demonstrates the skills and judgment necessary to implement the plan of care, nursing interventions and procedures as necessary for the care and safety of the patient.</li><li>Maintains concurrent and accurate documentation of nursing care provided to ensure the integration of information for use by the multidisciplinary team, in order to ensure quality care.</li><li>Demonstrates respect and regard for the dignity of all patients, families, visitors and fellow employees to ensure a professional, responsible and courteous environment.</li></ul> UBHC - CRSC Newark RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8817 Newark NJ 26ST0508 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279829 2026-08-21T13:15:45-04:00 2026-08-21T13:15:45-04:00 MGSA - Department of Dance - Coadjutant - Casual  Instructional Support Positions Fall 2026 <div>The Department of Music, Mason Gross School of the Arts, Rutgers University invites applications for instructional positions with the Dance Department for Fall 2026 semester. Positions include: Teaching courses in Concussion Awareness, Motor Learning Dance, Special Topics Dance, Production Study Dance Production, Pilates Teacher Training and others to undergraduates and graduates.</div> Dance New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Mason Gross School of Arts Dea-L3 6864 26FA0729 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277677 2026-06-24T13:12:29-04:00 2026-06-24T13:12:29-04:00 Physician Faculty (Instructor/Assistant Professor/Associate Professor) for Complex and Minimally Invasive Gynecological Surgery <div>The Department of Obstetrics, Gynecology and Reproductive Sciences at Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School is seeking a fellowship-trained, board-eligible or board-certified Complex Benign and Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgeon to join the newly established Division of Complex and Minimally Invasive Gynecological Surgery (CMIGS). This is a full-time, open-rank academic position in an innovative and growing program that serves as a regional referral center for complex benign gynecologic conditions.<br><br>About the Division of Complex and Minimally Invasive Gynecological Surgery. The Division provides comprehensive surgical care for patients with complex gynecologic conditions including, but not limited to, endometriosis, large-volume fibroids, pelvic pain, adhesions, isthmoceles, C-section scar ectopic pregnancies, adnexal pathology, abnormal uterine bleeding, and congenital anomalies. The Division emphasizes minimally invasive laparoscopic, robotic, hysteroscopic, and/or vaginal surgical techniques and is committed to advancing the field through research, education, and interdisciplinary collaboration.<br><br>Key Responsibilities</div><ul><li>Provide advanced minimally invasive, laparoscopic, robotic, hysteroscopic, and/or vaginal surgical care for complex benign gynecologic conditions.</li><li>Participate in the education of medical students and OB/GYN residents through clinical teaching and simulation training.</li><li>Collaborate on quality improvement initiatives within gynecologic surgery.</li><li>Engage in clinical or translational research aligned with Division priorities.</li><li>Support the development of a formal referral program and interdisciplinary partnerships.</li></ul> RWJ - Obstetrics & Gynocology RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7787 26FA0630 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274580 2026-05-07T16:44:54-04:00 2026-05-07T16:44:54-04:00 Open-Rank Faculty <div>The Department of Psychiatric Rehabilitation and Counseling Professions is one of seven academic Departments, located in the School of Health Professions. The Department offers a full career ladder of graduate and undergraduate degrees, including an M.S. in Rehabilitation Counseling, Clinical Mental Health Counseling Track that is accredited by CACREP. The Department also offers a Ph.D. in Counselor Education and Supervision. Additional information about the School of Health Professions is available at http://shp.rutgers.edu<br><br>This is an open rank, 12-month faculty position. The successful candidate will support the preparation of students who will become professional counselors, educators, researchers, and advanced clinicians in the effective treatment of people with mental illnesses and disabilities via counseling services and rehabilitation intervention.<br><strong><br>Essential Duties and Responsibilities:</strong><br>• Teach master’s and doctoral level counseling courses related to mental health counseling and rehabilitation counseling<br>• Teach undergraduate courses<br>• Develop curricula materials for on-campus and web-based courses<br>• Teaching in both on-campus and web-based learning environments is required<br>• Pursue a relevant research agenda<br>• Assist in program accreditation preparation<br>• Advise graduate students<br>• Participate in professional association, community service and university<br> service activities<br>• Understand and adhere to legacy Rutgers RBHS compliance standards as they appear in legacy UMDNJ’s Corporate Compliance Policy and Code of Conduct and Conflict of Interest Policy</div> SHP - Psychiatric Rehabilitati RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Health Professions-L3 7581 26FA0471 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266178 2025-12-31T09:33:44-05:00 2025-12-31T09:33:45-05:00 Radiation Oncology Physician Scientist; Tenure Track (Assistant to Associate Professor) <div>The Department of Radiation Oncology at Robert Wood Johnson Medical School and Rutgers Cancer Institute is seeking applications for a physician-scientist faculty position. This is a tenure track position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level that requires excellence in clinical practice and demonstrated accomplishments in scientific research. In addition to education, clinical, and research responsibilities, this faculty position will collaborate closely with other Rutgers Cancer Institute programs, accessing state-of-the-art resources and integrated cancer care opportunities.<br><br></div><div>The Rutgers Cancer Institute oncology service line is the largest academic health care system in NJ with a service area covering nine counties and a population of five million people. The Institute is the only NCI-designated Comprehensive Cancer Center in the state of NJ, and operates the recently completed Jack and Sheryl Morris Cancer Center- a 12 story, 520,000 square foot freestanding cancer hospital in New Brunswick, NJ. The department leads clinical and translational programs in MR-Linac based adaptive radiotherapy, IMRT/IGRT, SBRT, Brachytherapy, GKRS, Proton therapy, and Radiopharmaceutical therapy.<br><br></div><div>Candidates must have and MD/DO degree, be board certified/eligible in Radiation Oncology, and be eligible for a NJ Medical License. Candidates should also possess a strong publication record and the capacity to obtain extramural research funding. For more information about our department, please visit: <a href=\"https://sites.rutgers.edu/cinj-radiation-oncology/\"><strong>https://sites.rutgers.edu/cinj-radiation-oncology/</strong></a>. For additional information or to apply please contact:<a href=\"mailto:cinjcareers@cinj.rutgers.edu\"><strong>cinjcareers@rutgers.edu</strong></a>.</div> Cancer Institute of New Jersey CINJ-Director's Office-L2 Cancer Institute of New Jersey-L3 7963 25FA0800 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280080 2026-08-27T11:48:19-04:00 2026-08-27T11:48:20-04:00 Financial Assistance Advisor <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Financial Assistance Advisor for the Newark Outpatient Services within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>Under the direction of the Office Manager and/or the Supervising Program Assistant, is responsible for the registration process for the UBHC Ambulatory Programs.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Interviews and registers patients into the revenue cycle system.</li><li>Forwards patients’ registration packages to Clinical Records to achieve a complete Medical Records folder.</li><li>Determines customer’s eligibility for the Charity Care program as set forth by NJ Department of Health N.J.A.C. 8:31B-4.37 and UBHC policy.</li><li>Enters completed insurance data into revenue cycle system.</li><li>Completes requirement tracking when a client is initially registered and/or routinely updated.</li><li>Documents the type of registration, client’s benefits information, HIPAA restriction and action taken on the account.</li><li>Accesses, prints and prepares the daily Intake report and IC that identifies patients with scheduled appointment: IPMS report and IPMS.</li></ul> UBHC - Outpatient Newark RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8059 Newark NJ 26ST0737 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278375 2026-07-07T18:21:35-04:00 2026-07-07T18:21:36-04:00 Mental Health Specialist II - Per Diem - NJ Hopeline <div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Mental Health Specialist II (Per Diem) in the 988 Lifeline Services of Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>Performs functions in support of the Unit’s mission providing streamlined, prompt, and “customer friendly” services to clients of the 988 Lifeline Services. Receives telephone, chat and/or text requests for service, undertakes assessment of the service need of the client and responds by offering support and appropriate referrals or disposition. Demonstrates competency in recognizing the unique needs of clients and applying relevant assessment and support skills with regard to a wide range of issues.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Interacts with client in a therapeutic manner.</li><li>Participates in ensuring that all service requests are handled in an effective and “client friendly” manner.</li><li>Assesses service requests/referrals and responds in accordance with prescribed procedures.</li><li>Assesses client’s condition in order to make/authorize an appropriate disposition.</li><li>Assumes overall responsibilities for completion of all request and documentation for disposition.</li><li>Documents assessments, interventions, and interactions with clients in a timely manner and in accordance with established policies.</li></ul> UBHC - NJ Hopeline RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8707 Remote NJ 26ST1485 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267272 2026-01-14T12:14:10-05:00 2026-01-14T12:14:11-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor-Cardiology <div>Rutgers New Jersey Medical School (NJMS) seeks qualified candidates at the Assistant or Associate Professor level for Non-Invasive Cardiology. Preference will be given to candidates with a focus in advanced cardiac imaging, cardio-oncology, cardiac amyloid or cardiac intensive care medicine. Responsibilities will include patient care, research, and teaching (medical students/resident physicians and sub-specialty fellows) in concert with the policies of Rutgers NJMS, University Hospital, and the Division of Cardiology.The successful candidate will be board certified/board eligible Cardiovascular Disease and one or more areas of cardiovascular imaging</div> NJMS - Medicine Cardiology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7436 25FA1268 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280238 2026-08-31T14:55:58-04:00 2026-08-31T14:55:59-04:00 Manager Retail Operations <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Manager Retail Operations for the Department of Dining Services. Reporting to the Executive Director of Dining Services, and in accordance with policies and procedures set forth by Rutgers University Dining Services, supervises all activities, with an annual operation budget of $500,000.<br><br>Among the key duties of the position are the following:</div><ul><li>Oversees all food production forecasting and planning of a major dining facility of Rutgers University Dining Services, including student board, cash, catering and special events.</li><li>Identifies food services objectives and special problem areas and determines means by which objectives might be met and weaknesses eliminated</li><li>Handles the auditing of all unit activities, funds, records and supplies: Food and nonfood inventories, billing of service (weekly operations reports) and receiving food in accordance to standards set by specifications of Dining Services.</li><li>Assures compliance with all safety and sanitations rules and regulations.</li></ul> Dining Services New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Student Affairs - New Brunswic-L3 8110 TBD NJ 26ST1698 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278827 2026-07-15T10:36:06-04:00 2026-07-15T10:36:07-04:00 Sr. Financial Analyst I <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Sr. Financial Analyst in the Department of Pharmacology, Physiology and Neuroscience within the New Jersey Medical School (NJMS).<br><br>The Sr. Financial Analyst will assist in management of all aspects of the departments financial processes, including management of the departments’ annual operating budget, grant management, preparation of current year forecasts, financial analysis of monthly operating results, oversight of the purchasing and accounts payable functions for the department, participation in pre-award activities.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Manages and monitors all fiscal/financial matters within the department, including development and application of financial programs and policies.</li><li>Monitors all accounts and programs to evaluate effectiveness of administration in terms of objectives: and ensures that expenditures are in accord with budget constraints and agency/institutional regulations.</li><li>Advises faculty and staff on matters pertaining to purchasing of supplies and equipment. Evaluates and makes recommendations on proposed plans of organization and budget requests. Ensures request meet the University and budgetary guidelines.</li><li>Conducts and supervises department’s financial and statistical data analysis to create reports: ensures the maintenance of historical data, and develops improvements to internal reporting procedures.</li><li>Monitor grants to comply with the granting agency’s as well as the University regulations and provides reports of expenditures with all investigators, Director of Administration and Chairman to anticipate problems with spending and to make timely budgetary decisions.</li></ul> NJMS - Pharmacology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7431 Newark NJ 26ST1032 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/270243 2026-03-04T18:24:17-05:00 2026-03-04T18:24:17-05:00 Spine Neurosurgeon <div><strong>Job Summary: </strong>The Faculty member will support the RWJBH &amp; Rutgers Health Neurosurgical service-line. This position will support the Department of Neurosurgery in its clinical and academic mission.</div><div><br></div><div><strong>DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></div><div><em>Clinical Responsibilities</em></div><div>1. Demonstrates clinical competence and surgical excellence in neurosurgery.</div><div>2. Demonstrates factual knowledge and technical skills in the preoperative evaluation, operative management, and postoperative care of patients, including critical care, with pathologic conditions pertaining to neurosurgical care.</div><div>3. Demonstrates the knowledge and surgical experience in evolving techniques, such as endovascular procedures.</div><div>4. Maintains compliance with all applicable State, Federal, UNOS, CMS, and Joint Commission laws, rules, regulations and requirements and create policies and procedures that ensure compliance for the programs with the foregoing.</div><div>5. Surgically evaluates and treats patients who are determined to require services.</div><div>6. Rounds daily on patient(s) in accordance with best practices.</div><div>7. Attends departmental and interdepartmental physician meetings, morbidity and mortality conferences, quality improvement process, selection meetings and other meetings deemed as appropriate.</div><div>8. Completes required medical documentation for patients' charts in a timely manner according to hospital bylaws. Completes and signs operative reports within 24 hours of surgery.</div><div>9. Provides accurate and detailed reports to referring physicians in a timely manner.</div><div>10. Provides accurate and complete information required for billing and coding.</div><div>11. Provides clear instructions and explanations regarding diagnosis, treatment, medications and follow-up to patients and their respective family members.</div><div>12. Collaborates with surgeons, members of the surgical team, nurses, nurse practitioners, ancillary staff and other physicians and promotes a cohesive team environment.</div><div>13. Maintains effective working relationships with attending physicians outside of the Department, as well as other Hospital department staff and Administration.</div><div>14. Respects others' time, including punctual arrival to meetings and concluding meetings as scheduled.</div><div>15. Demonstrates thorough knowledge and adherence to Hospital policies and procedures.</div><div>16. Responsible for up to 120 days per year of neurosurgery on-call coverage, based on a schedule mutually agreeable with your department Chair and hospital’s CMO.</div> RWJ - Neurosurgery RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7839 25FA0697 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280476 2026-09-04T15:41:50-04:00 2026-09-04T15:41:51-04:00 Medical Records Technician (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Medical Records Technician in the Health Information Management of Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>On an ongoing basis, the Medical Records Technician enforces security and ensures the accessibility of clinical information/records. Plays a key role in the chart completion process by possessing a thorough, up-to-date knowledge of internal recordkeeping standards. Completes all requests for information which includes disability, insurance, other organizations and individuals requests for information. Assists UBHC staff with the completion of chart deficiencies.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Processes all release within five (5) days of receipt.</li><li>Thoroughly reviews and verifies the authenticity of all written requests for patient information submitted by various organizations, as observed by Manager.</li><li>Responds to Social Security Disability (SSD) requests and sends patient records via the disability portal/fax/mail.</li><li>Professionally and courteously interacts with patients and their families, providing them with accurate and thorough information about the release of information process as observed by the Manager.</li><li>Accurately performs clerical duties (i.e., typing, data entry, photocopying, etc.), associated with processing releases as observed by Manager.</li></ul> UBHC - HIM Health IM ACCR & St RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7999 Piscataway NJ 26ST0006 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279433 2026-08-07T16:36:13-04:00 2026-08-07T16:36:13-04:00 Clinic Services Representative II <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Clinic Services Representative II for the department of Surgery at the Robert Wood Johnson Medical School.<br><br>The RWJMG Clinical Services Representative II performs administrative tasks as assigned to support effective and efficient office operations.&nbsp;<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Answers the telephone with a pleasant demeanor, always identifying self, and location.&nbsp;</li><li>Competently performs the following financial functions based on assignment: Scheduling, pre-registration, recording patient arrival, administering financial and HIPAA paperwork, obtaining necessary signatures, receiving referral and pre-certification numbers; performs online insurance verification to assist patient with their payment options.&nbsp;</li><li>Advises patients regarding preparation of necessary forms; counsels patients regarding paperwork requirements.&nbsp;</li><li>Maintains Computer Databases entering changes in demographic, insurance, and other information as required.&nbsp;</li><li>Collects co pays, and posts in the financial system; administers receipts and prepares necessary paperwork for later reconciliation of the batch transactions.&nbsp;</li><li>Processes, researches and answers any verbal or written routine patient billing inquiries in a timely manner. Refers more complex inquiries to appropriate individual or area in accordance with established policies and procedures.&nbsp;</li></ul> RWJ - Surgery General RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7835 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1600 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/276597 2026-06-05T13:15:24-04:00 2026-06-05T13:15:25-04:00 Mental Health Clinician II <div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Mental Health Clinician II in the Brief Treatment<strong> </strong>of Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>Under direction, the Mental Health Clinician II serves as the senior mental health practitioner who provides lead functions for the program, to include screening of intakes and referrals, care coordination, ensuring completion of program specific documentation and/or comprehensive assessment and therapeutic intervention for the psychological and social needs of adult individuals served, experience with the geriatric population, including development of treatment plans, conducting family sessions.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Contributes to and supports goals and objectives of the Unit and UBHC.</li><li>Demonstrates knowledge of University Behavioral Health Care’s vision, mission and values as they relate to service provision, daily activities, decisions and quality improvement priorities and consistently behaves in accordance with established policies and procedures as observed by supervisor.</li><li>Effectively contributes to and supports an environment that enhances the positive self-image of individuals served and their families and preserves their human dignity, right to fair and equitable treatment, self-determination, individuality, privacy and civil rights as observed by supervisor and with minimal complaints and positive feedback from peers, patients and their families.</li><li>Actively and enthusiastically participates in ensuring the smooth functioning and operation of the program, and participates in UBHC-wide meetings, performance improvement activities, committees and task forces as assigned and as observed by supervisor and program administration.</li><li>Consistently ensures that individuals served, families and system partners understand and adhere to procedures while at UBHC.</li></ul> UBHC - Edison RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8002 Edison NJ 25ST2653 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274045 2026-04-30T11:45:47-04:00 2026-04-30T11:45:47-04:00 Lecturers, Chemistry <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the Faculty of Arts &amp; Sciences, Chemistry Department, is seeking lecturers to teach laboratory and lecture courses in Introductory, General, or Organic Chemistry as well as Biochemistry and Forensic Chemistry or related disciplines for courses in Fall 2026, Winter 2027, Spring 2027 and/or Summer 2027. Duties include, but are not limited to, presenting course material during the assigned course times, holding office hours, administering exams/tests, assigning grades, and coordinating any other requirements related to course instruction as well as preparing material for the course.</div> Chemistry Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 6759 26FA0410 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/265948 2025-12-31T09:05:25-05:00 2025-12-31T09:05:25-05:00 Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Mathematics <div>Subject to availability of funding, the Department will have two openings at the level of Tenure-Track Assistant Professor, with the possibility of appointment at a higher level (including the ranks of Associate Professor, Full Professor, and Distinguished Professor) for exceptional candidates. The department has identified priority areas of Algebra &amp; Algebraic Geometry, and Discrete Mathematics, but outstanding candidates in any area of mathematics may be considered. Candidates must have a PhD in mathematics by employment start date. Candidates will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in mathematics, perform research, and supervise graduate students. The normal teaching load for research-active faculty is 2–1.<br><br></div><div>To apply, complete the application associated with this listing and include a curriculum vitae. In addition, you must submit an application on mathjobs.org for the job code TT25 listed under Rutgers University-New Brunswick (https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/25893). Rutgers University is an exciting, large public state university with one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications begins November 22, 2024. Applications completed after that date are still welcome but may not receive full consideration.<br><br></div> Mathematics New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 8125 24FA1242 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279719 2026-08-19T14:33:49-04:00 2026-08-19T14:33:50-04:00 Physician Specialist (Psychiatrist) FT UCHC NSP-2 Openings <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care (UCHC) is seeking a Physician Specialist (Psychiatrist) for Northern State Prison, located in Newark, NJ. The Physician Specialist provides direct clinical care to state prisoners, functions collaboratively with multidisciplinary teams and maintains effective communication with staff and administration.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Provides assessments, direct clinical care and treatment planning to inmates.</li><li>Conducts comprehensive psychiatrist assessments demonstrating a review of the electronic record, psychotropic medications, history of mental illness, prior psychiatric hospitalization, suicidal, unusual, or bizarre behavior) for new admissions to UCHC’s Special Needs roster according to established timeframes.</li><li>Is knowledgeable about and follows DOC and UCHC policies and procedures, including, but not limited to, emergency and non-emergency forced medication, management of potentially suicidal inmates, psychiatry services, and therapeutic restraint.</li><li>Orders, initiates and interprets laboratory tests according to required time frames or as medically necessary including metabolic monitoring, mood stabilizer blood levels, thyroid function, AIMS testing, and other appropriate biochemical monitoring.</li><li>Prescribes and renews medications that are deemed medically necessary within required time frames.</li></ul> UCHC Northern State Prison Med RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7656 Newark NJ 26ST1628 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280023 2026-08-26T12:17:40-04:00 2026-08-26T12:17:41-04:00 Health Safety Specialist I (Senior Biosafety) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Health Safety Specialist I (Senior Biosafety) for the Division of Institutional Planning &amp; Operations (IP&amp;O). Department's continual presence, liaison, and provider of routine services to the University community<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Assist or has a program responsible for the development, implementation, and auditing of environmental, health, and safety programs.</li><li>All services and activities are carried out and performed without adverse health effects to faculty, staff, students, or public, in a manner that will protect the environment,</li><li>in accordance with federal, state, and local regulations, accepted professional standards, in accordance with University policies and procedures, and in an open and sensitive manner so that University's resources are conserved and future liability is limited.</li></ul> Environmental Health & Safety EVP & Chief Admin Officer Institutional Planning & Optns-L3 6593 Piscataway NJ 26ST1663 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277784 2026-06-25T11:28:07-04:00 2026-06-25T11:28:08-04:00 Staff Nurse FT Eves UCHC EMCFW <div>Rutgers University Correctional Healthcare is seeking a Full Time UCHC Staff Nurse for Edna Mahan Correctional Facility located in Clinton, NJ. The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus. Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br><br>Among the duties are:</div><ul><li>Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the inmate-patient including adults (18 to 64 years), and geriatrics (65+) within the framework established by the correctional system.</li><li>Utilizes effective communication skills by demonstrating respect, concern and courtesy in all interpersonal relationships.</li><li>Uses current knowledge to promote a safe environment for providing health care to inmate-patients.</li></ul> UCHC-Edna Mahan Corr-Ancillary RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7682 Clinton NJ 26ST0988 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275549 2026-05-20T14:29:14-04:00 2026-05-20T14:29:15-04:00 Dining Services Student Worker (Cafe West) <div>Join the Rutgers Dining team as a Dining Services Student Worker in one of our dining halls or retail operations across the New Brunswick, Piscataway and Camden campuses. Rutgers Dining Services strives to be the best in culinary excellence and as a Dining Services Worker you play a critical role in the customer experience. From assisting in the preparation and service of food, to maintaining the presentation of the dining halls, to assisting guests, we have a variety of roles and will find the right one for you!<br><br>Dining Service Workers earn a paycheck and more:</div><ol><li>Student employee meal privileges.</li><li>Flexible schedules (10/20 hours/week) that work around your classes and activities.</li><li>Convenient on-campus locations.</li><li>Opportunities to advance to leadership positions such as Captain, Meal Manager and Student Unit Manager.</li><li>Valuable work experience to add to your resume.</li><li>Learn important job skills including interpersonal communications, team dynamics, dependability and time management.</li><li>A fun and welcoming environment.</li></ol> Cafe West New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Student Affairs - New Brunswic-L3 8455 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1109 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266336 2025-12-31T09:51:22-05:00 2025-12-31T09:51:22-05:00 POSTDOCTORAL POSITIONS ON THE CMS EXPERIMENT RUTGERS UNIVERSITY <div>We have immediate availability for postdoctoral associate researchers in experimental particle physics on the CMS experiment at Rutgers University.<br><br></div><div>Our group, led by Profs. John Paul Chou, Yuri Gershtein, Eva Halkiadakis, Amit Lath, Sunil Somalwar, and Scott Thomas, has major involvement in physics, software, and hardware of the CMS experiment. We collaborate closely with our particle theorist colleagues at Rutgers. The successful candidate is expected to participate in analysis of CMS data and to contribute to our responsibilities on the HL-LHC Upgrades on L1 Track Trigger and Outer Tracker modules production. The group has additional responsibilities on both the HCAL and BRIL subsystems.<br><br></div><div>Applicants should provide their curriculum vitae, bibliography of publications listing only those articles to which the candidate has made crucial contributions, and a signed cover letter that includes a statement of accomplishments and interests. The candidate should also list at least three reference letter writers to be collected by the ROCS system.<br><br></div><div>Further questions can be directed to John Paul Chou, who coordinates postdoctoral hiring for the group&nbsp; (<a href=\"mailto:johnpaul@physics.rutgers.edu\"><strong>johnpaul@physics.rutgers.edu</strong></a>).<br><br></div> Physics & Astronomy New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 8126 25FA0934 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280157 2026-08-31T08:43:59-04:00 2026-08-31T08:44:00-04:00 Staff Nurse PT Days UCHC SWSP (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Part Time Staff Nurse for the Southwoods State Prison located in Bridgeton, NJ. The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus for inmates in the New Jersey Department of Corrections.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br>* Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the resident-patient including adolescents (13-17 years), adults (18 to 64 years) and their family within the framework established by the correctional system.<br>* Performs assessments of resident-patient in a variety of settings such as initial intake area, health care unit for sick call, emergency situations in housing, chronic care clinics and infirmary.<br>* Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br>* Identifies inmate-centered goals and nursing objectives and implements prescribed interventions and solutions for the identified problems.<br>* Plans nursing care by identification of resident-patient needs based on assessments. Makes appropriate, timely referrals and initiates appropriate nursing care based on institutional policies and procedures.<br>* As team leader or charge nurse, delegates duties to other health care team members based on their skill, knowledge and experience and guides the provision of care by others.</div> UCHC-South Woods Psn-Ancillary RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7685 Bridgeton NJ 26ST0538 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278578 2026-07-10T11:05:18-04:00 2026-07-10T11:05:19-04:00 Staff Nurse PT Eves UCHC BSP <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Part Time Staff Nurse for the Bayside State Prison located in Leesburg, NJ<br><br>The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus for inmates in the New Jersey Department of Corrections.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br>* Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the resident-patient including adolescents (13-17 years), adults (18 to 64 years) and their family within the framework established by the correctional system.<br>* Performs assessments of resident-patient in a variety of settings such as initial intake area, health care unit for sick call, emergency situations in housing, chronic care clinics and infirmary.<br>* Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br>* Identifies inmate-centered goals and nursing objectives and implements prescribed interventions and solutions for the identified problems.<br>* Plans nursing care by identification of resident-patient needs based on assessments. Makes appropriate, timely referrals and initiates appropriate nursing care based on institutional policies and procedures.<br>* As team leader or charge nurse, delegates duties to other health care team members based on their skill, knowledge and experience and guides the provision of care by others&nbsp;</div> UCHC Bayside State Prison Anci RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7684 Leesburg NJ 26ST0660 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/268504 2026-02-03T16:42:07-05:00 2026-02-03T16:42:07-05:00 Open Rank- multiple positions available <div>The Center Emerging and Re-emerging Pathogens and the Public Health Research Institute at New Jersey Medical School, Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences, located in Newark, NJ, invites applications for full time, tenure-track appointments at the Professor level. We are currently recruiting candidates with expertise in basic and applied research in Covid-19, Tuberculosis or Tuberculosis and HIV. The position will be supported by a competitive start-up package with exceptional candidates being considered for further support as Chancellor Scholars.</div> NJMS - PHRI Center RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7422 21FA0962 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279656 2026-08-17T15:38:46-04:00 2026-08-17T15:38:47-04:00 Staff Nurse - Per Diem - Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a per diem Staff Nurse for the Inpatient Units, Crisis and Acute Psychiatric Services within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the per diem Staff Nurse position is to deliver person centered goal directed nursing care in alignment with the departmental and hospital policies and procedures and all regulatory requirements. The staff nurse functions as a member of the interdisciplinary team; participates in quality improvement activities, educational activities, and supports research endeavors. The role is consistent with the scope and standards outlined in the Psychiatric-Mental Health Nursing: Scope and Standards of Practice.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Incorporates specific assessment of bio/psycho/social/sexual/spiritual status at the time of admission and throughout care; compares to age norms as one indicator of health, actual or potential deviations from health, and individualized need for nursing intervention.</li><li>Documents initial nursing assessment and individualized, goal directed plan of care considering the psychological, social, physical health and safety needs of the patient, in accordance with unit standards.</li><li>Develops, discusses and communicates a realistic, individualized plan of care for each patient, in collaboration with the patient, family and significant other in an effort to promote wellness and recovery.</li><li>Demonstrates the skills and judgment necessary to implement the plan of care, nursing interventions and procedures as necessary for the care and safety of the patient.</li><li>Evaluates identified problems and care provided and the patient’s responses are reassessed in order to meet the patient and family/significant other needs to ensure overall quality of care delivered.</li><li>Maintains concurrent and accurate documentation of nursing care provided to ensure the integration of information for use by the multidisciplinary team, in order to ensure quality care.</li><li>Maintains current knowledge/certification/licensure. Pursues professional growth and development.</li><li>Demonstrates respect and regard for the dignity of all individuals served, families, visitors and fellow employees to ensure a professional, responsible and courteous environment.</li></ul> UBHC - Acute Psychological Ser RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7987 Piscataway NJ 26ST0802 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279961 2026-08-25T14:28:24-04:00 2026-08-25T14:28:25-04:00 Research Teaching Specialist V <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Researching Teaching Specialist V in the Department of Microbiology, Biochemistry &amp; Molecular Genetics with the New Jersey Medical School (NJMS).&nbsp;<br><br>Under the direction of the Principal Investigator, Laboratory Manager, Research Teaching Specialist V, performs research activities. Performs work requiring application of standard techniques and procedures.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>As directed, performs various research and technical operations relative to the ongoing investigatory activities of the laboratory.</li><li>Participates in the evaluation of existing procedures suggesting revisions where necessary, and proposing new procedures where required.</li><li>Assists with training fellows, medical students and lab technicians in laboratory techniques as directed.</li><li>Responsible for submitting purchase recommendations to his/her supervisor.</li><li>Ensures that laboratory equipment is maintained in good working orders.</li><li>Keeps detailed records of procedures and experiments.&nbsp;</li></ul> NJMS - Emerging Pathogen Affil RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7485 Newark NJ 26ST1656 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277765 2026-06-25T11:07:34-04:00 2026-06-25T11:07:35-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse PT Eves UCHC NSP (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Part Time Licensed Practical Nurse for Northern State Prison located in Newark, NJ<br><br>The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br>* Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs.<br>* Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.<br>* Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.<br>* Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.<br>* Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.<br>* Documents all aspects of patient care.</div> UCHC Northern State Prison Phy_DUP RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7679 Newark NJ 26ST0679 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275341 2026-05-19T08:25:20-04:00 2026-05-19T08:25:21-04:00 Pediatric Bone Marrow and Stem Cell Transplantation Clinical Researcher (Assistant Professor) <div>Rutgers Cancer Institute is seeking a clinical researcher specializing in pediatric bone marrow transplant, with strong clinical and educational skills. Candidates should have demonstrated experience in <strong>pediatric bone marrow and stem cell transplantation.</strong>Responsibilities would center on providing care to children, adolescents and young adults receiving stem cell transplantation, cellular therapies, or gene therapy. Unique opportunities exist for collaborations between clinical and research programs, clinical trials research, cancer chemoprevention, clinical and basic pharmacology, novel cell therapy constructs, and participation in a broad range of teaching initiatives with medical students, housestaff, and fellows.<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate will have the opportunity to build on a strong foundation of excellence, including preeminent research, renowned clinical services, a CART cell therapy program, gene therapy, and prominent educational programs. The academic appointment will be in the Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School with a resident faculty appointment at the Rutgers Cancer Institute. Faculty at the Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School will have the opportunity to engage in exciting teaching and mentorship activities for fellows and graduate students. The position will be 0.7-0.8 cFTE based on their experience in clinical research, with clinical responsibilities in BMT clinic at Rutgers Cancer Institute -New Brunswick.</div><div><br></div><div>Applicants must have an M.D. or D.O. degree, board certification in Pediatric Hematology/Oncology. Must have training in bone marrow and stem cell transplant and/or 2+ years of experience working in stem cell transplant or cellular therapy. Faculty rank and salary is commensurate with experience.</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://www.cinj.org/about-cinj/faculty-opportunities\"><strong>See all our open faculty positions here</strong></a>!</div> CINJ - Pediatric Hematology/On RBHS Chancellor-L2 Cancer Institute of New Jersey-L3 7910 26FA0377 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266266 2025-12-31T09:42:21-05:00 2025-12-31T09:42:22-05:00 Post Doctorial Associate <div>Our group is seeking a postdoctoral associate to work on mechanistic and translational research projects funded by NIH investigating drug-induced kidney injury and identifying factors that influence the likelihood of drug toxicity/failure. Based at Rutgers University in New Jersey, the Brunetti team has access to outstanding core facilities, dynamic researchers and trainees, and excellent opportunities for career development. State-of-the-art Core Facilities are available for Genomics, Genetics, Proteomics, Imaging, Histopathology, Analytical Chemistry, Flow Cytometry, and Cell Sorting, High</div><div>Content Imaging, Gene Editing, and Biostatistics. Postdocs can become members of various professional and social networks of trainees fostering peer support and inter-laboratory collaboration and participating in the pharmaceutical sciences conference series. available immediately to study molecular mechanisms of disease and the influence of acute illness on drug disposition and outcomes. Applicants must have Ph.D. plus strong expertise in molecular biology, cell culture, mammalian cellular/in vivo biology, and gene transcription/ regulation. Applicants having RNA sequencing and LCMS experience will be a plus.</div> Pharmacy Practice & Administra RBHS Chancellor-L2 Ernest Mario School of Pharmac-L3 6720 25FA0688 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280141 2026-08-28T16:59:44-04:00 2026-08-28T16:59:45-04:00 Senior Department Administrator, SPVR <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Senior Department Administrator SPVR for the Music Department, Mason Gross School of the Arts (MGSA).&nbsp; Reporting directly to Director of Music Department and dotted line reporting MGSA Associate Dean for Finance &amp; Administration, serves as the chief non-academic officer for the Music Department.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Among the key duties of the position are the following:</div><ul><li>Provides administrative leadership in department accounting and budgeting, purchasing, personnel and payroll, facilities coordination, events, and all administrative, operational, and financial functions.</li><li>Manages departmental accounts, unrestricted and restricted accounts, including and not limited to, faculty research funds and grants, gifts, and endowment.</li><li>&nbsp;Builds and oversees a team of staff and ensuring an inviting, professional, responsive atmosphere for students, faculty, staff, and other stakeholders.</li></ul> Music New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Mason Gross School of Arts Dea-L3 6865 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1679 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278551 2026-07-10T09:02:35-04:00 2026-07-10T09:02:35-04:00 Habilitation Counselor <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Habilitation Counselor for the Outpatient Treatment – Certified Community Behavioral Health Clinic (CCBHC) Case Management Department within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Habilitation Counselor position is to provide site and community-based case management and supported employment services to individuals receiving treatment services through UBHC’s Outpatient Certified Community Behavioral Health Clinic (CCBHC) services.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Supports individuals to gain access to needed medical, social, education, mental health, addiction, co-occurring, and other services.</li><li>Provides psychoeducation to individuals served, promoting wellness and recovery goals.</li><li>Demonstrates the ability to engage and establish a working relationship with and provide services to individuals who are diagnosed with a serious and persistent mental illness and co-occurring disorders who present engagement challenges.</li><li>Collaborates effectively with members of the department, and with external departments, staff, referral sources, other service providers and social support networks to provide services and rehabilitative care for consumers and families.</li><li>Communicates observations and information about the consumer to the program supervisor, and all staff involved with the services delivered by the program.</li><li>Maintains appropriate clinical records according to the time frames and quality guidelines established by UBHC policy and applicable accrediting organization standards.</li><li>Actively participates in and contributes to smooth functioning and operations of unit.</li></ul> UBHC - Outpatient Newark RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8059 Newark NJ 26ST0511 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267879 2026-01-23T11:55:57-05:00 2026-01-23T11:55:57-05:00 Part Time Course Support (Course Assistant) - Summer 2026 <div>The Professional Science Master’s Program (PSM) invites applications for Course Support (Course Assistants) for the Summer 2026 term.<br><br>Successful candidates will be responsible for the following:</div><ul><li>Assisting faculty with their course(s) (may include traditional lecture, hybrid, and/or fully online courses); may be required to provide LMS software assistance.</li><li>Attending all assigned course meetings (at the discretion of the faculty member teaching the course)</li><li>Preparing course materials (i.e., syllabi, presentations, hand-outs, reading materials, etc.) as directed by the faculty member.</li><li>Providing constructive feedback to students as well as critical instruction regarding student work and academic standards</li><li>Responding to student emails and inquiries, and address student concerns</li><li>Practice innovative educational methodology</li></ul> Professional Science Masters New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Professional Science Masters-L3 6665 26FA0061 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280286 2026-09-01T13:50:10-04:00 2026-09-01T13:50:11-04:00 Theatre, Gallery and Event Staff (Part Time) <div>Rutgers University-Camden SASC seek multiple part -time positions for Theatre, Gallery and Event Staff. This position will assist the Department and the Production Manager (Technical Supervisor) with the construction of scenery and set design, setting up lights, sound equipment, props and special effects for productions, concerts, and events in theaters and exhibitions in the galleries, as well as front-of-house operations and audience support for the Department. Duties may vary dependent on specific role and department needs but may include the following tasks: - Set up and operation of lighting and/or sound equipment - Construction of scenery, props - Operation of special effects - Front of house operations and audience support Qualified candidates will have live technical theater and stagehand experience, or experience with audience development and front-of-house operations. Lead positions in audio, lighting, video, stage management and scenic carpentry are available.</div> Fine Arts Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 6757 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278990 2026-07-21T00:19:47-04:00 2026-07-21T00:19:49-04:00 Research Project Assistant <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Research Project Assistant at the Center for Pharmacoepidemiology and Treatment Science (PETS). The Research Project Assistant will have the opportunity to work in a collegial work environment to support innovative, multidisciplinary studies. The position will directly report to the Center’s Director of Sponsored Research and will provide support services to PETS faculty and project managers at the Center by assisting with research proposals and ongoing research projects, and by supporting the day-to-day administrative operations of the Center. The Research Project Assistant will also assist in research in the areas of pharmacoepidemiology, medical devices, and use of real-world data. They will contribute to impactful research studies focusing on medical devices, including the drafting and implementation of research protocols, publication in scientific journals, and have opportunities to present methods and research findings.<br><br>Among the key duties of the position are the following:</div><ul><li>Conducts comprehensive literature review to support research projects and grant proposals.</li><li>Provides assistance with required regulatory documentation (e.g., Institutional Review Board, Data Use Agreements).</li><li>Provides basic support in the creation of code lists and data tables and conduct of data analyses as directed by Center faculty and staff.</li><li>Assists with ongoing project support under the guidance of the faculty PI or project manager, including, but not limited to, scheduling and taking of minutes, providing assistance with reporting to funders, submission of procurement materials, and engaging with coinvestigators, consultants, and other collaborators.</li><li>Assists with grant submissions, protocol development, and manuscript development through drafting of passages under guidance from faculty, the review of formatting, spelling and grammar, the creation of figures and tables, and the submission of conference abstracts and manuscripts.</li><li>Provides general administrative support in support of PETS faculty, Center leadership, and PETS operations</li></ul> Institute for Health, Health C RBHS Chancellor-L2 Institute for Health, Health C-L3 8086 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1514 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/271614 2026-03-25T11:10:19-04:00 2026-03-25T11:10:20-04:00 Faculty (Open Rank) of Obstetrics and Gynecology – Maternal Fetal Medicine <div>The Division of Maternal Fetal Medicine in the Department of Obstetrics, Gynecology, and Reproductive Sciences at Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School seeks an accomplished Maternal Fetal Medicine specialist to join our academic faculty. This is an <strong>open‑rank position</strong>, and the successful candidate’s experience and qualifications will determine the academic rank at which they are appointed.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The faculty member will contribute to the division’s clinical, educational, and research missions while providing high‑quality, patient‑centered care for high‑risk pregnancies. The role includes collaboration with faculty, fellows, residents, and medical students, as well as active participation in clinical practice, teaching, and scholarly activity.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>This position is well‑suited for a clinician‑educator and researcher committed to excellence in maternal fetal medicine and dedicated to advancing clinical care, research, and education within a collaborative academic environment.</div> RWJ - OB/GYN MFM/Atu Spmc RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7791 25FA0857 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279511 2026-08-11T12:33:53-04:00 2026-08-11T12:33:55-04:00 RBHS Instructor/Assistant Professor; Non-Tenure Track <div>The Department of Community Health is searching for one (1) full time General Dentists at the rank of RBHS Instructor/Assistant Professor, Non-Tenure Track in Somerdale, NJ (Camden County) at the RSDM University Dental Center at Somerdale. This faculty member in the Department of Community Health provides support for students, assure timely care for the patients, serve as a nucleus for interdepartmental faculty communication and provide all phases of patient care as required.<br><br>Essential Duties and Responsibilities:<br>• Oversee all aspects of patient care and ensuring proper post-treatment management, including recare;<br>• Ensure that the standards, policies and procedures of RSDM, as outlined in the Clinic Manual, Radiation Hazard, Infection Control, Patient’s Bill of Rights, and RSDM Confidentiality policies, and Quality Assurance protocols are followed at the sites.<br>• Supervise and instruct students in their respective disciplines, by demonstration when required;<br>• Review the records of patients who treatment has been documented as completed;<br>• Review patient records prior to termination of patient treatment. Authorization is documented in the consultation section of the patient’s record;<br>• Ensure, with site faculty, that RSDM standards for the education of students are maintained;<br>• Conduct small group discussions with students when possible;<br>• Participate in CODE faculty standardization and calibration;<br>• Perform evaluation of students’ competencies.<br>• Assists in quality and quantity review for all dental personnel when requested.<br>• Remains current in the field of dentistry on a level applicable to the title.<br>• Accomplishes dentistry using pharmacological adjuncts depending on individual circumstances and dentist qualifications.<br>• Consults with the medical staff in cases showing oral manifestations of medical conditions.<br>• Is available for consultation by the medical staff in cases of oral pathology and other related conditions of common interest.<br>• Arranges program and treatment for patients experiencing oral trauma, oral pain, oral infection and other pathology.<br>• Assists in conducting program of preventive dentistry, dental education and oral hygiene.<br>• Diagnoses and treats diseases, injuries and malformations of teeth, gingiva, mucosa, and related oral structures with reasonable patient acceptable sensitivity.<br>• Cleans, restores, extracts and replaces teeth using rotary and hand instruments, dental appliances, medications and surgical instruments.<br>• Administers local anesthesia and other supportive medication.<br>• Keeps such records and reports as are necessary for the discharge and control of his/her patients.<br>• Serves on call, administratively, operationally and clinically and handles dental emergencies.<br>• Understands and adheres to Rutgers’ compliance standards as they appear in RBHS’s Corporate Compliance Policy, Code of Conduct and Conflict of Interest Policy.<br>• Keeps abreast of all pertinent federal, state and Rutgers’ regulations, laws and policies as they presently exist and as they change or are modified.<br>• Ensures that the staff are trained and evaluated on their knowledge of and adherence to compliance policies and procedures specific to their jobs.<br>• Performs other related duties as assigned.</div> RSDM-Extramural Clinics RBHS Chancellor-L2 Rutgers School of Dental Medic-L3 7555 26FA0183 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279762 2026-08-20T09:13:18-04:00 2026-08-20T09:13:19-04:00 Licensed Pratical Nurse Per Diem UCHC ADTC <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Per Diem Licensed Practical Nurse for the Adult Diagnostic Treatment Center located in Avenel, NJ<br><br>The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment. Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.</div><div><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs.</li><li>Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.</li><li>Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.</li><li>Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.</li><li>Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.</li><li>Documents all aspects of patient care.</li></ul> UCHC Adult Treatmt Center Nurs RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7688 Avenel NJ 26ST1365 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277116 2026-06-15T11:35:07-04:00 2026-06-15T11:35:07-04:00 Assistant/Associate Professor - Multiple Positions (OB/GYN Generalist/Hospitalist) <div>The Department of Obstetrics, Gynecology and Reproductive Health at Rutgers – New Jersey Medical School has full time positions available at the Assistant or Associate Professor level, depending on experience, for Board Certified or Board Eligible Physicians, as a generalist specialist in the Division of General Obstetrics and Gynecology. Family Planning Specialists are welcomed to apply to the position. Hospitalist, laborist and nocturnist options can be considered for these roles, depending on the candidate.</div><div>The generalist will treat diseases and disorders of the female reproductive system, as well as caring for women during the prenatal, in labor, and postnatal periods. The generalist will perform all aspects of generalist OB/GYN practice including cesarean delivery, hysterectomy, and all standard outpatient OB/GYN procedures.</div><div><br></div><div>The practice is based at University Hospital using the renovated labor floor, the Ambulatory Care Center and other sites associated with Rutgers New Jersey Medical School. The practice is fully integrated in the teaching mission of the Rutgers New Jersey Medical School with faculty appointments in the medical school. The scope and breath of the faculty’s clinical activities promote professional interests while covering the clinical needs of the service and the educational mission. Professional interests in global health, clinical research, patient safety/quality and addiction medicine are encouraged. Leadership opportunities are available commensurate with experience and interest.</div> NJMS - Obstetrics & Gynocology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7455 24FA0876 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274105 2026-05-01T08:18:36-04:00 2026-05-01T08:18:36-04:00 Lecturers-Physics <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the Faculty of Arts &amp; Sciences, Department of Physics, seeks new lecturers to teach in various topics within the discipline for courses in Fall 2026, Winter 2027, Spring 2027 and/or Summer 2027 semester(s). The instructor will present course material during the assigned course times, hold office hours, administer exams, assign grades, and coordinate any other requirements related to course instruction.</div> Physics Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 6768 26FA0431 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266054 2025-12-31T09:21:45-05:00 2025-12-31T09:21:46-05:00 Assistant Professor, Pediatric Otolaryngology <div>Rutgers New Jersey Medical School, Department of Otolaryngology-Head and Neck Surgery is recruiting a fellowship-trained Pediatric Otolaryngologist to join our expanding faculty.<br><br></div><div>Experience in Clinical Outcomes Research is desired. The successful applicant will join a very busy Pediatric and Adult practice, provide care for complex pathology, and join a quickly growing clinical and research enterprise. The Department collaborates with an extensive array of health care providers across the Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences units.<br><br></div><div>Applicants for this position must be able to perform at a high level both clinically and academically.&nbsp; Salary will be commensurate with ability, training, and experience and demonstrated prior performance.<br><br></div> NJMS - Otolaryngology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7505 22FA0039 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280051 2026-08-26T15:01:07-04:00 2026-08-26T15:01:08-04:00 Mental Health Clinician III <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Mental Health Clinician III for the Emergency Screening Department in Newark within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Mental Health Clinician III is to provide comprehensive evaluation, assessment and therapeutic intervention to address the psychological, emotional and social needs of individuals served by the unit. Duties include formulating evaluations, developing and implementing treatment plans, conducting individual, group, and family therapy and providing case management functions.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Actively participates in and contributes to smooth functioning of the department and demonstrates initiative and flexibility regarding work assignments.</li><li>Effectively contributes to and supports an environment that enhances the positive self-image of individuals served and preserves their human dignity.</li><li>Consistently provides individual, group and family therapy based on sound clinical judgment.</li><li>Adapts the assessment and treatment processes to accommodate variations in readiness for treatment/change, and implications of age, cultural, medical, economic or other relevant factors.</li><li>Formulates clinically appropriate evaluations consistent with Clinical Records standards in accordance with prescribed time as indicated by periodic record review.</li><li>Effectively collaborates as clinically indicated with other staff members, referral sources, community resources, service providers, case management organizations, families and support systems</li><li>Actively participates in program development within program services.</li></ul> UBHC - Emergency Screening New RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8052 Newark NJ 25ST2313 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278215 2026-07-02T14:36:50-04:00 2026-07-02T14:36:51-04:00 Dental Assistant II <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Dental Assistant II within the Rutgers Health University Dental Associates at the Rutgers School of Dental Medicine.<br><br>The Dental Assistant II provides support to faculty at RHUDA-New Brunswick. In this role, The Dental Assistant II performs work related to the care, sterilization, packing, and disbursement of equipment and supplies. The Dental Assistant II also maintains all aspects of sterilization procedures related to dental instruments and supplies associated with patient care within the various clinical operations. Additionally, the Dental Assistant II provides chair side dental assisting to providers in all disciplines and takes various dental x-rays as assigned by providers.<br><br>Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Reviews providers schedule and sets up treatment rooms for procedures being performed.</li><li>Assists various faculty chairside in the delivery of outstanding quality care.</li><li>Maintains inventory of supplies, instruments and equipment according to department policy. Restocks equipment and supplies in the examination rooms and supply area. Reports depleted items following the established procedure.</li><li>Checks returned instruments and prepares them for sterilization.</li><li>Examines equipment to detect leaks, worn or loose parts, or other indication of disrepair, verifying that equipment functions properly. Reports findings of defective equipment and maintenance needs as per department protocol.</li><li>Exposes and scans digital radiographs using digital sensor or phosphor plate.</li><li>Exposes Panoramic, Cephalometric and CBCT x-rays using specialized machinery.</li><li>Assists with maintaining established departmental policies and procedures, objectives, and quality improvement, safety and environmental and infection control standards.</li><li>Operates and monitors sterilization equipment, steam autoclaves, sonic washers and other sterilization equipment. Decontaminates, processes and sterilizes instruments and treatment equipment with proper handling to prevent loss or damage. Ensures quality and consistency of the sterilization process.</li><li>Checks for past due patient visits. Aids front desk area with scheduling patient visits.</li></ul> RSDM - New Brunswick RBHS Chancellor-L2 Rutgers School of Dental Medic-L3 8282 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1462 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266403 2026-01-04T21:32:33-05:00 2026-01-04T21:32:34-05:00 Post Doctoral Associate <div>The Rutgers Air Quality Lab led by Dr. Xiaomeng Jin within the Department of Environmental Sciences at Rutgers University invites applications for a Postdoctoral Research Associate to work on remote sensing of air quality. Emphasis will be placed on using satellite observations to understand the impacts of wildfires and prescribed burning on air quality. The candidatemust have a Ph.D. in a related field (e.g., Atmospheric Science, Remote Sensing, Earth Science, Environmental Science, Environmental Engineering) by the time of appointment. Background in atmospheric remote sensing is strongly preferred. Experience with atmospheric models (e.g., GEOS-Chem, CMAQ) and skills in python, Fortran and high-performance computing are also desired.</div> Environmental Science New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 7137 25FA0918 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280189 2026-08-31T10:49:28-04:00 2026-08-31T10:49:29-04:00 Forensic Mental Health Clinician UCHC SWSP <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care (UCHC) is seeking a Forensic Mental Health Clinician for the Southwoods State Prison located in Bridgeton, NJ. Reporting to the Clinician Supervisor, the Forensic Mental Health Clinician completes specialized psychological testing and assessment of clinical needs of adult inmates sentenced to the Department of Corrections.<br><br>Among the key duties for this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Arrives at DSM IV diagnoses with precision and accuracy through psychological testing and evaluation sessions.</li><li>Provides crisis intervention, individual and group psychotherapy and psycho-education programming as clinically indicated to assigned inmates.</li><li>Involves inmates and Department of Corrections staff in developing achievable and understandable psychosocial treatment plans.</li><li>Advocates for appropriate resources for inmates based on assessed needs.</li><li>Manages caseload demands effectively while considering both qualities of care and the security needs of the Department of Corrections.</li><li>Assumes overall case management responsibilities for assigned inmates including coordination of treatment and liaison with community agencies; maintains appropriate inmate records.</li><li>Demonstrates competency in psychological testing and in recognizing the unique needs and behaviors of adult inmates and seniors, and individual therapies.</li></ul> UCHC South Woods Prison Physic RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7672 Bridgeton NJ 26ST0857 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278631 2026-07-10T13:48:39-04:00 2026-07-10T13:48:40-04:00 Secretary II - Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Secretary II for the Brandt Behavioral Health Treatment Center &amp; Retreat within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Secretary II is to provide secretarial and administrative services to Unit<br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Ensures completion of typing assignments in accordance with established department format.</li><li>Prepares and maintains attendance records for the department.</li><li>Acts as principal liaison with the Access/Transfer Center on daily operations.</li><li>Coordinates meeting arrangements on an as needed basis in a professional and courteous manner.</li><li>Notifies participants of meetings particulars in a timely manner.</li><li>Prepares and distributes minutes within appropriate time frames.</li><li>Maintains appropriate log sheets and records needed for efficient operation of department.</li><li>Receives, audits and submits staff’s daily schedules to data control.</li><li>Prepares weekly or monthly reports for department staff review.</li><li>Greets patients and visitors in a prompt and courteous fashion.</li></ul> Brandt Center Retreat RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8887 Piscataway NJ 25ST1971 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/269365 2026-02-17T13:50:48-05:00 2026-02-17T13:50:49-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor Behavioral Neurology <div>FUNCTION: Participate in clinical care of patients with Behavioral Disorders, Alzheimer’s Disease, according to a schedule determined by the Chair.<br>ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES include the following:<br>1. Evaluates Behavioral Neurology patients.<br>2. Monitors communication with other Behavioral Neurology providers for patient to be seen on an emergency basis.<br>3. Maintains follow-up care for Behavioral Neurology patients.<br>4. Partaking in our Neurology Grand Rounds<br>5. Perform night call and weekend inpatient coverage at Barnabas-Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital in equal proportion with the other faculty in rotation.<br>6. Participate in the teaching mission of RWJMS to the extent determined in consultation with the Department Chair. This may include teaching and mentoring medical students, neurology residents, Behavioral Neurology fellows and rotators from other departments. The teaching will take place in inpatient and outpatient settings and in seminars and occasional formal lectures in the preclinical setting. It may also include supervising a weekly resident Continuity Clinic.<br>7. Participate as site principal investigator or sub-investigator in clinical trials sponsored by industry and other sources.<br>8. Perform and publish other research to the extent consistent with the track of the appointment (Professional Practice, Clinical Educator or Clinical Scholar).<br>9. Refer patients as appropriate to clinical trials and other research activity in the department and otherwise participate in the scholarly productivity and culture of the department.<br>10. Participate in community service responsibilities of the department in such areas as providing neurological care for indigent patients and teaching or advising lay community groups in the area of Behavioral Neurology.<br>11. Participate in the administrative tasks of the department of Neurology and RWJMS. This will include membership in standing or ad hoc departmental and institutional committees as determined in consultation with the Chair and according to RWJMS By-Laws; and attending departmental and institutional faculty meetings.<br>12. Maintain knowledge through continuing education and by maintaining Board certification in neurology and any relevant subspecialty certification.</div> RWJ - Neurology RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7784 26FA0125 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280441 2026-09-04T09:39:38-04:00 2026-09-04T09:39:39-04:00 Executive Assistant to Chair <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking an Executive Assistant to Chair in the Department of Otolaryngology-Head and Neck Surgery within the New Jersey Medical School (NJMS).&nbsp;<br><br>This position provides advanced, diversified and confidential administrative and management support within a department or executive office of the University. Exercises considerable discretion and independent judgement. Coordinates projects, correspondence, reports, and fiscal procedures for the department.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>Provides support to the Chair and the Chair’s Office.</li><li>Plans and schedules the work needs of the department to make maximum effective utilization of time, resources, equipment and material within budgetary requirements.</li><li>Conducts research and studies on assigned administrative matters and prepares reports with background material, providing input and support for policy decisions and formulation.</li><li>Coordinates projects and prepares correspondence, reports, and handles fiscal procedures for the Chair.</li><li>Updates and maintains administrative policies and procedures applicable to the department to maintain a stable, efficient and cooperative working environment. Analyzes complex information requests. Investigates and develops solutions to administrative problems, identifies and eliminates unnecessary practices.</li><li>Identifies departmental needs and maintain confidential files and correspondence.&nbsp;</li></ul> NJMS - Otolaryngology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7505 Newark NJ 26ST1722 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279361 2026-08-06T12:05:05-04:00 2026-08-06T12:05:06-04:00 Facilities Manager <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Facilities Manager for the Division of Institutional Planning &amp; Operations (IP&amp;O). Under the direction of the Campus Manager, ensures the safe, efficient and effective operation and maintenance of all physical systems and real property at the ICPH/RBL or other NJMS Laboratory facilities.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Assists the Campus Manager in the development and implementation of departmental goals, operating objectives and protocols, and adds value to all Physical Plant provided services.</li><li>Interacts with the NJMS Director of Facilities for coordination of user needs in the RBL, ICPH and other NJMS Laboratory facilities.</li><li>The Facility Manager will be responsible for developing and managing the overall maintenance of the HVAC/Mechanical and Electrical Systems, as well as all other facility related systems throughout related facilities.</li><li>Develops test protocols, monitors required periodic inspections and required reports and provides oversight of staff Engineers of the RBL/ICPH facilities.</li></ul> Facilities Maintenance Newark EVP & Chief Admin Officer Institutional Planning & Optns-L3 8412 Newark NJ 26ST1594 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/276078 2026-05-29T09:51:07-04:00 2026-05-29T09:51:08-04:00 MGSA – Department of Theater – (Fall 2026) <div>The Department of Theater, Mason Gross School of the Arts, Rutgers University invites applications for part-time instructional and academic support for undergraduate and graduate in a variety of areas, including but not limited to: Acting, Directing, Design, Production, Play/Screenwriting, and Theater History, Theory, and Appreciation.</div> Theater Arts New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Mason Gross School of Arts Dea-L3 6866 26FA0499 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/273434 2026-04-21T14:01:11-04:00 2026-04-21T14:01:12-04:00 Lecturers / Coadjutants <div>The Department of Labor Studies and Employment Relations at Rutgers University seeks to hire lecturers who can teach a range of courses (i.e., Intro to Labor Studies; Youth and Work; Occupational Safety and Health;; History of Labor and Work in the U.S. 1880-1945;) in our undergraduate and graduate programs. The instructors will present course materials during assigned course times, hold office hours, administer exams, assign grades, complete assessment of student learning reports, and coordinate any other requirements related to course instruction. Rutgers University is a leading research university that has a culturally-diverse student population of 67,620 students from all 50 states and more than 120 countries including 48,040 undergraduates and more than 19,580 graduate students. Our department offers courses online, in person in New Brunswick, and in person in a select number of off-campus courses in partnerships between Rutgers and Brookdale and Mercer Community Colleges.</div> Labor Studies & Employee Relat New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Management & Labor R-L3 7195 25FA1199 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/265769 2025-12-23T12:17:23-05:00 2025-12-23T12:17:23-05:00 Deputy Director of Rutgers Brain Health Institute <div>The <a href=\"https://brainhealthinstitute.rutgers.edu/\"><strong>Rutgers Brain Health Institute (BHI)</strong></a> serves as the umbrella neuroscience organization across Rutgers University, encompassing over 300 research laboratories and 900 trainees. Members include faculty from 50 departments and 14 schools at Rutgers. This represents one of the largest concentrations of neuroscience- and brain health-related research talent in the world. Our work is organized into four key focus areas: neurodevelopment, neurodegeneration, motivational and affective neuroscience, and cognitive and sensory neuroscience. Since our inception in 2014, BHI has experienced tremendous growth. We have successfully recruited over 48 tenure-track faculty members, with more on the way, and established five Centers of Research Excellence. These include centers dedicated to addiction research, autism research, Alzheimer’s disease research, human neuroimaging, and computational cognitive neuropsychiatry. Additional centers in pain research and neurotechnology are being developed.<br><br></div><div>We seek an accomplished scientist, at the Professor or Associate Professor level, to join the BHI as its new Deputy Director. The deputy director will play a key role in helping to develop and execute the vision and mission of BHI in addition to leading an active federally funded research program in their area of research interest. The Deputy Director will be responsible for leading the implementation of <a href=\"https://brainhealthinstitute.rutgers.edu/strategic-plan/\"><strong>the BHI Strategic Plan</strong></a>, as well as revising and developing new plan goals.&nbsp; In addition, the Deputy Director will lead BHI efforts to develop research training and mentoring programs for physician-researchers. The Deputy Director will also help recruit and retain physician-researchers in neuroscience and brain health research.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>The ideal candidate will be a leader in a research area within neuroscience or brain health research with a strong, federally funded research program, who can leverage, stimulate, and lead translational science approaches from basic science to clinical to population levels.&nbsp; We seek candidates who have a broad understanding and vision of translational neuroscience and strongly believe in advancing brain health through cutting-edge interdisciplinary research. The ideal candidate will also need to be comfortable with a forward-facing role, consistent with the high profile this role will hold at Rutgers and within New Jersey.&nbsp; Physician-researchers are especially encouraged to apply. With two teaching hospitals and neuroscience labs in Newark and New Brunswick/Piscataway, an affiliation with the largest and most accomplished health systems in the state (RWJBH), as well as proximity to the New York, Princeton and Philadelphia neuroscience communities, Rutgers BHI offers tremendous collaborative opportunities and core facilities to support and grow outstanding research programs. &nbsp;<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate will be a visionary leader who can foster collaborations among existing research and training programs, develop new research opportunities based on relevant federal, state and industry priorities, and actively engage in BHI philanthropic initiatives. Applicants must have an MD/PhD, MD, or PhD, with demonstrated ability to lead an independent NIH-funded research program. Prior leadership and administrative experience in academia will be important. We offer substantial resources to support the deputy director’s research activities, as well as activities across BHI. With a NIH CTSA, Rutgers also offers unique opportunities to speed the translation of research discoveries into clinical trials and improved patient care. Outstanding core facilities will support this position. Rutgers values a culturally diverse faculty; we strongly encourage applications from female and candidates underrepresented in medicine. Applicants should submit a CV and statement of research accomplishments and vision to Dr. Carlos Pato, the Chair of the search committee, at <a href=\"mailto:bhi@bhi.rutgers.edu\"><strong>bhi@bhi.rutgers.edu</strong></a>.&nbsp;</div> Brain Health Institute RBHS Chancellor-L2 Brain Health Institute-L3 8146 25FA1265 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278580 2026-07-10T11:08:49-04:00 2026-07-10T11:08:49-04:00 Technician I PT Eves UCHC EJSP <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Part Time UCHC Technician I for the East Jersey State Prison, located in Rahway, NJ. The UCHC Technician I participates as a member of the clinical and administrative medical team at the Prison.<br><br>Among the duties for this position are:<br><br></div><ul><li>Takes vital signs, height and weight and documents in electronic medical records (EMR).</li><li>Assists the physician/associate practitioner with procedures, including preparing the inmate for the examination.</li><li>Obtains specimen collection and handling, including, but not limited to, drawing blood.</li><li>Assists with the cleaning, sterilization and securing of equipment within the Health Service Unit.</li><li>Maintains or assists in maintaining the supply stock in the Health Service Unit by ordering in a timely and appropriate manner. Maintains the supply stock in the examination rooms.• Aggregates the orders of all medications and forwards to the pharmacy provider / local pharmacy.</li></ul> UCHC East Jersey State Prison_DUP RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7677 Rahway NJ 26ST0986 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/268661 2026-02-05T12:01:07-05:00 2026-02-05T12:01:08-05:00 Lecturer <div>The Graduate School of Applied and Professional Psychology (GSAPP), Rutgers University invites applications for Par Lecturer teaching positions for several doctoral level courses in the clinical department to fit required coursework or high-needs electives. Opportunities for recurring appointments exist. A prepared syllabus is available for review for any of the below courses at: https://gsapp.rutgers.edu/current-students/syllabi. Candidates will assume primary responsibility for developing or refining the course syllabus, presenting high quality lectures, running class discussions and other teaching activities, and evaluating students based on course expectations and program-wide competencies. PTL’s are expected to adhere to high quality instructional practices that integrate multiple modalities and approaches, such as whole class lecture, small group activities, videos, role playing etc. Hybrid formats using a combination of online and in-person platforms may be applied with the appropriate plan. Courses in search of a PTL include:</div><div>•Biological Basis of Behavior (18:820:622),</div><div>•Cognitive and Affective Psychology (18:820:505),</div><div>•Learning Disability: Psychological Assessment (18:821:558),</div><div>•Statistical Methods and Research Design (18:820:581),</div><div>•Adult Psychopathology (18:820:565),</div><div>•Advanced Statistics and Research Design (18:820:585),</div><div>•Cognitive Assessment (18:820:633:01),</div><div>•Treatment of At-Risk Minority Adolescents (18:821:538),</div><div>•Psychological Interventions with Ethnic Minority Clients (18:820:570),</div><div>•Health Psychology (18:821:561) or Behavior Medicine (18:821:631)</div><div>Clinical Interviewing and Assessment (18:820:531)</div> Clinical Psychology New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Graduate School of Applied & P-L3 6827 26FA0110 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280378 2026-09-03T10:43:20-04:00 2026-09-04T10:53:55-04:00 Professor, Associate Director-Camden, Rutgers Democracy Lab <div>The Associate Director will be a vital administrative and programmatic leader for theRutgers Democracy Lab (RDL) at Rutgers-Camden. Reporting to the RDL Director with adotted line to the Senior Vice Chancellor for Strategy, Diversity and Community Engagementat Rutgers-Camden, the Associate Director is responsible for the overall strategic andoperational management of the RDL's activities, programs, and partnerships at Rutgers-Camden. This role requires a highly organized, entrepreneurial, and collaborative individual capableof managing complex administrative processes, overseeing budgets and personnel, andserving as a key liaison to academic, civic, and community stakeholders to advance theRDL’s mission of strengthening democracy through research and engagement.<br><br><strong>Core Duties and Responsibilities</strong><br>The Associate Director's primary duties are focused on administrative management,<br>programmatic leadership, and campus representation:<br><br><strong>I. Strategic &amp; Programmatic Leadership</strong></div><div>· <strong>Program Oversight:</strong> Develops, plans, and oversees the execution of all RDL-affiliated programs, events, and workshops on the assigned campus (e.g., policy forums, speaker series, civic engagement initiatives, Think and Do Tank).</div><div>· <strong>Strategic Planning:</strong> Works with the RDL Director to set and implement the strategic agenda for the campus location, translating the Lab’s broad mission into actionable goals and outcomes that align with the local university and community priorities.</div><div>· <strong>Partnership Management:</strong> Serves as the primary RDL liaison to academic, administrative, and external partners within the Camden ecosystem, including faculty, deans, local non-profits, and government officials.</div><div>· <strong>External Communications:</strong> Manages and produces outreach materials (web content, newsletters, press releases) specific to the campus programs, ensuring a consistent and professional public profile.<br><br></div><div><strong>II. Administrative &amp; Operational Management</strong></div><div><strong>· Budget &amp; Finance: </strong>Manages the operational budget for the campus location, including tracking expenditures, processing purchasing requests, reconciling accounts, and ensuring compliance with university and grant guidelines working closely with the RDL Business Manager.</div><div>· <strong>Grant Administration:</strong> Works closely with the RDL Director and University Foundation/Sponsored Research offices to assist in the drafting of proposals and manages the non-research administrative execution and reporting requirements for all awarded grants.</div><div>· <strong>Personnel Supervision:</strong> Directly supervises, mentors, and manages the professional staff (e.g., Fellows, Graduate Assistants and student employees associated with the campus's RDL activities, including hiring and training).</div><div>· <strong>Policy &amp; Compliance:</strong> Ensures all campus-level RDL operations and programming adhere to university policies, procedures, and relevant compliance requirements (e.g., venue contracts, risk management).</div><div><br></div><div><strong>III. Campus-Specific Coordination</strong></div><div>With regards to the partnership at Camden, the associate director should be someone who can work collaboratively with the other centers at the Division of Diversity, Inclusion and Community Engagement (DICE) and across the Camden campus, including areas of urban studies and public policy. They should have a commitment to partnering with K-12 schools around civic engagement. They should have an understanding of local south Jersey, as well as NJ state-wide initiatives based in this region and be open to Philadelphia regional partnerships, such as the Philadelphia Higher Education Network for Neighborhood Development (PHENND).</div><div>Cross‑Unit Coordination will be essential and includes the following types of activities.</div><div><strong>DICE Core Activities</strong></div><div>· Participation in regular standing meetings such as DICE Division meetings, Community Engagement unit meetings, one-on-one meetings with the Senior Vice Chancellor of Strategy, Diversity, and Community Engagement and the Director of Community Engagement.</div><div>· Participate in planning committees with representatives from the Community Engagement unit, academic departments, student affairs, and other Rutgers Camden offices that align with the work of RDL.</div><div>· Building strong relationships to the work with the community engagement unit and collaborating closely with the staff within the unit.</div><div><strong>Faculty &amp; Academic Department Activities</strong></div><div>· Working with the Director of Community Engagement and the Faculty Director of Engaged Scholarship to connect with department chairs to identify faculty whose courses or research align with funded projects.</div><div>· Collaborate with the community engagement unity to host faculty info sessions targeted to specific departments (e.g., Public Policy, Social Work).</div><div>· Aligning project timelines with course planning cycles and curriculum deadlines.</div><div><strong>Student-Facing Activities:</strong></div><div>· Collaborating with DICE to promote project-based assistantships opportunities or paid roles.</div><div>· Partnering with DICE, Academic Affairs, Student Academic Success to integrate student research or internships into RDL initiatives.</div><div>· Coordinating with the Office of Student Involvement to schedule student-led events or workshops.</div><div><strong>Administrative &amp; Operational Activities:</strong></div><div>· Managing logistics for meetings and events.</div><div>· Handling risk management for community engaged activities involving external partners.</div><div>· Coordinating HR, payroll and onboarding for any student employee or staff hires.</div><div><strong>Communication &amp; Marketing Activities:</strong></div><div>· Developing marketing materials in collaboration with the Office of Marketing and Communications.</div><div>· Developing and sharing announcements of RDL activities within DICE networks and with Marketing and Communication.</div><div>· Creating a central landing page managed by DICE but updated with RDL inputs.</div><div><strong>Community Partner Activities:</strong></div><div>· Establishing partnership agreements vetted collaboratively with the Community Engagement unit/DICE.</div><div>· Coordinating partner presentations with faculty and program directors to ensure alignment with academic learning goals.</div><div><strong>Data, Evaluation &amp; Reporting Coordination</strong> <strong>Activities:</strong></div><div>· Aligning evaluation plans with Rutgers Camden / DICE to ensure standard metrics.</div><div>· Developing shared impact dashboards updated by DICE, academic departments, and community partners.</div><div>· Coordinate data collection for RDL programs that also align with DICE initiatives, such as ECL courses, co-curricular programs and community partner initiatives</div><div><strong>Funding &amp; Resource Coordination</strong> <strong>Activities:</strong></div><div>· Working closely with DICE and Rutgers-Camden Development/Advancement to pursue co‑funding or donor alignment.</div><div><br></div> Eagleton Institute of Politics New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Eagleton Institute of Politics-L3 8087 26FA0746 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279241 2026-07-31T11:27:08-04:00 2026-07-31T11:27:09-04:00 Disability Specialist <div>Rutgers University- Newark (RU-N), an urban public research university and anchor institution, located in Newark, New Jersey, a city of promise is seeking a Disabilities Specialist. Reporting to the Director of Disability Services, this position is responsible for ensuring the delivery of reasonable accommodations to all eligible students at the Newark campus at Rutgers in accordance with relevant federal regulations and university policies. Responsible for, and not limited to the following.</div><ul><li>Plan, organize and provide reasonable accommodations that include academic adjustments, auxiliary aids, and services to students with disabilities - physical, psychological, learning, health-related, and neurological disabilities (e.g., mobility impairments, Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder, learning disorders, hearing impairments, visual impairments, traumatic brain injuries, and epilepsy);</li><li>Conduct initial interviews with students; keeping accurate, comprehensive and up-to-date notes/records related to students; reviewing documentation and evaluative reports; preparing letters of accommodation; evaluating eligibility for services; conducting follow-up meetings with students; organizing reasonable accommodations, services and auxiliary aids for students; and making referrals to appropriate community and University services or agencies;</li><li>Consult with faculty and staff regarding the implementation of reasonable accommodations and services; develop and present disability awareness programs for the University community;</li><li>Collaborate with other offices and outside agencies, as needed and appropriate.</li></ul> Student Affairs Newark Newark Chancellor-L2 Student Affairs Newark-L3 8069 Newark NJ 26ST1577 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/272709 2026-04-09T09:39:07-04:00 2026-04-09T09:39:08-04:00 Program Director (Director of Clinical Training; DCT) <div>The Graduate School of Applied and Professional Psychology (GSAPP) at Rutgers University–New Brunswick seeks an innovative leader to join our faculty as a full-time Program Director (Director of Clinical Training; DCT) of the Psy.D. program in the Department of Clinical Psychology. This non-tenure track, Assistant or Associate Professor position provides an exciting opportunity to sustain and shape the direction of one of the nation’s leading programs in clinical psychology. The Program Director will play a leading role in cultivating the strategic direction of the Clinical Psychology Psy.D. program, including engaging in critical program operations (e.g., admissions, student progress monitoring, curriculum development, training and supervision, ensuring alignment of the program with accreditation standards). The Program Director will also oversee student internship placements and provide guidance to the practicum coordinator, ensuring students have access to robust and meaningful practicum and externship experiences. Beyond administrative leadership, this position offers the opportunity to teach courses that align with the candidate’s expertise and departmental needs, contributing directly to the education and professional growth of the next generation of clinical psychologists.</div><div>For more information about the Department of Clinical Psychology, see: <a href=\"https://gsapp.rutgers.edu/academic-programs/clinical-department\"><strong>https://gsapp.rutgers.edu/academic-programs/clinical-department</strong></a></div> Clinical Psychology New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Graduate School of Applied & P-L3 6827 26FA0341 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279601 2026-08-14T12:18:41-04:00 2026-08-14T12:18:42-04:00 Staff Nurse - Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Staff Nurse for the Inpatient Units, Crisis and Acute Psychiatric Services within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Staff Nurse is to provide nursing services and participates in the delivery of individualized, goal directed nursing care through the use of the nursing process in accordance with the departmental and hospital policies and procedures and all regulatory requirements. The staff nurse functions as a member of the interdisciplinary team; participates in quality improvement activities, educational activities and supports research endeavors. The role is consistent with the scope and standards outlined by the American Psychiatric Nurses Association for Psychiatric-Mental Health Nursing.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Assesses and diagnoses patient, family and significant other needs in order to provide quality care to assigned patients.</li><li>Documents initial nursing assessment and individualized, goal directed plan of care considering the psychological, social, physical health and safety needs of the patient, in accordance with unit standards.</li><li>Develops, discusses and communicates a realistic, individualized plan of care for each patient, in collaboration with the patient, family and significant other in an effort to promote wellness and recovery.</li><li>Evaluates identified problems and care provided and the patient’s responses are reassessed in order to meet the patient and family/significant other needs to ensure overall quality of care delivered.</li><li>Facilitates daily patient groups.</li><li>Demonstrates the skills and judgment necessary to implement the plan of care, nursing interventions and procedures as necessary for the care and safety of the patient.</li><li>Demonstrates knowledge of procedures and theories related to the care of patients in acute psychiatric crises.</li><li>Demonstrates respect and regard for the dignity of all patients, families, visitors and fellow employees to ensure a professional, responsible and courteous environment.</li></ul> UBHC - Acute Psychological Ser RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7987 Piscataway NJ 26ST0813 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279852 2026-08-24T09:13:03-04:00 2026-08-24T09:13:04-04:00 Research Project Coordinator II <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Research Project Coordinator II for the Rutgers Center for State Health Policy (Center/CSHP) within the Institute for Health, Health Care Policy, and Aging Research (IFH), a unit of Rutgers Health. This position requires basic research skills (e.g,. literature reviews, IRB submissions, quantitative and qualitative research approach coordination, spreadsheet tracking of deliverables) and project coordination experience (e.g,. management of workplan and timelines, developing progress reports, and engaging with external collaborators) to support the Center's broad health services research portfolio. The selected candidate will receive strong policy and research mentorship from the a talented team of faculty and research staff at the Center. The Research Project Coordinator II will be given the opportunity to participate in policy meetings with senior state officials, and will have the opportunity to contribute to peer reviewed publications as appropriate.</div><div><br>Among the key duties of the position are the following:</div><ul><li>Identifies tasks and complete activities for quantitative and qualitative approaches as required for specific research projects .</li><li>Conducts rigorous literature reviews to inform the development of interview protocols and related documents.</li><li>Drafts interview materials including questionnaires and consent forms.</li><li>Prepares and submits E IRB applications, and manages ongoing human subjects compliance.</li><li>Drafts findings reports and presentations for PI review.</li><li>Conducts literature reviews, performs qualitative interviewing, and maintains Excel spreadsheets to track project deliverables.</li><li>Maintains project work plans to ensure that timelines are met and deliverables are received from internal and external members of the project teams.</li><li>Schedules project meetings and prepares agendas and other necessary materials as requested by the project PI.</li></ul> State Health Policy Center RBHS Chancellor-L2 Institute for Health, Health C-L3 6842 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1386 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277721 2026-06-25T00:01:05-04:00 2026-06-25T00:01:06-04:00 Administrative Assistant <div>Rutgers University- Newark (RU-N), an urban public research university and anchor institution, located in Newark, New Jersey, a city of promise is seeking an Administrative Assistant. Reporting to the Senior Executive Associate, the Administrative Assistant provides confidential general office administrative support to the Office of the Chancellor, Rutgers – Newark, prepares documents for entry into University administrative systems, and provides support for office projects and programs.</div><div>This position is responsible for and not limited to the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Serves as the first point of contact for in-person visits and phone inquiries, organizing and maintaining office records and databases, tracking office supply inventory and ensuring replenishment as needed, organizing meetings, scheduling conference room space, coordinating travel arrangements, coordinating staff moves, removal of surplus equipment and archiving documents</li><li>Utilizes University administrative systems to prepare requisitions, create expense reports, enter payroll time sheets, and maintain absence records</li><li>Works with vendors to ensure timely payment of invoices and accuracy of payments</li><li>Provides support for projects and programs originating in the Office of the Chancellor</li><li>Prepares reports and communications, compile research, organize data and prepare spreadsheets</li><li>Maintains project plans and timelines</li><li>Performs at a high level of professionalism and will always maintain the confidentiality of the Office of the Chancellor</li><li>Completes other assignments consistent with the mission, vision, role, and goals of the Office of the Chancellor</li></ul> Newark Chancellor Newark Chancellor-L2 Newark Chancellor-L3 6602 Newark NJ 26ST1304 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274657 2026-05-08T14:08:05-04:00 2026-05-08T14:08:06-04:00 Lecturer <div>The Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering Department at The School of Engineering at Rutgers University is currently looking to fill a Lecturer positions for the Fall 2026 semester.<br><br>Duties: Instruction of an undergraduate or graduate course on campus, including preparing lesson plans, preparing and grading mid-term and final exams. The duties may also include coordinating and mentoring undergraduate students, and sharing administration responsibilities as well as other duties assigned by the department Chairperson.</div> Mechanical & Aerospace Eng New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Engineering-L3 8113 26FA0453 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266201 2025-12-31T09:36:42-05:00 2025-12-31T09:36:43-05:00 Assistant or Associate Professor - Tenure Track <div>Robert Wood Johnson Medical School at Rutgers University invites applications for tenure-track positions at the assistant or associate professor level in the <a href=\"https://rwjms.rutgers.edu/departments/pharmacology/message-from-the-chair\"><strong>Department of Pharmacology</strong></a><strong>.</strong> Successful candidates will join a group of supportive colleagues who conduct research across diverse disciplines including cell signaling and growth control, gene expression, ‘omics approaches to cancer and age-related disease, host-pathogen interactions, ion channel biophysics and electrophysiology, metabolic and liver disease, pulmonary medicine and translational pharmacology, therapeutic target development, and drug discovery. We value innovation, curiosity and collegiality, and seek candidates who aim to address impactful questions in fundamental and/or translational science that complement and diversify our department's existing strengths.<br><br></div><div>The research laboratories and office space for these faculty positions will be housed within medical school research facilities on the Piscataway (Busch) campus of RBHS and Rutgers. Successful candidates will be provided with a competitive start up package, laboratory space, access to high-performance computing clusters and other core resources, and will be expected to develop and maintain a strong, externally funded research program and participate in collaborative projects with other Departments and Institutes at Rutgers. Major duties and responsibilities include developing a robust, externally funded research program to conduct studies in fields related to human health, development and disease, and to support the educational goals and activities of Rutgers University through teaching and service, including participation in the teaching of professional, graduate and undergraduate students, and mentorship of trainees. The successful candidates will gradually assume teaching responsibilities commensurate with the teaching load of other tenure-track faculty in the departments.<br><br></div><div>Research programs utilizing interdisciplinary and translational approaches that develop interactions with the Departments of Medicine, Pediatrics, Surgery, Neurosurgery, Psychiatry, or Neurology, the Rutgers Institute for Translational Medicine and Science, the Rutgers Center for Advanced Biotechnology and Medicine, the Rutgers Cancer Institute of New Jersey, and other clinical departments within RBHS are encouraged.<br><br></div><div>Rutgers is located at the center of the northeast corridor, with access to New York, Philadelphia, and the New Jersey shore within an hour. The region is a hub of academic excellence and innovation, home to top-tier universities, leading pharmaceutical and biotech research facilities, and major corporate headquarters. Central New Jersey offers a high quality of life with vibrant and diverse cultural institutions, outstanding public and private schools, and a range of residential options--from urban living to, suburban communties and picturesque small-towns--all within close proximity to campus.<br><br></div><div>The medical school is home to a large group of interactive and collegial faculty with federally funded research programs in broad areas of biomedical science. Pharmacology and the basic science departments are well integrated into a large, highly collaborative research community across the schools and departments of Rutgers University with multiple centers of excellence. Medical School faculty have access to interdisciplinary, Ph.D.-level graduate training programs and outstanding core facilities including genomics, proteomics, metabolomics, genome editing, confocal microscopy, human neuroimaging, and cryo-EM among others. Rutgers is also affiliated with the largest university-spinoff biorepository and is home to the Protein Data Bank.</div> RWJ - Pharmacology RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7821 24FA1091 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280089 2026-08-27T13:55:20-04:00 2026-08-27T13:55:21-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Postdoctoral Associate for the department of Medicine at the Robert Wood Johnson Medical School.<br><br>Under the direction of Principal Investigator, the Postdoctoral Associate will transfer existing IRB protocols to Rutgers, obtain and maintain regulatory approval, identify and consent participants, oversee data entry, and coordinate with other sites. The post doc will also present at monthly multisite meetings including collating and presenting data from participants. The post doc will contribute to writing manuscripts from this project and help with grant applications. Working closely with the PI, the postdoc will also have opportunity to participate and lead other projects in the PIs group. The position also includes mentorship and supervision of trainees and research staff, and active participation in the academic mission of the division.<br><br>The position offers a highly collaborative, intellectually dynamic environment with strong mentorship and a clear path toward scientific independence, including opportunities to develop first-author publications and pursue independent funding to embark on an academic career in the area of nephrology. This position is ideally suited for candidates with strong interpersonal and analytical skills. Clinical and basic science knowledge is an additional benefit that will help candidate succeed.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Obtain and maintain regulatory approval.</li><li>Set up screening algorithms to identify eligible participants.</li><li>Recruit participants, collect/ process samples.</li><li>Design data collection tools (e.g., redcap).</li><li>Present at monthly multisite meeting.</li><li>Drive scientific discovery through active involvement in data interpretation, hypothesis generation, and experimental design.</li></ul><div><br></div> RWJ - Medicine Nephrology RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7778 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1673 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278381 2026-07-08T07:22:18-04:00 2026-07-08T07:22:19-04:00 Post Doctoral Associate (Semenova Lab) <div>The Semenova laboratory at the Waksman Institute of Microbiology has an open Postdoctoral Associate position to investigate CRISPR-Cas13-mediated immunity. Under the supervision of Dr. Semenova, the postdoctoral fellow will participate in grant-funded research aimed at:<br><br></div><div>· Characterizing collateral RNA cleavage by diverse Cas13 homologs and determining their RNA substrate preferences and mechanisms of activation.</div><div>· Defining cellular defense pathways induced by collateral RNA cleavage, with a focus on defense mechanisms triggered by tRNA cleavage.</div><div>· Investigating spacer acquisition in RNA-targeting type VI CRISPR-Cas systems.</div><div>· Exploring the evolutionary diversity of Cas13 effectors and their implications for technologies.<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate will receive interdisciplinary training in CRISPR-Cas systems, RNA biology, phage biology, and microbial defense mechanisms. The Semenova laboratory provides a collaborative and supportive environment that fosters scientific independence and career development. The candidate will have opportunities to lead projects, develop independent research directions, prepare fellowship and grant applications, and build a strong foundation for future academic or industry careers.<br><br>Key Duties:<br><strong>60 %</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<strong>1.</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Conduct research on RNA-targeting type VI CRISPR-Cas systems.</div><div><strong>15 %</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<strong>2.</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Analyze research data and prepare manuscripts for publication.</div><div><strong>15 %&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;3.</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Mentor and train undergraduate students in the lab.</div><div><strong>5%</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; <strong>4.</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Prepare proposals for postdoctoral fellowships.</div><div><strong>5 %</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<strong>5.</strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Present research findings at local and international conferences.<br><br>Level of Decision Making:<br>The postdoc will design and optimize experiments, particularly for Next Generation Sequencing workflows, including library preparation and data analysis. They will exercise independent judgment in data analysis, troubleshooting unexpected results, adjusting protocols, and ensuring high-quality data for publication.<br><br>Scope &amp; Impact:<br>The position involves complex experimental research on RNA-targeting CRISPR-Cas systems, requiring technical expertise and independent problem-solving. The scope includes the specific project, collaboration with other labs, mentoring undergraduates, and contributing to publications, conferences, and future grant proposals.<br><br></div> Waksman Institute of Microbiol New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 6726 26FA0661 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267364 2026-01-15T11:37:41-05:00 2026-01-15T11:37:42-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor – Multiple Positions (GI Hepatology) <div>The Department of Medicine, Division of Liver Disease and Transplant Hepatology at Rutgers New Jersey Medical School (NJMS) seeks qualified candidate(s) at the Assistant or Associate Professor level for full-time academic position(s) in liver disease and transplant hepatology. Successful candidate(s) will be board eligible/certified in Gastroenterology and board eligible/certified in Transplant Hepatology.</div><div>These position(s) will support general and advanced inpatient and outpatient liver disease and transplant hepatology consultation services at University Hospital. In addition, candidate(s) will also perform gastroenterology procedures consistent with their training. Candidate(s) will serve as core faculty for the training of gastroenterology and transplant hepatology fellows and will also support the general medicine residency training program and the educational needs of New Jersey Medical School. Candidate(s) will actively support the research mission of the division and be expected to lead investigator initiated and grant supported clinical research studies. The ideal candidate(s) will be fully engaged in further enhancement and expansion of our liver transplant program. Responsibilities will include patient care, research, and teaching (medical students/resident physicians and subspecialty fellows) in concert with the policies of Rutgers NJMS, University Hospital, and the Division of Liver Disease and Transplant Hepatology.</div> NJMS - Medicine Gastroenterolo RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7439 23FA1088 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280243 2026-08-31T15:06:48-04:00 2026-08-31T15:06:49-04:00 Grants & Contracts Analyst III <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Grants &amp; Contracts Analyst III for the Military Services within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.&nbsp;<br><br>Under the direction, assists in the preparation and submission of grant proposals, monitors budgets for grants and contracts, ensures all grant and contract activities are compliant with state and federal regulations, prepares financial and progress reports to funding agencies, monitors the progress of funded projects, serves as a resource for staff on grant and contract management.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Assists Principal Investigator in the preparation and submission of grant proposals ensuring compliance with funding agency guidelines, ensuring all necessary documentation is complete and adheres to funder guidelines. &nbsp;</li><li>Oversees pre- and post-award financial management for federal, state, corporate, and private foundation grants and contracts.&nbsp;</li><li>Reviews and monitors budgets for grants and contracts, ensuring proper allocation of funds. &nbsp;</li><li>Serves as the financial bridge between program operations and management.&nbsp;</li><li>Submits required invoices and financial reports, and prepares and submits progress reports to funding agencies, ensuring accuracy and timeliness.&nbsp; &nbsp;</li><li>Monitors the progress of funded projects with the Principal Investigator, ensuring milestones are met and expenditures are within budget.</li></ul> UBHC - Military Services RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8040 Piscataway NJ 26ST1700 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278829 2026-07-15T10:40:33-04:00 2026-07-15T10:40:34-04:00 Research Teaching Specialist III (Research Tech Developing Infectious Disease Diagnostics) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Research Teaching Specialist III in the Public Health Research Institute within the New Jersey Medical School (NJMS).<br><br>Under the direction of the Principal Investigator and Research Operations Assistant Director, the Research Teaching Specialist III conducts research activities in diagnostic microbiology within a specialized biosafety level three (BSL3) containment laboratory. Assists the Principal Investigator with budgetary, lab maintenance, training and administrative responsibilities, income revenue streams.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Cultures and quantitates pathogenic and non-pathogenic bacteria and viruses including M. Tuberculosis and SARSCoV2 requiring work in BSL3 facilities.</li><li>Performs detailed MICs and DNA/RNA extraction of above described bacteria using various systems and performs preliminary analysis.</li><li>Assists in the development and testing of new assays to detect bacteria and viruses from various body sites and clinical matrixes.</li><li>Assists in writing IRB and IBC submissions.</li><li>Assists in obtaining informed consent and collecting and processing non-invasive samples from study participants according to experimental protocols.</li></ul> NJMS - Medicine Infectious Dis RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7442 Newark NJ 26ST1070 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/270374 2026-03-06T15:58:39-05:00 2026-03-06T15:58:40-05:00 Lecturers/Coadjutant Instructors, School of Nursing <div>The Rutgers School of Nursing-Camden seeks expert practitioners and clinicians 