r the Acute Inpatient Division within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Mental Health Specialist III is to participate as a member of the unit team providing care for all age groups in accordance with facility policy and procedure. Demonstrates leadership skills and assists the Staff Nurse with staff assignments, orientation of new staff and formulation of patient groups.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Assists the Staff Nurse with MHS IV assignments, orientation of new staff and formulation of patient groups when required.</li><li>Assists the Staff Nurse in planning patient care.</li><li>Provides care based on the patient’s established care plan, under the supervision of the Staff Nurse.</li><li>Observes patient’s behaviors and when necessary notifies appropriate staff.</li><li>Assists in maintaining a safe, therapeutic environment that respects patients’ rights.</li><li>Assists the patients with activities of daily living, encouraging independent behavior, when appropriate.</li><li>Assists patients and observes patients during mealtimes in the cafeteria and on the unit.</li><li>Monitors the milieu for changes in patient behavior. Also, observes interaction between patients and visitors.</li></ul> UBHC - Acute Psychological Ser RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7987 Piscataway NJ 26ST1418 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279442 2026-08-10T10:07:43-04:00 2026-08-10T10:07:44-04:00 Mental Health Clinician II UCHC GSYCF <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care (UCHC) is seeking a Mental Health Clinician II for the Garden State Youth Correctional Facility, located in Yardville, NJ. The Mental Health Clinician II completes specialized psychological testing and assessment of clinical needs of adult inmates sentenced to the Department of Corrections.<br><br>The Mental Health Clinician II completes specialized psychological testing and assessment of clinical needs of adults sentenced to the Department of Corrections; arrives at diagnoses with precision and accuracy by the end of psychological testing and the evaluation session; develops treatment plans; and makes clinically based decisions regarding appropriateness for treatment, as well as preferred treatment modality. The Mental Health Clinician II should be skilled in in providing group, individual and family therapies Assesses and make referrals for higher levels of care, as appropriate; and recognizes the unique needs and behaviors of adult inmate/patients, seniors and their families.&nbsp;</div> UCHC Garden State Youth Medica RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7653 Yardville NJ 26ST0348 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/276627 2026-06-08T08:44:41-04:00 2026-06-08T08:44:41-04:00 Post Doc Associate <div>Niu Lab in Biomedical Engineering is seeking a highly motivated Postdoctoral Associate to join our research group at Rutgers University to work on a project funded by the New Jersey Spinal Cord Injury Commission. The successful candidate will lead the development of next-generation wearable devices specifically designed for spinal cord injury applications. This role involves the end-to-end development of advanced sensor systems, from the physical fabrication of flexible printed circuit boards (FPCBs) to the implementation of machine learning algorithms for real-time signal analysis. The postdoc will collaborate in a multidisciplinary environment, managing laboratory resources and producing high-quality progress reports and publications.</div> Biomedical Engineering New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Engineering-L3 7102 26FA0563 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274052 2026-04-30T11:56:02-04:00 2026-04-30T11:56:03-04:00 Lecturers, Childhood Studies <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the Faculty of Arts &amp; Sciences, Childhood Studies Department, seeks lecturers to teach various courses online and in class within the disciplin