ental health services to the inmate population at the Prison.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Performs dental assessments on inmates upon intake, to determine dental needs and urgency of needs.</li><li>Charts results in the Electronic Medical Record and develops initial plan of treatment.</li><li>Performs and/or interprets radiographic exams.</li><li>Provides dental treatment including emergency treatment of teeth and surrounding soft tissues such as oral surgery, restorative dentistry, and periodontal therapy, within the scope of a general dentist.</li><li>Corrects significant oral problems which may adversely affect inmate’s health.</li><li>Makes referrals for procedures which cannot be performed at the institution.</li><li>Provides professional consultation to all members of the Health Services team relative to the inmate’s health care management.</li><li>In conjunction with the Medical Director, prescribes medications from formulary for inmate’s healthcare needs.</li></ul> UCHC Midstate Correction Physi RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7680 Trenton NJ 26ST1630 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280025 2026-08-26T12:21:35-04:00 2026-08-26T12:21:36-04:00 Behavioral Health Aide <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Behavioral Health Aide for the Inpatient Services Department within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Behavioral Health Aide is to provide continuous, direct, one-to-one observation and support for patients experiencing acute mental health symptoms. Assists in maintaining a safe and supportive environment for patients.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Provides constant, uninterrupted one-to-one observation for assigned patients who are at risk for self-harm, harm to others, aggression, or emotional distress.</li><li>Assists in maintaining a safe and supportive environment by promptly reporting escalating patient behaviors, mood changes, and concerning activities to the clinical care team.</li><li>Completes and documents accurate, timely, and objective safety observations in accordance with organizational policy, regulatory requirements, and established observation intervals (including every 15-minute checks as assigned).</li><li>Maintains a calm and professional demeanor during patient escalation or crisis situations and utilizes approved verbal redirection and de-escalation techniques.</li><li>Follows all suicide precautions, restraint and seclusion policies, procedures, and required trainings.</li><li>Assists patients with basic activities of daily living, ambulation, meals, hydration, and comfort measures as directed.</li><li>Assists with patient orientation to the unit environment, reinforcing unit expectations, behavioral standards, safety protocols, and patient rights as directed by clinical leadership.</li></ul> UBHC - Acute Psychological Ser RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7987 Piscataway NJ 26ST1652 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277795 2026-06-25T13:10:15-04:00 2026-06-25T13:10:16-04:00 Lecturers, Various Disciplines/Coadjutants <div>The Law School at Rutgers University-Camden seeks lecturers for the 2026-2027 semesters (Fall 26, Winter 27, Spring 27, Summer 27) to teach in various disciplines. The instructor will present course material during the assigned course times, hold office hours, administer exams, assign grades and coordinate any other requirements related to course instruction.&nbsp;</div> LAW-Dean's Office Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 LAW-Dean's Office-L3 8075 26FA0634 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275691 2026-05-22T07:01:28-04:00 2026-05-22T07:01:29-04:00 Dining Services Student Worker - Server Position - (The Rutger's Club) <div>Join the Rutgers Dining team as a Dining Services Student Worker in one of our dining halls or retail operations across the New Brunswick and Piscataway campuses. Rutgers Dining Services strives to be the best in culinary excellence and as a Dining Services Worker you play a critical role in the customer experience. From assisting in the preparation and service of food, to maintaining the presentation of the dining halls, to assisting guests, we have a variety of roles and will find the right one for you!<br><br>Dining Service Workers earn a paycheck and more:<br>1. Student employee meal privileges.<br>2. Flexible schedules (10/20 hours/week) that work around your classes and activities.<br>3. Convenient on-campus locations.<br>4. Opportunities to advance to leadership positions such as Captain, Meal Manager and Student Unit Manager.<br>5. Valuable work experience to add to your resume.<br>6. Learn important job skills including interpersonal communications, team dynamics, dependability and time management.<br>7. A fun and welcoming environment.</div> The Rutgers Club New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Student Affairs - New Brunswic-L3 6702 Piscataway NJ 26ST1136 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266345 2025-12-31T09:52:31-05:00 2025-12-31T09:52:32-05:00 Lecturer -School Psychology <div>The Graduate School of Applied and Professional Psychology, Rutgers University invites applications for Part-Time Lecturer (PTL) teaching positions in the Department of School Psychology during the academic year 2024-2025, (Fall’24, Spring’25, Summer’25). and academic year 2025-2026 (Fall’25, Spring’26, Summer’26)</div><div>The position entails teaching doctoral level courses in the Department of School Psychology. Candidates will assume primary responsibility for developing or refining course syllabi, presenting high quality lectures, and evaluating students based on course expectations and program-wide competencies. Lecturer is expected to adhere to high quality instructional practices that integrate multiple modalities and approaches, such as whole class lecture, small group activities, videos, role playing etc.</div> School Psychology New Brunswick Chance