:</div><div>1. Continuously evaluate and seek opportunities for growth, expansion and improvement of the</div><div>educational, research, service, and patient care programs; faculty and staff performance; and administrative processes of the department and make appropriate recommendations to the Vice Dean regarding all issues of concern to the department:</div><div>a. Enhance faculty recruitment with particular attention to gender equity, diversity and inclusion;</div><div>b. Pursue contracted clinical services with other entities;</div><div>c. Consider the establishment of a faculty practice (non-hospital based);</div><div>d. Conduct annual performance evaluations of all faculty and establish annual goals and objectives for individual faculty members;</div><div>e. Optimize the quality of the residency training program.</div><div><br>2. Work to maintain a balanced budget annually for the department, as well as the distribution formula for the department's faculty practice earnings, and manage the expenses of clinical practice.</div><div><br>3. Achieve budget transparency and enhance the understanding and involvement of the department's faculty.</div><div><br>4. Optimize the operation of departmental programs and clinical affiliations.</div><div><br>5. Work with other departments and centers to achieve mutually agreed upon interdepartmental goals across the research, educational, and clinical mission areas.</div><div><br></div><div>6. Ensure that the clinical faculty of the department provide timely reporting and attestation of effort at University Hospital in compliance with the Clinical Services Agreement between NJMS and UH.</div><div>7. Assure departmental compliance with all University policies and mandatory training requirements for faculty and staff, including but not limited to, compliance, HIPAA, Outside Activity Questionnaires, Faculty Time and Effort Reporting.</div><div><br>8. Regularly attend the monthly department chairs meetings, Faculty Council meetings, and other standing and ad hoc committee meetings as assigned by the Vice Dean or Dean.</div><div>9. Any other duties as assigned by the Vice Dean and/or Dean.</div> NJMS - Emergency Medicine RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7494 25FA0484 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279659 2026-08-17T16:07:35-04:00 2026-08-17T16:07:36-04:00 Behavior Analyst (Outreach) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Behavior Analyst (Outreach) for the Douglass Development Disability Center. The position reports to the Associate Director of Consultation and Communications.<br><br>Among the key duties of the position are the following:</div><ul><li>Supervises and monitors the services and programs related to the education of children and adults with autism and their families within an assigned caseload through the DDDC’s Outreach unit.</li><li>Ensures best practice applied behavior analysis procedures are maintained and applied in the education and treatment of children and adults in community settings.</li></ul> Douglass Developmnt Disab Cntr New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Graduate School of Applied & P-L3 6829 New Bunswick NJ 26ST1368 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279981 2026-08-25T16:54:04-04:00 2026-08-25T16:54:05-04:00 Senior Financial Analyst - Strategic Budget Modeling (SBM) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Senior Financial Analyst - Strategic Budget Modeling (SBM) for UFA Financial Planning &amp; Analytics.</div><div><br></div><div>Among the key duties of the position are the following:</div><ul><li>Plays a central role in advancing Rutgers’ enterprise Multi-Year Planning capability and building and maintaining its fully functional ten-year operating outlook.</li><li>Develops long-range forecasts, reconciliations, scenario analyses, and leadership reporting.</li><li>Works across the University Budget Office, Chancellor-Led Units, and functional partners to ensure model assumptions and outputs are accurate, controlled, and decision-ready, and communicates analyses and findings to senior and/or executive leadership.</li></ul> UFA Financial Planning & Analy EVP & Chief Admin Officer University Finance & Administr-L3 8784 Piscataway NJ 26ST1636 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277767 2026-06-25T11:10:20-04:00 2026-06-25T11:10:21-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse Mental Health PT Eves UCHC NSP <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a PartTime Licensed Practical Nurse Mental Health for Northern State Prison located in Newark, NJ<br><br>The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br>* Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs.<br>* Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.<br>* Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.<br>* Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.<br>* Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.<br>* Documents all aspects of patient care.</div> UCHC Northern State Prison Med RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7656 Newark NJ 26ST0682 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275346 2026-05-19T08:31:03-04:00 2026-05-19T08:31:04-04:00 Associate Director for Clinical Research (Associate Professor - Professor Rank) <div>The Associate Director for Clinical Research will have responsibility for oversight of all clinical research activity of all Rutgers Cancer Institute programs. This includes oversight of the Office of Human Research Services, the clinical Disease Specific Groups, clinical research related shared resources, and inter-programmatic meetings with clinical and translational researchers across the Cancer Institute.</div><div>Specific responsibilities include but are not limited to:</div><ul><li>Planning and evaluation of clinical investigations at Rutgers Cancer Institute.</li><li>Overseeing the development, integration, and coordination of the clinical scientists into cohesive groups.</li><li>In collaboration with the Deputy Director for Administration &amp; Planning, overseeing the activities of the Office of Human Research Services.</li><li>Ensuring that the shared resources support the clinical science programs.</li><li>Promoting inter- and intra-programmatic collaborations.</li><li>Assisting in recruiting new clinical science members to the center.</li><li>Participating in the planning of the Annual Scientific Retreat.</li><li>Reviewing all clinical research protocol budgets.</li><li>Helping basic and population scientists link their proposals to the clinical science base.</li><li>Ensuring the quality and scientific integrity of clinical research.</li><li>Developing a clinical research strategy across the service line, promoting clinical research across all hospital sites, and leading efforts to optimize trial portfolio and patient enrollments across the service line.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>The Associate Director for Clinical Research will be expected to serve on the Rutgers Cancer Institute Executive Leadership Team, Research Leadership Council, and participate in the Internal and External Advisory Board meetings.<br><br></div><div>Qualified candidates must have international recognition, prior leadership experience that supports the advancement of clinical research programs, and a proven ability to attract and sustain national cancer research funding. Candidates should also be adept at building productive relationships with community partners and patient advocacy groups, fostering engagement that enhances clinical research participation and impact.</div><div><br></div><div>Rutgers Cancer Institute, the state’s only NCI-designated Comprehensive Cancer Center located in New Brunswick, NJ, and RWJBarnabas Health, the state’s largest health care delivery system, partner to deliver high-quality and sophisticated oncology care to patients close to home. This integrated cancer care model combines the strength of both entities, offering access to the most advanced diagnostic and treatment options for adult and pediatric cancer patients, including clinical trials, immunotherapy, proton therapy, precision medicine, CAR T-cell therapy and cardio-oncology. Unique opportunities exist for collaborations between clinical and research programs, including clinical trials research, cancer chemoprevention, clinical and basic pharmacology, and Phase 1 clinical trials. Visit <a href=\"http://www.cinj.org\"><strong>www.cinj.org</strong></a>.</div><div><br><br><a href=\"https://www.cinj.org/about-cinj/faculty-opportunities\"><strong>See all our open faculty positions here</strong></a>!</div> Cancer Institute of New Jersey RBHS Chancellor-L2 Cancer Institute of New Jersey-L3 7893 26FA0066 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266270 2025-12-31T09:42:30-05:00 2025-12-31T09:42:30-05:00 Post-Doctoral Associate: Research in Medicinal Chemistry in Jun Wang Lab (Medicinal Chemistry Dept) <div>The Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy at Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey is seeking a post-doctoral associate to join the laboratory of Dr Jun Wang within the Department of Medicinal Chemistry on or about November 3, 2025. The successful candidates will participate in NIH-funded research projects in designing and developing small molecule antivirals targeting emerging and re-e