ding preparing the inmate for the examination.</li><li>Obtains specimen collection and handling, including, but not limited to, drawing blood.</li><li>Assists with the cleaning, sterilization and securing of equipment within the Health Service Unit.</li><li>Maintains or assists in maintaining the supply stock in the Health Service Unit by ordering in a timely and appropriate manner. Maintains the supply stock in the examination rooms.• Aggregates the orders of all medications and forwards to the pharmacy provider / local pharmacy.</li></ul> UCHC Adult Treatment Center Ph RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7674 Avenel NJ 26ST0902 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/268074 2026-01-27T14:54:03-05:00 2026-01-27T14:54:04-05:00 Post Doctoral Associate - Rail <div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, with the Center for Advanced Infrastructure and Transportation (CAIT) is seeking a Postdoctoral Associate. This position reports to Professor Xiang Liu and will work independently with clearly defined research objectives associated with projects.&nbsp;</div><div>The qualified candidate will have the following responsibilities:</div><div>· Coordinates internal resources and third parties for the successful execution of projects</div><div>· Track project performance to analyze the successful completion of short- and long-term goals</div><div>· Meet budgetary objectives and make adjustments to project constraints based on financial analysis</div><div>· Directly oversees work done by other team members and students</div><div>· Responsible for the interviewing and hiring of additional team members as needed</div><div>· Performs quality control and quality assurance on projects through expert knowledge of rail and transit engineering</div><div>· Writes technical reports and contributes to preparation of journal articles and prepares conference presentations</div><div>· Updates related research knowledge by participating in educational opportunities; reading professional publications; maintaining personal networks; participating in professional organizations.</div><div>· Use and continually develop leadership skills</div><div>The position also assumes collaboration with a group of researchers and graduate students from both academic and industrial partners. The candidate will be responsible for project reporting related to his/her research activities, supervision of graduate students, preparation of research proposals and publications, and presentations at professional and research conferences and meetings. The candidate is expected to have strong expertise in rail and transit transportation and engineering</div><div>The candidate may be required to travel independently to various locations in the U.S. and work offsite without any manager supervision. In addition, the employee will demonstrate a leadership role in forming and maintaining productive working relationships, and the ability to work autonomously in the prescribed duties, as well cooperatively with CAIT's faculty and staff in general.</div> Advanced Infrastructure Center New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Engineering-L3 6709 26FA0069 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280305 2026-09-01T16:43:19-04:00 2026-09-01T16:43:20-04:00 Mental Health Specialist III <div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Mental Health Specialist III within the Community Based Services - Residential Department-Outpatient, at the Rutgers University Behavioral Healthcare (UBHC).<br><br>The primary purpose of the Mental Health Specialist III is to ensure the safety of residents and assist them in carrying out activities of daily living.<br><br>Among the key duties for this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Provides direct care services to individuals served in compliance with all policies and regulations.</li><li>Maintains consumer resident’s records.</li><li>Maintains knowledge of UBHC and Unit policies and procedures.</li><li>Maintains a cooperative 