l setting.<br>10. Participate in the community service responsibilities of the department such as providing<br>neurological care for indigent patients, teaching or advising lay community groups in the<br>area of neurological disorders according to a schedule to be determined by the Chair and<br>Division Chief<br>11. Participate in the consult rotation and the weekend call schedules<br>12. Attend departmental and institutional faculty/other meetings<br>13. Participate in administrative tasks including membership in standing or ad hoc<br>departmental and institutional committees<br>14. Perform other duties as required.</div> RWJ - Neurology RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7784 26FA0119 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280446 2026-09-04T10:46:43-04:00 2026-09-04T10:46:44-04:00 RBHS Faculty Instructor <div>The Department of Psychiatry at Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School (RWJMS) seeks a Faculty Instructor to expand our research portfolio in network and computational neuroscience approaches to psychiatric illness. The Instructor will be housed within the laboratory of Dr. Avram Holmes and will work to support the research initiatives of that group/lab under the supervision of the lab head. Priority will be given to work aligned with the Center for Advanced Human Brain Imaging Research (CAHBIR; (<a href=\"https://sites.rutgers.edu/cahbir/\"><strong>https://sites.rutgers.edu/cahbir/</strong></a>).</div><div>We seek candidates with expertise in network neuroscience, computational modeling, neuroimaging, and related approaches to understanding psychiatric illness. The Faculty Instructor will conduct collaborative research, contribute to the department’s strategic research initiatives, and work closely with a multidisciplinary team. The position includes faculty mentorship and is intended as a transitional appointment to a faculty career track. Appointment is contingent on funding and is limited to a maximum of three years.</div> RWJ - Psychiatr