ty during inflammation and tissue repair. The Student Assistant appointee will work on a project as directed by the PI to study the role of mitochondrial reactive oxygen species in macrophage and neutrophil functions during wound healing using larval zebrafish models of sterile injury.&nbsp;<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Perform microinjection, CRISPR-Cas9 screen, PCR, and other molecular assays as directed by the PI.</li><li>Perform zebrafish experiments.</li><li>Perform microscopy and image analysis</li><li>Maintain clear and comprehensive laboratory records.</li><li>Perform statistical analyses of research data.</li><li>Perform other related duties of the research.&nbsp;</li></ul> NJMS - CCI - Cell Signaling Ce RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7525 Newark NJ 26ST1671 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/271466 2026-03-24T10:01:47-04:00 2026-03-24T10:01:47-04:00 Application Developer I <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking an Application Developer I in the Central Administration within the Office of Information Technology (OIT).<br><br>Under the direction of the Director of IT for Enterprise Student Services and Integration, the Application Developer I designs and implements integration processes between various Rutgers systems and services using enterprise cloud-based services, including AWS, Heroku, Oracle Integration Cloud (OIC), and Artificial Intelligence (AI) technology. Additional tasks related to the ongoing documentation, maintenance, and improvement of supported web-based applications will also be performed.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Designs and implements data integration processes between various Rutgers systems and services using enterprise cloud-based services, including AWS, Heroku, Oracle Integration Cloud (OIC), and Artificial Intelligence (AI) technology.</li><li>Maintains and improves supported web-based a