eatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs. Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.</li><li>Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.</li><li>Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.</li><li>Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.</li><li>Documents all aspects of patient care.</li></ul> UCHC New Jersey State Prison M RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7660 Trenton NJ 26ST1014 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/268893 2026-02-10T09:33:52-05:00 2026-02-10T09:33:53-05:00 Open Rank Faculty - Physician Assistant Program <div>Principal faculty members play an integral role in the academic and operational success of the program. Under the guidance of the Program Director, they are responsible for advancing the program’s mission and ensuring compliance with ARC-PA standards. This includes active involvement in curriculum design and implementation, student instruction and assessment, academic counseling, admissions, program evaluation, and scholarly and service activities.<br><br><strong>Essential Responsibilities</strong></div><div><strong>Teaching and Instruction</strong></div><ul><li>Deliver didactic instruction in courses such as Patient Assessment Skills, Clinical Medicine Modules, Radiology, EKG, Nutrition, Medical Ethics, Applied Clinical Research, Evidence-Informed Decision-Making, and others within the didactic and clinical curriculum.</li><li>Facilitate laboratory and simulation-based education.</li><li>Advise and mentor students through research projects, guiding clinical question development, literature appraisal, and dissemination of findings.</li><li>Evaluate student performance in classroom, laboratory, and clinical settings, including site visits and review of end-of-rotation assessments.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Curriculum and Course Management</strong></div><ul><li>Serve as course director for assigned courses, responsible for scheduling, syllabus development, coordination of faculty/guest lecturers, exam development, item writing, and day-to-day course oversight.</li><li>Participate in curriculum development, revision, and mapping to program competencies and accreditation standards.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Student Advisement and Support</strong></div><ul><li>Provide academic and professional advising to current students.</li><li>Participate in student remediation planning as needed.</li><li>Serve as a resource for prospective students during the admissions process.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Scholarship</strong></div><ul><li>Engage in scholarly activities including original research, presentations, and publications appropriate to academic rank.</li><li>Collaborate on or independently pursue grant writing and other scholarly initiatives aligned with faculty expertise and program priorities.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Service</strong></div><ul><li>Participate in program admissions processes, including reviewing applications, conducting candidate interviews, and coordinating recruitment activities.</li><li>Represent the PA Program at information sessions, outreach events, and promotional activities.</li><li>Serve on departmental, school, or university committees.</li><li>Contribute to accreditation-related responsibilities, including the preparation of self-study documents and other reports.</li></ul> SHP - Physician Assistant Stud RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Health Professions-L3 7590 26FA0122 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280417 2026-09-03T15:32:41-04:00 2026-09-03T15:32:41-04:00 Center for Professional Development Adjunct Clinical Instructor Faculty <div>We are seeking qualified adjunct clinical instructors to teach on a per diem basis in our continuing education program through the Center for Professional Development. We deliver a variety of cutting edge offerings throughout the year, which can be found on our course schedule.</div> Entry Baccalaureate Nursing Pr RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Nursing Dean's Offic-L3 7611 25FA0730 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279290 2026-08-03T14:52:19-04:00 2026-08-03T14:52:20-04:00 Student Assistant (7 Positions) <div>Rutgers School of Health Professions (SHP) is seeking a Student Assistant to work in the Department of Rehabilitation and Movement Science.<br><br>Under direction, the Student Assistant will assist faculty with classroom records and assignments. The Student Assistant also leads discussion sections and meets with students during office hours, conferencing with them individually or in small groups. Additionally, the Student Assistant assists with organizing and maintaining equipment and materials needed for courses and performing other related duties as assigned.<br><br></div><div>Essential duties and responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Interacts with faculty and staff.</li><li>Assists with classroom set up..</li><li>Performs other related duties as assigned.</li></ul><div><br></div> SHP - Rehabilitation & Movemen RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Health Professions-L3 7594 Newark NJ 26ST1522 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275989 2026-05-28T12:20:41-04:00 2026-05-28T12:20:42-04:00 Lecturers (Adjunct Faculty) for the Master’s Program in Information (Fall 2026) <div>The Department of Library and Information Science seeks part-time lecturers for its master’s program in Information. Please see the description of our program at https://comminfo.rutgers.edu/academics/graduate/master-information and the list of courses we offer at https://comminfo.rutgers.edu/academics/courses?courses=&amp;program=32. Within your cover letter, please let us know which courses in our program you feel most prepared to teach. Please submit a cover letter, resume/curriculum vitae, and names and contact information for at least three references. You may also upload any evidence of your teaching experience such as sample syllabi or course materials, results of student instructional ratings, or published work.</div> Library & Information Science New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School  Communicatn & Info Sci-L3 7090 26FA0376 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/273087 2026-04-16T09:36:32-04:00 2026-04-16T09:36:33-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate (Singson) <div>The Singson laboratory at the Waksman Institute of Microbiology is seeking a postdoctoral associate to participate in our studies of reproductive biology in the C.elegans model system. Specifically, the candidate will contribute to our fertilization synapse, sperm activation, and sperm mitochondria dynamics projects. Experience with C.elegans genetics, reproduction, cell biology are required. Further, experience with protein-protein interaction methods like the split ubiquitin yeast-two hybrid method and SIM microscopy training will be needed. The individual will report directly to the laboratory Principle Investigator (PI).<br><br>The scope of the work is primarily as a member of the Singson Lab research time. However scientific interactions at the Waksman Institute, Department of Genetics, and other relevant units will be required as the research progresses.</div> Waksman Institute of Microbiol New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 6726 26FA0362 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/265051 2025-12-12T08:59:34-05:00 2025-12-12T08:59:35-05:00 NTT Lecturer at the rank of Assistant Teaching Professor <div>The Department seeks applications for two one-year, possibly-renewable teaching positions at the rank of NTT Lecturer at the rank of Assistant Teaching Professor available beginning September 2026, subject to the availability of funding, with the possibility of appointment at a higher level for well-qualified candidates. <br><br>This position has a teaching load of 4-4 (four undergraduate mathematics courses in each of the fall and spring semesters), with possible teaching reductions for administrative, advising or other departmental duties. Applicants should have received a Ph.D. and show outstanding evidence of teaching at the undergraduate level. Ideally, candidates will have had at least three years teaching experience by the time the position starts. <br><br>The academic year salary for an assistant resp. associate resp. full teaching professor will not be less than $82,110 based on the most recent collective bargaining agreement between the faculty union (AAUP-AFT) and Rutgers University.<br><br>Applicants should complete the online form associated with this listing and submit a curriculum vitae. In addition, you should register as a job applicant at mathjobs.org <a href=\"https://nam02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.mathjobs.org%2Fjobs%2Flist%2F27753&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cmb1186%40math.rutgers.edu%7Cee965d5ad8c84b009c5508de2b92c92d%7Cb92d2b234d35447093ff69aca6632ffe%7C1%7C0%7C638996106599156270%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=wt6NXS1euVJB74NzOm3ZSvl6vMtmqZQLHvcPfZ0hB0g%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/27753</strong></a> and complete the application, with the requested supporting documents, for position TF26A under the Rutgers University-New Brunswick listing. Review of applications begins on February 1, 2026. Since new positions may become available throughout academic year, applications up to and including February 1, 2027 are encouraged.</div> Mathematics New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 8125 25FA1192 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279634 2026-08-17T11:23:48-04:00 