ers, New Jersey Medical School, seeks an anesthesiologist with additional training in pain management for a full-time position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. We are a vibrant service with over 5,500 outpatient visits and over 1,500 Interventional Procedures per year. In addition, we have an ACGME accredited pain fellowship with one fellow per annum.</div><div>Clinical responsibilities will include: providing outpatient care at the Comprehensive Pain Center and procedures at our new state-of-the-art Pain Procedural Suite located at University Hospital as well as providing on-site anesthesia services to adult patients at University Hospital.</div><div>Teaching the students, residents, and fellow takes place intra-operatively, in clinic plus formal didactic sessions. There is an opportunity for the right candidate to become further involved in the fellowship program as an Associate Director.</div><div>In addition, the candidate will participate in Faculty Development programs, work collaboratively with the members of the department both clinically and administratively and have the ability to participate in research that forwards the discipline both academically and clinically.<br>Discipline both academically and clinically.</div><div>Qualified applicants must: 1. Have a medical doctorate or equivalent, 2. Hold or be eligible for medical licensure in the state of New Jersey, and 3. Be a BC/BE Anesthesiologist and in Pain Management. The effective day of the appointment is August 1st, 2026</div><div>The Rutgers NJMS is an Equal opportunity, Affirmative Action Employer. Minorities, women, individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply.We embrace and celebrate the multiple dimensions of diversity that each member of our community offers, including but not limited to socioeconomic status, race, ethnicity, language, nationality, sex, gender identity/expression, sexual orientation, religion, geography, disability, and age. Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmation Action Employer and is compliant with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). For more information, please visit <a href=\"http://recruitment.rutgers.edu/TheRUCommitment-2.htm\"><strong>http://recruitment.rutgers.edu/TheRUCommitment-2.htm</strong></a> and for the University’s commitment to equal employment opportunity and affirmative, please go to <a href=\"https://policies.rutgers.edu/sites/default/files/60.1.8%20-%20current.pdf\"><strong>https://policies.rutgers.edu/sites/default/files/60.1.8%20-%20current.pdf</strong></a>. <strong>We encourage applications from women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities.</strong></div><div><br></div> NJMS - Anesthesiology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7432 26FA0478 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266238 2025-12-31T09:39:01-05:00 2025-12-31T09:39:02-05:00 Spring Semester 2026: Lecturer, Educational Theory, Policy, and Administration <div>The Graduate School of Education, Rutgers University invites applications for Lecturers (formerly Part Time Lecturers) in the department of Educational Theory, Policy and Administration during the Spring 2026 Semester, February 1, 2026 through June 30, 2026.<br><br>Successful applicants will instruct undergraduate or graduate level courses in social and philosophical foundations of education, educational policy, social studies education, and/or educational leadership. Specific courses might include history of education; philosophy of education; gender in education; race, ethnicity and inequality; urban education; sociology of education; public school finance; policy analysis; school leadership; and queer issues in schools, among others.<br><br>Courses will be offered in a range of modalities beyond traditional settings, including hybrid and online formats as well as synchronous and asynchronous instruction. Course appointments are in the New Brunswick area, as well as, hybrid/online format.</div> Education Theory, Policy & Adm New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Graduate School of Education-L3 6814 25FA0915 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280126 2026-08-28T15:20:40-04:00 2026-08-28T15:20:40-04:00 Lecturers, School of Nursing <div>The Rutgers School of Nursing-Camden seeks expert practitioners and clinicians to join our<br>dynamic team of faculty to share knowledge and experience with undergraduate students<br>preparing for licensure as registered nurses in a wide variety of care settings. Successful<br>applicants will work closely with faculty course coordinators to ensure the achievement of learning<br>outcomes consistent with course objectives, including the maintenance of collaborative effective<br>and ongoing communication with the course coordinator concerning student progress and/or<br>concerns. Responsibilities include attending orientation, reviewing course syllabi with the course<br>coordinator, using the electronic resources associated with the course to access information<br>pertinent to the education of students providing care, grading assignments in Canvas, providing<br>student formative and summative evaluation, documenting clinical observations and/or reportable<br>incidents which may occur during the clinical experience. The posting of grades, completion of the<br>end of semester clinical course report, responding in a timely fashion to student emails via the<br>Rutgers email system and adhering to all policies, procedures, and deadlines of the School of<br>Nursing-Camden are expectations. Some clinical sites require meetings at the site in advance of<br>the clinical assignment and completion of additional site-based requirements. Successful<br>applicants will be required to submit a copy of all required documents including an official<br>transcript of the highest nursing degree earned and a health clearance to<br>JK2485@camden.rutgers.edu no later than one week following notification of their assignment.</div> School of Nursing Camden Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 School of Nursing Camden-L3 6631 26FA0631 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278489 2026-07-09T10:53:43-04:00 2026-07-09T10:53:44-04:00 Mental Health Specialist II - Per Diem - NJ Hopeline <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Mental Health Specialist II&nbsp; (Per Diem) in the 988 Lifeline Services - NJ Hopeline within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.&nbsp;<br><br>Performs functions in support of the Unit’s mission providing streamlined, prompt, and “customer friendly” services to clients of the 988 Lifeline Services. Receives telephone, chat and/or text requests for service, undertakes assessment of the service need of the client and responds by offering support and appropriate referrals or disposition. Demonstrates competency in recognizing the unique needs of clients and applying relevant assessment and support skills with regard to a wide range of issues.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Interacts with client in a therapeutic manner.&nbsp;</li><li>Participates in ensuring that all service requests are handled in an effective and “client friendly” manner.&nbsp;</li><li>Assesses service requests/referrals and responds in accordance with prescribed procedures.&nbsp;</li><li>Assesses client’s condition in order to make/authorize an appropriate disposition.&nbsp;</li><li>Assumes overall responsibilities for completion of all request and documentation for disposition.&nbsp;</li><li>Documents assessments, interventions, and interactions with clients in a timely manner and in accordance with established policies.&nbsp;</li></ul> UBHC - NJ Hopeline RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8707 Remote NJ 26ST1504 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267733 2026-01-21T22:15:48-05:00 2026-01-21T22:15:48-05:00 Curriculum Developer/Designer (Part-Time) - 2026 <div>The Professional Science Master’s Program (PSM) invites applications for part time Curriculum Developers/Designers. We seek qualified instructors who can contribute to the university’s educational mission and bridge the gap between the classroom and the industry.<br><br>Successful candidates will create and/or update curriculum to meet and include the evolving topics and industry, as well as the demand for hybrid and fully online courses. Applicant’s core knowledge should include, but is not limited to, any concentration under agriculture, biotechnology, environmental science, food science, kinesiology and physiology, life sciences (chemistry, biology, physics, etc.), engineering (i.e., biomedical, biochemical, chemical, electrical, computer, pharmaceutical, etc.), pharmacology, computer and information science (i.e., statistics and biostatistics, discovery informatics and data science, applied computing, information technology, networking, etc.), and business (i.e., accounting, finance, leadership, marketing, etc.)<br><br>Successful candidates will be responsible for the following:</div><ul><li>Conducting research of curricula in order to determine what materials, resources and innovations should be added, revised, or adapted to meet new learning models.</li><li>Developing/redesigning curricula at the graduate level, which will include traditional lecture, hybrid, and/or fully online courses (e.g., transitioning from traditional lecture to hybrid courses)</li><li>Preparing course materials (i.e., syllabi, presentations, hand-outs, reading materials, videos etc.) in multiple variations for se in both traditional lectures and online platforms/technology.</li></ul> Professional Science Masters New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Professional Science Masters-L3 6665 26FA0053 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279566 2026-08-13T10:08:14-04:00 2026-08-13T10:08:15-04:00 Program Coordinator <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Program Coordinator in the Child &amp; Adolescent Services – School Based Programs of Rutgers University Behavioral Healthcare.<br><br>The Program Coordinator coordinates and supervises day-to-day operations of School Based Program. Takes a leadership role in program planning and development. Provides clinical supervision to staff of varied disciplines. Coordinates referral process and ongoing collaboration with district personnel. Provides advanced level clinical treatment which meets quality and quantity standards. Documents this treatment appropriately and within specified time frames and ensures that all staff meet documentation requirements. Demonstrates competency in recognizing the unique needs and applying relevant treatment approaches for children (ages 0-12 years), adolescents (ages 12-17 years), and/or young adults (ages 18-21 years).<br><br>Among the key duties of this position of the following:</div><ul><li>Responsible for the strategic planning as well as programmatic and fiscal development of the program.</li><li>Responsible for day-to-day operations of the programs serving children (ages 3-12 years) and/or adolescents (ages 13-21 years).</li><li>Supervises all program personnel and assures that the program complies with all contracted, procedural, and regulatory expectations.</li><li>Provides clinical supervision to clinical staff to ensure that children and adolescents receive treatment interventions that meet their needs.</li><li>Supervises the work operations of assigned staff, develops performance standards, and conducts performance evaluations.</li></ul> UBHC - Acute Children RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7992 South New Brunswick NJ 25ST2651 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279820 2026-08-21T12:14:18-04:00 2026-08-21T12:14:20-04:00 Sr Design Engineer Mechanical <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Sr Design Engineer Mechanical for the Division of Institutional Planning &amp; Operations (IP&amp;O). Under the guidance and direction of the Assistant Director of Construction Technology in the Office of Architecture and Design, this professional coordinates, develops, designs, and budgets mechanical systems for renovation, alternation, and new construction projects and acts as the University’s representative for design related mechanical issues on larger construction projects being designed by independent engineering consultants.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>This position has statewide responsibilities, addressing a wide variety of academic, administrative, research, healthcare, and infrastructure projects.</li><li>Interfaces with a dynamic team of university technical staff including project management, maintenance, safety, controls, commissioning and utilities groups to ensure that mechanical designs are implemented properly from conception through final acceptance.</li><li>Responsible for the content and interpretation of the mechanical design content included in the University Design Standards.</li><li>Provides mechanical engineering guidance to the Project Manager.</li><li>Responsible for reviewing, signing and sealing in house mechanical designs.</li><li>Responsible for the professional engineering review of documents created by external consultants to ensure projects comply with University Design Standards and applicable codes.</li></ul> Institutional Planning & Optns EVP & Chief Admin Officer Institutional Planning & Optns-L3 6605 Piscataway NJ 26ST0016 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277557 2026-06-23T09:06:13-04:00 2026-06-23T09:06:14-04:00 Laboratory/Technical Assistant Casual (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers University-Newark (RU-N), an urban public research university and anchor institution located in Newark, New Jersey, a city of promise, is seeking a Laboratory/Technical Assistant. Reporting to the Principal Investigator, the Laboratory/Technical Assistant (Research Assistant) will assist in supporting the day-to-day operations of the Gluck Lab in the Center for Molecular and Behavioral Neuroscience, facilitating research studies and data analysis.</div><div><br>This position is responsible for and not limited to the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Supporting research studies for the Rutgers African American Brain Health Initiative (AABHI).</li><li>Conducting health screenings and assessing the eligibility of study candidates for the AABHI and other studies.</li><li>Administering neuropsychological and physical tests to study participants, performing initial data interpretation, and archiving data.</li><li>Administering fMRI scans and assisting other laboratory personnel with analysis.</li><li>Running a Polysomnography (PSG) device to conduct nap/sleep studies and working with laboratory personnel on analysis.</li><li>Working with laboratory personnel, helping to develop and implement new cognitive tasks.</li><li>Coordinating community and University-based educational events for survivors of sexual violence.</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>This position is contingent on the continuation of external funding.</strong></div> CMBN Newark Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences Newa-L3 6804 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274384 2026-05-06T11:09:14-04:00 2026-05-06T11:09:15-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate - CEE Urban Informatics Lab & The Infrastructure Resilience Group <div>The Rutgers CEE Urban Informatics lab &amp; The Infrastructure Resilience Group at Rutgers Center for Advanced Infrastructure and Transportation (CAIT) invite applications for two postdoctoral fellow positions in the general areas of community resilience, critical infrastructure protection, and smart cities. The candidates are expected to work in research projects funded by NSF, FEMA, DHS, and other local agencies. They will lead research activities involving harnessing and synthesizing the latest developments in artificial intelligence, remote sensing, and simulation and modeling techniques in the fields of infrastructure engineering, social science, and hydrologic science to improve the resilience and security of urban environments during natural and man-made extreme events. They will have opportunities to work in a state of-the-art lab as Rutgers Urban Informatics laboratory is equipped with a suite of sensing systems such as mobile and static lidar systems, infrared thermography cameras, drones, and EEG as well as advanced computing and visualization systems such as CAVE (an immersive visualization facility),VR, and AR and computing clusters for data intensive research. The candidates will also have access to several live testbeds deployed in critical facilities and communities for studies related to early flood warning systems, air quality prediction, and security in soft target and crowded places. The candidates are expected to publish conference and journal papers, collaborate in multi-disciplinary teams, and write grant proposals.</div> Advanced Infrastructure Center New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Engineering-L3 6709 26FA0456 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266168 2025-12-31T09:32:26-05:00 2025-12-31T09:32:26-05:00 Post Doctoral Associate (Ebright Lab) <div>This position conducts research on RNA polymerase structure and function and on small-molecule inhibitors of RNA polymerase in the Richard Ebright Lab. Uses cryo-ET, cryo-EM, and X-ray crystallography to define structures and structural transitions of transcription complexes and transcription-translation complexes and to identify and characterize small-molecule inhibitors of transcription. Prepares and assays proteins and nuceleic acids. Prepares and assays ribosomes. Prepares text, tables, and figures for patent applications publications. Presents results at scientific meetings.</div><div>Performs professional level experiments and research using various techniques. Carries out routine and non-routine work with review of work outputs by supervisor. Documents work performed and maintains a notebook and database. Communicates effectively with supervisor. Uses and helps maintain highly specialized equipment, in addition to maintaining and keeping the workplace and laboratory organized in a clean and safe manner in accordance with established procedures. Trains and leads research staff, postdoctoral associates, students, and technicians in laboratory related activities. Performs professional work requiring specialized knowledge and application and use of concepts, theories, terminology, and practices.</div> Waksman Institute of Microbiol New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 6726 25FA0757 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280075 2026-08-27T11:18:39-04:00 2026-08-27T11:18:40-04:00 Mental Health Specialist II UBHC <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Mental Health Specialist II for the Acute Psychiatric Services (APS) Department within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Mental Health Specialist II is to provide services which support the delivery of clinical services in the Unit.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Takes primary responsibility for answering telephone calls from consumers.</li><li>Conducts initial triage of consumers and families when they arrive onsite five (5) minutes after arrival and provides immediate report to the Program Coordinator.</li><li>Assists Public Safety in their search for consumers and belongings when they are admitted to the Extended Care Evaluation Bed (ECEB) area.&nbsp;</li><li>Provides direct care for individuals in the ECEB.</li><li>Maintains appropriate client records in a timely manner as mandated by Center policy.</li><li>Assumes responsibility for managing the transfer of consumers into and out of the Unit.</li><li>Assists consumers and/or families in the completion of registration paperwork as required.</li><li>Assists the Program Coordinator in transporting the Unit vehicles for servicing as needed.</li></ul> UBHC - Emergency Screening Psy RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8029 Piscataway NJ 26ST1641 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278332 2026-07-07T10:17:06-04:00 2026-07-07T10:17:07-04:00 Tenure-Track Assistant/Associate Professor <div>Rutgers is a research-intensive university with state of the art research core services and a strong research support infrastructure. Rutgers School of Health Professions (SHP), one of the top ranked schools of its kind in the nation, offers a unique and nurturing environment to conduct interdisciplinary and team based research. The School has fostered a culture of collaboration and a strong community of support for research faculty to build their programs and to thrive.<br><br>The Department of Biomedical and Health Informatics at Rutgers SHP is looking for a tenure-track faculty (multiple openings) with expertise in Biomedical and Health Informatics, Data Science, Health-related AI, Digital Health or related field. Special consideration will be given to candidates with Health AI expertise, applicable to aging, opioid addition, and neurodegenerative disorders.<br><br>The tenure-track faculty member’s primary responsibility is in conducting research (80-90% effort) to grow and sustain an extramurally and federally funded research program. A small allocation of effort is towards teaching and service (10-20% maximum). Teaching may include mentoring of graduate students and post-docs.</div> School of Health Professions RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Health Professions-L3 7567 26FA0632 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267050 2026-01-09T11:24:31-05:00 2026-01-09T11:24:31-05:00 Post-Doctoral Associate: Research in Biochemistry (Medicinal Chemistry Dept) <div>The Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy at Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey is seeking multiple post-doctoral associates to join the laboratory of Dr Jun Wang within the Department of Medicinal Chemistry on or about September 1, 2022. The successful candidates will participate in NIH-funded projects in antiviral research.</div> Medicinal Chemistry RBHS Chancellor-L2 Ernest Mario School of Pharmac-L3 6716 22FA0971 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280230 2026-08-31T14:21:22-04:00 2026-08-31T14:21:23-04:00 Supervising Program Assistant I <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Supervising Program Assistant I for the Military Services within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>Under direction, manages office support operations and activities for the Call Center and is responsible for grant management and reporting. This position provides related administrative services as required.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Provides day-to-day supervision of clerical/secretarial staff assigned to the office.&nbsp;</li><li>Works collaboratively with program leadership and Clinical staff to ensure that the unit operates efficiently and effectively on a daily basis to include nights and weekends. &nbsp;</li><li>Provides detailed call reports to include phone and data management systems work and the ability to analyze reports to assist the Executive Director/Director and supervisory staff in daily operations.&nbsp;</li><li>Coordinates and performs detailed documents, fiscal procedures and maintains records associated with grant accounts and state and federal budgets, donations and fund raising activities.&nbsp;</li><li>Tracks budgets for programs and ensures funds are utilized according to policy and regulations.&nbsp;</li><li>Compiles necessary data and justification for projected expenditures.&nbsp;</li><li>Subject matter expert on fiscal procedures.&nbsp;</li><li>Prepares a myriad of reports, organization charts, work flow processes and spreadsheets containing findings, analyses, conclusions and recommendations as requested. &nbsp;</li><li>Maintains multiple department accounts, monitoring expenditures and insuring compliance with budgets. &nbsp;</li></ul> UBHC - Military Services RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8040 Piscataway NJ 26ST1695 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278805 2026-07-14T13:24:20-04:00 2026-07-14T13:24:21-04:00 Statewide Specialty Counselor (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers University- Newark (RU-N), an urban public research university and anchor institution, located in Newark, New Jersey, a city of promise, is seeking a Statewide Specialty Counselor to join the New Jersey Small Business Development Center (NJSBDC) network. This role supports small business clients throughout New Jersey by providing personalized, one-on-one counseling, along with educational webinars and training sessions designed to address and resolve complex business challenges.<br><br></div><div>The Statewide Specialty Counselor will guide entrepreneurs and small business owners in starting, managing, and expanding their businesses. Specific areas of focus include business planning and strategic development, entity formation, marketing and sales strategy, financial management and access to capital, legal and compliance matters, certification and procurement readiness, human resources and talent management, cybersecurity and digital transformation, operations and process improvement, exporting and international trade, and industry-specific challenges such as manufacturing, retail, and food service.</div><div>This position is responsible for and not limited to the following:</div><ul><li>Utilizing critical thinking and analytical expertise to create customized strategies tailored to each small business client's specific needs through individualized one-on-one counseling</li><li>Developing and delivering group training sessions and webinars to disseminate knowledge and resources, depending on area(s) of specialty</li><li>Collaborating closely with other NJSBDC counselors to provide comprehensive client support</li><li>Staying informed on emerging trends, regulatory changes, and industry best practices relevant to the assigned specialty area</li><li>Delivering on assigned metrics for federal and state requirements</li><li>Engaging in activities that facilitate cross-functional coordination, stakeholder communication, and the ongoing alignment of programmatic efforts with strategic objectives</li><li>Maintaining and creating new productive working relationships with key statewide small business stakeholders</li><li>Tracking and reporting outreach and consulting activities, ensuring compliance with organizational guidelines</li><li>Building and maintaining strong client relationships, fostering collaboration and trust throughout the consulting process</li></ul><div><br></div> NJSBDA - Headquarters Newark Chancellor-L2 Rutgers Business School-L3 6938 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/269992 2026-02-27T14:44:10-05:00 2026-02-27T14:44:11-05:00 Part-time Oral and Maxillofacial Surgeon <div>The Department of Oral and Maxillofacial Surgery is searching for several part time oral and maxillofacial surgeons at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. Responsibilities will include staffing the predoctoral and resident clinics as well as participation in the didactic curriculum offered by the department. The ideal candidate must have completed an accredited OMFS training program and be eligible for New Jersey dental licensure with preference for board certification by the American Board of Oral and Maxillofacial Surgeons. Position will remain open until filled. Salary and rank will be commensurate with experience and training.</div> RSDM - OMFS RBHS Chancellor-L2 Rutgers School of Dental Medic-L3 7546 26FA0032 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280467 2026-09-04T14:21:57-04:00 2026-09-04T14:21:58-04:00 Finance and Accounting Assistant (part-time) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a part-time Finance and Accounting Assistant for Mason Gross School of the Arts (MGSA).&nbsp; Reporting directly to the Budget Analyst Supervisor, this position provides support in business and accounting for the MGSA Business Office. Among the key duties of the position are the following:</div><div>&nbsp;</div><ul><li>Prepares a variety of financial transactions, including and not limited to, procurement, journal entries and project cost adjustments, and payroll.</li><li>Reconciles expenditures and commitments and maintain financial tracking database</li><li>Prepares and distributes recurring financial reports.</li><li>Serves as a liaison with Accounts Payable, Payroll, Procurement, and other administrative offices to resolve financial and operation matters.</li></ul> Mason Gross School of Arts Dea New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Mason Gross School of Arts Dea-L3 8090 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279421 2026-08-07T13:43:13-04:00 2026-08-07T13:43:14-04:00 Post Doc Assoc - Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Postdoctoral Fellow for the Behavioral Research and Training Institute (BRTI)– Center for Integrated Care within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Postdoctoral Fellow is to be responsible for research and clinical activities with the Behavioral Research and Training Institute.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Conceptualizes, designs and implements research and program evaluation projects in support of the lab’s mission.</li><li>Based on a thorough knowledge of the field and the research literature, identifies research projects that would contribute to increasing the body of knowledge related to integrated behavioral health, addiction, psychology.</li><li>Translates research ideas into concrete, specific and implementable research projects that meet the standards of scientific inquiry and that comport with University requirements.</li><li>Assists the AVP in the preparation of research proposals to obtain grant support from federal, state and local units of government, as well as foundations.</li><li>Provides technical assistance to research lab based on needs assessment and data collection.</li><li>Under the supervision of the AVP, manages and coordinates research projects.</li><li>Remains up-to-date on the knowledge related to addiction, psychology, and integrated care through regular review of the professional literature.</li><li>Prepares manuscripts summarizing the center’s research projects for submission to professional journals and publications.</li><li>Conducts surveillance of funding opportunities from government and foundation sources and communicates relevant opportunities to the AVP.</li></ul> UBHC - BRTI Institute RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8044 Piscataway NJ 26ST1265 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/276480 2026-06-04T10:26:34-04:00 2026-06-04T10:26:35-04:00 Pulmonary Hypertension Faculty <div>Medical Director of the Pulmonary Hypertension Program. Provide outpatient and inpatient consultation and follow-up, and perform all procedures related to pulmonary hypertension and build the Pulmonary Hypertension Program for the Southern region of RWJ Barnabas Health.&nbsp;</div> RWJ - Medicine Pulmonary RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7779 26FA0541 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274041 2026-04-30T11:27:20-04:00 2026-04-30T11:27:21-04:00 Instructor/Internship Coordinator for CCAS <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the Faculty of Arts &amp; Sciences is seeking a course instructor/Internship Coordinator for the Internship programs within the College for academic year 2026-2027.<br>Responsibilities include:<br>- Prepare course material for topics related to experiential learning and professional development;<br>- Ensures/follows the student's internship includes learning objectives, observation, reflection, evaluation and assessment;<br>- Promotes academic, career and/or personal development;<br>- Prepare materials for an Online Internship Course to be available to students completing their degrees at one of Rutgers-Camden's satellite campuses and to Rutgers-Camden campus students who are doing an internship outside of a 50 mile radius of campus.</div> Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 8076 26FA0407 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/265919 2025-12-31T09:02:45-05:00 2025-12-31T09:02:45-05:00 Teaching Instructor or Assistant/Associate Teaching Professor <div>Teaching Instructor, Assistant Teaching Professor, or Associate Teaching Professor of Mathematics. Subject to the availability of funding, the Department of Mathematics at Rutgers University-New Brunswick expects to have one or more renewable, non-tenure-track teaching positions at the level of Teaching Instructor, with the possibility of appointment at a higher level (Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor) for exceptionally well-qualified candidates.<br><br></div><div>This position has a teaching load of 4-4 (four undergraduate mathematics courses in each of the fall and spring semesters), with possible teaching reductions for administrative, advising or other departmental duties. Applicants should have received a Ph.D. and show outstanding evidence of teaching at the undergraduate level. Ideally, candidates will have had at least three years teaching experience by the time the position starts.<br><br></div><div>To apply, complete the application associated with this listing and include a curriculum vitae. In addition, you must also submit an application on mathjobs.org for the job code TF24 listed under Rutgers University-New Brunswick (https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/25894). Rutgers University is an exciting, large public state university with one of the most diverse student bodies in the nation.<br><br>All applicants should also register at mathjobs.org, and submit the following materials for the Rutgers University-New Brunswick position “TF24” there:<br><br></div><div>(a) AMS cover sheet<br><br></div><div>(b) CV<br><br></div><div>(c) one or more letters of recommendation addressing their teaching qualifications<br><br></div><div>(d) a teaching statement<br><br></div><div>(e – optional) their teaching portfolio, including results of student surveys of classes they have taught.<br><br></div><div>Review of applications begins on November 22, 2024. Since new positions may become available throughout the Spring and Summer of 2025, applications up to and including August 31, 2025 are encouraged.<br><br></div> Mathematics New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 8125 24FA1241 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279681 2026-08-18T14:03:49-04:00 2026-08-18T14:03:50-04:00 Research Associate II <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Research Associate II in the Department of&nbsp; Pharmacology, Physiology &amp; Neuroscience within the New Jersey Medical School (NJMS).<br><br>Under direction of the Principal Investigator, the Research Associate II will contribute to development and testing of solutions for data integration, including data from single cell and epigenomic assays. Contributing to maintenance of genomic and imaging data analysis pipelines, including data from chromatin conformation, 3D spatial imaging, and super-resolution microscopy. Collaborating with experimental scientists to explore and interpret various genomic and epigenomic data types. Participation in lab and departmental meetings and discussions.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:&nbsp;</div><ul><li>Designs, performs and analyzes experiments in microbiology, immunology, molecular biology, biochemistry, cell biology, genetics or data science.</li><li>Participates in the development of performance standards, selection of methodology and instrumentation and coordination of the analytical, biochemical, physiology and instrumentation functions with the clinical and research areas to ensure conformance with the goals and objectives of the department.</li><li>Under supervision, assists in the conducting of continuous program of research and development regarding the analytical and instrumentation functions of the laboratory, participates in the evaluation of the existing procedures, suggesting revision where necessary and proposing new procedures where required.</li><li>Remains up-to-date in relevant scientific literature.</li><li>Writes scientific papers for submission to journals.&nbsp;</li></ul> NJMS - Pharmacology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7431 Newark NJ 26ST1624 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280007 2026-08-26T09:56:03-04:00 2026-08-26T09:56:03-04:00 Coadjutant Non-Teaching <div>Looking for a candidate that can Oversee the operation and coordination of the Packaging Engineering laboratories, including laboratory facilities, equipment, and laboratory instructional activities.<br>Responsibilities include ensuring that laboratories are properly maintained, equipment is operational and available for teaching safety procedures are followed, and laboratory resources effectively support the Packaging Engineering curriculum.<br>Coordinate with faculty, staff, and students regarding laboratory needs, equipment use, maintenance, and improvements.</div> Mechanical & Aerospace Eng New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Engineering-L3 8113 26FA0711 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277781 2026-06-25T11:23:47-04:00 2026-06-25T11:23:48-04:00 Staff Nurse Mental Health PT Eves UCHC EMCFW <div>University Correctional Healthcare is seeking a Part Time UCHC Staff Nurse for Edna Mahan Correctional Facility, located in Clinton, NJ. The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus. Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br><br>Among the duties are:</div><ul><li>Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the inmate-patient including adults (18 to 64 years), and geriatrics (65+) within the framework established by the correctional system.</li><li>Utilizes effective communication skills by demonstrating respect, concern and courtesy in all interpersonal relationships.</li><li>Uses current knowledge to promote a safe environment for providing health care to inmate-patients.</li></ul> UCHC Edna Mahan Correction Med RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7659 Clinton NJ 26ST0713 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275528 2026-05-20T13:54:04-04:00 2026-05-20T13:54:05-04:00 Dining Services Student Worker (Harvest Juice Bar) <div>Join the Rutgers Dining team as a Dining Services Student Worker in one of our dining halls or retail operations across the New Brunswick and Piscataway campuses. Rutgers Dining Services strives to be the best in culinary excellence and as a Dining Services Worker you play a critical role in the customer experience. From assisting in the preparation and service of food, to maintaining the presentation of the dining halls, to assisting guests, we have a variety of roles and will find the right one for you!<br><br>Dining Service Workers earn a paycheck and more:</div><ol><li>Student employee meal privileges.</li><li>Flexible schedules (10/20 hours/week) that work around your classes and activities.</li><li>Convenient on-campus locations.</li><li>Opportunities to advance to leadership positions such as Captain, Meal Manager and Student Unit Manager.</li><li>Valuable work experience to add to your resume.</li><li>Learn important job skills including interpersonal communications, team dynamics, dependability and time management.</li><li>A fun and welcoming environment.</li></ol> Harvest Juice Bar New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Student Affairs - New Brunswic-L3 8456 Piscataway NJ 26ST1104 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266317 2025-12-31T09:48:46-05:00 2025-12-31T09:48:46-05:00 Post-Doctoral Associate <div>The Department of Statistics at Rutgers University invites applications for a full-time post-doctoral position, with a start date as early as December 1, 2025, but otherwise flexible. The successful applicant will work in the areas of causal inference and statistical learning with high-dimensional observational data, including development of statistical and computational methods, and applications in comparative effectiveness research through collaboration with the Rutgers Institute for Health, Health Care Policy and Aging Research.<br><br></div><div>Applicants must have a doctoral degree in statistics, computer science, or a related field. Expertise in causal inference and machine learning (in particular reinforcement learning), and strong experience with programming are desired.. Excellent communication and writing skills are needed.s</div> Statistics New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 7018 25FA1113 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280154 2026-08-31T08:42:14-04:00 2026-08-31T08:42:15-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse FT Nights UCHC SWSP <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking Full Time Licensed Practical Nurse (Medical) for Southwoods State Prison, located in Bridgeton, NJ<br><br>The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs.</li><li>Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.</li><li>Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.</li><li>Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.</li><li>Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.</li><li>Documents all aspects of patient care.</li></ul> UCHC-South Woods Psn-Ancillary RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7685 Bridgeton NJ 26ST0552 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278573 2026-07-10T11:00:42-04:00 2026-07-10T11:00:43-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse PT Days UCHC BSP <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Part Time Licensed Practical Nurse for the Bayside State Prison, located in Leesburg, NJ.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Initiates the admission process and assists with the identification of recurrent health problem, symptoms and behavioral changes of the resident.</li><li>Collects pertinent data through observation, interview and other members of the health team and communicates changes in the resident condition to other resident care providers.</li><li>Maintains clinical area in clean, neat, safe manner and participates in required counts and cleaning assignments.</li><li>Adheres to institution and medical unit infection control policies.</li><li>Maintains current professional skills and continues professional growth to enhance the practice of correctional nursing and the image of the organization.</li></ul> UCHC Bayside State Prison Anci RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7684 Leesburg NJ 26ST0662 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/268290 2026-01-30T10:21:58-05:00 2026-01-30T10:21:58-05:00 Co Adj Non-Teaching - NJTSS-ER Trainer/Coach <div>The New Jersey Tiered Systems of Support for Early Reading (NJTSS-ER) Project provides professional development to school districts to facilitate implementation of NJTSS-ER with students in kindergarten through third grade. With funding from a recent New Jersey Department of Education grant, Rutgers University is seeking co-adjunct staff to provide part-time regional training and coaching to expand NJTSS-ER implementation capacity for school districts throughout the state. Through web-based training and ongoing coaching, these new regional trainers/coaches will maintain a crucial role in scaling implementation of NJTSS-ER.</div> Inclusive Schools Project New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Graduate School of Applied & P-L3 6826 25FA0709 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280353 2026-09-03T09:29:11-04:00 2026-09-03T09:29:12-04:00 Administrative Coordinator II <div>Rutgers School of Public Health (SPH) is seeking an Administrative Coordinator II in the Department of Health Behavior, Society and Policy, located in Piscataway, NJ. The Administrative Coordinator II will perform a wide variety of administrative support to the Department and Chair focused on academic planning, educational programming, the teaching and learning agenda, and student success. Assists in the planning, coordination and support of Department-related activities.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Assists the Chair with administrative tasks and calendaring; represents the Chair and Department with professionalism; and maintainsconfidentiality regarding sensitive information.</li><li>Provides administrative support for faculty research activities, including processing research-related expenses and reimbursements,ordering supplies for research projects, assisting with onboarding and orientation logistics for research staff, maintaining relatedadministrative records, and coordinating with faculty, staff, and university offices to support timely research operations.</li><li>Performs office management duties for programs overseen by the department. Determines workflow; monitors and processesnecessary paperwork; maintains records and filing systems; maintains the department emergency contact list and relatedadministrative records; handles subject fee vouchers, departmental deposits, gift cards, and associated tracking logs; maintainsdepartmental calendars; coordinates with School offices to avoid scheduling conflicts; and manages room scheduling and setup forcourses, seminars, meetings, and in-person events.</li><li>Monitors and assists with student admissions and recruitment processes. Convene meetings of concentration leads and tracks outreachefforts to prospective students.</li></ul> SPH - Health Systems RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Public Health-L3 7711 Piscataway NJ 26ST1607 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279216 2026-07-31T07:52:28-04:00 2026-07-31T07:52:29-04:00 Postdoctoral Associate <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Postdoctoral Associate in the Department of Microbiology, Biochemistry and Molecular Genetics within the New Jersey Medical School (NJMS).<br><br>Under the direction of the Principal Investigator the Post doctoral Associate will perform research. The Altindis Lab studies viral insulin/IGF‑1‑like peptides (VILPs) – sequences encoded by viruses that mimic human insulin and IGF‑1. We investigate how VILPs interact with and inhibit the human IGF‑1 receptor (IGF1R) with high specificity, without affecting the insulin receptor. Using structural biology (cryoEM), proximity labeling (TurboID), phosphoproteomics, and mouse models (including bGHTg acromegaly mice and breast cancer xenografts), we aim to uncover fundamental mechanisms of IGF1R antagonism and develop peptide‑based inhibitors for diseases such as cancer and diabetic complications.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Performs independent research involving cell culture, receptor signaling assays, in vivo mouse models, and molecular biology techniques under the PI’s guidance.</li><li>Meets with the principal investigator to establish goals and objectives for VILP-related projects</li><li>Communicates regularly with the P.I.</li><li>Maintains detailed and accurate experimental records.</li><li>Supervises and trains subordinate staff.</li><li>Reads current scientific and technical literature relevant to the laboratory’s mission.</li></ul> NJMS - Microbiology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7430 Newark NJ 26ST1116 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/272490 2026-04-06T16:59:51-04:00 2026-04-06T16:59:52-04:00 Coadjutant - RBS Executive Education -Multiple positions open <div>Non-credit instructors needed to teach various Executive Education courses. Successful Applicants will instruct courses in the field of business and related subjects. Courses will be offered in a range of modalities beyond traditional settings. Successful candidates will develop and instruct courses on a wide variety of topics. Instructors shall report to the Associate Dean of the Executive Education department, prepare and submit course syllabi and materials, and adhere to the grade submission policies and deadlines.</div> Executive Education Center Newark Chancellor-L2 Rutgers Business School-L3 6965 26FA0304 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280137 2026-08-28T15:52:00-04:00 2026-08-28T15:52:01-04:00 Mental Health Clinician II <div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Mental Health Clinician II for the Outpatient Services Department within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>Provides culturally competent outpatient mental health services that meet the needs of the designated adult population. Participates in the assessment of clinical needs and provides skill acquisition and symptom management using evidence based individual, group, and family therapy for mental health and co-occurring chemical abuse/dependency.<br><br>Among the key duties of the position are the following:</div><ul><li>Assesses treatment needs and provides evidence supported individual, group, and family treatment that is consistent with the service design and philosophy of the program, as clinically indicated, to assigned clients.</li><li>Coordinates with CCBH case managers’ linkages and referrals for assigned clients, including coordination of treatment and liaison with medical providers and community agencies.</li><li>Maintains clinical documentation standards as mandated by UBHC policy and other applicable accreditation and certification entities.</li><li>Develops and applies knowledge of trends and advancements in the field of practice.</li><li>Champions the utilization of evidence-based and preferred practices by developing own skills, mentoring others, and providing case consultation, as observed by supervisor.</li><li>Effectively contributes to and supports an environment that enhances the positive self-image of clients and preserves their human dignity, as observed by supervisor.</li></ul> UBHC - Outpatient New Brunswic RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8016 Piscataway NJ 25ST2074 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278503 2026-07-09T11:42:58-04:00 2026-07-09T11:42:59-04:00 Business Manager <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Business Manager within the Finance Department at the Rutgers Cancer Institute.<br><br>Under the direction of the Associate Directors of Finance, and in close collaboration with the Program Lead(s), the Business Manager is responsible for the business management of the Assigned Programs. In this capacity, the Business Manager maintains thorough knowledge of Program plans, goals, and activities, and works closely with the Program Lead(s) on business/financial planning and evaluation. Additionally, the Business Manager is responsible for maintaining the integrated financial profiles of all investigators within Assigned Programs, producing meaningful data analysis to support decision making, and developing financial forecasting and presentation data.&nbsp;<br><br>The incumbent also oversees the day-to-day administrative grants management of all projects, grants, contracts and other restricted accounts and related functions associated with research, sponsored programs, and restricted as well as unrestricted funds activities of Assigned Programs at Rutgers Cancer Institute. Further, the Business Manager ensures that both pre- and post-award activities comply with Federal and State, University, and Sponsor requirements and acts as a liaison with other University departments.</div><div><br>Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Serves as the primary business partner of and maintains close communication with the Assigned Program Leader(s).</li><li>Participates in Assigned Program(s) planning and operating committees and meetings to ensure a thorough understanding of Center goals, objectives and activities and an ability to provide well-informed business guidance.</li><li>Maintains the integrated (restricted and unrestricted) financial profiles of the Assigned Program(s) as a whole and of all investigators within the Assigned Program.</li><li>Produces meaningful data analysis to support decision making and develops financial forecasting and reporting.</li><li>Provides accounting management involving accountability for effective internal systems and controls within University financial policy for tracking income and expenditures.</li><li>Responsible for oversight and management of Assigned Program(s) operating budgets. Provides oversight and management of department operating budgets (expenses and revenue), sponsored research, contract and gift funds, federal funds, and endowments.</li><li>Provides relevant reports for department leadership including financial, clinical, research and teaching productivity.</li><li>Creates effective work plans and works closely with staff by supervising and addressing their training needs in order to achieve competency of work performance and understanding of personnel and non-personnel operating budgets.</li><li>Oversees and reviews personnel requests for unfilled positions (new and replacement positions) as they relate to the established budget. Provides fiscal pre-approval, or alerts department and Senior Leadership of insufficient funding.</li><li>Meets with faculty to review existing budgets and map out goals and strategies for the new fiscal year; works with PIs on annual requests for institutional research support, as needed.</li><li>Oversees creation of “Just in time” documentation for NIH applications as well as any formal communications (e.g., No Cost Extension requests) regarding submissions or progress inquiries to respective implementing agencies.</li></ul> CINJ - Finance RBHS Chancellor-L2 Cancer Institute of New Jersey-L3 7962 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1505 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267844 2026-01-23T09:48:35-05:00 2026-01-23T09:48:35-05:00 Division Chief, Pediatric Pulmonary Medicine <div><strong>Division Chief, Pediatric Pulmonary Medicine<br></strong><br></div><div><strong>Rutgers University, Robert Wood Johnson Medical School<br></strong><br></div><div><strong>Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital, New Brunswick, NJ<br></strong><br></div><div><strong><br></strong><br></div><div>The Department of Pediatrics at Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School (RWJMS) is seeking an outstanding leader to serve as Division Chief of Pulmonary Medicine.<br><br></div><div>The Division Chief will be board certified in Pediatric Pulmonology Medicine. The Division Chief will have a strong academic and clinical background and be responsible for all scholarly, clinical, educational, and administrative activities of the Division. The role will include scholarly clinical and educational activities. The Division Chief will have a proven track record in investigative work, clinical care and education. The Division Chief will join 3 full time faculty members who provide Pediatric pulmonology coverage. The Division Chief will be responsible for overall supervision of the Division’s faculty members’ activities, including teaching, clinical care, research, and other Division and Department duties. The Division Chief will also have the opportunity to participate in either clinical or lab-based research. The clinical services of the division of pediatric pulmonology are conducted at Bristol-Myers Squibb Children’s Hospital (BMSCH) of the Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital, New Brunswick, NJ. The Division Chief will provide overall oversight of Pediatric Pulmonology at Bristol-Myers-Squibb Children’s Hospital. The Division Chief will be committed to the academic mission of Rutgers and RWJMS which includes education across the spectrum of trainees including medical students, residents and fellows in the institution.</div><div>The Department of Pediatrics has a full complement of pediatric medical and surgical subspecialists. Outpatient services are provided at the Child Health Institute of New Jersey which also houses our research faculty. The commitment to the academic mission of Rutgers RWJMS allows for the educational opportunities across the spectrum of trainees including students, residents, and fellows. The Department of Pediatrics includes physicians and basic scientists who conduct collaborative research with an emphasis on mechanisms of disease, novel therapies, epidemiology and/or outcomes research in the areas of relevance to childhood diseases. The Department provides a collaborative setting for the study of basic mechanisms of disease and outcomes research that would provide new insights to the treatment of childhood diseases. The Robert Wood Johnson School of Medicine is consistently ranked as one of the highly NIH-funded academic universities and Rutgers is a member of the Association of American Universities comprising the top research universities in North America.<br><br></div><div>Adjacent to the Children’s hospital is the PSE&amp;G Children’s Specialized Hospital which is one of the country’s largest inpatient acute rehabilitation hospitals for children. Across the street is the Rutgers Cancer Institute of New Jersey – the only NCI designated center in the state of New Jersey as well as the Ronald MacDonald House. As the state’s premiere institution, located in central Jersey, there are many opportunities to collaborate across campuses with all the health professional schools and biomedical science schools at the Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences.<br><br></div><div>Interested candidates should email a cover letter and your CV to:<br><br></div><div><strong><br></strong><br></div><div><strong>Vikas Dharnidharka, MD MPH<br>Chair Department of Pediatrics, RWJMS<br></strong><br></div><div><strong><br></strong><br></div><div><strong>Office address:<br>Clinical Academic Building, Rm 7106<br>125 Paterson Street<br>New Brunswick, NJ 08901<br>Email: vikas.d@rutgers.edu<br></strong><br></div> RWJ - Pediatrics Pulmonary RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7811 25FA0872 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280267 2026-09-01T08:52:59-04:00 2026-09-01T08:53:00-04:00 Student Assistant (Research), Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking multiple Student Assistants for the department of Emergency Medicine at the Robert Wood Johnson Medical School.<br><br>Under the direction of the Principal Investigator, the Student Assistant will work for the Department of Emergency Medicine at Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School (RWJMS). The Student Assistant (Research) will assist the Principal Investigator with a research study to better understand how patient-reported feedback loops for diagnostic excellence could work in the real-world, as well as other research studies as needed.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Will obtain knowledge on project-related research topics including emergency medicine and public health.</li><li>Participates in phone, electronic, and in-person communications and meetings with principal investigator and study team to support the development and improvement of programs.</li><li>Assists with project activities as needed, including participant recruitment, consent, scheduling, interviewing participants off-site or online to collect quantitative and qualitative data.</li><li>Works with the Principal Investigator to develop appropriate and detailed standard operating procedures, training manuals and other materials for study conduct and data collection.</li><li>Performs other related duties as assigned.</li></ul> RWJ - Emergency Medicine RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7854 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1567 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278940 2026-07-17T12:16:54-04:00 2026-07-17T12:16:55-04:00 Program Director of the Master of Science in Clinical Laboratory Science <div>Rutgers University’s School of Health Professions (SHP) invites applications for an open-rank, full-time, 12-month, non-tenure-track faculty position serving as Program Director of the Master of Science in Clinical Laboratory Science (MS-CLS) with the Department of Clinical Laboratory and Medical Imaging Sciences (CLMIS). Major responsibilities are to provide leadership and administration of the program in alignment with the strategic plan of the department and school, including program budget, resource allocation, curricular planning, and assessment. Faculty responsibilities include course development and instruction in remote graduate courses, graduate research advisement, active participation in research, grant writing, and other scholarly activities, and service to the university, school, and professional community.</div><div><br><strong>Primary Responsibilities:</strong></div><ul><li>Provide overall coordination of the MS-CLS program and participate in meetings at SHP, RBHS, Rutgers University, and collaborating departments.</li><li>Communicate regularly with the CLMIS Chair and Division leadership regarding program operations.</li><li>Administer SHP, CLMIS, and MS-CLS policies related to program and student matters.</li><li>Maintain MS-CLS program records of active and inactive MS-CLS students, graduate certificate students, academic files, and program documentation and files.</li><li>Provide program data, including enrollment, courses, and activities, for departmental reporting.</li><li>Assign faculty advisors for student registration and graduate project mentors.</li><li>Collaborate with faculty teaching \"Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis\" to assign CLS content advisors.</li><li>Collaborate with the CLMIS Chair and DCLS Program Director to plan and coordinate faculty resources and budget needs annually.</li><li>Collaborate on curriculum review and revision for MS-CLS and Graduate Certificate programs.</li><li>Ensure submission and tracking of new or revised courses through required approval processes (e.g., CCCR).</li><li>Update course descriptions and graduation requirements documentation as needed, including necessary learning management system management.</li><li>Develop and maintain multi-year course scheduling plans and manage semester scheduling updates.</li><li>Communicate schedule changes to students and update tracking systems.</li><li>Orient new students to the program and assist with enrollment and onboarding.</li><li>Participate in program assessment, accreditation activities, committees, and<br>institutional service.</li><li>Engage in teaching, research, scholarly activity, and professional development.</li><li>Ensure compliance with Rutgers, Rutgers Health Corporate Compliance policies, Code of<br>Conduct, and Conflict of Interest policies.</li><li>Performs other related duties as assigned.</li></ul> SHP - CLMIS RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Health Professions-L3 7592 26FA0551 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/271485 2026-03-24T10:19:22-04:00 2026-03-24T10:19:23-04:00 Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Pediatric Hospital Medicine <div>The Department of Pediatrics at Rutgers Robert Wood Medical School is seeking to hire a faculty member in the division of Pediatric Hospital Medicine. Candidates should be fellowship-trained and board-eligible in Pediatric Hospital Medicine. At RWJMS Pediatric Hospitalists see patients and mentor students and residents on our inpatient units, well newborn nurseries and same day medical units of the Bristol-Myers Squibb Children’s Hospital (BMSCH). BMSCH is located on our academic child health campus, which also includes the PSEG Children’s Specialized Hospital (for acute Rehabilitation) and the Child Health Institute of NJ. The children’s hospital is adjacent to the RWJUH adult hospital which is connected via a bridge to the Rutgers Cancer Institute of NJ – the only NCI designated center in the state of New Jersey.</div><div>We are seeking a candidate who has a passion for teaching and enjoys caring for children with a wide variety of conditions including those who are medically complex. We value leadership. Applicants with research training and a portfolio of scholarly productivity are encouraged to apply. As a part of Rutgers University RWJMS, faculty have the opportunity to collaborate with colleagues in the basic and social sciences, other clinical arms of the university (e.g. Social Work, Pharmacy) and the Rutgers School of Public Health, among others. We embrace applicants from diverse backgrounds and experience including those underrepresented in medicine.</div><div>Rutgers is NJ’s State University and provides broad opportunities for collaboration within the School and across the state. Rutgers Health Professions Schools and the Institute for Health, Healthcare Policy, and Health Policy, and Brain Health Institute comprise Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences Rutgers University is the lead institution (along with Princeton University and NJ Instituted of Technology), in NJ ACTS, an Translational Research Institute that is one of 42 funded by the NIH as part of its Clinical and Translations Science Award (CTSA) program.</div><div>This is an excellent opportunity for a dynamic career-oriented physician. The position offers a competitive salary and benefits package and academic rank commensurate with experience.</div><div><br>Interested candidates should email a cover letter and CV to:</div><div>Dalya Chefitz, MD</div><div>Professor and Division Director</div><div>Pediatric Hospital Medicine Division</div><div>Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School</div><div>1 Robert Wood Johnson Place, MEB-348</div><div>New Brunswick, NJ 08901</div><div><a href=\"mailto:chefitda@rwjms.rutgers.edu\"><strong>d.chefitz@rutgers.edu</strong></a></div> RWJ - Pediatrics Hospital Medi RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7810 25FA0868 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279500 2026-08-11T10:58:39-04:00 2026-08-11T10:58:40-04:00 Post-Doctoral Associate <div>The Department of Psychology in the School of Arts and Sciences-Newark seeks a Post-Doctoral Associate under the supervision of Dr. Luis M. Rivera, Professor of Psychology and Vice Provost for Academic Innovation, the Post-Doctoral Associate will be mainly responsible for contributing to Rutgers-Newark's STE[A]M broadening participation and persistence initiatives. The Post-Doctoral Associate will support programming; conduct original research, including meta-analytic reviews and the design of studies, as well as the collection, analysis, and interpretation of data; prepare scientific manuscripts for publication; and present research findings at professional conferences. The Post-Doctoral Associate will also have opportunities to receive training in a social cognition laboratory and collaborate with STE[A]M faculty across Rutgers University-Newark. Additional responsibilities may include mentoring and collaborating with graduate and undergraduate student researchers.</div> Psychology Newark Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences Newa-L3 6795 26FA0708 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279757 2026-08-20T09:08:45-04:00 2026-08-20T09:08:46-04:00 Staff Nurse FT NIghts UCHC ADTC <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Full Time Staff Nurse for the Adult Diagnostic Treatment Center STU, located in Avenel, NJ. The UCHC Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus; works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment; frequently functions guided by nursing protocols; and functions as a team leader as assigned.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the inmatepatient including adults (18 to 64 years), and geriatrics (65+) and their family within the framework established by the correctional system.</li><li>Utilizes effective communication skills by demonstrating respect, concern and courtesy in all interpersonal relationships.</li><li>Attends appropriate in-services and continuing education offerings to obtain and maintain necessary skills.</li><li>Participates in offering education to inmates, security officers and other members of the health care team.</li><li>Participates in in-service meetings and educational programs either as attendee or as a teacher, as arranged and approved by supervisor.</li></ul> UCHC Adult Treatment Center Ph RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7674 Avenel NJ 26ST0984 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277080 2026-06-12T17:31:25-04:00 2026-06-12T17:31:25-04:00 Part-time Lecturers, Various Disciplines <div>The Law School at Rutgers University-Newark seeks lecturers and coadjutants for the 2026-2027 semesters (Summer 26, Fall 26, Winter 26, Spring 27) to teach in various disciplines. The instructor will present the course material during the assigned course times, hold office hours, administer exams, assign grades, and coordinate any other requirements related to course instruction.&nbsp;</div> Law School Newark Newark Chancellor-L2 Law School Newark-L3 8071 26FA0550 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274091 2026-04-30T15:21:56-04:00 2026-04-30T15:21:56-04:00 Coadjutant Instructors, Historic Preservation <div>The Mid-Atlantic Regional Center for the Humanities (MARCH) seeks part-time instructors for Fall 2026, Spring 2027, and/or Summer 2027 semesters to teach courses in our Continuing Education in Historic Preservation Certificate Program. MARCH is seeking instructors for the specific courses of Preservation Planning and Introduction to Preservation of Historic Interiors. The certificate program is also looking to develop and offer elective courses on environmental preservation practice and issues of climate change and resistance, as well as other elective topics as yet to be developed.<br>Courses in the Historic Preservation Program are taught as either ten-week 2-credit or five-week 1-credit courses in virtual, hybrid, and in-person models. The program also offers one-day or weekend-long workshops. Please visit https://preservation.rutgers.edu/ to see examples of courses and workshops offered by the program.<br>Applicants should have an MA in Historic Preservation, History or a related field; advanced, up-to-date practical and theoretical experience and knowledge of historic preservation practice and issues in the Mid-Atlantic. Ideally, applicants will also have a good track record teaching historic preservation courses or workshops--or related subjects-- for diverse student populations in continuing education settings.<br>For returning instructors, your cover letter may note that you wish to return to teach for the courses(s) you have taught in prior years.</div> English Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 6762 26FA0426 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266033 2025-12-31T09:16:38-05:00 2025-12-31T09:16:39-05:00 General Anesthesiologist <div>The Department of Anesthesiology at Rutgers, New Jersey Medical School, seeks to recruit a qualified General Anesthesiologist for a full-time position as Assistant Professor, Non-Tenure Track. Duties include on-site anesthesia services to adult patients at University Hospital; intraoperative and didactic teaching of residents; participation in Faculty Development programs; working collaboratively with the members of the surgical services both clinically and administratively; contributing to research that forwards the discipline academically and clinically.</div><div>Qualified applicants must: 1. Have a medical doctorate or equivalent, 2. Hold or be eligible for medical licensure in New Jersey, and 3. Be a BC/BE Anesthesiologist. Candidates on H1B VISA are welcome to apply. The effective day of the appointment is July 1, 2025.</div><div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmation Action Employer and is compliant with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA). Diversity as a core value of RBHS, embodies inclusiveness, mutual respect, and multiple perspectives and serves as a driver for excellence for achieving equity in health and health care. For more information, please visit <a href=\"http://recruitment.rutgers.edu/TheRUCommitment-2.htm\"><strong>http://recruitment.rutgers.edu/TheRUCommitment-2.htm</strong></a> and for the University’s commitment to equal employment opportunity and affirmative, please go to <a href=\"https://policies.rutgers.edu/sites/default/files/60.1.8%20-%20current.pdf\"><strong>https://policies.rutgers.edu/sites/default/files/60.1.8%20-%20current.pdf</strong></a>. <strong>We encourage applications from women, minorities, veterans, and persons with disabilities.</strong></div><div>We offer excellent benefits and a highly competitive salary. The University Hospital, a primary teaching hospital of the Rutgers New Jersey Medical School, is a widely recognized tertiary care center and Level 1 Trauma Center. Located in the vibrant city of Newark, just 20 minutes from Manhattan, you'll be surrounded by the idyllic communities of Northern New Jersey.</div> NJMS - Anesthesiology RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7432 25FA0748 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280047 2026-08-26T14:29:37-04:00 2026-08-26T14:29:38-04:00 Screening Clinician Per Diem (Multiple Positions) <div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Screening Clinician in the Acute Psychiatric Services (APS) of Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Screening Clinician position is to perform psychiatric emergency services, screening, and screening outreach assessments as well as other mental health services. Demonstrate competence in providing generic crisis assessment of individuals of all ages (birth through 65+ years) and in determining the need for any additional professional consultation. Demonstrates competence in devising an appropriate intervention/disposition plan.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Provides an in-depth clinical assessment for all persons served.</li><li>Identifies the appropriate level of care disposition from skill based knowledge of the Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders, Fifth Edition (DSM-5) criteria, clinical expertise, and departmental criteria.</li><li>Understands the impact of the person’s age, cognitive functioning and developmental level.</li><li>Involves person, family, significant other in developing a plan for disposition. Explains referral/disposition to person served in a clear and supportive fashion</li></ul> UBHC - Emergency Screening Psy RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8029 Piscataway NJ 26ST0045 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278055 2026-06-30T17:00:14-04:00 2026-06-30T17:00:15-04:00 Open Rank Faculty Positions in the Krieger Klein Alzheimer Research Center in the Rutgers Brain Health Institute <div>The Herbert and Jacqueline Krieger Klein Alzheimer’s Research Center at the Rutgers Brain Health Institute (BHI), is recruiting a tenured or tenure-track faculty member at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor level to expand our research portfolio in the basic science of neurodegenerative diseases. We seek scholars with innovative, rigorous, and impactful basic research programs focusing on the gut-brain axis related to aging, Alzheimer’s disease, or associated dementias.</div><div>This recruitment is part of a newly approved diversity cluster hiring opportunity towards Addressing Health Equity in Age-related Disorders (AHEAD). The AHEAD cluster envisions hiring and bringing together a cohort of scholars from the Rutgers Health (RH), the School of Engineering (SoE) and School of Arts and Sciences (SAS) at Rutgers New Brunswick, and to collectively advance knowledge of neurodegenerative disorders, develop treatments and technology solutions that help people experience a higher quality of life, and develop a deep understanding of the social, racial and ethnic health disparities associated with the onset and treatments of neurodegenerative disorders to map a path towards health equity and healthy aging.</div><div>The successful applicant will join a collaborative neuroscience community in the Rutgers Brain Health Institute (BHI) and serve as a core member within the Herbert and Jacqueline Krieger Klein Alzheimer’s Center at BHI. The Herbert and Jacqueline Krieger Klein Alzheimer’s Research Center is a <em>new</em> center within BHI at Rutgers University with the mission of establishing an interdisciplinary, integrated program to provide comprehensive research focused on prevention and treatment of Alzheimer’s disease and related dementias. This center is the first of its kind in New Jersey, and the successful applicant will be integral to its development. Ideal candidates will bring vision and experience in modern aging and memory research and enthusiasm for team science and collaboration.</div><div>Qualifying applicants must have an established scholarly record demonstrating ability to conduct independent, extramurally funded research focusing on aging, Alzheimer’s disease, or associated dementias. Candidates must have current and active extramural NIH funding.</div><div>Rutgers values a culturally diverse faculty; we strongly encourage applications from women and candidates underrepresented in medicine. Rutgers University is committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion. The Herbert and Jacqueline Krieger Klein Alzheimer’s Research Center is actively working to ensure that our faculty composition reflects diversity.</div><div>To become a part of our vibrant community, applicants should submit a CV, a brief statement of research accomplishments and plans to Dr. Miriam Bocarsly at <a href=\"mailto:bocarsme@njms.rutgers.edu\"><strong>bocarsme@njms.rutgers.edu</strong></a> and a copy to <a href=\"mailto:bhi@bhi.rutgers.edu\"><strong>bhi@bhi.rutgers.edu</strong></a>.</div> Brain Health Institute RBHS Chancellor-L2 Brain Health Institute-L3 8146 24FA0182 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266391 2026-01-04T21:31:14-05:00 2026-01-04T21:31:15-05:00 Lecturers-Environmental Sciences <div>The Department of Environmental Sciences in the School of Environmental and Biological Sciences at Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking Lecturers for the Academic Year to teach various undergraduate courses within the discipline including environmental microbiology laboratory and water and wastewater treatment. The Lecturer will present course materials during the assigned courses times, hold office hours, help proctor, grade exams and assignments, develop homework/exam questions and coordinate any other requirements related to the instruction of the course. Additional duties may include assisting students with laboratory activities, preparing for laboratory instruction and delivering lectures.</div> Environmental Science New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 7137 25FA0674 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280186 2026-08-31T10:45:42-04:00 2026-08-31T10:45:43-04:00 Forensic Mental Health Clinician UCHC NSP <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care (UCHC) is seeking a Forensic Mental Health Clinician for Northern State Prison, located in Newark, New Jersey. Reporting to the Clinician Supervisor, the Forensic Mental Health Clinician completes specialized psychological testing and assessment of clinical needs of adult inmates sentenced to the Department of Corrections.<br><br>Among the key duties for this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Arrives at DSM IV diagnoses with precision and accuracy through psychological testing and evaluation sessions.</li><li>Provides crisis intervention, individual and group psychotherapy and psycho-education programming as clinically indicated to assigned inmates. Involves inmates and Department of Corrections staff in developing achievable and understandable psychosocial treatment plans. Advocates for appropriate resources for inmates based on assessed needs.</li><li>Manages caseload demands effectively while considering both qualities of care and the security needs of the Department of Corrections.</li><li>Assumes overall case management responsibilities for assigned inmates including coordination of treatment and liaison with community agencies; maintains appropriate inmate records.</li><li>Demonstrates competency in psychological testing and in recognizing the unique needs and behaviors of adult inmates and seniors</li></ul> UCHC Northern State Prison Med RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7656 Newark NJ 26ST0413 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278626 2026-07-10T12:59:41-04:00 2026-07-10T12:59:42-04:00 Staff Nurse Mental Health PT Days UCHC NJSP <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Part Time UCHC Mental Health Staff Nurse for New Jersey State Prison, located in Trenton, NJ<br><br>The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus for inmates in the New Jersey Department of Corrections.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological and emotional needs of the resident-patient including adolescents (13-17 years), adults (18 to 64 years) and their family within the framework established by the correctional system.</li><li>Performs assessments of resident-patient in a variety of settings such as initial intake area, health care unit for sick call, emergency situations in housing, chronic care clinics and infirmary.</li><li>Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.</li><li>Identifies inmate-centered goals and nursing objectives and implements prescribed interventions and solutions for the identified problems.</li><li>Plans nursing care by identification of resident-patient needs based on assessments.</li><li>Makes appropriate, timely referrals and initiates appropriate nursing care based on institutional policies and procedures. As team leader or charge nurse, delegates duties to other health care team members based on their skill, knowledge and experience and guides the provision of care by others.</li></ul> UCHC New Jersey State Prison M RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7660 Trenton NJ 26ST1015 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/269216 2026-02-13T13:57:39-05:00 2026-02-13T13:57:39-05:00 Oral Biology Department Chair <div>Rutgers School of Dental Medicine (RSDM) is searching for a Chair of the Department of Oral Biology. This is a full-time faculty appointment up to the rank of Full Professor, tenure track or tenured, commensurate with experience. The Chair will provide academic, research, and administrative leadership for the Department and play a central role in advancing RSDM’s missions of research, education, and patient care.<br><br></div><div>Department Overview</div><div>The Department of Oral Biology serves as the foundational biomedical sciences hub for RSDM, supporting predoctoral, graduate, and postgraduate education through rigorous training in oral biology, microbiology, immunology, biomaterials, and translational oral health research. The Department contributes substantially to the DMD, Master’s and PhD training programs as well as interdisciplinary research initiatives across Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences.<br><br></div><div>The Department maintains a strong and growing portfolio of basic, translational, and clinical research, supported by extramural funding and collaborative programs spanning dentistry, medicine, bioengineering, and public health.<br><br>The Chair of Oral Biology will be responsible for the overall administration and strategic leadership of the Department .<br><br>The successful candidate will be expected to strengthen the Department’s national and international reputation and align departmental priorities with the School’s Mission and Vision.<br><br>Preference will be given to candidates with dual degrees (DDS/PhD or equivalent) and active NIH grant support. Candidates with Dental degrees may be eligible for intramural clinical practice opportunities upon fulfilling NJ state board dental licensure qualifications.&nbsp;</div> RSDM - Oral Biology RBHS Chancellor-L2 Rutgers School of Dental Medic-L3 7553 26FA0101 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280428 2026-09-04T00:00:49-04:00 2026-09-04T00:00:50-04:00 Program Coordinator II <div>Rutgers University- Newark (RU-N), an urban public research university and anchor institution, located in Newark, New Jersey, a city of promise, is seeking a Program Coordinator II for the Office of Lifelong Learning. Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Assist in the coordination and administration of programs, projects, and/or processes that align with the logistics and daily operations of summer, winter, academic, certificate, and personal enrichment programs and activities, ensuring a seamless experience for students, faculty, and staff.</li><li>Coordinate routine moving parts that support academic and student programs, personal enrichment programs, business office functions (such as procurement and human resources transactions), and summer/winter visiting students, allowing programs to run efficiently and effectively while maintaining high standards of service and delivery.</li><li>Support student needs, enrollment, and assist student success initiatives by ensuring an outstanding student experience.</li><li>Assist in the coordination, administration, and execution of traditional and digital marketing and recruitment initiatives to promote programs and activities.</li><li>Perform professional work that requires general program coordination practices and the basic application of office concepts, theories, and terminology.</li><li>Provide administrative support to the Assistant Director and other Department administrators as needed.</li></ul><div><br><br></div> Lifelong Learning Newark Chancellor-L2 Provost-L3 8136 Newark NJ 26ST0040 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279355 2026-08-06T11:32:05-04:00 2026-08-06T11:32:06-04:00 Sr Facilities Project Manager <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Sr Facilities Project Manager for the Division of Institutional Planning &amp; Operations (IP&amp;O). Under the guidance of the Department Head/Director, the Senior Facilities Project Manager coordinates, develops, designs, and budgets renovation projects throughout the University.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Interfaces with adynamic team of University technical staff, including project management, maintenance, safety, controls, commissioning, and utilities groups, to ensure that projects are implemented properly from conception through final acceptance.</li><li>The Sr. Project Manager runs anywhere from 5 -15 projects in various stages of Design and Construction with minimal supervision from the Director.</li><li>The Sr. Project Manager needs to be highly motivated, organized, and persistent with follow-up to keep projects on schedule and under budget.</li><li>The Sr. PM is responsible for Millions of dollars of design/construction work per year.</li></ul> Renovations & Utilities UW EVP & Chief Admin Officer Institutional Planning & Optns-L3 8699 Piscataway NJ 26ST1592 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275993 2026-05-28T12:34:12-04:00 2026-05-28T12:34:12-04:00 Lecturers (Adjunct Faculty) for the Undergraduate Program in  Communication (Fall 2026) <div>The Department of Communication seeks lecturers for its undergraduate program in Communication. Please see the description of our program at https://comminfo.rutgers.edu/academics/undergraduate/communication-major and the list of courses we offer at https://comminfo.rutgers.edu/academics/courses?courses=&amp;program=26. Within your cover letter, please let us know which courses in our program you feel most prepared to teach. Please submit a cover letter, resume/curriculum vitae, and names and contact information for at least three references. You may also upload any evidence of your teaching experience such as sample syllabi or course materials, results of student instructional ratings, or published work.</div> Communication New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School  Communicatn & Info Sci-L3 7088 26FA0367 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/273305 2026-04-20T13:10:25-04:00 2026-04-20T13:10:25-04:00 Clinical Assistant Professor <div><strong>RBHS Overview:</strong></div><div>New Jersey’s premier academic health center, Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences (RBHS) takes an integrated approach to educating students, providing clinical care, and conducting research, all with the goal of improving human health. Aligned with Rutgers University–New Brunswick and collaborating university wide, RBHS includes eight schools, a behavioral health network, and five centers and institutes that focus on cancer treatment and research, neuroscience, advanced biotechnology and medicine, environmental and occupational health, and health care policy and aging research.</div><div>Our elite and renowned faculty are teachers, health researchers and providers, and scientists with unparalleled experience who advance medical innovation and provide patient care informed by the latest research findings. We offer an outstanding education and training in medicine, dentistry, pharmacy, public health, nursing, biomedical research, and the full spectrum of allied health careers. An important mission of RBHS is to promote the careers of faculty, staff, and learners. &nbsp;</div><div>Through this community of healers, scientists, and scholars, Rutgers is equipped as never before to transform lives.</div><div><strong>School Overview:</strong></div><div>The Rutgers School of Dental Medicine (RSDM) is New Jersey’s only dental school, encompassing education, patient care and community outreach. It’s also the state’s largest oral healthcare provider, treating more than 130,000 patient visits annually at its student clinic in Newark and three sites in South Jersey.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Formerly the New Jersey Dental School, RSDM was established in 1956, as part of the Seton Hall College of Medicine and Dentistry, which later became the University of Medicine and Dentistry of New Jersey (UMDNJ). In 2013, UMDNJ integrated with Rutgers University and the dental school was renamed again.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Known for its intensive clinical programs and close-knit, supportive environment, RSDM is one of the most diverse dental schools in the nation. It also has an ethnically and economically diverse patient pool, including many who are underserved. RSDM’s special needs clinic is one of the only facilities in the region that provides dental care for patients with disabilities. Its Dental Specialty Center for post-doctoral students is equipped with cutting-edge technology and a design that fosters collaborative care. For pre-doctoral students, RSDM’s match rate is consistently well above the national average and students routinely score above the 95th percentile on board exams.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Research at the dental school spans clinical studies of dental disease and groundbreaking work that explores the potential of oral microbiomes to fight drug resistant pathogens and treat cancer and autoimmune disease. New research laboratories, totaling 25,000 square feet, were added in the fall of 2018.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>RSDM students and faculty perform community service and outreach in Newark and other New Jersey municipalities and embark on annual overseas dental missions. There are two trips to the Dominican Republic: one in the village of La Romana and another on the border of the Dominican Republic and Haiti, where patients from both nations receive care. Other missions include trips to Bangladesh and Sri Lanka to treat patients with cleft palates and a summer mission to Native American reservations, where patients are treated at clinics run by the federal government.&nbsp;</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>The school is extremely competitive, choosing about 100 students a year from a field of more than 2,000 applicants for its incoming DMD program. Many students are from New Jersey and several are among the first generation in their families to attain a college degree<strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>Position Summary:</strong></div><div>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Provide instruction in the development of treatment plans for limited and comprehensive Orthodontic treatment, one full-day per week.</div><div>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Provide clinical supervision to undergraduate and postgraduate dental students for screenings and comprehensive care treatment, in compliance with clinic standards and University policies.</div><div>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Participate in the educational mission of the Department by giving lectures and seminars, in addition to clinic supervision, and participate in, and moderate Case Conferences as assigned.</div><div>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;These expectations are not all inclusive and other duties maybe assigned as needed by the department Chair.</div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>Essential Duties and Responsibilities: </strong>&nbsp;</div><div>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Understands and adheres to legacy UMDNJ’s compliance standards as they appear in legacy UMDNJ’s Corporate Compliance Policy and Code of Conduct and Conflict of Interest Policy.</div><div>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Stays current with all pertinent federal, state and legacy UMDNJ regulations, laws and policies as they presently exist and as they change or are modified.</div><div><strong>&nbsp;</strong></div><div><strong>Minimum Education/Specialty, License/Certification:</strong></div><div>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;DDS/DMD from an accredited institution. Completion of an advanced education program in orthodontics at an institution accredited by the Commission on Dental Accreditation, and eligibility for licensure in New Jersey.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>Preferred Qualifications:</strong></div><div>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;American Board of Orthodontics certification and previous teaching and research activity are highly desirable.</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div><strong>Physical Demands and Work Environment</strong></div><div>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Standing, walking, sitting – some for extended periods of time.</div><div>·&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Clinic, classroom and office setting. Moderate noise.</div> RSDM - Orthodontics RBHS Chancellor-L2 Rutgers School of Dental Medic-L3 7547 26FA0348 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/265494 2025-12-18T11:22:19-05:00 2025-12-18T11:22:20-05:00 RBS - Non-Instructional Positions (Part Time) - 2026 <div>The Rutgers Business School is seeking individuals to assist with non-instructional assignments for its non-credit programs and centers.<br><br>Successful candidates will provide assistance, guidance, research, and other duties as assigned (e.g., design, recruitment, curriculum development, course design, research, etc.) on a variety of topics, including, but not limited to: accounting, accounting information systems, financial accounting, government accounting, taxation, administrative studies, finance, economics, real estate, marketing, management, management science and information systems, operational management, strategic leadership, supply chain, and much more.<br><br>Candidates may be responsible for, but not limited to, the following:</div><ul><li>Conducting research</li><li>Preparing materials (e.g., presentations, proposals, documents, etc.) as assigned by the hiring manager</li><li>Generate reports, summaries, and materials for distribution to internal and external entities</li><li>Developing curriculum, course designs, and course material review</li></ul><div><br>Some positions may be grant funded.</div> Human Resources Newark Newark Chancellor-L2 Rutgers Business School-L3 6942 25FA1259 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279643 2026-08-17T12:04:54-04:00 2026-08-17T12:04:55-04:00 Career Counseling Officer (Graduate Student Career Pathways) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, seeks a dynamic team leader to serve as the Career Counseling Officer (Graduate Student Career Pathways Program) within the Office of Career Exploration and Success at Rutgers University–New Brunswick. Reporting to the Associate Director, Scarlet Career Mentoring Network, this role will lead and expand career pathways initiatives for graduate students, with a particular focus on doctoral students pursuing careers in industry. The position will support graduate students in clarifying career goals, exploring career pathways, developing career competencies, and building professional networks through mentoring, advising, and career-connected programming.<br><br></div><div>A central responsibility of the position is the design and expansion of mentoring-based programming that connects graduate students with faculty, alumni, employers, and industry professionals. The Career Counseling Officer will also serve as the primary liaison to the School of Graduate Studies and Graduate Student Life while managing the Graduate Student Career Pathways Community and its advisory board of campus partners, employers, and student leaders.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Leads career preparation initiatives for graduate students, including mentoring-based programming that connects students with faculty, alumni, employers, and industry professionals.</li><li>Recruits and manages Career Pathways Fellows, coordinates student-alumni mentoring opportunities, and organizes major career programming and events for graduate students.</li><li>Builds partnerships with career professionals and campus units that support graduate students, including the Rutgers School of Graduate Studies, Graduate Student Life, and the Rutgers Graduate Student Association.</li><li>Leads the Graduate Student Career Pathways Community Advisory Board and serves as the primary contact for career presentations, workshops, and community engagement efforts.</li><li>Provides direct career advising services primarily for doctoral students across all stages of their career journeys.</li><li>Develops scalable advising strategies, including group programming and other approaches that expand support capacity.</li><li>Participates in meetings, professional development activities, and other assigned responsibilities.</li><li>Supports Rutgers University’s visibility within the career services field through conference presentations, professional engagement, and award nominations.</li></ul> Career Exploration & Success New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Undergraduate Education-L3 7231 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1064 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279949 2026-08-25T13:04:03-04:00 2026-08-25T13:04:04-04:00 Executive Director <div>Rutgers University – Newark, an urban public research anchor institution, located in Newark, New Jersey, a city of promise, is seeking an Executive Director.<br><br>Rutgers University – Newark (RUN) often is recognized for providing an affordable high quality education that serves first-generation and low-income college students especially well (e.g., RU-N was ranked 9th among National Universities in the Washington Monthly “Bang for the Buck” listing, which recognizes RUN’s relatively high numbers of Pell-eligible students in its incoming first-year class, relatively high 6-year graduation rate, and relatively low student loan default rate).<br>As documented in a September 2014 report by The Education Trust (http://edtrust.org/resource/leading-the-way-in-diversity-and-degrees-rutgers-university-newark/), the achievement of such high graduation rates for this population of students is a relatively recent phenomenon at RUN and attributable in substantial measure to cultural shifts on campus that occurred in the wake of RU-N’s repeated recognition as the top national university for campus ethnic diversity and the embracing of this ranking by RU-N leadership.<br><br>At the same time, while RU-N’s graduation rate is high relative to what might be predicted from national norms from its student demographics, its 6-year graduation rate is nowhere near the top of national universities is absolute terms (118th) and its 4-year graduation rate is well less than half of that of any of those ranked in the top 25 for public universities. In order to continue to improve its graduation rates, especially at the 4-year mark, RU-N needs to adopt a much more strategic approach to student retention and degree attainment that cuts across all of its undergraduate serving schools and ideally encompassing many of its graduate programs as well. To this end, RU-N recently has contracted with the EAB Collaborative to provide in-depth analytics and consultancy services about student performance and retention as well as technology to assist students, faculty, and academic advisors in applying the results of such analyses to concrete daily student academic decisions. It also has added multiple dual enrollment and special cohort-based programs, especially in recent years, to improve student preparation and engagement and to help defined pathways for students through to graduation.<br><br>These efforts require high level coordination to bring the efforts of external consultants and the academic deans and departments chairs into alignment and, in collaboration with senior leadership of the university, to set a strategic direction for RU-N as a whole in the area of student success, retention, and degree attainment programming.<br><br>This position is responsible for and not limited to the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Reviews student outcomes and retention and graduation rates of various student populations and sub-populations – paying special attention to low-income, first-generation, and historically under-represented minority populations as well as populations of students at risk academically or otherwise.</li><li>Reviews registration, packaging, and billing practices and makes recommendations to deans and directors on possible operational revisions in light of best practices.</li><li>Reviews learning outcomes at RUN and makes recommendations to faculty and department chairs on possible pedagogical and curricular revision in light of recognized best practices.</li></ul> Student Success & Retention Newark Chancellor-L2 Provost-L3 8907 Newark NJ 26ST1444 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277762 2026-06-25T11:05:44-04:00 2026-06-25T11:05:45-04:00 Staff Nurse FT Eves UCHC NSP (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Full Time Staff Nurse for Northern State Prison located in Newark, NJ<br><br>The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus for inmates in the New Jersey Department of Corrections.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br>* Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the resident-patient including adolescents (13-17 years), adults (18 to 64 years) and their family within the framework established by the correctional system.<br>* Performs assessments of resident-patient in a variety of settings such as initial intake area, health care unit for sick call, emergency situations in housing, chronic care clinics and infirmary.<br>* Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br>* Identifies inmate-centered goals and nursing objectives and implements prescribed interventions and solutions for the identified problems.<br>* Plans nursing care by identification of resident-patient needs based on assessments. Makes appropriate, timely referrals and initiates appropriate nursing care based on institutional policies and procedures.<br>* As team leader or charge nurse, delegates duties to other health care team members based on their skill, knowledge and experience and guides the provision of care by others.</div> UCHC Northern State Prison Phy_DUP RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7679 Newark NJ 26ST0676 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275256 2026-05-18T09:26:20-04:00 2026-05-18T09:26:21-04:00 Summer Session Instructor 2026 (Multiple Vacancies) <div>The School of Environmental and Biological Sciences, Rutgers invites applications for Part-Time teaching positions in the Department of Ecology, Evolution, and Natural Resources for Summer Session 2026. Instructors are needed for Principles of Ecology lab, and Ornithology (lab component)</div> Ecology, Evolutn & Ntrl Rescrc New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 7144 26FA0429 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266262 2025-12-31T09:42:15-05:00 2025-12-31T09:42:16-05:00 Research Programmer <div>The Rutgers Artificial Intelligence and Data Science (RAD) Collaboratory is seeking one or more Research Programmers to support leveraging modern Machine Learning (ML) and Deep Learning (DL) techniques by Rutgers faculty, postdoctoral fellows, and students. The ideal candidate will have a strong ML/DL and cyberinfrastructure (CI) background and a willingness to contribute to interdisciplinary research across diverse basic and applied science and engineering domains.<br><br></div><div>Responsibilities will include:<br>● Design, develop, and deploy ML/DL algorithms for domain science and engineering fields<br>● Support RAD Collaboratory research on national cyberinfrastructure (e.g., ACCESS, NAIRR, and DOE supercomputers) or cloud environments (e.g., AWS, GCP, and Azure)<br>● Support application of ML/DL/CI techniques across topics and domains<br>● Deliver training on ML/DL/CI techniques and best practices to a broad range of researchers<br>● Stay at the forefront of new ML/DL techniques and ML/DL systems that support science and engineering research<br>● Co-author peer-reviewed interdisciplinary research publications<br>● Contribute to funding applications from external sources (e.g., NSF, NIH)</div> Quantitative Biomedicine Inst New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 6749 25FA0745 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/272644 2026-04-08T11:09:08-04:00 2026-04-08T11:09:08-04:00 Course Assistant (Course Support) - Fall 2026 <div>The Professional Science Master’s Program (PSM) invites applications for Course Assistants (Course Support) for the Fall 2026 term.<br><br>Successful candidates will be responsible for the following:</div><ul><li>Assisting faculty with their course(s) (may include traditional lecture, hybrid, and/or fully online courses); may be required to provide LMS software assistance.</li><li>Attending all assigned course meetings (at the discretion of the faculty member teaching the course)</li><li>Preparing course materials (i.e., syllabi, presentations, hand-outs, reading materials, etc.) as directed by the faculty member</li><li>Providing constructive feedback to students as well as critical instruction regarding student work and academic standards</li><li>Responding to student emails and inquiries, and address student concerns</li><li>Practice innovative educational methodology</li></ul> Professional Science Masters New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Professional Science Masters-L3 6665 26FA0334 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279571 2026-08-13T11:19:30-04:00 2026-08-13T11:19:31-04:00 Co Adj – Non Teaching, Supervisor <div>The Center for Psychological Services at the Graduate School of Applied and Professional Psychology (GSAPP) announces an opening for a Clinical Supervisor to provide weekly supervision for the ADHD Compassion Project Clinic. The Clinical Supervisor will provide supervision and training to doctoral students in Mentalization-Based Therapy for children, adolescents, and families. The Clinical Supervisor will provide 1 hour of individual supervision weekly on Fridays for doctoral-level students placed in this specialty clinic. In addition to supervision, it is expected the Supervisor will provide didactic training related to the treatment of ADHD and Mentalization-Based Therapy as part of their supervision. This position will report to the Director of the Center for Psychological Services at GSAPP and will have a standing biweekly or monthly meeting with the Director of CPS, as needed.</div> Psychological Services Center New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Graduate School of Applied & P-L3 6823 26FA0686 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279828 2026-08-21T13:14:43-04:00 2026-08-21T13:14:44-04:00 MGSA – Department of Art & Design - Coadjutant Academic Support Positions Fall 2026 <div>The Art &amp; Design Department, Mason Gross at Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is currently looking to fill multiple COAD Non-Teaching positions for AY26-27. These positions are needed to assist several academic support duties as needed, including and not limited to: course administration support, canvas site management, lecture recording management, work collection and display, material/classroom maintenance, set-up/clean-up, other research assistance, and any additional tasks for class support assigned by the leading teaching instructor as needed.</div> Art & Design New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Mason Gross School of Arts Dea-L3 6863 26FA0728 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277669 2026-06-24T12:03:15-04:00 2026-06-24T12:03:15-04:00 Open Rank - Maternal Fetal Medicine Division Director <div>The Department of Obstetrics, Gynecology, and Reproductive Sciences at Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School (RWJMS) seeks a highly qualified, innovative, and collaborative leader to serve as the Maternal-Fetal Medicine (MFM) Division Director. The Division Director will be responsible for advancing the clinical, educational, and research missions of the MFM Division while fostering a culture of excellence, collaboration, and academic achievement. This position offers a unique opportunity to lead a growing division within an academic medical center and health system partnership, expanding perinatal services and high-risk pregnancy care across the region. The individual will report to the Chair of Obstetrics, Gynecology, and Reproductive Sciences and collaborate with the Women’s Health Service line leadership to address local and system wide goals and initiatives.</div> RWJ - OB/GYN MFM/Atu Spmc RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7791 26FA0633 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274393 2026-05-06T11:39:17-04:00 2026-05-06T11:39:17-04:00 Postdoc – Drug Discovery Development and Application Scientist <div>The Laboratory for Biomolecular Simulation Research (http://lbsr.rutgers.edu) and Institute for Quantitative Biomedicine (https://iqb.rutgers.edu/) at Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is in search of a postdoctoral-level drug discovery application scientist. Our current endeavor involves an exciting NIH-funded project aimed at developing a state-of-the-art next-generation simulation package. We are actively seeking a skilled and enthusiastic researcher to join our team. As part of this opportunity, you will be able to:</div><div>· Contribute cutting-edge research in biomolecular simulations, gaining valuable practical experience and expanding your expertise in this field.</div><div>· Establish connections within the dynamic simulation community, fostering strong networks with other academic and industrial researchers, especially those involved in molecular simulation-based computer-aided drug discovery.</div><div>This position is ideally suited for individuals with career aspirations as application scientists within the drug-discovery field.</div> Quantitative Biomedicine Inst New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 6749 26FA0457 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266170 2025-12-31T09:32:31-05:00 2025-12-31T09:32:31-05:00 Post Doctoral Associate (Singson) <div>The Singson laboratory at the Waksman Institute of Microbiology is seeking a postdoctoral associate to participate in our studies of reproductive biology in the <em>C. elegans </em>model system. Specifically, the candidate will contribute to our fertilization synapse, sperm activation, and sperm mitochondria dynamics projects. Experience with <em>C. elegans </em>genetics, reproduction, cell biology are required. Further, experience with protein-protein interaction methods like the split ubiquitin yeast-two hybrid method and SIM microscopy training will be needed. The individual will report directly to the laboratory Principle Investigator (PI).<br><br>The position requires being able to design and carry out experiments with the&nbsp;<em>C. elegans</em> model system as well as other experimental systems in the lab such as yeast two hybrid protein-protein interaction methods. The candidate should be able to work unsupervised day-to-day, but in consultation with the primary investigator for long term goals of the research. The candidate should also be able to professionally communicate and justify experimental approaches and results in both oral and written form. Any manuscripts for publication will be corresponded by the candidate.<br><br>The scope of work is primarily as a member of the Singson lab research team. However, scientific interactions at the Waksman Institute, Department of Genetics, and other relevant units will be required as the research progresses.</div> Waksman Institute of Microbiol New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 6726 25FA1166 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280077 2026-08-27T11:37:14-04:00 2026-08-27T11:37:15-04:00 Mental Health Clinician II <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Mental Health Clinician II for the Child and Adolescent Partial Hospital within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Mental Health Clinician II is to serve as the senior mental health practitioner who provides lead functions for the program, to include screening of intakes and referrals, care coordination, ensuring completion of program specific documentation and/or comprehensive assessment and therapeutic intervention for the psychological and social needs of child and adolescent (ages 3-17 years) and/or adult individuals served (18 and over), including development of treatment plans, conducting individual, group, and family therapy, and providing case management. Assists with the provision of clinical supervision to licensing candidates as assigned.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Effectively contributes to and supports an environment that enhances the positive self-image of individuals served and their families and preserves their human dignity, right to fair and equitable treatment, self-determination, individuality, privacy and civil rights.</li><li>Provides assessments and ongoing therapeutic services with flexibility, empathy and concern for individuals served based on sound clinical judgment.</li><li>In clinical programs, assesses individuals for mental health and substance use disorders, arrives at accurate DSM5 diagnosis by the end of the evaluation in consultation with team members, completes documentation and updates diagnosis when new information and clinical status warrant.</li><li>In community programs, acts as a liaison with referral source and community based services, coordinates and schedules intake appointments and outreaches, conducts and documents eligibility screenings and clinical assessments including rehabilitation needs assessments for program referrals and intakes, updates diagnosis when new information and clinical status warrant, maintains records and submits reports as required.</li><li>Takes a lead role in providing orientation, training, team leadership in the department.</li><li>Assists with the provision of clinical supervision to licensing candidates as assigned, mentors and trains students and interns. c. Facilitates and leads staff/team meetings, case-conferences and clinical case review meetings and participates actively in ensuring program activities are adequately covered.</li><li>Participates in development, implementation, and evaluation of program services.</li></ul> UBHC - Child & Adolescent PH P RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8803 Newark NJ 26ST0816 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278361 2026-07-07T14:57:38-04:00 2026-07-07T14:57:39-04:00 Director, Counseling Center <div>Rutgers University – Newark (RU-N), an urban public research university and anchor institution located in Newark, New Jersey, a city of promise, is seeking a Director, Counseling Center. Under the general direction of the Assistant Vice Chancellor for Student Health &amp; Wellness, responsibilities include directing clinical and support staff and all administrative activities related to the provision and management of mental health services to over 11,000 undergraduate and graduate students. The role requires availability to respond to urgent student mental health situations outside of normal business hours, including after-hours crisis intervention and occasional scheduled evening or weekend responsibilities.<br><br>This position is responsible for and not limited to the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Evaluates and treat students for developmental and psychological/emotional difficulties.</li><li>Directs campus outreach programs.</li><li>Consults with staff, faculty, and students.</li><li>Maintains liaison relationships with health professionals at the Student Health Services.</li><li>Provides leadership in formulating campus policies on psychological issues.</li><li>Recruits, select, train and supervise clinicians, professional staff and graduate students in mental health fields.</li><li>Conduct research relevant to the needs of the student population.</li><li>Serves as a key member of both the Campus Awareness Response and Education (CARE) Team and Threat Assessment and Safety Committee which evaluates the level of risk in given situations, recommends appropriate interventions, and monitors students who represent a potential threat to self or others.</li><li>Provides campuswide training on current student mental health and wellness issues to faculty, staff and student constituencies.</li></ul> Counseling Center Newark Newark Chancellor-L2 Student Affairs Newark-L3 7216 Newark NJ 26ST1410 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267166 2026-01-12T16:16:42-05:00 2026-01-12T16:16:42-05:00 Co-adjutant position in Medicinal Chemistry at Rutgers <div>The Department of Medicinal Chemistry at Rutgers University Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy is seeking a co-adjutant to help team-teach medicinal chemistry courses.</div> Medicinal Chemistry RBHS Chancellor-L2 Ernest Mario School of Pharmac-L3 6716 26FA0011 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280237 2026-08-31T14:47:58-04:00 2026-08-31T14:47:59-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse PT Eves UCHC EMCFW <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Part Time Licensed Practical Nurse for Edna Mahan Correctional Facility, located in Clinton, NJ<br><br>The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br>* Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs.<br>* Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.<br>* Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.<br>* Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.<br>* Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.<br>* Documents all aspects of patient care.&nbsp;</div> UCHC-Edna Mahan Corr-Ancillary RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7682 Clinton NJ 26ST1697 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278818 2026-07-15T00:01:28-04:00 2026-07-15T00:01:32-04:00 Senior Program Coordinator <div>Rutgers University – Newark, an urban public research anchor institution, located in Newark, New Jersey, a city of promise, is seeking a<strong> </strong>Sr. Program Coordinator under the direction of the Senior Director of Development, this position independently manages development, alumni engagement, and alumni communications programs for Rutgers Law School. Responsibilities include planning events for alumni reunions and major programs, overseeing and co-managing alumni marketing and communication strategies, co-implementing and co-maintaining the RLaw Connect (Hivebrite) platform, and administering alumni and donor data systems, including Salesforce, Tableau, and Cvent.<br><br>This position is responsible for and not limited to the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Research, retrieve, and analyze data on donor giving and engagement using the RU Foundation’s software: Salesforce (AQ) and Tableau.</li><li>In conjunction with the Assistant Director, Alumni Engagement, prepare marketing materials; manage vendor hiring; provide customer service; manage the Foundation response vehicle interface; handle registration; manage logistics; and handle post-event communications for at least six annual class reunions and other alumni receptions.</li><li>Assist the Associate Dean in various administrative duties, including supervising mailings, transmitting gift checks, processing procurement, and ordering supplies.</li></ul> Law School Newark Newark Chancellor-L2 Law School Newark-L3 8071 Newark NJ 26ST1461 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/270241 2026-03-04T18:20:43-05:00 2026-03-04T18:20:44-05:00 Chief of Pediatric Neurosurgery <div>New Jersey’s premier academic health center, Rutgers Biomedical and Health Sciences (RBHS) takes an integrated approach to educating students, providing clinical care, and conducting research, all to improve human health. Aligned with Rutgers University–New Brunswick and collaborating university-wide, RBHS includes Robert Wood Johnson Medical School and seven other schools, a behavioral health network, and five centers and institutes that focus on cancer treatment and research, neuroscience, advanced biotechnology and medicine, environmental and occupational health, and health care policy and aging research.<br><br></div><div>Our elite and renowned faculty are teachers, health researchers and providers, and scientists with unparalleled experience who advance medical innovation and provide patient care informed by the latest research findings. We offer an outstanding education and training in medicine, dentistry, pharmacy, public health, nursing, biomedical research, and the full spectrum of allied health careers. An important mission of RBHS is to promote the careers of faculty, staff, and learners. Through this community of healers, scientists, and scholars, Rutgers is equipped to transform lives.<br><br>Robert Wood Johnson Medical School, Department of Neurosurgery is seeking a Chief of Pediatric Neurosurgery to clinically perform neurosurgery for pediatric and adult patients while administratively providing leadership, strategy, and oversight for the Division of Pediatric Neurosurgery.<br><br><strong>DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:</strong></div><div><em>Chief of Pediatric Neurosurgery:</em></div><div>• Assist the Department Chair in relevant strategic planning for the delivery of pediatric neurosurgical services.</div><div>• Provide oversight for operational and programmatic aspects for Pediatric Neurosurgery with a focus on quality of surgical care and expansion of the pediatric service line.</div><div>• Direct professional activities and projects to ensure excellence within the area of pediatric neurosurgery.</div><div>• Oversee clinical and research resources of the Division to ensure optimal use and best practices.</div><div>· Collaborate with RWJBH Neuroscience service line leadership for innovation and integration of neurosurgical services throughout the health system.</div><div>· Mentor and develop junior faculty in accordance with the RBHS Appointments and Promotions Guidelines.</div><div>· Support the clinical and educational activities of the Department of Neurosurgery.</div><div><br></div><div><em>Neurosurgeon:</em></div><div>1. Demonstrates clinical competence and surgical excellence in neurosurgery.</div><div>2. Demonstrates factual knowledge and technical skills in the preoperative evaluation, operative management, and postoperative care of patients, including critical care, with pathologic conditions pertaining to neurosurgical care.</div><div>3. In theory and practice, demonstrates familiarity with diagnostic procedures appropriate to neurological diseases.</div><div>4. Demonstrates knowledge and surgical experience in evolving techniques, such as endovascular procedures.</div><div>5. Maintains compliance with all applicable State, Federal, UNOS, CMS, and Joint</div><div>Commission laws, rules, regulations and requirements and create policies and procedures that ensure compliance for the programs with the foregoing.</div><div>6. Surgically evaluates and treats patients who are determined to require services.</div><div>7. Actively participates in the Department's physician on-call schedule</div><div>8. Rounds daily on patient(s) in accordance with best practices</div><div>9. Attends departmental and interdepartmental physician meetings, morbidity and mortality conferences, quality improvement process, selection meetings and other meetings deemed as appropriate.</div><div>10. Completes required medical documentation for patients' charts in a timely manner.</div><div>11. Completes and signs operative reports within 24 hours of surgery.</div><div>12. Provides accurate and detailed reports to referring physicians in a timely manner.</div><div>13. Provides accurate and complete information required for billing and coding.</div><div>14. Provides clear instructions and explanations regarding diagnosis, treatment, medications and follow-up to patients and their respective family members.</div><div>15. Lectures the medical community, patients and general public on cardiac surgery, transcatheter valve procedures, transplant and mechanical surgical device services.</div><div>16. Develops and participates in clinical trials.</div><div>17. Collaborates with surgeons, members of the surgical team, nurses, nurse practitioners, ancillary staff and other physicians and promotes a cohesive team environment.</div><div>18. Maintains effective working relationships with attending physicians outside of the</div><div>19. Department, as well as other Hospital department staff and Administration.</div><div>20. Maintains a team player attitude; creates a positive work environment.</div><div>21. Respects others' time, including punctual arrival to meetings and concluding meetings as scheduled.</div><div>22. Safeguards patient confidentiality at all times.<br>23. Participates in on-call schedule as assigned by Department Chair.</div><div>24. Demonstrates thorough knowledge and adherence to Hospital policies and procedures.</div><div><br><br></div> RWJ - Neurosurgery RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7839 25FA0559 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280472 2026-09-04T14:57:13-04:00 2026-09-04T14:57:14-04:00 Student Assistant <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Student Assistant within Cancer Health Equity at the Rutgers Cancer Institute.<br><br>Under the direction of the Principal Investigator, the Student Assistant performs clerical research activities and work requiring the application of standard techniques and procedures<br><br>This pilot project will use a community-engaged approach, employing patient navigators who are at the frontline of research and clinical support. They will seek to understand how Medicaid beneficiaries perceive clinical trials, how health related social needs impact these perceptions, and what further supports may be necessary to achieve clinical trial participation.</div><div><br>Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following:</div><ul><li>Assists with creating and maintaining spreadsheets, program materials, data collection, and assists with acquiring and distributing participant incentives.</li><li>As directed, performs various research and technical operations relative to the ongoing investigatory activities of the study.</li><li>Participates in the evaluation of existing procedures suggesting revisions where necessary, and proposing new procedures where required.</li><li>Responsible for submitting purchase recommendations to one’s supervisor.</li><li>Ensures that study materials are maintained in good working orders.</li><li>Keeps detailed records of study materials.</li></ul> CINJ - Cancer Health Equity & RBHS Chancellor-L2 Cancer Institute of New Jersey-L3 7888 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1728 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279430 2026-08-07T16:17:48-04:00 2026-08-07T16:17:49-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Licensed Practical Nurse for the department of Surgery at the Robert Wood Johnson Medical School.<br><br>The Rutgers–Robert Wood Johnson Medical School Licensed Practical Nurse, in collaboration with physicians, nursing staff, and other members of the healthcare team, provides focused, technical nursing care to clinical and office operations.&nbsp;<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Provides and documents nursing care within the scope of practice for colorectal surgery patients in face-to-face and telephone encounters; provides input to the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status to the physician and other members of the healthcare team as appropriate and in a timely manner.&nbsp;</li><li>May be required to travel to offsite locations to assist providers during clinic hours, including Steeplechase Cancer Center.&nbsp;</li><li>Assists physicians and advanced practice nurse during scheduled office hours, including preparation and setup of clinic exam and procedure rooms for patient visits. Assists in office procedures. Reviews and prepares patient charts prior to office visits for essential paperwork and test results.&nbsp;</li><li>Places orders and obtains insurance precertification for prescribed clinical testing for special procedures (CT, MRI, Ultrasound etc.) Provide patients with results of prescribed clinical tests after discussing them with the appropriate physicians.&nbsp;</li><li>Coordinates pre-operative testing and medical clearance prior to surgical procedures. Calls patients to check in pre- and post-operatively.&nbsp;</li><li>Completes return to work/school letters and disability paperwork for patients.&nbsp;</li></ul> RWJ - Surgery Colon Rectal RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7836 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1599 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/276580 2026-06-05T11:47:02-04:00 2026-06-05T11:47:03-04:00 Open Rank Faculty <div>This is an open-rank, 12-month, co-terminus faculty position that is partially state-funded and partially grant-funded, with continued appointment contingent upon funding. The successful candidate will help prepare students to become professional counselors, educators, researchers, and advanced clinicians specializing in effective treatment of people with mental illnesses and disabilities via counseling services and rehabilitation interventions.&nbsp;</div> SHP - Psychiatric Rehabilitati RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Health Professions-L3 7581 26FA0480 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274044 2026-04-30T11:40:04-04:00 2026-04-30T11:40:05-04:00 Non-Credit Instructors, CELG <div>Rutgers University-Camden, Center for Executive Leadership in Government (CELG) is seeking Course Instructors for the for the academic year 2026-2027. Programs are designed for training managers in non-profit, government, and public service organizations. The training provided includes professional certification and/or professional development for managers.<br>The position/s will collaborate with content experts and instructors to prepare materials for the creation of an online version, and provide pedagogical support for new instructors building modules, including public-sector-specific examples for cases and course framing content. Instructors will develop and share standard frameworks for Canvas, including discussions, collaborations, and cases. Successful candidates will be responsible for the following:<br>• Instructing/co-instructing non-credit courses (may include traditional lecture, hybrid, and/or fully online formats)<br>• Prepare course materials (e.g., syllabi, presentations and videos, hand-outs, reading materials, case studies, discussion questions, and knowledge checks)<br>• Provide constructive feedback in online discussions with students as well as critical instruction regarding student work that meets overall training goals<br>• Respond to student emails and inquiries<br>• Adhere to grade submission policies and deadlines (if applicable)<br>• Adhere to University policies and regulations<br>• Practice innovative educational methodology<br><br>The position/s will be responsible for non-credit course content development, course administration and content delivery, material development, revisions, updates, online materials and audio/visual/presentations for the following programs:<br>• Mini Master in Public Administration<br>• Public Leadership<br>• Strategic Communications<br>• Elevating Personal Leadership Skills<br>• Technology for Public Managers<br>• Human Resources and the Public Manager<br>• Grant Writing<br>• Other courses and seminars as needed</div> Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 8076 26FA0409 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/265921 2025-12-31T09:02:50-05:00 2025-12-31T09:02:51-05:00 Lecturer Fall 2025 <div>The Center for Latin American Studies invites applications for a Lecturer teaching position during the Fall 2025 semester.</div> Latin American Studies Program New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 7031 25FA0548 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279715 2026-08-19T13:11:19-04:00 2026-08-19T13:11:20-04:00 Assistant or Associate Professor Position in Entrepreneurship-- Management & Global Business <div>The Department of Management and Global Business at Rutgers Business School – Newark and New Brunswick is recruiting for a tenure-track faculty member at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. We seek candidates with a strong research interest in the broadly defined area of Entrepreneurship area with possible interests in related areas such as Strategic Management and International Business.<br><br>The Department of Management and Global Business has world-renowned faculty with specialties in International Business, Strategic Management, Corporate Social Responsibility, Entrepreneurship, Organizational Theory, Ethics, and Organizational Behavior. Our department also works with a talented group of Ph.D. students and hosts visiting scholars from around the world. <br><br><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></div><div>Participate actively in research, teach undergraduate, graduate and doctoral-level courses, supervise and work with doctoral students, and engage in service activities as required by the department and/or the school.</div><div><br><br></div> Management & Global Business Newark Chancellor-L2 Rutgers Business School-L3 6936 26FA0722 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280022 2026-08-26T12:13:04-04:00 2026-08-26T12:13:05-04:00 Staff Nurse (RN) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Staff Nurse for the Acute Psychiatric Services Department within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Staff Nurse is to deliver person centered goal directed nursing care in alignment with the departmental and hospital policies and procedures and all regulatory requirements. The staff nurse functions as a member of the interdisciplinary team; participates in quality improvement activities, educational activities, and supports research endeavors. The role is consistent with the scope and standards outlined in the Psychiatric-Mental Health Nursing: Scope and Standards of Practice.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Assesses and diagnoses patient, family and significant other needs in order to provide quality care to assigned patients.</li><li>Documents initial nursing assessment and individualized, goal directed plan of care considering the psychological, social, physical health and safety needs of the patient, in accordance with unit standards.</li><li>Develops, discusses and communicates a realistic, individualized plan of care for each patient, in collaboration with the patient, family and significant other in an effort to promote wellness and recovery.</li><li>Demonstrates the skills and judgment necessary to implement the plan of care, nursing interventions and procedures as necessary for the care and safety of the patient.</li><li>Evaluates identified problems and care provided and the patient’s responses are reassessed in order to meet the patient and family/significant other needs to ensure overall quality of care delivered.</li><li>Maintains concurrent and accurate documentation of nursing care provided to ensure the integration of information for use by the multidisciplinary team, in order to ensure quality care.</li><li>Performs all responsibilities/duties required by Acute Services as defined in the scope of service, to ensure that the uniqueness of the individual is addressed.</li><li>Demonstrates respect and regard for the dignity of all individuals served, families, visitors and fellow employees to ensure a professional, responsible and courteous environment.</li></ul> UBHC - Acute Psychological Ser RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7987 Piscataway NJ 26ST1653 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277783 2026-06-25T11:25:57-04:00 2026-06-25T11:25:58-04:00 Technician I PT Eves UCHC STU <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Part Time UCHC Technician I for the Adult Diagnostic Treatment Center located in Avenel, NJ. The UCHC Technician I participates as a member of the clinical and administrative medical team at the Prison.<br><br>Among the duties for this position are:<br><br><br></div><ul><li>Takes vital signs, height and weight and documents in electronic medical records (EMR).</li><li>Assists the physician/associate practitioner with procedures, including preparing the inmate for the examination.</li><li>Obtains specimen collection and handling, including, but not limited to, drawing blood.</li><li>Assists with the cleaning, sterilization and securing of equipment within the Health Service Unit.</li><li>Maintains or assists in maintaining the supply stock in the Health Service Unit by ordering in a timely and appropriate manner. Maintains the supply stock in the examination rooms.• Aggregates the orders of all medications and forwards to the pharmacy provider / local pharmacy.</li></ul> UCHC Adult Treatment Center Ph RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7674 Avenel NJ 26ST0905 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275545 2026-05-20T14:23:49-04:00 2026-05-20T14:23:50-04:00 Dining Services Student Worker (Livingston Starbucks) <div>Join the Rutgers Dining team as a Dining Services Student Worker in one of our dining halls or retail operations across the New Brunswick and Piscataway campuses. Rutgers Dining Services strives to be the best in culinary excellence and as a Dining Services Worker you play a critical role in the customer experience. From assisting in the preparation and service of food, to maintaining the presentation of the dining halls, to assisting guests, we have a variety of roles and will find the right one for you!<br><br>Dining Service Workers earn a paycheck and more:</div><ol><li>Student employee meal privileges.</li><li>Flexible schedules (10/20 hours/week) that work around your classes and activities.</li><li>Convenient on-campus locations.</li><li>Opportunities to advance to leadership positions such as Captain, Meal Manager and Student Unit Manager.</li><li>Valuable work experience to add to your resume.</li><li>Learn important job skills including interpersonal communications, team dynamics, dependability and time management.</li><li>A fun and welcoming environment.</li></ol> Livingston Starbucks New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Student Affairs - New Brunswic-L3 6683 Piscataway NJ 26ST1108 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266332 2025-12-31T09:51:11-05:00 2025-12-31T09:51:11-05:00 Tenure-Track Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Full Professor <div>Subject to availability of funding, the Department will have multiple openings at the level of Tenure-Track Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Full Professor (with the possibility of appointment at Distinguished Professor for exceptional candidates). The department has identified priority areas of discrete mathematics, applied mathematics, and algebra; but outstanding candidates in any area of mathematics will be considered. Candidates must have a PhD in mathematics by employment start date. Candidates will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in mathematics, perform research, and supervise graduate students. The normal teaching load for research-active faculty is currently 2–1. To apply, complete the application associated with this listing, making sure in particular to include a curriculum vitae.<br><br>Review of applications begins October 15, 2025 and will continue until the positions are filled. Applications completed after that date are still welcome but may not receive full consideration. Review of applications will continue on September 1, 2025, and continue until the position is filled.<br><br>Applicants should complete the online form associated with this listing and submit a curriculum vitae. In addition, you should register as a job applicant at mathjobs.org</div><div><a href=\"https://nam02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.mathjobs.org%2Fjobs%2Flist%2F26838&amp;data=05%7C02%7Cmb1186%40math.rutgers.edu%7Cf828c38cad5a4ae57b9208de2b8c4af9%7Cb92d2b234d35447093ff69aca6632ffe%7C1%7C0%7C638996078723971402%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=QYS5Gv1mJ72W2mgmCAt5MR78YPsJqMmKA8YSHH6aSd8%3D&amp;reserved=0\"><strong>https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/26838</strong></a>and complete the application, with the requested supporting documents, for position TT26 under the Rutgers University-New Brunswick listing.</div> Mathematics New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 8125 25FA0771 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280156 2026-08-31T08:43:49-04:00 2026-08-31T08:43:50-04:00 Staff Nurse FT Days UCHC SWSP (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care is seeking a Full Time Staff Nurse for the Southwoods State Prison located in Bridgeton, NJ.The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus for inmates in the New Jersey Department of Corrections.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br>* Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the resident-patient including adolescents (13-17 years), adults (18 to 64 years) and their family within the framework established by the correctional system.<br>* Performs assessments of resident-patient in a variety of settings such as initial intake area, health care unit for sick call, emergency situations in housing, chronic care clinics and infirmary.<br>* Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br>* Identifies inmate-centered goals and nursing objectives and implements prescribed interventions and solutions for the identified problems.<br>* Plans nursing care by identification of resident-patient needs based on assessments. Makes appropriate, timely referrals and initiates appropriate nursing care based on institutional policies and procedures.<br>* As team leader or charge nurse, delegates duties to other health care team members based on their skill, knowledge and experience and guides the provision of care by others.</div> UCHC-South Woods Psn-Ancillary RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7685 Bridgeton NJ 26ST0537 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278576 2026-07-10T11:02:31-04:00 2026-07-10T11:02:32-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse Per Diem UCHC BSP (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking Per Diem Licensed Practical Nurse (Medical) for Bayside State Prison, located in Leesburg, NJ<br><br>The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs. Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.</li><li>Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.</li><li>Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.</li><li>Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.</li><li>Documents all aspects of patient care</li></ul> UCHC Bayside State Prison Nurs RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7698 Leesburg NJ 26ST0697 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/268432 2026-02-03T10:56:01-05:00 2026-02-03T10:56:02-05:00 Custodian (Part-Time, Temporary) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Custodian (Part-Time, Temporary) for the Division of Institutional Planning &amp; Operations (IP&amp;O).<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Performs a wide variety of routine custodial duties required to maintain buildings and grounds in a clean and habitable condition.</li><li>Performs basic maintenance and repair duties on University facilities and equipment.</li></ul> Environmental Services NB EVP & Chief Admin Officer Institutional Planning & Optns-L3 6755 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280359 2026-09-03T10:05:14-04:00 2026-09-03T10:05:15-04:00 Dining Services Worker B <div>Rutgers, The State University is seeking a Dining Services Worker B for Kilmer's Market.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Performs general food service utility duties in various dining hall facilities.</li><li>Assists cooks, bakers, and Dining Services supervisors in tasks involving sanitary food handling.</li><li>Provides dining room services, including cash register duties.</li></ul> Kilmer's Market New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Student Affairs - New Brunswic-L3 6682 Piscataway NJ 26ST1713 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279226 2026-07-31T09:38:01-04:00 2026-07-31T09:38:02-04:00 Temporary Research Assistant <div>The Rutgers School of Public Health is seeking a highly motivated and detail oriented Temporary Research Assistant for the Shiau Research to support ongoing research projects addressing comorbidities associated with infections, including HIV, across the lifespan. The Temporary Research Assistant will work under the supervision of Dr. Stephanie Shiau in the Department of Biostatistics and Epidemiology at School of Public Health (SPH).<br><br></div><div>This position offers an opportunity to contribute to a dynamic research program spanning epidemiology, aging, molecular epidemiology, and health services research. The successful candidate will lead and support data management and statistical analyses, contribute to the development and publication of scientific manuscripts, and mentor students working on related projects. The position is well suited for an individual seeking to further develop expertise in epidemiologic methods, scientific writing, grantsmanship, and collaborative multidisciplinary research.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Conduct data management, cleaning, quality assurance, and preparation of research datasets.</li><li>Perform statistical analyses using SAS, R, and other relevant analytical tools to address study objectives.</li><li>Lead and contribute to the preparation of scientific manuscripts, including drafting, revising, and</li><li>submitting papers for publication in peer-reviewed journals.</li></ul> SPH - Epidemiology RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Public Health-L3 7710 Piscataway NJ 26ST1574 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/275334 2026-05-18T16:08:20-04:00 2026-05-18T16:08:20-04:00 Post-Doc Nakamura Lab <div>The Nakamura lab in Department of Genetics at Rutgers university has two postdoctoral positions available. The long-term goal of Nakamura lab is to identify the genetic mechanisms underlying fish diversity and their contribution to the fish-to-tetrapod transition. To this end, we bridge functional genomics, genetics, and embryology using model and non-model organisms, including zebrafish, skates, sharks, and spotted gar. More information about ongoing research projects can be found on the lab website (http://nakamuralab.com/).</div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>Candidates should have strong research records in any of the following areas: developmental biology, evolutionary biology, genomics, or other relevant fields. Our lab is a highly interdisciplinary environment, therefore, scientific curiosity and strong communication skills are indispensable. Experience in fish embryology, comparative anatomy, high-throughput sequencing, or bioinformatics data analysis is preferred, but not required.&nbsp;<br><br></div><div>Rutgers University is located in New Brunswick, NJ, which is only 45 minutes away from NYC by train. Many competitive research universities and institutes are in the Northeast area, offering remarkable opportunities for collaboration and research conferences.</div> Human Genetics Institute of NJ New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 8177 26FA0484 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266264 2025-12-31T09:42:18-05:00 2025-12-31T09:42:19-05:00 Post Doctorial Associate <div>Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy, Pharmacy Practice, and Pharmacy Administration – Health Outcomes, Policy &amp; Economics, Rutgers University is part of Rutgers Biomedical Health Sciences (RBHS) and participates in interdisciplinary professional education and training partnership with Rutgers School of Public Health and the Robert Wood Johnson Medical School.<br><br>Though certain responsibilities of the resident are required, the program has the flexibility to develop activities consistent with the resident’s background and career goals. In general, the resident responsibilities include: 1. Attend daily rounds and make appropriate recommendations to inter-disciplinary treatment teams 2. Design, monitor, and evaluate treatment goals for patients that consider patient-, disease-, and drug-specific information and ethical considerations 3. Present educational in-services on pharmacy topics to patients, pharmacy staff, and inter-disciplinary treatment team 4. Lead inpatient and outpatient pharmacy medication education groups 5. Supervise pharmacy students on Advanced Pharmacy Practice Experience (APPE) rotations. 6. Present didactic lectures to pharmacy students at the Rutgers Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy 7. Complete a research project related to the provision of pharmacy care, as well as presenting this research at a national conference.</div> Pharmacy Practice & Administra RBHS Chancellor-L2 Ernest Mario School of Pharmac-L3 6720 25FA0629 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280140 2026-08-28T16:45:18-04:00 2026-08-28T16:45:19-04:00 Temporary Research Assistant, Per Diem <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Temporary Research Assistant, Per Diem within Radiation Oncology/Cancer Biology at the Rutgers Cancer Institute.<br><br>Under the direction of the Principal Investigator or designee, the Temporary Research Assistant will assist in research on the lab grant deliverables. Incumbent will review, provide quality control, and analyze study data.</div><div><br>Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Works under the direction of the PI or his/her designee. Responsible for executing laboratory tasks as outlined by the Principal Investigator or a senior member of laboratory team.</li><li>Performs functions as directed for experiments that are proposed in the grant, under the direction of the principal investigator and other designated lab members.</li><li>Maintains department database on a computer. Candidate must have competent computer skills and be able to utilize equipment and technology in support of the assigned project(s).</li><li>Must possess effective oral and written communication skills and ability to summarize scientific research process and communicate project findings.</li></ul> CINJ - HU Signaling Pathways RBHS Chancellor-L2 Cancer Institute of New Jersey-L3 8565 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1678 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278508 2026-07-09T12:54:24-04:00 2026-07-09T12:54:24-04:00 Habilitation Counselor <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Habilitation Counselor for the Edison Outpatient Treatment within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The purpose of the Habilitation Counselor position is to provide site and community-based case management and supported employment services to individuals receiving treatment services through UBHC’s Outpatient Dementia Clinic.<br><br></div><div>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Supports individuals with Dementia and their family/caregiver to gain access to needed medical, social, education, mental health, addiction, co-occurring, and other services.&nbsp;</li><li>Demonstrates the ability to engage and establish a working relationship with and provide services to individuals who are diagnosed with a serious and persistent mental illness and co-occurring disorders who present engagement challenges.&nbsp;</li><li>Collaborates effectively with members of the department, and with external departments, staff, referral sources, other service providers and social support networks to provide services and rehabilitative care for individuals served and family members.&nbsp;</li><li>Maintains appropriate clinical records according to the time frames and quality guidelines established by UBHC policy and applicable accrediting organization standards.</li><li>Maintains knowledge of trends and developments in the field.</li><li>Contributes to and supports the mission, vision, values, goals and objectives of UBHC.</li></ul> UBHC - Edison RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8002 Edison NJ 26ST0673 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/267878 2026-01-23T11:55:23-05:00 2026-01-23T11:55:23-05:00 Part Time Teaching - Summer 2026 <div>The Professional Science Master’s Program (PSM) invites applications for part time instructors for the Summer 2026 term. We seek qualified instructors who can contribute to the university’s educational mission and bridge the gap between the classroom and the industry.<br><br>Successful candidates will instruct/co-instruct on a wide variety of topics. Applicant’s core knowledge should include, but is not limited to, any concentration under agriculture, biotechnology, environmental science, food science, kinesiology and physiology, life sciences (chemistry, biology, physics, etc.), engineering (i.e., biomedical, biochemical, chemical, electrical, computer, pharmaceutical, etc.), pharmacology, computer and information science (i.e., statistics and biostatistics, discovery informatics and data science, applied computing, information technology, networking, etc.), and business (i.e., accounting, finance, leadership, marketing, etc.)<br><br>Successful candidates will be responsible for the following:</div><ul><li>Instructing/co-instructing course(s) at the graduate level (may include traditional lecture, hybrid, and/or fully online courses)</li><li>Prepare course materials (i.e., syllabi, presentations, hand-outs, reading materials, etc.)</li><li>Provide constructive feedback to students as well as critical instruction regarding student work and academic standards</li><li>Respond to student emails and inquiries</li><li>Adhere to grade submission policies and deadlines</li><li>Adhere to university policies and regulations</li><li>Practice innovative educational methodology</li></ul> Professional Science Masters New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Professional Science Masters-L3 6665 26FA0062 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280283 2026-09-01T13:26:36-04:00 2026-09-01T13:26:37-04:00 Per Diem Healthcare Provider (Multiple Vacancies) <div>Rutgers, the State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Per Diem Healthcare Provider for the First Responder Peer Services programs within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Per Diem Healthcare Provider position is to provide assessments for first responders throughout the State of New Jersey that meet quality and quantity standards within the First Responder Peer Services programs. Performs functions in support of the First Responder Peer Services programs mission as well as the programs project goals providing streamlined, prompt, and “consumer friendly” access to University Behavioral Health Care services.<br><br>Among the key duties of the position are the following:</div><ul><li>As part of the First Responder Peer Services team, actively participates in ensuring the telephone calls/service requests are handled in an effective and “consumer friendly” manner.</li><li>Maintains comprehensive and up-to-date knowledge of eligibility and admission criteria for units and programs served by the First Responder Peer Services programs, as observed by supervisor.</li><li>Performs clinical assessment and makes appropriate disposition, often by scheduling an appointment at an UBHC unit, as indicated by feedback from receiving unit or other provider.</li><li>Acquires familiarity with other UBHC units, outside providers, and other pertinent organizations and resources, in order to facilitate telephone activities, develop work relationships, and provide information and guidance to callers.</li><li>Assists in supervision of daily operations of the First Responder Peer Services programs when needed.</li><li>Conforms to unit policies relating to functional needs of the program.</li></ul> UBHC - Cop2Cop RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8008 Piscataway NJ 25ST2083 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278987 2026-07-20T16:11:13-04:00 2026-07-20T16:11:14-04:00 Temporary Research Assistant <div>Rutgers School of Health Professions (SHP) is seeking a Temporary Research Assistant to work in the Department of Psychiatric Rehabilitation &amp; Counseling Professions.<br><br>Under the direction of Associate Professor, Temporary Research Assistant is responsible for providing support for research activities.<br><br></div><div>Essential duties and responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Assists in coordinating project activities.</li><li>Assists with IRB related tasks including inform consent and participant recruitment.</li><li>Assists with creating the project web page.</li><li>Creates SNS advertisement script and conducts advertisement activities.</li><li>Conducts community outreach and focus groups.</li><li>Collects necessary data, checks data quality and tracks data.</li><li>Performs data analysis under supervision.</li><li>Assists in developing success stories, evaluating the project, and generating reports.</li></ul> SHP - Psychiatric Rehabilitati RBHS Chancellor-L2 School of Health Professions-L3 7581 Piscataway NJ 26ST1546 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/271487 2026-03-24T10:19:58-04:00 2026-03-24T10:19:59-04:00 Post Doctorial Associate <div>Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy, Pharmacy Practice, and Pharmacy Administration – Health Outcomes, Policy &amp; Economics, Rutgers University is part of Rutgers Biomedical Health Sciences (RBHS) and participates in interdisciplinary professional education and training partnership with Rutgers School of Public Health and the Robert Wood Johnson Medical School.<br><br>Though certain responsibilities of the resident are required, the program has the flexibility to develop activities consistent with the resident’s background and career goals. In general, the resident responsibilities include: 1. Attend daily rounds and make appropriate recommendations to inter-disciplinary treatment teams 2. Design, monitor, and evaluate treatment goals for patients that consider patient-, disease-, and drug-specific information and ethical considerations 3. Present educational in-services on pharmacy topics to patients, pharmacy staff, and inter-disciplinary treatment team 4. Lead inpatient and outpatient pharmacy medication education groups 5. Supervise pharmacy students on Advanced Pharmacy Practice Experience (APPE) rotations. 6. Present didactic lectures to pharmacy students at the Rutgers Ernest Mario School of Pharmacy 7. Complete a research project related to the provision of pharmacy care, as well as presenting this research at a national conference</div> Pharmacy Practice & Administra RBHS Chancellor-L2 Ernest Mario School of Pharmac-L3 6720 26FA0273 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279510 2026-08-11T12:23:12-04:00 2026-08-11T12:23:13-04:00 Research Teaching Specialist V <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Research Teaching Specialist V to join the Hinrichs Lab within Medical Immunology at Rutgers Cancer Institute.<br><br>Under the direction of the Principal Investigator, the primary role of the Research Teaching Specialist V (RTS V) is to perform research activities requiring the application of standard techniques and procedures.<br><br>As directed, The RTS V performs various research and technical operations relative to highly specialized, technical research in tumor immunology with a focus on the discovery and development of T cell therapy for cancer, including tumor-infiltrating lymphocytes and gene-engineered T cells.<br><br>Active areas of research include T cell receptor discovery, membrane-tethered cytokine technologies, tumor resistance mutations, target antigen discovery, and preclinical development of new TCR-based treatments. There will be opportunities to work in an interdisciplinary team both in clinical and laboratory research settings on a variety of high impact, cutting edge projects.<br><br></div><div>Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>As directed, performs various research and technical operations relative to the ongoing investigatory activities of the laboratory in the areas of tumor immunology and cancer immunotherapy, especially with detailed knowledge of T cell biology, antigen presentation, T cell receptors, and cellular therapy. This research includes cell culture, transduction, transfection, retroviruses, lentiviruses, construction of vectors and DNA cloning, flow cytometry, cytolysis assays, cytokine assays, proliferation assays, PCR, analysis of human samples, and murine tumor models.</li><li>Assists in the investigation, review, modification, development, and testing of new analytical procedures and methodologies.</li><li>Interprets raw analytical data and presents and submits conclusions to the Principal Investigator for approval.</li><li>Participates in the preparation of sound, accurate, written and oral reports relating to research, grant, and other activities containing findings, conclusions, or recommendations.</li><li>Keeps detailed laboratory notebooks and stores digital research data in designated locations.</li><li>Follows laboratory rules and research protocols.</li><li>Collaborates with other laboratory members to maintain laboratory equipment, manage shared supplies and inventories, review and update laboratory protocols, and dispose of hazardous waste properly.</li></ul> CINJ - Medical Immunology RBHS Chancellor-L2 Cancer Institute of New Jersey-L3 8185 New Brunswick NJ 26ST1603 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279761 2026-08-20T09:11:50-04:00 2026-08-20T09:11:51-04:00 Staff Nurse Mental Health Per Diem Multiple Vacancies UCHC NJSP <div>University Correctional Healthcare is seeking a Per Diem UCHC Staff Nurse Mental Health for New Jersey State Prison, located in Trenton, NJ. The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus. Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.<br><br>Among the duties are:</div><ul><li>Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological, psychosocial and emotional needs of the inmate-patient including adults (18 to 64 years), and geriatrics (65+) within the framework established by the correctional system.</li><li>Utilizes effective communication skills by demonstrating respect, concern and courtesy in all interpersonal relationships.</li><li>Uses current knowledge to promote a safe environment for providing health care to inmate-patients.</li></ul> UCHC Nursing Per Diem Medical RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7664 Trenton NJ 26ST1018 Per Diem https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277108 2026-06-15T10:18:43-04:00 2026-06-15T10:18:44-04:00 Medical Director, Section of Transfusion Medicine <div>The Transfusion Medicine Medical Director will hold a crucial leadership role in maintaining patient safety, regulatory compliance, and advancing transfusion medicine practices within RWJMS and RWJUH. This faculty member will serve as both a collaboratory and leader of the multidisciplinary transfusion team at RWJMS and RWJUH; will be an active participant in the educational programs of the Department, including teaching medical students, residents, and will be expected to engage in productive research activities. The Division is responsible for Transfusion Medicine and Blood Banking services at Robert Wood Johnson University Hospital (RWJUH), the school’s 650-bed tertiary care core teaching hospital in New Brunswick, NJ.<br><br>A comprehensive list of job duties and responsibilities will be shared with candidates as part of the interview process<br><br>Academic rank and compensation will be commensurate with the candidate’s qualifications and academic experience.</div> RWJ - Pathology RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7798 26FA0584 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/274093 2026-04-30T15:34:00-04:00 2026-04-30T15:34:00-04:00 Lecturers, Philosophy and Religion <div>Rutgers University-Camden, the Faculty of Arts &amp; Sciences, Philosophy and Religion Department, may seek new lecturers for various courses during the Fall 2026, Winter 2027, Spring 2027 and/or Summer 2027.</div> Philosophy & Religion Camden Chancellor's Office-L2 Faculty of Arts & Sciences Cam-L3 6767 26FA0428 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266035 2025-12-31T09:17:16-05:00 2025-12-31T09:17:16-05:00 Assistant/Associate Dean Program Evaluation and Continuous Quality Improvement <div>This newly developed role will report to the Executive Vice Dean and will provide services across the medical education continuum including faculty affairs. The Assistant/Associate Dean for Program Evaluation and Continuous Quality Improvement (CQI) will oversee the program development, data collection and analysis to inform and support the improvement of our educational programs along the educational continuum including our faculty and resident development programs. In addition, this role will work closely with other units and individual faculty to promote the scholarship of education across New Jersey Medical School. The successful candidate will be appointed at a faculty rank commensurate with experience and consistent with RBHS guidelines for appointments and promotions.</div><div><br>Specific responsibilities include:</div><ul><li>Oversee all aspects of evaluation of the medical education program, including planning, data collection, compilation/ analysis and interpretation as well as activities related to preparation and dissemination of program evaluation data reports.</li><li>Lead efforts to optimize the survey and assessment systems for evaluation of 1) individual curricular elements and 2) the overall educational programs, for continuous quality improvement of the curriculum and to monitor the impact of curricular changes.</li><li>Collaborate with members of the leadership team to support the development of a comprehensive learner assessment system that will allow for evaluation of learner outcomes along the full extent of the MD-degree program curriculum.</li><li>Direct the continuous monitoring process for compliance with all twelve LCME accreditation standards; serve as a core member of the LCME preparation team.</li><li>Lead efforts with appropriate individuals/groups to develop and implement plans that address any identified areas of potential non-compliance with LCME accreditation standards.</li><li>Serve as a member of the professional development team, working to promote and expand medical education scholarship. As appropriate, apply for and work with other units to apply for grants to support educational scholarship, present work nationally, and publish scholarship that advances education.</li><li>Actively participate in curriculum, student affairs, admissions, and faculty meetings as needed and requested by the Executive Vice Dean.</li></ul><div><br></div> NJMS - Education Special Progr RBHS Chancellor-L2 New Jersey Medical School-L3 7511 22FA1014 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280050 2026-08-26T14:41:48-04:00 2026-08-26T14:41:49-04:00 Habilitation Counselor - Multiple Vacancies <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey is seeking a Habilitation Counselor for the Children’s Mobile Response and Stabilization Services within Rutgers University Behavioral Health Care.<br><br>The primary purpose of the Habilitation Counselor is to provide assessments for the Children’s Mobile Response and Stabilization Services (CMRSS) program in designated catchment area that meet quality and quantity standards within UBHC and the Children’s System of Care (CSoC). Performs functions in support of the UBHC mission providing streamlined, prompt, and “consumer friendly” crisis response services. Receives telephone requests for service, undertakes crisis assessment of the service needs of the client or customer, responds by outreach to the family, assesses the youth and family strengths and current crisis situation, makes appropriate referrals for time-limited stabilization services, monitors effectiveness of services and makes linkages for aftercare. Demonstrates competency in recognizing the unique needs and applying relevant crisis stabilization approaches for children and adolescent and their families.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br></div><ul><li>Ensures that telephone contacts with clients or family members occur in an appropriately courteous, helpful fashion.</li><li>Responds to families telephone referrals, inquiries, and other contacts with professionals, outside agencies and other parties in a professional and cordial manner, per caller feedback.</li><li>Maintains comprehensive and up-to-date knowledge of eligibility and admission criteria for units and programs served by the CMRSS program.</li><li>Obtains crisis assessment information in accordance with CMRSS protocols and accurately and appropriately inputs data in unit’s information system.</li><li>Provides face to face interventions in the community including, but not limited to, families’ homes, schools, group homes, foster homes, shelters, and the detention center.</li><li>Provides case management services to inform and assist families with gaining access to needed legal, medical, social, education, mental health, addiction, co-occurring, and other services.</li><li>Acquires familiarity with agencies in the designated catchment area that provides services to children, adolescents and their families that can provide crisis stabilization services and providing ongoing support/resources for the family.</li></ul> UBHC - Mobile Response RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 8026 Piscataway NJ 26ST0451 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278143 2026-07-01T13:00:42-04:00 2026-07-01T13:00:54-04:00 Pharmacy Technician UCHC Central <div>University Correctional Healthcare (UCHC) is seeking a Pharmacy Technician for the Central Regional Office, located in Trenton, NJ. Under the direction of the Clinical Pharmacy Manager and Director of Pharmacy, performs a variety of technical functions for the correctional unit dose drug distribution system. Responsible for reviewing physician orders and prescriptions, maintaining confidential reports, entering and retrieving data utilizing the computer system, responding to requests for drug information, medication refill and 340b drug pricing program processing, and delivering medication to the appropriate units as necessary.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Accurately profiles medication orders into the pharmacy information system<ul><li>Ensures that outpatient prescriptions are accurately entered into the pharmacy information system.&nbsp;</li><li>Ensures that medications are delivered to the proper nursing units, ancillary departments.&nbsp;</li><li>Ensures that medications dispensed are correct drug/strength, dosage form/quality.</li></ul></li><li>Prepares controlled substance requests from nursing units for verification by the Registered Pharmacist.&nbsp;<ul><li>Documents additions/deletions of controlled substance medications in the appropriate section of the controlled substance record with appropriate signatures.&nbsp;</li><li>Correctly totals and documents the running balance of controlled substance medications upon addition or deletion of controlled substance medications to/from nursing unit stock.</li><li>Logs the controlled substances returned from nursing units into the proper pharmacy records and returns to stock or places with DEA returns.&nbsp;</li></ul></li><li>Prepares requests and restocks nursing units with floor stock medications and supplies.<ul><li>Fills floor stock and internal requisitions with the correct medication/strength/dosage form.&nbsp;</li><li>Ensures that quantities do not exceed established par levels.</li><li>Delivers floor stock and internal requisitions to nursing units on the same shift they are received.&nbsp;</li></ul></li><li>Reorders pharmacy supplies from approved vendor</li></ul> UCHC Administration RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7673 Trenton NJ 26ST1442 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/266395 2026-01-04T21:31:27-05:00 2026-01-04T21:31:28-05:00 Part-time Lecturers and Coadjutants for Spring 2026 Semester - Various Courses <div>The Department of Food Science in the School of Environmental and Biological Sciences at Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is currently seeking Part-time Lecturers or Co-adjutants to teach or Co-adjutants to provide academic support for various undergraduate or graduate courses such as: Food and Health; Field to Table; Food Process Engineering; Current Issues in Food Science and Food Law; Food Product Development; Food Microbiology Lab; Carbohydrates in Foods; Nutragenomics &amp; Nutraceuticals, and possibly others during the Spring 2026 semester.<br><br>The instructors will present course materials during assigned course times and non-teaching co-adjutants will provide academic support. Other duties include holding office hours, administering exams, assigning grades and coordinating any other requirements related to course instruction. Applicants should specify which course is of primary interest.</div> Food Science New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School Environ & Biologicl Sci-L3 7138 25FA1169 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280188 2026-08-31T10:47:24-04:00 2026-08-31T10:47:25-04:00 Forensic Mental Health Clinician UCHC GSYCF <div>Rutgers University Correctional Health Care (UCHC) is seeking a Forensic Mental Health Clinician for Garden State Youth Correctional Facility, located in Yardville, NJ. Reporting to the Clinician Supervisor, the Forensic Mental Health Clinician completes specialized psychological testing and assessment of clinical needs of adult inmates sentenced to the Department of Corrections.<br><br>Among the key duties for this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Arrives at DSM IV diagnoses with precision and accuracy through psychological testing and evaluation sessions.</li><li>Provides crisis intervention, individual and group psychotherapy and psycho-education programming as clinically indicated to assigned inmates.</li><li>Involves inmates and Department of Corrections staff in developing achievable and understandable psychosocial treatment plans.</li><li>Advocates for appropriate resources for inmates based on assessed needs.</li><li>Manages caseload demands effectively while considering both qualities of care and the security needs of the Department of Corrections.</li><li>Assumes overall case management responsibilities for assigned inmates including coordination of treatment and liaison with community agencies; maintains appropriate inmate records.</li><li>Demonstrates competency in psychological testing and in recognizing the unique needs and behaviors of adult inmates and seniors</li></ul> UCHC Garden State Youth Medica RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7653 Yardville NJ 26ST0635 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/278629 2026-07-10T13:03:15-04:00 2026-07-10T13:03:15-04:00 Staff Nurse Mental Health PT NIghts UCHC NJSP <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Part Time UCHC Mental Health Staff Nurse for New Jersey State Prison, located in Trenton, NJ<br><br>The Staff Nurse utilizes the nursing process to meet a variety of health care needs with ambulatory care as a primary focus for inmates in the New Jersey Department of Corrections.<br><br>Duties include:</div><ul><li>Provides direct and indirect nursing care to meet physiological and emotional needs of the resident-patient including adolescents (13-17 years), adults (18 to 64 years) and their family within the framework established by the correctional system.</li><li>Performs assessments of resident-patient in a variety of settings such as initial intake area, health care unit for sick call, emergency situations in housing, chronic care clinics and infirmary.</li><li>Works with a variety of health care professionals and security officers in a correctional environment.</li><li>Identifies inmate-centered goals and nursing objectives and implements prescribed interventions and solutions for the identified problems.</li><li>Plans nursing care by identification of resident-patient needs based on assessments.</li><li>Makes appropriate, timely referrals and initiates appropriate nursing care based on institutional policies and procedures. As team leader or charge nurse, delegates duties to other health care team members based on their skill, knowledge and experience and guides the provision of care by others.</li></ul> UCHC New Jersey State Prison M RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7660 Trenton NJ 26ST1272 Part Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/269359 2026-02-17T12:14:54-05:00 2026-02-17T12:14:55-05:00 Research Associate Position in Stem Cell Biology and Neuroscience <div>The Jiang Laboratory in the Department of Cell Biology and Neuroscience at Rutgers University–New Brunswick invites applications for a Research Associate non tenure track position in the areas of human pluripotent stem cell biology and neuroscience.<br><br></div><div>The Jiang lab investigates the cellular and molecular mechanisms underlying human brain development and neurological disease, with a particular emphasis on the roles of glial cells, especially human microglia, in neurodevelopmental and neurodegenerative disorders. Using human pluripotent stem cell–based platforms, our research employs innovative in vitro brain organoid systems and in vivo chimeric mouse brain models to elucidate disease mechanisms and to develop novel glia-based therapeutic strategies.<br><br></div><div>We use a wide range of multidisciplinary approaches, including human pluripotent stem cell reprogramming and differentiation, CRISPR/Cas9–mediated genome editing, electrophysiology and patch-clamp recordings, advanced imaging techniques, molecular and cellular biology, biochemistry, and pharmacology, bulk and single-cell RNA sequencing and data analysis, transgenic and surgically induced animal models, as well as behavioral analyses.<br><br></div><div>Recent publications from the laboratory include:<br><br></div><div>Jin, Ma, Zhang, et al., Cell Reports (2026)</div><div>Jin et al., Nature Neuroscience (2026)</div><div>Papetti, Jin, et al., Neuron (2025)</div><div>Qiao &amp; Jiang, Cell Stem Cell (2025)</div><div>Jin et al., Cell Stem Cell (2022)</div><div>Xu et al., Nature Communications (2020)</div><div>Xu et al., Stem Cell Reports (2020)</div><div>Kim et al., Stem Cell Reports (2019)</div><div>Xu et al., Cell Stem Cell (2019)<br><br></div><div>Additional information about the laboratory can be found at: https://cbn.rutgers.edu/peng-jiang-lab/339-peng-jiang-lab</div> DLS Cell Biology & Neuroscienc New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 School of Arts & Sciences-L3 7060 26FA0085 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/280438 2026-09-04T09:29:38-04:00 2026-09-04T09:29:39-04:00 PostDoctoral Associate in Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning and Data Science <div>The Rutgers Artificial Intelligence and Data Science (RAD) Collaboratory is seeking to appoint two highly motivated postdoctoral researchers with expertise in artificial intelligence/machine learning and data science. Applicants must have completed their Ph.D. studies within the past year. Prior to submitting an application, they must identify an existing RAD Collaboratory faculty member as their postdoctoral mentor and provide the Mentor's Letter of Nomination (on Rutgers Letterhead) with their application materials. Successful candidates will work under the supervision of the Nominating Mentor and contribute to interdisciplinary research projects focused on important problems in science and engineering. Eligible subject areas include computational biology and/or biomedicine, multi-modality fusion and inference (visual and NLP data), computationally efficient ML, environmental sciences, business applications, chemistry, and physics. The RAD Collaboratory offers a rich environment for collaboration with ample access to computational resources.</div> Quantitative Biomedicine Inst New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 ORI-L3 6749 26FA0744 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279360 2026-08-06T11:44:54-04:00 2026-08-06T11:44:55-04:00 Sr. Facilities Project Manager <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Sr Facilities Project Manager for the Division of Institutional Planning &amp; Operations (IP&amp;O). Under the guidance of the Department Head/Director, the Senior Facilities Project Manager coordinates, develops, designs, and budgets renovation projects throughout the University.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:</div><ul><li>Interfaces with adynamic team of University technical staff, including project management, maintenance, safety, controls, commissioning, and utilities groups, to ensure that projects are implemented properly from conception through final acceptance.</li><li>The Sr. Project Manager runs anywhere from 5 -15 projects in various stages of Design and Construction with minimal supervision from the Director.</li><li>The Sr. Project Manager needs to be highly motivated, organized, and persistent with follow-up to keep projects on schedule and under budget.</li><li>The Sr. PM is responsible for Millions of dollars of design/construction work per year.</li></ul> Renovations & Utilities UW EVP & Chief Admin Officer Institutional Planning & Optns-L3 8699 Piscataway NJ 26ST1593 Full Time https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/276072 2026-05-29T09:43:50-04:00 2026-05-29T09:43:50-04:00 MGSA – Department of Arts Online – Coadjutant Non-Teaching Academic support <div>The Division of Rutgers Arts Online, Mason Gross School of the Arts, Rutgers University invites applications for part-time casual academic support for the Fall 2026 term. Positions include but are not limited to curriculum content development, course review, research and other non-teaching academic support duties.</div> Rutgers Arts Online New Brunswick Chancellor-L2 Mason Gross School of Arts Dea-L3 8712 26FA0526 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/273433 2026-04-21T13:55:40-04:00 2026-04-21T13:55:41-04:00 Lecturers / Coadjuta