to students as well as critical instruction regarding student work and academic standards</li><li>Responding to student emails and inquiries and addressing student concerns</li><li>Practicing innovative educational methodology</li><li>Assisting with research assignments</li><li>Proctoring course exams, if applicable and approved by the faculty member</li></ul> Human Resources Newark Newark Chancellor-L2 Rutgers Business School-L3 6942 25FA1260 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279653 2026-08-17T15:01:43-04:00 2026-08-17T15:01:43-04:00 Postdoc Associate -Pharmacology & Toxicology <div>TBD</div> Pharmacology & Toxicology RBHS Chancellor-L2 Ernest Mario School of Pharmac-L3 6718 26FA0719 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/279958 2026-08-25T14:10:03-04:00 2026-08-25T14:10:04-04:00 Instructor/Assistant Professor <div>The Department of Emergency Medicine at Rutgers Robert Wood Johnson Medical School a in New Brunswick, New Jersey, is seeking a board-certified or board-eligible Emergency Medicine physician to join our faculty as a <strong>Nocturnist</strong>. The Emergency Department manages more than 80,000 patient visits annually and serves as a regional referral center for trauma, critical care, stroke, cardiac emergencies, and complex tertiary care.</div><div>The successful candidate will provide high-quality emergency care during overnight shifts while contributing to the department's mission of excellence in patient care, education, and academic development. Faculty members work collaboratively with emergency medicine residents, medical students, advanced practice providers (APPs), nursing staff, and multidisciplinary consultants in a fast-paced academic environment.</div> RWJ - Emergency Medicine RBHS Chancellor-L2 RWJ - Robert Wood Johnson Medi-L3 7854 26FA0734 https://jobs.rutgers.edu/postings/277764 2026-06-25T11:07:27-04:00 2026-06-25T11:07:28-04:00 Licensed Practical Nurse Per Diem UCHC NSP (multiple vacancies) <div>Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey, is seeking a Per Diem Licensed Practical Nurse for Northern State Prison located in Newark, NJ<br><br>The primary purpose of the Licensed Practical Nurse position is to, in accordance with professional nursing standards, skillfully administer total patient care based on the individualized needs of assigned patients and families. Under the direction and supervision of a Registered Nurse, provides technical nursing care to assigned patients, performs treatments and procedures within established guidelines, and provides a safe and therapeutic environment.<br><br>Among the key duties of this position are the following:<br><br>* Participates in data collection related to the patients’ status and needs.<br>* Provides input to Registered Nurse for incorporation into the plan of care by communicating information pertinent to the patient’s status.<br>* Provides direct patient care within scope of practice to ensure implementation of the plan of care.<br>* Informs and instructs patients/significant others on patient’s health/illness state and plan of care.<br>* Assists patient/significant other in preparation for discharge and health maintenance in the home.<br>* Documents all aspects of patient care.</div> UCHC New Jersey State Prison N RBHS Chancellor-L2 University Behavioral Health-L3 7693 Newark NJ 26ST0680 Per Diem"
